ss-rights/roles-and-relations-322","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#the-same-relations-in-the-modules--nexmap-nexcare-nexforge","content":"yes (human only)"},"601":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-323","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#the-same-relations-in-the-modules--nexmap-nexcare-nexforge","content":"—"},"602":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-324","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#the-same-relations-in-the-modules--nexmap-nexcare-nexforge","content":"never"},"603":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-325","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#the-same-relations-in-the-modules--nexmap-nexcare-nexforge","content":"Module content is kept read-only when a pack is removed and returns when it is installed again; only a person inside\nthe module deletes anything."},"604":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-326","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"When a flow or a tool call pauses for a human, the run's creator resolves at that moment who may decide —\nnormally the Project's owners — and writes those ids on the request. A later change of membership does not\nwiden the list."},"605":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-327","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"Rule"},"606":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-328","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"Answer"},"607":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-329","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"The person is not in the organization, or the request is above their clearance"},"608":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-330","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"*Not found* — nothing is revealed."},"609":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-331","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"An agent or a service tries to decide"},"610":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-332","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"**403 · humans only** — even the agent that requested it."},"611":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-333","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"The request is already decided, withdrawn or expired"},"612":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-334","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"**409** — an expired request is never approved silently."},"613":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-335","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"The decider is the person the run acts for, and self-approval is not allowed for this request"},"614":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-336","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"**403 · self-approval** — someone else in the list must decide."},"615":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-337","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"A member of the Project who is not on the decider list"},"616":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-338","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"**403 · not a decider** — the card shows &#x2A;Waiting for \\<owner>* without buttons."},"617":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-339","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"A listed decider"},"618":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-340","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"Approve or reject, with a note; the run continues or ends; the decision is immutable and audited."},"619":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-341","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#who-may-decide-an-approval","content":"The base Blueprint sets *Self-approval: forbidden* (the row you read in the Blueprint matrix); a deployment may\nallow it below *DSK*, and the organization layer may only tighten. Nexi never lets a model decide: the engine\nparks the run, a person answers, the engine resumes."},"620":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-342","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#clearance-and-classification","content":"Every person carries a **clearance**, every resource a **classification** — *Public · Confidential · DSK · Secret\n· Top secret*. A relation never overrides clearance: an owner cleared to *Confidential* is refused their own\nProject the day it is reclassified *Secret*. A Project's classification is set at creation and may be tightened,\nnever loosened below the organization's default; cloud models are capped by the Blueprint (*Confidential* in the\nbase pack), so a *Secret* Project can only ever use local models."},"621":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-343","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#agents-are-not-people-with-fewer-rights","content":"An agent added to a Project reads what the Project offers and acts through the person who started it. Three\nthings are closed to it by identity, whatever relation it holds: **authoring** (it cannot create, change, publish or\ndelete agents, skills, tool bindings or flows — it may only *request* a capability, which a human grants),\n**approving** (it can neither decide nor read an approval it did not cause), and **payloads** (it never reads what a\nmodel was told or answered). Above *Confidential* an agent must also be able to name the person it acts for, or it\nis refused outright."},"622":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-344","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#checklist-for-administrators","content":"Give **organization roles** sparingly: Owner (one), a second Admin for continuity, an Auditor if compliance\nneeds read-only history. Everyone else *Member* or *Builder*."},"623":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-345","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#checklist-for-administrators","content":"Give **Project relations** for the work: owners who publish and approve, editors who do, viewers who read."},"624":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-346","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#checklist-for-administrators","content":"Set **clearance** to the highest classification the person needs, not the highest they might."},"625":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-347","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#checklist-for-administrators","content":"Let the **Blueprint** carry policy (cloud ceiling, approvals, builder-only tools) rather than individual\nexceptions — it is inherited by every Project and shown on each Project's *Governance* tab."},"626":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-348","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#checklist-for-administrators","content":"Read **Audit** for the *Deny* rows once a week: they show where roles and expectations differ."},"627":{"id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations-349","page_id":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/access-rights/roles-and-relations#checklist-for-administrators","content":"See also: How Nexi decides what you may do ·\nCreate a Project and give people a place in it ·\nWhat the base pack gave you — capabilities and the Blueprint's ceilings ·\nDecide the approval and read the run."},"628":{"id":"/docs/api","page_id":"/docs/api","type":"page","content":"API reference","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api"},"629":{"id":"/docs/api-0","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api","content":"The Chat, Platform, Tasks, Graph and BI APIs — generated from the published contracts, with a live playground on every operation."},"630":{"id":"/docs/api-1","page_id":"/docs/api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api#try-it-in-three-moves","content":"Try it in three moves"},"631":{"id":"/docs/api-2","page_id":"/docs/api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"What you are calling"},"632":{"id":"/docs/api-3","page_id":"/docs/api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api#module-apis--not-in-this-reference-yet","content":"Module APIs — not in this reference yet"},"633":{"id":"/docs/api-4","page_id":"/docs/api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"What the answers mean"},"634":{"id":"/docs/api-5","page_id":"/docs/api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api#what-is-not-here","content":"What is *not* here"},"635":{"id":"/docs/api-6","page_id":"/docs/api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api#running-the-portal-against-your-own-nexi","content":"Running the portal against your own Nexi"},"636":{"id":"/docs/api-7","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api","content":"Every page in this section is generated at build time from the contract files the platform ships, so what you\nread is exactly what the API accepts. Every operation has a **playground**: fill the fields, press *Send*, read the\nreal answer of a real Nexi — yours."},"637":{"id":"/docs/api-8","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#try-it-in-three-moves","content":"The playground talks to Nexi **through this portal** (same origin, `/api/v1`), and Nexi recognises you by the\nsession cookie NexCore set when you signed in. Cookies belong to a host name, not a port — so the portal keeps\nitself on the host name NexCore uses (open it on `localhost` and it moves you to `127.0.0.1`, or the other way\nround, whichever Nexi runs on), and the **NexCore** link in the helper points at that same host. Sign in there,\ncome back to this tab: the first dot turns green by itself (the helper re-checks when you return, and every few\nseconds until it sees you). **Check my sign-in** forces a check and stamps the time it ran."},"638":{"id":"/docs/api-9","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#try-it-in-three-moves","content":"Being signed in is enough. The Chat, Tasks, Graph and BI APIs want a five-minute bearer token rather than the cookie, so the\nmoment you press **Send** on any playground whose *Authorization* field is still the empty `Bearer ` — or holds a\ntoken the portal minted that has since expired — the portal exchanges your NexCore sign-in for a fresh assertion\n(the same one NexCore mints for its own front-end) and puts it in the header. The token lives in your browser\nonly; nothing leaves it except the request you send, and the portal keeps no copy. A value you paste into the\nfield yourself is never touched. (The field you just sent from may still read `Bearer ` — the token went with the\nrequest all the same; every other playground you open now shows it pre-filled.)"},"639":{"id":"/docs/api-10","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#try-it-in-three-moves","content":"The second line of the helper shows the current token and its countdown. **Get my token now** mints one before\nyou send anything — handy when you want the header for curl or Postman (**Copy header**). Every other way to get\nand pass it is on Authenticate your API calls."},"640":{"id":"/docs/api-11","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#try-it-in-three-moves","content":"Open Chat API › Projects, find **List projects**, press **Send**. You get the Projects\n*you* may see — the same list as the sidebar in NexChat. Then try one you should not: paste a Project id from\nanother organization into **Get project** and read the `404` — that is the outer wall."},"641":{"id":"/docs/api-12","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"Five APIs, one sign-in. Which credential each one reads — and how to pass it in the playground, curl or code — is\non Authenticate your API calls."},"642":{"id":"/docs/api-13","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"API"},"643":{"id":"/docs/api-14","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"Who authenticates you"},"644":{"id":"/docs/api-15","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"Base path"},"645":{"id":"/docs/api-16","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"Typical use"},"646":{"id":"/docs/api-17","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"Chat API"},"647":{"id":"/docs/api-18","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"`Authorization: Bearer <assertion>`"},"648":{"id":"/docs/api-19","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"`/api/v1/chat/…`"},"649":{"id":"/docs/api-20","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"Projects, threads, messages, agents, skills, flows, runs"},"650":{"id":"/docs/api-21","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"Platform API"},"651":{"id":"/docs/api-22","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"your NexCore session cookie (the bearer is accepted but not needed)"},"652":{"id":"/docs/api-23","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"`/api/v1/…`"},"653":{"id":"/docs/api-24","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"Blueprints, packs, tools, models, connections, credentials"},"654":{"id":"/docs/api-25","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"Tasks API"},"655":{"id":"/docs/api-26","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"`Authorization: Bearer <assertion>`"},"656":{"id":"/docs/api-27","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"`/api/v1/tasks/…`"},"657":{"id":"/docs/api-28","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"Work projects, items, boards, iterations, milestones, references (VibeBan); approval requests and decisions"},"658":{"id":"/docs/api-29","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"Graph API"},"659":{"id":"/docs/api-30","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"`Authorization: Bearer <assertion>`"},"660":{"id":"/docs/api-31","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"`/api/v1/graph/…`"},"661":{"id":"/docs/api-32","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"Sources, pipeline runs, the graph, evidence, claim review, vocabulary, evidence bundles"},"662":{"id":"/docs/api-33","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"BI API"},"663":{"id":"/docs/api-34","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"`Authorization: Bearer <assertion>`"},"664":{"id":"/docs/api-35","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"`/api/v1/bi/…`"},"665":{"id":"/docs/api-36","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-you-are-calling","content":"Datasets, the semantic model, metrics, governed queries, dashboards, templates and plans, automations"},"666":{"id":"/docs/api-37","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#module-apis--not-in-this-reference-yet","content":"The three modules have their own APIs — **Map API** (`/api/v1/map/…`, :3207), **Care API** (`/api/v1/care/…` and the\npublic edge `/api/v1/care/public/v1/…`, :3208) and **Forge API** (`/api/v1/forge/…`, :3209) — behind the same\nassertion, plus the module gate. Their contracts are JSON Schemas in `packages/contracts/schemas/v1/` (`map-*`,\n`care-*`, `forge-*`, `guardrail-*`); **no OpenAPI file is committed for them yet** (ADR-0051 §4, ADR-0054, ADR-0057\nname the files and defer them), so this reference does not generate pages for them — it would otherwise be\ndescribing an API from memory. Until the files land, each API serves its own FastAPI `/docs` on the dev stack, and the\noperation lists are written out in NexMap, NexCare and\nNexForge. NexChat's voice doors (`/chat/voice/transcriptions`, `/chat/voice/speech`,\n`/chat/voice/files`) and the web-search port (`/synapse/web-search/*`) are in the Chat and Platform contracts and\nappear in those references."},"667":{"id":"/docs/api-38","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#module-apis--not-in-this-reference-yet","content":"The **server** menu at the top of each playground has two entries. *Through this portal* is the default and needs no\nconfiguration. *A Nexi deployment directly* sends the request from your browser to the origin you type — that\ndeployment must list this portal in its `CORS_ORIGINS`, otherwise the browser refuses before Nexi answers."},"668":{"id":"/docs/api-39","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"Status"},"669":{"id":"/docs/api-40","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"Meaning"},"670":{"id":"/docs/api-41","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"What to do"},"671":{"id":"/docs/api-42","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"`200` / `201` / `202`"},"672":{"id":"/docs/api-43","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"Done. `202` means *accepted, running* — a run id comes back, poll it."},"673":{"id":"/docs/api-44","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"—"},"674":{"id":"/docs/api-45","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"`401` `UNAUTHENTICATED` / `SESSION_REQUIRED`"},"675":{"id":"/docs/api-46","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"No valid session, or the token in the field is not one the portal can refresh."},"676":{"id":"/docs/api-47","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"Sign in to NexCore on this host (the helper's first dot must be green); if you pasted a token by hand, clear the field back to `Bearer ` and send again."},"677":{"id":"/docs/api-48","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"`403` `FORBIDDEN`"},"678":{"id":"/docs/api-49","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"Nexi knows the resource exists and you may not do this to it."},"679":{"id":"/docs/api-50","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"Ask for the relation the operation needs — see roles and relations."},"680":{"id":"/docs/api-51","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"`404` `NOT_FOUND`"},"681":{"id":"/docs/api-52","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"Either it does not exist or it is not in your organization — the answer is the same on purpose."},"682":{"id":"/docs/api-53","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"Check the id and your organization."},"683":{"id":"/docs/api-54","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"`409`"},"684":{"id":"/docs/api-55","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"State conflict — a name already taken, a run already finished, a version behind."},"685":{"id":"/docs/api-56","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"Read the `error_code`, reload the resource."},"686":{"id":"/docs/api-57","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"`422` `SCHEMA_VALIDATION`"},"687":{"id":"/docs/api-58","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"The body did not match the contract."},"688":{"id":"/docs/api-59","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"The *Body* panel shows every field; required ones are marked."},"689":{"id":"/docs/api-60","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"`502` `PORTAL_PROXY_UNREACHABLE`"},"690":{"id":"/docs/api-61","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"The portal could not reach Nexi."},"691":{"id":"/docs/api-62","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"Start the stack, or point the portal at your deployment with `NEXUS_API_ORIGIN` (and `NEXUS_GRAPH_ORIGIN` for `/api/v1/graph`, `NEXUS_BI_ORIGIN` for `/api/v1/bi` — NexGraph's and NexBI's origins serve those)."},"692":{"id":"/docs/api-63","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"Every error body carries a `correlation_id`. Administrators find the request in **NexCore › Audit** by that id —\nsee Read the audit trail of a run."},"693":{"id":"/docs/api-64","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-the-answers-mean","content":"On the **fixture (E2E) stack** the Tasks API answers `401 UNAUTHENTICATED` to every person, token or not: that\nstack does not start the key feed tasks-api needs to verify a human's assertion (a known platform gap, being fixed\nby the NexTasks team). Try the Tasks API against the development stack or a real deployment."},"694":{"id":"/docs/api-65","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-is-not-here","content":"**Service-to-service operations** — the Policy Enforcement Point check, creating and consuming approval\nrequests, the model gateway's inference calls, the OAuth callback, the BI and Graph *tool doors* agents call\nthrough chat-api, decision-outcome write-backs. They are called by Nexi services, never by a client, and are\nleft out of the public reference."},"695":{"id":"/docs/api-66","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-is-not-here","content":"**Doors that exist in a contract but are not served yet** — the BI *Insights* operations (the Insights screen is a\nprototype; its statistical engine is planned) and the VibeBan *automation* rules. They appear here the day they\nare served."},"696":{"id":"/docs/api-67","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-is-not-here","content":"**The organization and identity API** (sign-up, invitations, join requests, sessions) is served by NexCore but has\nno published contract yet; the user guide shows every call it makes. It will appear here once the contract ships."},"697":{"id":"/docs/api-68","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#what-is-not-here","content":"**Events (AsyncAPI)** — later."},"698":{"id":"/docs/api-69","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#running-the-portal-against-your-own-nexi","content":"The portal's server forwards `/api/v1/*` to one origin — by default the local NexCore dev stack\n(`http://127.0.0.1:3212`). Point it elsewhere with an environment variable:"},"699":{"id":"/docs/api-70","page_id":"/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api#running-the-portal-against-your-own-nexi","content":"Set `NEXUS_API_ORIGIN=off` to publish the docs without any forwarding; the playground then works only with the\n*deployment directly* server and a `CORS_ORIGINS` grant on that deployment."},"700":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","type":"page","content":"Authenticate your API calls","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/authentication"},"701":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-0","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication","content":"How Nexi knows who is calling — the session cookie, the five-minute bearer token, where to get it and how to pass it in the playground, in curl and in code."},"702":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-1","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/authentication#two-credentials-one-sign-in","content":"Two credentials, one sign-in"},"703":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-2","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/authentication#get-a-token","content":"Get a token"},"704":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-3","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/authentication#1--from-this-portal-recommended-for-the-playground","content":"1 · From this portal (recommended for the playground)"},"705":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-4","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/authentication#2--from-nexcore-by-hand","content":"2 · From NexCore, by hand"},"706":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-5","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/authentication#3--from-a-script-with-the-cookie","content":"3 · From a script, with the cookie"},"707":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-6","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/authentication#pass-the-token","content":"Pass the token"},"708":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-7","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/authentication#in-the-playground","content":"In the playground"},"709":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-8","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/authentication#in-curl","content":"In curl"},"710":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-9","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/authentication#in-javascript","content":"In JavaScript"},"711":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-10","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/authentication#in-python","content":"In Python"},"712":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-11","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"When it fails"},"713":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-12","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/authentication#service-accounts-and-api-clients","content":"Service accounts and API clients"},"714":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-13","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication","content":"Nexi never takes a password over the API. You sign in **once, in NexCore**, and everything else derives from that\nsession — in the browser, in the playground on these pages, in a script."},"715":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-14","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#two-credentials-one-sign-in","content":"Credential"},"716":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-15","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#two-credentials-one-sign-in","content":"What it is"},"717":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-16","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#two-credentials-one-sign-in","content":"Who accepts it"},"718":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-17","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#two-credentials-one-sign-in","content":"Lifetime"},"719":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-18","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#two-credentials-one-sign-in","content":"**Session cookie** `nexus_session`"},"720":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-19","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#two-credentials-one-sign-in","content":"Set by NexCore when you sign in. `HttpOnly`, same-site — your browser sends it, you never see it."},"721":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-20","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#two-credentials-one-sign-in","content":"**Platform API** (`/api/v1/…` served by NexCore)"},"722":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-21","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#two-credentials-one-sign-in","content":"Your session (hours; revoked from *Account › Sessions*)"},"723":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-22","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#two-credentials-one-sign-in","content":"**Session assertion** (bearer token)"},"724":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-23","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#two-credentials-one-sign-in","content":"A signed statement &#x2A;\"this is the person behind session X, valid until T\"*. NexCore mints it from your cookie on request."},"725":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-24","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#two-credentials-one-sign-in","content":"**Chat API** (`/api/v1/chat/…`), **Tasks API** (`/api/v1/tasks/…`) and **Graph API** (`/api/v1/graph/…`)"},"726":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-25","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#two-credentials-one-sign-in","content":"**5 minutes**, then mint a new one"},"727":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-26","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#two-credentials-one-sign-in","content":"The assertion carries *who you are* — never *what you may do*. Every call is still checked against your\norganization, clearance, Project relations and purpose (how access is decided).\nA valid token with no relation to a Project still gets `403` or `404`."},"728":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-27","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#1--from-this-portal-recommended-for-the-playground","content":"In the playground you do nothing: while you are signed in to NexCore, the portal calls `/api/v1/session/assertion`\non your behalf the moment a request needs it — when the *Authorization* field is still the empty `Bearer `, or holds\na portal-minted token that has expired — and stores `Bearer …` where every playground reads that field. To hold the\ntoken in your hand, press **Get my token now** below: **Copy header** puts the value on your clipboard for curl or\nPostman, and the countdown shows how long it lives (**Refresh token** for a new one)."},"729":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-28","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#2--from-nexcore-by-hand","content":"Signed in to NexCore, open this address in the same browser (replace the host with yours):"},"730":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-29","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#2--from-nexcore-by-hand","content":"You get a JSON document; the token is the `assertion` value:"},"731":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-30","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#2--from-nexcore-by-hand","content":"`GET /api/v1/session/assertion` is what NexCore's own front-end calls, but it is not yet part of the published\nPlatform contract, so it has no page in this reference. Its shape is the JSON above; it will appear here as soon\nas the contract lists it."},"732":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-31","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#3--from-a-script-with-the-cookie","content":"If you already hold a session cookie (for example exported from your browser's developer tools), exchange it for a\ntoken exactly as the NexCore front-end does:"},"733":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-32","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#3--from-a-script-with-the-cookie","content":"Treat the cookie like a password: it *is* your session. Never paste it into a page, a chat, or a ticket."},"734":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-33","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#in-the-playground","content":"Every operation on the reference pages has an **Authorization** row under the request line. Expand it and paste the\nvalue in the form the header takes — the word `Bearer`, a space, the token:"},"735":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-34","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#in-the-playground","content":"The field is remembered in this browser for all playgrounds until you clear it (the **Forget** button above, or the\nbrowser's site data). The **cURL / JavaScript / Python / Go / Java / C# / Rust** tabs next to each operation show\nthe exact request including the header you set — copy them into your tool of choice."},"736":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-35","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#in-the-playground","content":"Platform API operations accept your **cookie** through the portal, so the Authorization row may stay empty there;\nfilling it does no harm."},"737":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-36","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"You get"},"738":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-37","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"Why"},"739":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-38","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"Do"},"740":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-39","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"`401` `UNAUTHENTICATED` on Chat/Tasks"},"741":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-40","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"No header, malformed header (`Bearer` missing), or the token is older than five minutes."},"742":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-41","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"Mint a new token; send `Authorization: Bearer <token>` exactly."},"743":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-42","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"`401` `SESSION_REQUIRED` on Platform"},"744":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-43","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"No `nexus_session` cookie reached NexCore — you are signed in on another host name, or in another browser."},"745":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-44","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"Sign in to NexCore on the **same host** as the docs (`127.0.0.1` ≠ `localhost`); check again."},"746":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-45","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"`401` `SESSION_REVOKED`"},"747":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-46","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"You signed out or revoked this session in *Account › Sessions*."},"748":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-47","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"Sign in again."},"749":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-48","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"`403` `FORBIDDEN`"},"750":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-49","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"You are known — and not allowed this action on this resource."},"751":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-50","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"Not an authentication problem: see roles and relations."},"752":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-51","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"`404` on something that exists"},"753":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-52","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"It lives in another organization."},"754":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-53","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#when-it-fails","content":"Same answer as \"does not exist\", on purpose."},"755":{"id":"/docs/api/authentication-54","page_id":"/docs/api/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/authentication#service-accounts-and-api-clients","content":"Long-running integrations should not borrow a person's session. Nexi distinguishes **service identities** from\npeople: a service token names a service, not a user, and the server decides what a service may do from that type\n(for example, only services create approval requests; a person can only decide them). Today service tokens are\nissued for the platform's own services; **self-service API clients for your organization are not available yet** —\nwhen they ship, they will appear in *NexCore › Access & Policies* and on this page. Until then, automate through\nFlows and webhooks, which run as the Flow's publisher under\nthe Project's rules, with no token to keep."},"756":{"id":"/docs/api/bi/automations","page_id":"/docs/api/bi/automations","type":"page","content":"Automations","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","BI API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/bi/automations"},"757":{"id":"/docs/api/bi/automations-0","page_id":"/docs/api/bi/automations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/bi/automations","content":"Refresh, metric alert and subscription — each one is your Draft Flow in NexChat Flow Studio; bi-api mirrors it."},"758":{"id":"/docs/api/bi/automations-1","page_id":"/docs/api/bi/automations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/bi/automations#list-automations","content":"List automations"},"759":{"id":"/docs/api/bi/automations-2","page_id":"/docs/api/bi/automations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/bi/automations#create-automation","content":"Create automation"},"760":{"id":"/docs/api/bi/automations-3","page_id":"/docs/api/bi/automations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/bi/automations#set-refresh-binding