 logs"},"1288":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-6","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#get-processing-profile","content":"Get processing profile"},"1289":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-7","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#delete-processing-profile-draft","content":"Delete processing profile draft"},"1290":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-8","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#put-processing-profile-draft","content":"Put processing profile draft"},"1291":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-9","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#activate-processing-profile","content":"Activate processing profile"},"1292":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-10","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#list-runs-all","content":"List runs all"},"1293":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-11","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#get-run-all","content":"Get run all"},"1294":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-12","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#get-run-logs-all","content":"Get run logs all"},"1295":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-13","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#list-runs","content":"Pipeline runs (query: binding_id, status, since, cursor). Administrators without a Project relation see ids, stages and statuses — no titles."},"1296":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-14","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#get-run","content":"One run with stages, coverage and engine logs (closed codes, never document text)."},"1297":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-15","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#retry-run","content":"Retry the failed stage (body: stage). Re-materialises that asset partition only; reuse key prevents duplicates. 409 RUN_NOT_RETRYABLE."},"1298":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-16","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#pause-run","content":"Pause after the current asset."},"1299":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-17","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#get-run-logs","content":"Engine log lines (query: level, stage, cursor)."},"1300":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-18","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#get-processing-profile","content":"1.47.0: the Project's processing configuration — `active` (the platform default `prf_default@2` with runs_pinned when none was activated), `draft` (null when none) and `defaults`. Every member reads."},"1301":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-19","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#delete-processing-profile-draft","content":"1.47.0: discard the draft (owner/editor, 204; no draft → 404)."},"1302":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-20","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#put-processing-profile-draft","content":"1.47.0: create or replace the draft (owner/editor). Values outside the ranges or an unknown entity label → 422 PROFILE_INVALID. A draft changes nothing until the owner activates it."},"1303":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-21","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#activate-processing-profile","content":"1.47.0 (AC-946): the Project **owner** makes the draft the active profile — version `prf_<project>@N+1`, the previous active retired, `nexus.graph.processing_profile.activated.v1`. New SourceVersions pin the new version; every existing run keeps its own (a retry reproduces). No draft → 409 NO_DRAFT. Editors → 403 NOT_OWNER."},"1304":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-22","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#list-runs-all","content":"additive — the **All knowledge** view ( `project_plus_org`, c): no Project in the path = every Project the caller holds a relation on (the PEP's set, never a client list) plus the platform's `base` tier. Read-only; edits stay on the Project routes. Runs across the caller's Projects (query: binding_id, status, limit)."},"1305":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-23","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#get-run-all","content":"additive — the **All knowledge** view ( `project_plus_org`, c): no Project in the path = every Project the caller holds a relation on (the PEP's set, never a client list) plus the platform's `base` tier. Read-only; edits stay on the Project routes. One run of any of the caller's Projects."},"1306":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline-24","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/pipeline#get-run-logs-all","content":"additive — the **All knowledge** view ( `project_plus_org`, c): no Project in the path = every Project the caller holds a relation on (the PEP's set, never a client list) plus the platform's `base` tier. Read-only; edits stay on the Project routes. Engine log lines (query: level, stage)."},"1307":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/resolve","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/resolve","type":"page","content":"Evidence bundles","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Graph API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/resolve"},"1308":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/resolve-0","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/resolve","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/resolve","content":"What an answer in NexChat was grounded in — re-read a bundle you were shown."},"1309":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/resolve-1","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/resolve","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/resolve#get-evidence-bundle","content":"Get evidence bundle"},"1310":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/resolve-2","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/resolve","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/resolve#get-evidence-bundle","content":"Re-read a bundle for 'Why this answer?' — re-evaluates access at read time; items the caller may no longer read are removed and counted."},"1311":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","type":"page","content":"Review","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Graph API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/review"},"1312":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-0","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/review","content":"The verification queue; a curator's verdict within a named scope, a return for clarification, re-verification, entity merge proposals. Humans only."},"1313":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-1","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/review#list-review","content":"List review"},"1314":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-2","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/review#verify-claim","content":"Verify claim"},"1315":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-3","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/review#return-claim","content":"Return claim"},"1316":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-4","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/review#reverify-claim","content":"Reverify claim"},"1317":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-5","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/review#propose-entity-merge","content":"Propose entity merge"},"1318":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-6","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/review#list-merge-proposals","content":"List merge proposals"},"1319":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-7","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/review#decide-merge-proposal","content":"Decide merge proposal"},"1320":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-8","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/review#list-review","content":"The verification queue: proposed and contested claims/observations the caller may read (query: status, layer, cluster_id, cursor)."},"1321":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-9","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/review#verify-claim","content":"A HUMAN curator's verdict: creates an OracleRun {oracle.type=human_review, actor.kind=human} and moves the claim to verified|falsified; the verdict scope codes are mandatory. Agents and services get 403 AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN. Writes a curator_verdict GraphDecisionRecord. When the Blueprint requires it the decision is parked as a NexTasks approval and 202 is returned."},"1322":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-10","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/review#return-claim","content":"Return for clarification (closed reason_code + optional human note): status stays proposed/contested; the run's verification_request is answered; outcome written back to the proposing decision."},"1323":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-11","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/review#reverify-claim","content":"Re-run the deterministic oracle checks (arithmetic · transcription · schema · source_location · corroboration) for a claim in needs_reverification; the SERVICE oracle can never produce human_review. 202 with the run ref. 1.45.1 (4): a human owner/editor may ask for any claim that is not superseded — the claim enters needs_reverification (version +1), the event claim.reverification_required {trigger: manual} is published and a run from the oracle stage is queued (earlier stages skipped); the 202 body is the run with the updated claim under `claim`. 409 CLAIM_NOT_DECIDABLE for superseded / base-tier claims."},"1324":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-12","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/review#propose-entity-merge","content":"Propose merge/split of identities (body: other_ref, op). A proposal, never an immediate merge; the decision is a curator action recorded as entity_resolution decision data."},"1325":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-13","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/review#list-merge-proposals","content":"1.45.0 (AC-919): the Project's entity merge proposals, open first (query: status). Each carries its score, the conflicting attributes and the decision that proposed it. 1.45.1: each row also carries the two identities as they are now (`entity` · `other`) for the twin view."},"1326":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/review-14","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/review#decide-merge-proposal","content":"1.45.0: a curator decides — merge (the entity is absorbed: labels become aliases, mentions re-pointed, both rows keep merge_history), reject (the pair is never proposed again), undo (an accepted merge is reversed from the history). Human owner/editor only; a decision on a closed proposal is 409 PROPOSAL_NOT_OPEN."},"1327":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"page","content":"Sources","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Graph API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources"},"1328":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-0","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources","content":"Bindings of a Project (upload, server folder, Google Drive), grants, uploads and pinned source versions."},"1329":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-1","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#list-bindings","content":"List bindings"},"1330":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-2","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#create-binding","content":"Create binding"},"1331":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-3","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#pause-binding","content":"Pause binding"},"1332":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-4","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#resume-binding","content":"Resume binding"},"1333":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-5","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#update-binding-schedule","content":"Update binding schedule"},"1334":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-6","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#request-binding-sync","content":"Request binding sync"},"1335":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-7","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#revoke-binding","content":"Revoke binding"},"1336":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-8","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#share-binding","content":"Share binding"},"1337":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-9","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#get-binding","content":"Get binding"},"1338":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-10","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#delete-binding","content":"Delete binding"},"1339":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-11","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#get-grant","content":"Get grant"},"1340":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-12","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#revoke-grant","content":"Revoke grant"},"1341":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-13","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#upload-source","content":"Upload source"},"1342":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-14","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#list-source-versions","content":"List source versions"},"1343":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-15","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#get-version-diff","content":"Get version diff"},"1344":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-16","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#list-bindings-all","content":"List bindings all"},"1345":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-17","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#get-binding-all","content":"Get binding all"},"1346":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-18","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#list-source-versions-all","content":"List source versions all"},"1347":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-19","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#get-source-version-all","content":"Get source version all"},"1348":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-20","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#list-bindings","content":"Sources registry rows with five states each. Administrators without a Project relation see binding ids, kinds, states and lags — no titles."},"1349":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-21","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#create-binding","content":"Add-source (1.66.0 kind=web —: scope_rules carries start_urls · allow_hosts (confirmed by the person) · follow_links · max_depth · max_pages_per_run · goal; refusals 422 WEB_START_URL_REQUIRED / WEB_HOST_NOT_ALLOWED (a start URL outside allow_hosts) / WEB_URL_INVALID (an IP literal, a private host, a non-http scheme) / SCHEDULE_TOO_FREQUENT). The first sync is due at once; the worker publishes nexus.graph.binding.sync.requested.v1 and the Project's web_source Flow runs. Add-source wizard step 4. Body carries a Synapse connection_ref — never a credential; a missing OAuth consent returns 409 CONNECTION_NEEDS_AUTH with the ConnectionRequest ref to resume the wizard at step 2. Creates the BackgroundExecutionGrant when mode=continuous and emits binding.created.v1 + run.requested.v1."},"1350":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-22","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#pause-binding","content":"Pause NEW runs — a running job finishes its current asset. Emits binding.paused.v1."},"1351":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-23","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#resume-binding","content":"Resume; re-evaluates the grant (expired → 409 GRANT_EXPIRED, re-create explicitly)."},"1352":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-24","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#update-binding-schedule","content":"1.66.0 ( A1.3, -3): change when a continuous source is looked at again — cadence (SyncCadence), cron for custom, timezone. Owner / editor humans; a viewer needs an editor (403 NOT_EDITOR); agents and services are refused (403 AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN). A cadence tighter than the Blueprint ceiling → 422 SCHEDULE_TOO_FREQUENT; a `once` binding → 409 BINDING_NOT_CONTINUOUS. Audited graph.binding.schedule.changed; one binding_schedule decision (arms = the cadences, human_explicit)."},"1353":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-25","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#request-binding-sync","content":"1.66.0 ( A1.3): *Check now* — make a continuous binding due at once; the worker's next tick claims it (a web binding's claim publishes nexus.graph.binding.sync.requested.v1 and the Project's web_source Flow runs). binding.resume-class rights; a paused binding → 409 BINDING_PAUSED."},"1354":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-26","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#revoke-binding","content":"Revoke the binding and its grant: serving of derived knowledge stops in the same transaction (deny known → served = 0), indexes/claims/captures are cleaned by the retention asset afterwards (989). Emits binding.revoked.v1."},"1355":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-27","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#share-binding","content":"1.152.0 ( A4): the owner shares the source with the whole organization (`tier: organization`) or takes it back (`project`). The binding, its versions and their Lexical records (items · chunks · page renders · embeddings · datasets) move to the tier; the origin project_id stays; entities and claims remain the origin Project's. Owner-only; operable from the origin Project alone (404 elsewhere). Emits binding.shared.v1. Idempotent."},"1356":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-28","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#get-binding","content":"One binding with states, lags, grant and allowed_actions."},"1357":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-29","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#delete-binding","content":"1.80.0 (c, A2.2 ¶3): delete a *revoked* binding — the second step, never the first. Human owner only; 409 BINDING_NOT_REVOKED unless revoked, 409 ALREADY_DELETED once. Writes a `binding_delete` DecisionRecord (arms delete_now · keep_revoked, propensity 1.0, human_explicit; state features = versions · datasets · captures · claims · revocation age) and queues one `PipelineOrder(mode=purge)` per SourceVersion — the worker's purge asset exports decisions first, then detaches captures, empties datasets (rows_purged), withdraws claims, removes Silver/Bronze/vectors/AGE, tombstones the version (`deleted_at`), expires bundles and emits source_version.deleted.v1."},"1358":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-30","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#get-grant","content":"The BackgroundExecutionGrant of a continuous binding (budget, spent, expiry, status)."},"1359":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-31","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#revoke-grant","content":"Revoke only the grant: the binding stays, runs stop at the next protected operation."},"1360":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-32","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#upload-source","content":"Upload one file (multipart, ≤ limits.max_item_bytes, allow-listed MIME) into the Project's `upload` binding → Bronze blob → SourceVersion → run.requested.v1. 413 / 415 on refusal; the file is scanned as untrusted content. 1.60.0 (1): with `folder` + `relative_path` the file joins the folder's own upload binding (many files, one binding, relative paths kept); 422 SUBPATH_INVALID on an escaping / hidden path."},"1361":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-33","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#list-source-versions","content":"Versions of a source, newest first, with page manifests."},"1362":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-34","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#get-version-diff","content":"1.47.0 (AC-944): what changed between this SourceVersion and `against` (default: the version it supersedes, else the previous version_no of the same source; none → against_ref null and everything added). Computed from both versions' document items and claims — pages · sections · tables · figures · claims, added · removed · changed with item refs and bounded labels; never stored, never page text. PEP source_version.read on both versions; a version the actor may not see → 404."},"1363":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-35","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#list-bindings-all","content":"additive — the **All knowledge** view ( `project_plus_org`, c): no Project in the path = every Project the caller holds a relation on (the PEP's set, never a client list) plus the platform's `base` tier. Read-only; edits stay on the Project routes. Every row says which Project it belongs to (`project_id: null` = the platform's base tier)."},"1364":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-36","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#get-binding-all","content":"additive — the **All knowledge** view ( `project_plus_org`, c): no Project in the path = every Project the caller holds a relation on (the PEP's set, never a client list) plus the platform's `base` tier. Read-only; edits stay on the Project routes. One binding of any of the caller's Projects."},"1365":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-37","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#list-source-versions-all","content":"additive — the **All knowledge** view ( `project_plus_org`, c): no Project in the path = every Project the caller holds a relation on (the PEP's set, never a client list) plus the platform's `base` tier. Read-only; edits stay on the Project routes. Versions across the caller's Projects, newest first (query: binding_id)."},"1366":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/sources-38","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/sources#get-source-version-all","content":"additive — the **All knowledge** view ( `project_plus_org`, c): no Project in the path = every Project the caller holds a relation on (the PEP's set, never a client list) plus the platform's `base` tier. Read-only; edits stay on the Project routes. One version of any of the caller's Projects."},"1367":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"page","content":"Graph Studio","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Graph API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio"},"1368":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-0","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio","content":"The allowed subgraph: the landscape of groups, a group's members, one object and its neighbours, the searchable list."},"1369":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-1","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-landscape","content":"Get landscape"},"1370":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-2","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#list-cluster-members","content":"List cluster members"},"1371":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-3","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-nearby","content":"Get nearby"},"1372":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-4","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-entity-detail","content":"Get entity detail"},"1373":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-5","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#list-entity-mentions","content":"List entity mentions"},"1374":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-6","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-entity-neighbourhood","content":"Get entity neighbourhood"},"1375":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-7","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-relation-detail","content":"Get relation detail"},"1376":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-8","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#search-knowledge","content":"Search knowledge"},"1377":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-9","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-object","content":"Get object"},"1378":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-10","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-object-figure","content":"Get object figure"},"1379":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-11","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#list-objects","content":"List objects"},"1380":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-12","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#list-views","content":"List views"},"1381":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-13","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#create-view","content":"Create view"},"1382":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-14","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#delete-view","content":"Delete view"},"1383":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-15","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#update-view","content":"Update view"},"1384":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-16","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-landscape-all","content":"Get landscape all"},"1385":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-17","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-entity-detail-all","content":"Get entity detail all"},"1386":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-18","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#list-entity-mentions-all","content":"List entity mentions all"},"1387":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-19","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-entity-neighbourhood-all","content":"Get entity neighbourhood all"},"1388":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-20","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-relation-detail-all","content":"Get relation detail all"},"1389":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-21","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#search-knowledge-all","content":"Search knowledge all"},"1390":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-22","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-landscape","content":"Clusters + flows of the caller's ALLOWED objects for the scope (query: scope, tier, layer, q). Counts are computed after the PEP filter; truncation is reported with counts. Never the tenant graph."},"1391":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-23","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#list-cluster-members","content":"Paged members of a cluster (cursor, limit ≤ 100) — the Space 'Enter' page and the Lanes focus rows."},"1392":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-24","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-nearby","content":"One-hop neighbours grouped by NeighbourKind (query: kinds=sources,claims,entities,checks; limit per kind ≤ 50). Every hop is PEP-checked; a hidden intermediate node drops the path and is counted in `truncated`."},"1393":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-25","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-entity-detail","content":"1.75.0 (UX-R8 / C): everything a node can say about itself — facts + counts, the documents it was seen in with the best mention of each (Evidence Workspace), the claims about it, and how it was made (run · detect/resolve executors · score range · entity_resolution decision · merge history). Counts and lists respect the actor's clearance (995); no item text."},"1394":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-26","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#list-entity-mentions","content":"1.75.0: the mentions filed under an entity — stored surface · label · score · document · page · span, best first, ≤ 100 a page; `total` counts only versions below the actor's clearance."},"1395":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-27","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-entity-neighbourhood","content":"1.75.0 (UX-R8 b): the **complete** 1-hop of one entity, heaviest first, weights summed over documents — `total` · `shown` · `hidden` (neighbours the actor may not read: a count, never ids) · `cut`. The client draws this, never a neighbourhood inferred from a landscape page."},"1396":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-28","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-relation-detail","content":"1.75.0: what one edge is made of — the per-document rows behind an aggregated relation, either direction. A hidden end hides the edge (404); rows above the ceiling are not part of it."},"1397":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-29","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#search-knowledge","content":"1.75.0 (UX-R8): server-side search over the whole scope — entities by label / alias (own rows, then the base tier), documents by title, claims by title; ≤ 50 each; the ceiling applies to each list."},"1398":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-30","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-object","content":"The Inspector payload for any knowledge object by URI — one of Claim · NumericObservation · Entity · DocumentItem · SourceVersion · OracleRun · VocabularyTerm · KnowledgeCaptureRecord (discriminated by uri segment). 404 for hidden and for missing alike (no existence leak)."},"1399":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-31","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-object-figure","content":"1.44.0 (A1, d — PROPOSED): the bytes of a kind=figure DocumentItem (a platform screenshot of the docs bundle today, a Docling-extracted figure of an uploaded document next) with Content-Disposition: attachment and the sniffed image media type — the only way a figure leaves the store (: never a presigned or public URL; an EvidenceBundle carries the item ref + figure metadata, not a location). PEP object.read on the Project + clearance for the item's classification; the base tier is read through the platform tenant's unit of work ( b). 404 for hidden, missing and non-figure items alike. chat-api proxies this door for the browser (GET /chat/grounding/figures/{item_id}) with the actor's own assertion — no service-wide token."},"1400":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-32","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#list-objects","content":"The List twin / search (query: q, scope, tier, layer, status, kind, cluster_id, cursor, limit ≤ 100). Lexical + dense search over the allowed set; graph-api never returns objects the caller may not read."},"1401":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-33","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#list-views","content":"1.47.0: the Project's saved views — the author's first, then the others' — each a query + layout, never objects. Opening one is navigating to its query under the opener's PEP (AC-935)."},"1402":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-34","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#create-view","content":"1.47.0: save the current Studio state as a view of this Project. Any human member (viewers too — a view is a filter, not access); agents and services AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN. 422 when the title is empty or the query names more than the bounded ids."},"1403":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-35","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#delete-view","content":"1.47.0: the author deletes the view (204). Another member → 403 NOT_AUTHOR."},"1404":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-36","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#update-view","content":"1.47.0: the author replaces title · query · layout. Another member → 403 NOT_AUTHOR."},"1405":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-37","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-landscape-all","content":"additive — the **All knowledge** view ( `project_plus_org`, c): no Project in the path = every Project the caller holds a relation on (the PEP's set, never a client list) plus the platform's `base` tier. Read-only; edits stay on the Project routes. Source families keep their `project_id`; a concept several Projects' documents mention is one cluster with `project_id: null` and a flow from each family — how Projects show as related."},"1406":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-38","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#get-entity-detail-all","content":"1.75.0 (UX-R8 / C): everything a node can say about itself — facts + counts, the documents it was seen in with the best mention of each (Evidence Workspace), the claims about it, and how it was made (run · detect/resolve executors · score range · entity_resolution decision · merge history). Counts and lists respect the actor's clearance (995); no item text. All-knowledge twin: the actor's Projects (the PEP's set, never a client list) + the base tier."},"1407":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-39","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/studio#list-entity-mentions-all","content":"1.75.0: the mentions filed under an entity — stored surface · label · score · document · page · span, best first, ≤ 100 a page; `total` counts only versions below the actor's clearance. All-knowledge twin: the actor's Projects (the PEP's set, never a client list) + the base tier."},"1408":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/studio-40","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/studio","tags":[],"ty