ags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/system#health","content":"Health"},"1415":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/system-3","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/system#get-policy","content":"amendment: authz_mode (engine|embedded), bundle_ok, bundle_version, bundle_key_id, verified_at, staleness_allowed_s. Fails closed: with AUTHZ_MODE=engine and no valid bundle every other operation returns 503 POLICY_UNAVAILABLE."},"1416":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/system-4","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/system#health","content":"Process health. No business data. Also reports dagster_reachable and model roles bound (embedding, reranker, document_parser) as booleans."},"1417":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","type":"page","content":"Vocabulary","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Graph API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary"},"1418":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-0","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","content":"Terms in use and the ontology registry — managed terms, proposals, snapshots."},"1419":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-1","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#list-terms","content":"List terms"},"1420":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-2","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#list-terms-in-use","content":"List terms in use"},"1421":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-3","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#propose-term","content":"Propose term"},"1422":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-4","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#retire-term","content":"Retire term"},"1423":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-5","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#retire-all-terms","content":"Retire all terms"},"1424":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-6","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#restore-all-terms","content":"Restore all terms"},"1425":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-7","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#restore-term","content":"Restore term"},"1426":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-8","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#list-snapshots","content":"List snapshots"},"1427":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-9","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#publish-snapshot","content":"Publish snapshot"},"1428":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-10","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#list-terms-in-use-all","content":"List terms in use all"},"1429":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-11","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#list-terms","content":"Terms by level/tier/status with usage counts (query: level, tier, status, q, cursor). Base (L0) terms are read-only."},"1430":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-12","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#list-terms-in-use","content":"1.43.0 ( J): the vocabulary as terms *in use* — one row per resolved entity the Project's documents mention, most mentioned first, the platform's base tier after the Project's own rows; `types[]` is the rail. Not the ontology registry (listTerms, S4)."},"1431":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-13","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#propose-term","content":"Propose a new term or a merge (body: labels, type, extends_ref?, merge_of?). Creates an L1 candidate; nothing is published."},"1432":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-14","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#retire-term","content":"1.101.0 (e): the Project **owner** retires a type for this Project — L0 shipped or a stored L1/L2 term alike. An overlay, never a deletion: the entities of the type stay rows, but every read of the Project (in-use terms · landscape · search · neighbourhood) leaves them out and counts them as hidden; the type leaves `entity_label_choices` and the worker drops it from new runs' detector labels. Idempotent. `nexus.graph.vocabulary.type.retired.v1`."},"1433":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-15","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#retire-all-terms","content":"f: the Project **owner** retires every type of the chosen layers for this Project in one door — the owner's *remove all layers of ontology*. Default `levels: [L1, L2]` (candidates + published); `L0` only when named. The same reversible overlay as `retireTerm`, one control per type (types already retired are left as they are). `nexus.graph.vocabulary.type.retired.v1` per type, `bulk: true`."},"1434":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-16","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#restore-all-terms","content":"f: the Project **owner** lifts every type control of the Project — the reverse of `retireAllTerms`. `nexus.graph.vocabulary.type.restored.v1` per type, `bulk: true`."},"1435":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-17","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#restore-term","content":"1.101.0 (e): the Project **owner** restores a retired type — its entities are read again, the label is offered again. Idempotent. `nexus.graph.vocabulary.type.restored.v1`."},"1436":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-18","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#list-snapshots","content":"Published L2 snapshots, newest first."},"1437":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-19","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#publish-snapshot","content":"Publish an L2 snapshot (human action, Project owner; audited). 1.45.0: body names the L1 candidates to publish — they become published L2 terms, their merge_of terms deprecated; the snapshot carries content_hash and supersedes_ref. 422 NOTHING_TO_PUBLISH when no named term is a candidate."},"1438":{"id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary-20","page_id":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/graph/vocabulary#list-terms-in-use-all","content":"1.43.0 ( J): the All-knowledge twin of listTermsInUse — the actor's Projects (the PEP's set, never a client list) + the base tier."},"1439":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints","type":"page","content":"Blueprints","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Platform API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints"},"1440":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints-0","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints","content":"The effective ceilings a Project inherits from its organization."},"1441":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints-1","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints#list-blueprints","content":"List blueprints"},"1442":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints-2","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints#get-effective-blueprint","content":"Get effective blueprint"},"1443":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints-3","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints#get-blueprint","content":"Get blueprint"},"1444":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints-4","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints#publish-blueprint-layer","content":"Publish blueprint layer"},"1445":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints-5","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints#list-blueprints","content":"Blueprints visible to the caller's tenancy (base / domain / regulatory are platform-wide; organization / project are tenant-scoped)."},"1446":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints-6","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints#get-effective-blueprint","content":"Resolve the effective Blueprint for a tenancy (+ optional project) by merging layers — child layers only tighten allowlists / limits and may replace defaults. Deterministic; cached; invalidated by nexus.core.blueprint.published.v1. Fail closed (503) when the signed policy bundle referenced by any layer is missing in enterprise mode."},"1447":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints-7","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints#get-blueprint","content":"One layer as published (not merged)."},"1448":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints-8","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/blueprints#publish-blueprint-layer","content":"Create / replace an organization or project layer (admin; PepAction=administer). Base / domain / regulatory layers arrive only via signed packs. Validator rejects any loosening of the parent (tool allowlist grows, sandbox limit grows, cloud threshold rises, approval threshold rises)."},"1449":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/governance","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/governance","type":"page","content":"Governance","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Platform API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/governance"},"1450":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/governance-0","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/governance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/governance","content":"Records that wait for a human decision."},"1451":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/governance-1","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/governance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/governance#list-governance-records","content":"List governance records"},"1452":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/governance-2","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/governance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/governance#decide-governance","content":"Decide governance"},"1453":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/governance-3","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/governance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/governance#list-governance-records","content":"Current governance records of the tenant (chat-api overlay read; scope narrows, never widens)"},"1454":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/governance-4","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/governance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/governance#decide-governance","content":"Review / approve / block a NexChat definition (human NexCore admin; PEP `administer`; audited; emits `nexus.core.governance.decided.v1`)\n\n`target_uri` must be `nexus://agent/<id>`, `nexus://skill/<id>` or `nexus://workflow/<id>` in the caller's tenant.\n`blocked` sets `user_message_key` = `agent.blocked.governance` / `skill.blocked.governance` / `flow.blocked.governance`\nwhich chat-api surfaces on picker-hide and run-refusal. Non-human actors → 403."},"1455":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/packs","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/packs","type":"page","content":"Packs","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Platform API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/packs"},"1456":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/packs-0","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/packs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/packs","content":"Signed bundles of capabilities an organization installs."},"1457":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/packs-1","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/packs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/packs#list-packs","content":"List packs"},"1458":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/packs-2","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/packs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/packs#import-pack","content":"Import pack"},"1459":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/packs-3","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/packs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/packs#install-pack","content":"Install pack"},"1460":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/packs-4","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/packs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/packs#export-pack","content":"Export pack"},"1461":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/packs-5","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/packs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/packs#list-packs","content":"Installed and available packs with PackInstallStatus."},"1462":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/packs-6","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/packs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/packs#import-pack","content":"Upload a `.nexuspack` (multipart). Verifies ed25519 signature, digests, dependency ranges and `contains_secrets=false`; scans for secret patterns; runs the pack's evaluations in dry-run. Returns the manifest + required bindings — nothing is installed yet. PepAction=administer."},"1463":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/packs-7","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/packs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/packs#install-pack","content":"Install into the caller's tenancy — binds `requires.connections` to ToolConnections and `requires.models` to allowed model ids, stamps tenancy on templates / agents / skills, registers blueprint layer(s) as status=draft (admin publishes separately), applies pack migrations idempotently. Emits nexus.core.pack.installed.v1."},"1464":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/packs-8","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/packs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/packs#export-pack","content":"Export the organisation's intelligence / process layer as a signed `.nexuspack` — templates, agents, skills, tool definitions, policies, evaluations, sandbox profiles, UI config. Connections are replaced by `requires.connections`; tenancy and secrets are stripped and re-scanned before the archive is signed. PepAction=export."},"1465":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/registry","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/registry","type":"page","content":"App registry","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Platform API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/registry"},"1466":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/registry-0","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/registry","content":"Which applications this deployment ships."},"1467":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/registry-1","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/registry","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/registry#list-app-registry","content":"List app registry"},"1468":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/registry-2","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/registry#list-app-registry","content":"Suite apps for launcher (tenant-scoped)"},"1469":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/sandbox","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/sandbox","type":"page","content":"Sandbox","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Platform API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/sandbox"},"1470":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/sandbox-0","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/sandbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/sandbox","content":"Executions of model-generated code and their output."},"1471":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/sandbox-1","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/sandbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/sandbox#list-sandbox-profiles","content":"List sandbox profiles"},"1472":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/sandbox-2","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/sandbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/sandbox#get-effective-sandbox-profile","content":"Get effective sandbox profile"},"14