apse"},"1481":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-0","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","content":"Model Fabric — registered models, providers and evaluations."},"1482":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-1","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#list-models","content":"List models"},"1483":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-2","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#get-model-kpi","content":"Get model KPI"},"1484":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-3","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#get-model","content":"Get model"},"1485":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-4","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#list-model-providers","content":"List model providers"},"1486":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-5","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#check-model-provider-health","content":"Check model provider health"},"1487":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-6","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#list-model-invocations","content":"List model invocations"},"1488":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-7","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#list-tool-invocations","content":"List tool invocations"},"1489":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-8","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#get-tool-invocation","content":"Get tool invocation"},"1490":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-9","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#list-evaluation-suites","content":"List evaluation suites"},"1491":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-10","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#list-evaluation-runs","content":"List evaluation runs"},"1492":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-11","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#start-evaluation-run","content":"Start evaluation run"},"1493":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-12","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#get-evaluation-run","content":"Get evaluation run"},"1494":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-13","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#list-models","content":"ModelDefinitions the caller's tenancy may see (platform-wide + tenant-scoped), optionally narrowed to a role / classification"},"1495":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-14","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#get-model-kpi","content":"Frontier-avoidance KPI — share of invocations served by tier ≤ 3, per role; 1.36.0 adds the window's per-model usage and routing counts (NexCore Models posture)\n\nCore admin surface (`administer` on nexus://model/provider/_all). Successful invocations of the caller's organization only. With `window_h` every number is restricted to the trailing window; without it, since the first record. Counts and sums only — never prompt text, never a per-person breakdown."},"1496":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-15","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#list-model-providers","content":"ModelProviders with health (opaque refs only; NexCore admin projection)"},"1497":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-16","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#check-model-provider-health","content":"Probe the provider from inside the gateway (PEP `administer` on nexus://model/provider/<id>; audited). Returns the updated projection — never the probe response."},"1498":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-17","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#list-model-invocations","content":"Tenant-scoped ModelInvocation records, newest first (retention 90 days by default)\n\nAudit / metering projection — metadata only (role, operation, tier, model, provider, tokens, latency, routing,\nstatus); never prompt text, inputs or outputs. Filters combine with AND. `run_id` / `agent_id` accept the bare id\nor the full `nexus://agent/run/…` / `nexus://agent/…` URI. Records of other tenants are never listed."},"1499":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-18","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#list-tool-invocations","content":"Tenant-scoped ToolInvocation records, newest first \n\nTrace / audit projection — decision, status, connection, digests, duration, error code and user-message key;\nnever arguments, output or headers. Filters combine with AND. Records of other tenants are never listed (RLS)."},"1500":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-19","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#get-tool-invocation","content":"One ToolInvocation of the caller's tenancy"},"1501":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-20","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#list-evaluation-suites","content":"Evaluation suites shipped with the platform (role, operation, sample count, languages)"},"1502":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-21","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#list-evaluation-runs","content":"Tenant-scoped evaluation runs, newest first"},"1503":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-22","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#start-evaluation-run","content":"Run one suite against one model (Core administrators, humans only) and write its benchmark\n\nThe suite's role must be one of the model's roles (422 `MODEL_EVALUATION_ROLE_UNSUPPORTED`). `administer` on the\nmodel definition goes through the PDP — agents and services are refused (`AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN`). Samples run through\nthe ordinary Model Gateway pinned to the model under test; the model still has to be eligible for the administrator,\notherwise the run is `failed` with the model's own `MODEL_UNAVAILABLE_*` reason and nothing is written. A\n`succeeded` run persists `benchmarks[role] = score`, stamps `benchmarks_source = evaluation` /\n`benchmarks_evaluated_at` on the definition and records an audit entry `model_benchmark_written`. Runs execute\nsynchronously; sample inputs are never persisted with the run."},"1504":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-23","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse#get-evaluation-run","content":"One evaluation run (other tenants' runs are 404)"},"1505":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"page","content":"Integrations and connections","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Platform API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections"},"1506":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-0","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","content":"External systems Synapse can reach."},"1507":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-1","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#list-integrations","content":"List integrations"},"1508":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-2","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#register-integration","content":"Register integration"},"1509":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-3","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#get-integration","content":"Get integration"},"1510":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-4","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#list-knowledge-sources","content":"List knowledge sources"},"1511":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-5","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#admit-knowledge-source","content":"Admit knowledge source"},"1512":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-6","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#list-connections","content":"List connections"},"1513":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-7","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#create-connection","content":"Create connection"},"1514":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-8","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#get-connection","content":"Get connection"},"1515":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-9","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#revoke-connection","content":"Revoke connection"},"1516":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-10","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#get-connection-usage","content":"Get connection usage"},"1517":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-11","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#check-connection-health","content":"Check connection health"},"1518":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-12","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#connection-health-history","content":"Connection health history"},"1519":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-13","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#browse-connection","content":"Browse connection"},"1520":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-14","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#read-connection-content","content":"Read connection content"},"1521":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-15","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#download-connection-content","content":"Download connection content"},"1522":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-16","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#list-integrations","content":"Integration types (platform registry; refs only). `?capability=knowledge_source` (2) keeps only the definitions that declare the block."},"1523":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-17","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#register-integration","content":"Register / upgrade an integration type (human administrator; PEP `administer`; audited; `nexus.synapse.integration.registered.v1`). 1.20.0 — the Tool Builder's *create an integration from an import* step posts an IntegrationCreateRequest here (through the chat proxy, which adds the Project `builder` PEP); for a REST import `egress_hosts` MUST be confirmed by the human (`egress_hosts_confirmed: true`) and ⊆ the hosts the imported document's `servers[]` name — 422 EGRESS_HOST_UNCONFIRMED otherwise. `trusted_read` starts false. Agent / service principals → 403 AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN."},"1524":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-18","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#list-knowledge-sources","content":"The Connect list for the signed-in person: one row per knowledge-source integration with NexCore's state and the one action it allows (a Shared connection available to `project_id` first, then the person's own; `not_enabled` rows only for an administrator)."},"1525":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-19","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#admit-knowledge-source","content":"Service door (graph-api, `svc_graph_api`): may this integration be read as a knowledge source through this connection for this project by this person? Facts or one closed code — never a scope string."},"1526":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-20","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#list-connections","content":"`owner=me` — the caller's own user connections incl. expired/revoked (U8 Connected accounts); `workspace`; `service` (administrators only)"},"1527":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-21","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#create-connection","content":"Administrator creates a `workspace` / `service` connection with a `credential_ref` (never a value). `owner_kind=user` is refused (422)."},"1528":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-22","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#revoke-connection","content":"Revoke — owner of a `user` connection (U8 *Disconnect*: provider token revoke best effort + sealed row deleted) or administrator. Idempotent; `nexus.synapse.connection.revoked.v1`. 1.124.0 (c): the usage is read first — while any armed `schedule` flow depends on the connection the call answers 409 CONNECTION_IN_USE_SCHEDULED (details[] name the flows) unless `stop_scheduled=true`, which pauses those triggers (chat-api `trigger.paused`, reason connection_disconnected) and proceeds; 503 CONNECTION_USAGE_UNAVAILABLE while the flows edge does not answer. Governance `connection.disconnected` carries the counts."},"1529":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-23","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#get-connection-usage","content":"1.124.0 (c): what references the connection — flows (scheduled or not) and agents from chat-api, knowledge sources from graph-api, datasets from bi-api — aggregated over bearer service edges. Owner of a `user` connection or administrator; `unavailable[]` names the edges that did not answer."},"1530":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-24","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#check-connection-health","content":"On-demand probe (owner of a user connection or administrator). OAuth connections are probed through the token (refresh if due) before any endpoint."},"1531":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-25","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#browse-connection","content":"One folder of a connection as the signed-in person sees it (1b, the folder picker) — names and kinds, folders first, trashed items left out; never bytes, never a credential. The person's own `user` connection, or a Shared one available to `project_id`; a service principal is refused (403 SERVICE_NO_CREDENTIAL_ACCESS)."},"1532":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-26","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#read-connection-content","content":"Facts through a connection (listings, changes, permissions) — normalised JSON, never a credential. Service principals with `connection.read` only."},"1533":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections-27","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-connections#download-connection-content","content":"One item's bytes through a connection (`download`, Google-native documents exported via `export_mime`) — bounded by SYNAPSE_CONTENT_MAX_BYTES (413 beyond). Same checks and audit as `/read`."},"1534":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","type":"page","content":"Credentials and connection requests","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Platform API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials"},"1535":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-0","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","content":"Secrets the broker holds for you; you never see them again."},"1536":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-1","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#list-credentials","content":"List credentials"},"1537":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-2","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#create-credential","content":"Create credential"},"1538":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-3","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#get-credential","content":"Get credential"},"1539":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-4","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#delete-credential","content":"Delete credential"},"1540":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-5","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#list-my-connection-requests","content":"List my connection requests"},"1541":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-6","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#create-connection-request","content":"Create connection request"},"1542":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-7","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#get-connection-request","content":"Get connection request"},"1543":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-8","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#start-connection-request","content":"Start connection request"},"1544":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-9","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#decline-connection-request","content":"Decline connection request"},"1545":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-10","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#create-credential","content":"Write-only credential entry — the value is sent once, sealed by the broker; only the record comes back. PEP `credential_write` (humans; builders/admins; `owner_kind=workspace` only; 403 `BUILDER_SECRET_ENTRY_FORBIDDEN` when the Blueprint forbids builder entry)."},"1546":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-11","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#delete-credential","content":"Delete the sealed row (PEP `delete`; audited; `nexus.synapse.credential.deleted.v1`)"},"1547":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-12","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#create-connection-request","content":"Just-in-time access request — the card. Scopes := exactly what the named tools need minus what the user already granted. Already satisfied → `connected` at once; integration unavailable in the profile → `failed · OAUTH_UNAVAILABLE_IN_PROFILE` (card without a button)."},"1548":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-13","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#get-connection-request","content":"Requester only — anyone else gets 404"},"1549":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-14","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#start-connection-request","content":"*Connect …* — PEP `connection_authorise` (human · requester · pending/authorising · not expired). Returns the provider authorisation URL (state = HMAC, PKCE S256; scopes = requested ∪ already granted for incremental consent). `return_to` must be same-origin with SYNAPSE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_BASE (422 `OAUTH_RETURN_TO_NOT_ALLOWED`)."},"1550":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials-15","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/synapse-credentials#decline-connection-request","content":"*Not now* — the run ends with a plain explanation; the card stays usable later"},"1551":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","type":"page","content":"Tools","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Platform API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/tools"},"1552":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-0","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/tools","content":"Discover what a Project may use and try a tool before binding it."},"1553":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-1","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#list-tools","content":"List tools"},"1554":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-2","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#discover-tools","content":"Discover tools"},"1555":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-3","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#get-tool","content":"Get tool"},"1556":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-4","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#update-tool-mapping","content":"Update tool mapping"},"1557":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-5","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#try-tool","content":"Try tool"},"1558":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-6","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#enable-tool","content":"Enable tool"},"1559":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-7","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#list-tool-connections","content":"List tool connections"},"1560":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-8","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#create-tool-connection","content":"Create tool connection"},"1561":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-9","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#list-tool-collections","content":"List tool collections"},"1562":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-10","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#list-tool-invocations","content":"List tool invocations"},"1563":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-11","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#get-tool-invocation","content":"Get tool invocation"},"1564":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-12","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#list-tools","content":"ToolDefinitions visible to the caller's tenancy (platform tools are platform-wide; integration / custom tools are tenant-scoped)."},"1565":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-13","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#discover-tools","content":"Propose ToolDefinitions from an inline OpenAPI document, a registered MCP server (Synapse tools/list) or an existing integration.\n\nSide-effect operations (non-GET / MCP tools not marked read-only) are proposed with\n`enablement = disabled_pending_review` and `approval.mode = always`; read-only ones as `enabled`.\n`persist: true` registers the proposals; otherwise it is a dry run. Requires `administer` on the tenant.\n`openapi_url` (002) is fetched by NexCore through the Synapse egress pipeline:\nhost ∈ `target_integration_ref.egress_hosts`, private/loopback/link-local/metadata answers refused before\nconnecting, ≤ 3 re-validated redirects, 5 MiB / 10 s / JSON-or-YAML — anything else `422 OPENAPI_URL_*` with\naudit `synapse.import.rejected`. `integration_ref` alone registers the integration's declared capabilities\n(e.g. the Google Workspace P0 tools) as this tenant's definitions."},"1566":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-14","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#update-tool-mapping","content":"1.20.0 — the Tool Builder's *mapping* step. ONLY `display_name`, `description`, `input_hints` (ToolUpdateRequest); any other field → 422 TOOL_FIELD_IMMUTABLE — operation, side_effect, egress, enablement, approval, classification change only through discover / enable / governance. Humans with `administer` (or the chat proxy's Project `builder`); audited; a published tool keeps its uri and version bumps."},"1567":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-15","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#try-tool","content":"1.20.0 — a builder runs a READ-ONLY operation once to see what the tool returns (Tool Builder *Try it*). Humans only (403 AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN); PEP `execute` on the tool + `administer` on the tenant or the chat proxy's Project `builder`; a side-effect operation is refused 409 TRY_SIDE_EFFECT_REFUSED before any network; the call goes through the real adapter with InvokeContext bounds and the egress pipeline, records a ToolInvocation (purpose = try) and returns the output redacted to the caller's clearance. Nothing is stored for a model; a `disabled_pending_review` tool MAY be tried (that is the point), a `disabled` one may not (409 TOOL_DISABLED)."},"1568":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-16","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#enable-tool","content":"Governance — a human administrator enables a `disabled_pending_review` definition (or disables an enabled one).\n\nAgents and services can never call this (actor_type must be human; PEP `administer` on tool.definition). Emits nexus.core.tool.enabled.v1 and an audit record."},"1569":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-17","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#list-tool-connections","content":"Connections of a tool in the caller's tenancy (health + classification; never endpoint values)."},"1570":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-18","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#create-tool-connection","content":"Register a connection — endpoint_ref / credential_ref are references resolved by Synapse and the Credential Broker."},"1571":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-19","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#list-tool-invocations","content":"Tenant-scoped ToolInvocation records, newest first \n\nTrace / audit projection — decision, status, connection, digests, duration, error code and user-message key;\nnever arguments, output or headers. Filters combine with AND. Records of other tenants are never listed (RLS)."},"1572":{"id":"/docs/api/platform/tools-20","page_id":"/docs/api/platform/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/platform/tools#get-tool-invocation","content":"One ToolInvocation of the caller's tenancy"},"1573":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals","type":"page","content":"Approvals","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Tasks API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals"},"1574":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals-0","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals","content":"Requests a human must decide before a sensitive action runs."},"1575":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals-1","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals#list-approvals","content":"List approvals"},"1576":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals-2","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals#get-approval","content":"Get approval"},"1577":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals-3","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals#decide-approval","content":"Decide approval"},"1578":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals-4","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals#cancel-approval","content":"Cancel approval"},"1579":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals-5","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals#list-approvals","content":"Approvals visible to the actor — the inbox read model behind the thread card, the Studio run view and *Needs your decision*. PepAction=read: records where the actor is a decider or the `on_behalf_of` human (services: the tenant's); a record above the reader's clearance is left out (a `confidential` approval is invisible to an `internal` clearance). RLS on tenant_id — another tenant's records never appear. Newest first."},"1580":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals-6","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals#get-approval","content":"One ApprovalRequest (the card's source of truth; the browser polls it every 2 s while pending). PepAction=read: a human in `deciders.user_ids` or the `requested_by.on_behalf_of` human, with clearance ≥ the record's classification — otherwise 404, never 403 (no existence leak); other Project members see the card through chat-api's projection (tasks-api owns no Project membership). Service callers (core-api verifying an approval before it executes) read with their service token and see the un-redacted digest, never the raw arguments — those exist nowhere."},"1581":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals-7","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals#decide-approval","content":"Record the HUMAN decision (003/004; U3 — Approve primary / Reject secondary, no double confirm). PEP `approval_decide` per — human ∧ in `deciders.user_ids` ∧ pending ∧ not expired ∧ (not `requested_by.on_behalf_of` ∨ `deciders.allow_self_approval`) ∧ clearance covers the classification. Writes `decision {decision, decided_by, decided_at, comment}`, `status = approved | rejected`, one audit line, and emits `nexus.tasks.approval.completed.v1 {approval_uri, decision, decided_by, correlation_id}` after commit — the resume-router continues the run exactly once ( ≤ 5 s). Refusals — 403 `AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN` (agent or service principal — /02), 403 `NOT_DECIDER` (the card shows *Waiting for a Project owner*), 403 `SELF_APPROVAL`; 409 `APPROVAL_STATUS` (already decided / cancelled — a second decide changes nothing and emits nothing), 409 `APPROVAL_EXPIRED` (the sweep won; never auto-approved), 409 `NOT_ACTIONABLE` (subject `package_request` in S9)."},"1582":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals-8","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/tasks/approvals#cancel-approval","content":"Withdraw a pending approval — the requester service (the run was cancelled or its step failed for another reason) or the human `requested_by.on_behalf_of` (the user changed their mind). `status = cancelled`, no `decision`; emits `nexus.tasks.approval.completed.v1 decision=cancelled` so the parked step fails typed (`approval_cancelled`, category `cancelled`) instead of waiting for the sweep. Any other principal → 403; not pending → 409 `APPROVAL_STATUS`."},"1583":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/automation","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/automation","type":"page","content":"Automation","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Tasks API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/automation"},"1584":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/automation-0","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/tasks/automation","content":") AutomationBindings — a published Agent or Flow by URI with a closed trigger; run-now; derived tools are read from the target."},"1585":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/automation-1","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/automation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/automation#list-automation-targets","content":"List automation targets"},"1586":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/automation-2","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/automation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/automation#list-automation-runs","content":"List automation runs"},"1587":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/automation-3","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/tasks/automation#list-automation-targets","content":"The picker of the bind panel ( D): the published, unblocked Agents and Flows the CALLER may run for this scope — read through tasks-api's runtime port with the caller's own bearer, never stored, never the service's view. Bind-level access on the scope (`scope_ref`, REQUIRED)."},"1588":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/automation-4","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/tasks/automation#list-automation-runs","content":"The delivery log of a binding, newest first ( D): one row per (item, event) with the run ref chat-api gave and its mirrored status. Readable by whoever sees the scope."},"1589":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","type":"page","content":"Iterations","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","API reference","APIs","Tasks API"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations"},"1590":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-0","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","content":"Sprints of an Iterations project — plan, start, complete with dispositions, cancel."},"1591":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-1","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations#list-iterations","content":"List iterations"},"1592":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-2","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations#create-iteration","content":"Create iteration"},"1593":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-3","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations#get-iteration","content":"Get iteration"},"1594":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-4","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations#update-iteration","content":"Update iteration"},"1595":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-5","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations#add-iteration-items","content":"Add iteration items"},"1596":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-6","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations#remove-iteration-items","content":"Remove iteration items"},"1597":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-7","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations#start-iteration","content":"Start iteration"},"1598":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-8","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations#complete-iteration","content":"Complete iteration"},"1599":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-9","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations#cancel-iteration","content":"Cancel iteration"},"1600":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-10","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations#list-iteration-history","content":"List iteration history"},"1601":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-11","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations#list-iterations","content":"Iterations — Active · Planned · Past."},"1602":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-12","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations#create-iteration","content":"Plan an iteration (editor+). Emits `nexus.tasks.iteration.created.v1`."},"1603":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-13","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations#get-iteration","content":"One iteration with derived progress."},"1604":{"id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations-14","page_id":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/tasks/iterations#update-iteration","content":"Edit name · goal · dates (completed → owner-only aud