","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#what-you-get","content":"`:4222`"},"2300":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-48","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#what-you-get","content":"PostgreSQL 16 + Apache AGE + pgvector + PostGIS"},"2301":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-49","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#what-you-get","content":"Docker (`nexus/postgres`)"},"2302":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-50","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#what-you-get","content":"`127.0.0.1:5433` — databases `nexus_core · nexus_chat · nexus_tasks · nexus_graph · nexus_bi · nexus_map · nexus_care · nexus_forge · nexus_dagster · nexus_keycloak`"},"2303":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-51","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#what-you-get","content":"Embedding model · reranker"},"2304":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-52","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#what-you-get","content":"Ollama `:11434` · `llama-server --reranking :8081`"},"2305":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-53","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#what-you-get","content":"optional — step 6"},"2306":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-54","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#what-you-get","content":"Keycloak"},"2307":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-55","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#what-you-get","content":"Docker"},"2308":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-56","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#what-you-get","content":"admin console `http://127.0.0.1:3220/idp/admin/` (operators only)"},"2309":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-57","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#what-you-get","content":"Mailpit"},"2310":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-58","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#what-you-get","content":"Docker"},"2311":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-59","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#what-you-get","content":"inbox `http://127.0.0.1:8025` — every e-mail Keycloak sends lands here"},"2312":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-60","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"macOS or Linux; **Docker Desktop** (or Docker Engine) running."},"2313":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-61","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"**Node 22**, **Python 3.12**, `uv`."},"2314":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-62","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"`nats-server` on your PATH (`brew install nats-server`) — or skip it and set `JOB_BUS_DRIVER=postgres` in\n`apps/chat-api/.env` after the first start; the job bus then lives in Postgres."},"2315":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-63","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"A model provider — see step 4. Without one the stack starts, but every chat turn ends with *model unavailable*."},"2316":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-64","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"Disk: the knowledge pipeline's optional specialists (Docling, GLiNER-X) and the two small local models take about\n5 GB together — see step 6. Without them the pipeline runs with fixture parsers and a fixture embedder, enough to\nsee every screen but not to answer a real question."},"2317":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-65","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"The first run takes a few minutes: it creates a Python virtual environment per API with `uv`, copies each app's\n`.env.example` to `.env`, starts the three containers, creates the databases and roles (including `nexus_graph` with\nthe `age` and `vector` extensions, and `nexus_dagster` for the worker's own bookkeeping), runs every database\nmigration, then starts the processes in dependency order — core-api, chat-api and its worker, tasks-api, graph-api,\nbi-api, map-api, care-api and its worker, forge-api, the sandbox manager, the Dagster worker, the speech sidecars if\ninstalled, the eight web apps — and tails their logs. The module APIs start with their demo worlds on\n(`MAP_DEMO_WORLD=1`, `CARE_DEMO_WORLD=1`; Forge's is off) so the module chapters can be walked on a fresh\norganization; the packs still have to be installed in NexCore before a tile appears. On its first start with an\nadministrator it also runs the product-metrics measurement that seeds NexBI's platform dashboards.\nSubsequent runs take seconds. The script is idempotent: a `.env` you already have is never overwritten, only\ncompleted with keys a newer version needs."},"2318":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-66","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"Watch for the line that says the stack is up and lists the URLs. `Ctrl-C` stops everything the script started."},"2319":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-67","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"There is no seeded user and no default password. Open `http://127.0.0.1:3212/signup`, register with any e-mail\naddress, then open **Mailpit** at `http://127.0.0.1:8025` — the verification mail is there. Follow its link, sign\nin, and create your first organization. From here on the laptop behaves exactly like the product:\nYour first Project and conversation applies unchanged."},"2320":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-68","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"Sign-in on the laptop goes through the same Keycloak realm the packaged targets use. Google sign-in appears on the\npage only when you export `KEYCLOAK_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` and `KEYCLOAK_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` before `npm run stack`."},"2321":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-69","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"Each process also answers a health probe: `curl http://127.0.0.1:3200/api/v1/health` (core-api), `:3201` (chat-api),\n`:3204` (tasks-api), `:3205/api/v1/graph/health` (graph-api — its answer lists the drivers in use and whether Dagster\nis reachable), `:3206/api/v1/bi/health` (bi-api), `http://127.0.0.1:3203/health` (sandbox-manager). `npm run\nstack:status` also names the reranker when it is up. To fill VibeBan and NexBI with something to look at:\n`npm run vibeban:seed` creates the *NEXUS Platform* project from the platform's own documentation and the\n*Operations* triage board; the NexBI Logistics example in the guide is seeded by the documentation stack."},"2322":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-70","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"Nexi reaches every model through the Synapse Model Gateway; the laptop offers two ways to feed it."},"2323":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-71","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"**A cloud provider.** Put the key in `apps/core-api/.env` as `NEXUS_OPENAI_API_KEY=…` (or `NEXUS_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`)\nand restart the stack. The registry that ships with the stack (`config/synapse/models.yaml`, created from the\nexample on first start) references the key as `env://NEXUS_OPENAI_API_KEY` — the file holds a reference, never the\nkey, so it is safe to read and to commit. Never put a key into `models.yaml` itself: core-api refuses to start when\nit finds a literal secret there."},"2324":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-72","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"**A local model, no internet.** Start llama.cpp with the bundled helper, then start the stack in the disconnected\nprofile:"},"2325":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-73","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"`scripts/llama-server.sh --check` tells you whether the server answers. In this profile there is no cloud fallback:\nif the local server is down, every role refuses and the chat says so."},"2326":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-74","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"Whichever way you chose, confirm it in NexCore → **Models**: the provider shows *healthy*. The chapter\nRegister a model shows the screen."},"2327":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-75","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"You do not have to run the whole stack from one terminal. Each process has its own script and its own hot reload:"},"2328":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-76","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"Tests run per app and never touch your stack's databases: `npm run test:chat-api`, `npm run test:core-api`,\n`npm run test:tasks-api`, `npm run test:graph-api`, `npm run test:bi-api`, `npm run test:graph-worker`,\n`npm run test:chat`; the Postgres-backed variants (`test:*:pg`) use throw-away `*_test` databases on `:5433`."},"2329":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-77","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"NexGraph's pipeline needs three things a chat does not: a parser for documents, a detector for mentions, and an\nembedding model; an answer from the knowledge graph also wants a reranker. All of them run on the laptop, none\nleaves it, and each is optional — the stack detects what is installed and writes the choice into the worker's\n`.env` (`SPECIALISTS_DRIVER`, `EMBEDDER_DRIVER`) on every start."},"2330":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-78","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"The embedder and the reranker are ordinary entries in `config/synapse/models.yaml` (providers `local_ollama` and\n`local_llama_reranker`); the worker and graph-api reach them only through the Model Gateway, like every other model.\nWithout the specialists the worker parses with fixture parsers — the run page then names `fixture-parser@1` in\n*Processed by* instead of `docling@…`; without the embedder, *Ask the knowledge graph* finds nothing, because a\nfixture vector never matches a real question. The first real run downloads nothing: weights are read from the\nlocal caches only (`HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1`)."},"2331":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-79","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#before-you-start","content":"Then upload a document with a table in NexGraph and follow the run: Add a source\n→ Follow a pipeline run."},"2332":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-80","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"Path"},"2333":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-81","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"Per-app settings (never committed)"},"2334":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-82","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"`apps/core-api/.env` · `apps/chat-api/.env` · `apps/tasks-api/.env` · `apps/graph-api/.env` · `data-platform/dagster/nexus_graph_pipeline/.env`"},"2335":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-83","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"Model registry and connections (references only)"},"2336":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-84","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"`config/synapse/models.yaml` · `config/synapse/connections.yaml`"},"2337":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-85","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"Broker master key, session signing key (generated, git-ignored)"},"2338":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-86","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"`config/secrets/`"},"2339":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-87","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"Logs and pid files"},"2340":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-88","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"`.dev/logs/` · `.dev/pids/`"},"2341":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-89","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"NATS store, local model weights, Dagster home"},"2342":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-90","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"`.dev/nats/` · `.dev/models/` · `.dev/dagster/`"},"2343":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-91","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"Parser and detector weights (first use fills them)"},"2344":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-92","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"`~/.cache/huggingface` · `~/stanza_resources`"},"2345":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-93","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"Postgres data"},"2346":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-94","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#where-things-are","content":"Docker volume `nexus-pgdata`"},"2347":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-95","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#reset","content":"Then `npm run stack` again: migrations recreate the schema, Keycloak re-imports its realm, and `/signup` is waiting."},"2348":{"id":"/docs/deploy/local-96","page_id":"/docs/deploy/local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/local#reset","content":"Next rung: Docker Compose — the same processes as signed containers, one `.env`, one public port. What the processes are and why they are separated: How Nexi is built."},"2349":{"id":"/docs/deploy/operations","page_id":"/docs/deploy/operations","type":"page","content":"Operations","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Deploy","Run it"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/deploy/operations"},"2350":{"id":"/docs/deploy/operations-0","page_id":"/docs/deploy/operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deploy/operations","content":"Releases and where images come from, upgrades, the three tiers of secrets and how to rotate them, backups, health, hardening — and how to host this documentation next to your Nexi."},"2351":{"id":"/docs/deploy/operations-1","page_id":"/docs/deploy/operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deploy/operations#releases-and-where-images-come-from","content":"Releases and where images come from"},"2352":{"id":"/docs/deploy/operations-2","page_id":"/docs/deploy/operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deploy/operations#upgrades","content":"Upgrades"},"2353":{"id":"/docs/deploy/operations-3","page_id":"/docs/deploy/operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deploy/operations#secrets-three-tiers","content":"Secrets: three tiers"},"2354":{"id":"/docs/deploy/operations-4","page_id":"/docs/deploy/operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deploy/operations#rotation","content":"Rotation"},"2355":{"id":"/docs/deploy/operations-5","page_id":"/docs/deploy/operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url