page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"2980":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door#states","content":"States"},"2981":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"2982":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door","content":"**DS-6108** · `apps/sales/src/components/parts/NewLine.tsx#NewLine` · proposed"},"2983":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door","content":"*New account* / *New contact* open the `FormInspector` (DS-7002) with **NexChat's composer in its one-line start mode*&#x2A; first. The person writes what they know — &#x2A;\"Name, ЄДРПОУ or a website…\"&#x2A; / &#x2A;\"Name, phone or e-mail…\"* — and Enter or `↑` sorts it into the form **deterministically, without a model** (`lib/newLine.ts`: 8 · 10 · 12 digits → identifier, a domain → website, `+380…` / `0XX…` → phone, `@` → e-mail, the rest the name); the duplicate check answers on that line before the form is shown, so a twin is caught before a field is typed. *Start with an empty form* is the quiet exit (a link, never a second button). The composer is a `div` inside the Inspector's own form: `↑` is that form's submit, Enter asks it to submit; the footer's primary reads *Continue* on the line and *Create* on the form. One idiom for every record the suite creates ((1); NexForge's `/forge/new` and NexChat's *New flow* are the same door). Not a kit duplicate: the kit's composer is a chat turn, this is a record line; it is the promotion case for a `DS-3` *New … line* row once a third app uses it."},"2984":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door#in-the-workshop","content":"Also: written · contact · busy · in-the-inspector · in-the-inspector-form"},"2985":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door-7","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door#states","content":"`empty` · `written` · `contact` · `busy` · `in-the-inspector` · `in-the-inspector-form`"},"2986":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door-8","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/composer-line-door#accessibility","content":"the composer is a `group` labelled by its purpose; the input carries the same label; `↑` is a labelled submit, disabled until a word is written; the exit is a real button; the form that follows autofocuses its first field"},"2987":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/conversation-parts","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/conversation-parts","type":"page","content":"Conversation parts","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/conversation-parts"},"2988":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/conversation-parts-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/conversation-parts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/conversation-parts","content":"NexCare's conversation: the timeline (customer · agent · as