omponents/goal-card","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card","type":"page","content":"Goal card","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card"},"3098":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card","content":"The goal is the eighth executor on the same turn card with the goal's parts in its slots: the plan with Accept · Change · Not now, the latest result as the body with earlier result"},"3099":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3100":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card#states","content":"States"},"3101":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"3102":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card","content":"**DS-5002** · `apps/chat/src/components/thread/GoalCard.tsx#GoalCard` · adopted"},"3103":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card","content":"The goal is the eighth executor on the same turn card with the goal's parts in its slots: the plan with Accept · Change · Not now, the latest result as the body with earlier results folded beneath, the coverage line at completion, and the doors (view the plan · stop · pause · resume · open). The turn that opened the goal ends `done` while the goal continues; every later moment updates the same card — never a second card. The edges have no card of their own: a goal in another Project is not found exactly like any other not-found; an archived thread's card is read-only; a question to the running goal is prose in the thread. S8 adds two slots, no new card: the **Situation strip** above the plan — what NEXUS already holds about the subjects of the ask (NexSales · Vibeban · NexCare · artifacts · sources · the people on those records), each line a source word, the record's label and a door; one honest line naming the party when nothing was found; *not checked* for a source that did not answer; a record the person may not read is not a line and not a count — and the **Next line** at the proposal and at completion: 1–3 doors drawn only from found records, installed capabilities or the creation doors (*Create the account in NexSales* · *Add this request to Vibeban*), the colleague suggestion as a sentence then &#x2A;Ask ⟨name⟩*, and the one question &#x2A;What would you like me to do next?*. A drafted artefact's approval ask shows its security table (reads · writes · reaches) and the approval-required line when it reaches out."},"3104":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card#in-the-workshop","content":"Also: asked · working · waiting-on-you · waiting-on-other · done · stopped · failed · nothing-found · the-edges · reach-beyond-what-exists · did-we-check-our-own-system · the-authoring-harness"},"3105":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card-7","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card#states","content":"`asked` · `working` · `waiting_on_you` · `waiting_on_other` · `done` · `stopped` · `failed` · `nothing_found`"},"3106":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card-8","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/goal-card#accessibility","content":"as DS-5001; the plan's steps are a list, the decisions are buttons in Tab order; earlier results fold under a disclosure button with `aria-expanded`; the Situation strip is a list whose doors are links in Tab order; the Next line is one `nav` landmark labelled *Next*; the security table is a definition list"},"3107":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts","type":"page","content":"Governance parts","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts"},"3108":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts","content":"The classification chip (public · confidential · dsk · secret · top_secret — tone + the word), the record status dot (a trace record's lifecycle word), and the trace Inspector's tw"},"3109":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3110":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts#states","content":"States"},"3111":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/governance-parts#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"3112":{"id":"/docs/design-system/com