ocs/design-system/components/turn-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3497":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card#states","content":"States"},"3498":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"3499":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card","content":"**DS-5001** · `apps/chat/src/components/thread/TurnCard.tsx#TurnCard` · adopted"},"3500":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card","content":"One component renders every executor — agent · knowledge · data · search · research · Flow · resolver · goal — from one contract. The header line is &#x2A;‹title› · ‹who/what› · ‹elapsed or when›*, the title an executor's label and never an id. A plain answer is prose in the thread with no frame; work longer than the threshold shows **one** folded progress line that unfolds into the staged view and becomes the receipt with the result beneath it; a turn has at most one progress indicator. The eight states are closed, one copy class and one visual each; an unknown state renders `failed`, never blank. `waiting_on_you` carries the decision inline in the same idiom for every executor. Typography and borders only; no second colour. S8: the card has a `lead` slot — what it already holds about the ask, rendered first in every state, before the progress line and any wait; the goal fills it with its Situation strip (DS-5002), no other executor uses it yet."},"3501":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card#in-the-workshop","content":"Also: asked · working · waiting-on-you · waiting-on-other · stopped · failed · nothing-found"},"3502":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card-7","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card#states","content":"`asked` · `working` · `waiting_on_you` · `waiting_on_other` · `done` · `stopped` · `failed` · `nothing_found`"},"3503":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card-8","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/turn-card#accessibility","content":"one polite live region per thread announces a state change once; the progress line is `role=progressbar` with `aria-valuetext` = the copy (—: it has no accessible name yet, (c)); every inline decision is reachable by Tab from the composer and runs on Enter; Esc does nothing destructive"},"3504":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs","type":"page","content":"UrlTabs · LocalTabs","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs"},"3505":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs","content":"One underline tab row — 36 px, 600 weight when active, a 2 px accent line, no fill, optional counts."},"3506":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tab