xt","url":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs#states","content":"`page` · `inline` · `url` · `surface-legacy`"},"3514":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs-9","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs#accessibility","content":"WAI-ARIA tabs with roving tabindex; `id` wires `aria-controls` to panels"},"3515":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs-10","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/url-tabs-local-tabs#used-in","content":"Two-level page"},"3516":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields","type":"page","content":"Work-item glyphs and property fields","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields"},"3517":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields","content":"The atoms every VibeBan list, board card and Inspector row is built from."},"3518":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3519":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields#states","content":"States"},"3520":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"3521":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields","content":"**DS-6201** · `apps/tasks/src/components/tasks/common.tsx#PriorityChip · StageDot · TypeGlyph · BlockedGlyph · HealthDot · ActorChip · DueLabel · ItemRow; DateField · EstimateField · EnterField · Description · ShowMore; FieldRows.tsx#FieldRows · FieldInputs · CardFacts · RollupLine; FieldSpecEditor.tsx#FieldSpecList · FieldSpecEditor` · adopted"},"3522":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields","content":"The atoms every VibeBan list, board card and Inspector row is built from. Priority (`‼ ! · ◦` + the word), stage (`○ ◔ ◑ ◕ ● ⊘`), type (epic · story · task · bug glyphs), blocked (`n` + direction), health (`StatusDot` with the word) — glyph + text, never colour alone. `ActorChip` is a human, an agent or a service with its kind; `DueLabel` says overdue · today · the date. The property fields are the Inspector's editors — bare at rest, framed on hover/focus (`quiet`), Enter commits, Esc reverts; `EstimateField` carries the project's unit. `ShowMore` is the page foot (*n of total · Show more*). **Typed item fields**: a type's `fields[]` (text · number · money · date · choice · yes/no · reference) are Inspector rows under the built-in ones in the same quiet idiom (`FieldRows` — money is a number and a 3-letter currency; a reference shows its prefix and takes the id; a `financial` row is absent for a viewer, *Not set* for an editor); the create form shows them as `Field`s (`FieldInputs`, required marked, a problem named at its row); a board card carries up to three `show_on_card` values as a label-less facts strip (`CardFacts`, the label is the title — DS-6105's *account · amount · closes*); a column head says each `rollup: sum` once after the count pill (`RollupLine`; *mixed* when the currencies disagree). Settings › Types edits a type's fields (`FieldSpecEditor`: label en · uk, kind, key locked once saved, required / at a stage category, on the card, sum, sensitivity, a choice's options one per line, a reference's prefix; ≤ 16) and reads them as one quiet line each (`FieldSpecList`). Built on `Chip` (DS-3003), `StatusDot` (DS-3004), `Field` (DS-3020), `Select`, `Switch`, `PropertyRow` and `Menu` (DS-3005); not a kit duplicate — the kit has no notion of a work item's priority, stage, type, estimate or typed field."},"3523":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields#in-the-workshop","content":"Also: rows · fields · more · typed-fields · field-specs"},"3524":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields-7","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields#states","content":"`glyphs` · `rows` · `fields` · `more` · `typed-fields` · `field-specs`"},"3525":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields-8","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/work-item-glyphs-and-property-fields#accessibility","content":"every glyph is `role=img` with an `aria-label` and a `title`; the fields are labelled inputs; a fact carries `aria-label` *label: value*; an unparsable value is `aria-invalid` with a `role=alert` line"},"3526":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture","type":"page","content":"Workspace furniture","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture"},"3527":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture","content":"Everything that floats over NexMap's WebGL canvas and is DOM, not map: the kind glyphs (shipment · vessel · aircraft · hub by kind), the status line (cursor · zoom band · what is o"},"3528":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3529":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture#states","content":"States"},"3530":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"3531":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture","content":"**DS-6401** · `apps/map/src/components/workspace/labels.tsx#KindGlyph · StatusLine · MapControls · LayersPanel · ShortcutsSheet · Tooltip` · adopted"},"3532":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture","content":"Everything that floats over NexMap's WebGL canvas and is DOM, not map: the kind glyphs (shipment · vessel · aircraft · hub by kind), the status line (cursor · zoom band · what is on screen · loading), the map controls (layers · zoom · reset north — `IconButton`s in a dock), the layers panel (a floating surface, DS-7015, with one switch per layer and the unplaced count as a door), the keyboard sheet (`?`) and the hover tooltip (feature · cell · zone · event · lane — one grammar, `role=presentation`, never focusable). Layers and dock tokens: `--nexus-z-dock` · `--nexus-z-popover`; the canvas itself is not a story (WebGL) — UAT-3 compares the running workspace to these. Not a kit duplicate: the kit has no map, no layers and no hover card."},"3533":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture#in-the-workshop","content":"Also: controls · layers · shortcuts · hover"},"3534":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture-7","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture#states","content":"`glyphs` · `controls` · `layers` · `shortcuts` · `hover`"},"3535":{"id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture-8","page_id":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/components/workspace-furniture#accessibility","content":"controls are labelled buttons with `aria-keyshortcuts`; the layers panel is a dialog that returns focus; the status line is `role=status`"},"3536":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","type":"page","content":"Copy and language","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Writing and access"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language"},"3537":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","content":"How the suite speaks — one voice, two languages, nothing invented."},"3538":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language#every-string-is-a-key","content":"Every string is a key"},"3539":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language#honest-copy","content":"Honest copy"},"3540":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language#the-shape-of-a-sentence","content":"The shape of a sentence"},"3541":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language#title-case-numbers-units","content":"Title case, numbers, units"},"3542":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language#where-the-rules-live","content":"Where the rules live"},"3543":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","content":"The words on a screen are part of the design system. They follow the same rules in every application, and the rules\nare short."},"3544":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-7","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language#every-string-is-a-key","content":"Nothing is written into a component. Every label, hint, empty state and error is a key in the shared locale files,\npresent in **English and Ukrainian** at the same time — a string that exists in one language only does not ship. The\nworkshop renders every story in both, so a label that overflows in Ukrainian is caught before a screen is built."},"3545":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-8","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language#honest-copy","content":"**Never name a mechanism.** The screen says what happened and what to do, not which service, model, table or flag\nwas involved."},"3546":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-9","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language#honest-copy","content":"**Never invent a value.** A number, a name or a date appears only when the system holds it. A missing value is\nshown as missing, not as a placeholder that looks real."},"3547":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-10","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language#honest-copy","content":"**Not found and not yours read the same.** The interface cannot tell \"this does not exist\" from \"you may not see\nthis\", and it does not try — one wording for both."},"3548":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-11","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language#honest-copy","content":"**One card, one progress, one receipt.** An action shows one card while it runs, one line of progress, and one\nreceipt when it is done — the same shape whether it came from a chat, a button or a voice command."},"3549":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-12","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language#the-shape-of-a-sentence","content":"Labels are nouns (*Name*, *Region*). Actions are verbs that name the result (*Create project*, *Invite*), never\n*OK* or *Submit*. Hints say when something is needed, not what the control is. A confirmation that destroys\nsomething names the thing it destroys. No exclamation marks, no jokes, no capitals for emphasis."},"3550":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-13","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language#title-case-numbers-units","content":"Sentence case everywhere except proper names and the application names (NexChat, NexCore, VibeBan, NexBI, NexGraph,\nNexMap, NexCare, NexForge). Numbers use the reader's locale for grouping and decimals; units follow a thin space; a\nduration is *3 min 20 s*, a date is the locale's short form, a time is 24-hour."},"3551":{"id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language-14","page_id":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/copy-and-language#where-the-rules-live","content":"The principle is DS-0006 — Honest copy, two languages, one card;\neach component page lists its copy keys. Conversation surfaces — the composer, the thread, the cards — follow the\nConversation Register as well; this section describes how they look, not what they say."},"3552":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","type":"page","content":"For builders","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Building"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders"},"3553":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","content":"How to add a component, write its story, keep a screen inside the system — and what a new application starts from."},"3554":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#build-a-screen","content":"Build a screen"},"3555":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#add-a-component","content":"Add a component"},"3556":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#change-an-idiom","content":"Change an idiom"},"3557":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#start-a-new-application","content":"Start a new application"},"3558":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#run-the-workshop-locally","content":"Run the workshop locally"},"3559":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","content":"The system has one rule for the person building a screen: &#x2A;*find the row first.** Everything else follows from it."},"3560":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-7","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#build-a-screen","content":"Open Components and Patterns. A screen is a pattern composed of registered\ncomponents; name the pattern and the component ids in the screen's acceptance criteria, never a look."},"3561":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-8","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#build-a-screen","content":"Import the kit exports the rows name (`@nexus/ui`, `@nexus/ui/workbench`, `@nexus/app-shell`). Keep each\ncomponent's states; do not restyle it."},"3562":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-9","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#build-a-screen","content":"Every number on the screen is a token — spacing, type, radius, control height, layer, shadow, data colour. A raw\ncolour, a px radius, an off-scale size or a `z-index` literal in an application stylesheet fails the fitness check."},"3563":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-10","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#build-a-screen","content":"Render the state ladder: loading, empty, error, denied, offline, not found — before the content."},"3564":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-11","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#build-a-screen","content":"Write the screen's composition stories (populated and every state that applies). The stories *are* the UX review\nof the screen: they are rendered in the workshop before the screen is accepted, and the running screen is compared\nto them afterwards."},"3565":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-12","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#add-a-component","content":"A component that does not exist yet goes through the register, not around it."},"3566":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-13","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#add-a-component","content":"Propose the row: its contract in one sentence, its states, its accessibility, its copy keys, and the sources it\nrests on. The design-system owner approves the row."},"3567":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-14","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#add-a-component","content":"Build it in the kit, on tokens, with every state the row names."},"3568":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-15","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#add-a-component","content":"Write `<Name>.stories.tsx` beside the component — one export per state, fixtures from the workshop's synthetic\nfixtures only (no real name, number, address or document)."},"3569":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-16","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#add-a-component","content":"The story must render, pass its interaction, and pass the accessibility check with no serious or critical finding.\nA component without a story, or a story without a row, does not merge."},"3570":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-17","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#change-an-idiom","content":"Changing how an approved component looks is a register change with the owner's approval — never a side effect of a\nstory or a screen. A conversation component (the composer, the thread, the cards) is also governed by the\nConversation Register and changes only through a conversation change request."},"3571":{"id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders-18","page_id":"/docs/design-system/for-builders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/for-builders#start-a-new-application","content":"A new application is created from the suite's application scaffold: the shell, the kit, both languages, the\ncomposition stories, and the fitness baseline at zero arrive together, and the application claims its accent pair\nin the launcher. Until the scaffold ships, a new application starts from the kit and the shell by the same rules."},"3572":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations","type":"page","content":"Foundations","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Foundations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations"},"3573":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations","content":"Colour, type, spacing, radius, elevation, motion and icons — every number is a token."},"3574":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations","content":"Colour, type, radius, the shell's measures, surfaces and motion — 101 tokens in eight groups, read from `tokens.css` by the workshop so the page can never drift from the CSS."},"3575":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations","content":"Colour — Neutrals, semantic colour, the attention accents, per-application accents and the data palette — in both themes."},"3576":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations","content":"Type — One family, three weights, seven sizes with one line-height each."},"3577":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations","content":"Spacing and density — Ten steps; margins, paddings and gaps name a step, never a number."},"3578":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations","content":"Radius and borders — Seven radii and the shell measures every app shares."},"3579":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations","content":"Elevation — Borders separate; two shadows exist; nine layers, each a token."},"3580":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations-7","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations","content":"Motion — One shell transition, one progress pulse, reduced motion honoured."},"3581":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations-8","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations","content":"Icons — Lucide only, two sizes, always with an accessible name on the control."},"3582":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations-9","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations","content":"Breakpoints and the reference viewport — Designs are judged at 1440 × 900; one breakpoint matters to the kit."},"3583":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations-10","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations","content":"Brand — The Nexi glyph and the wordmark it is the capital of: the shell brand row, the rail, the doors, the favicon."},"3584":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations-11","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations","content":"The swatches, scales and layers in the workshop read the live tokens of the kit — open Foundations in the workshop."},"3585":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/brand","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/brand","type":"page","content":"Brand","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Foundations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/brand"},"3586":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/brand-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/brand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/brand","content":"The Nexi glyph and the wordmark it is the capital of: the shell brand row, the rail, the doors, the favicon."},"3587":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/brand-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/brand","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/brand#ds-1061--the-brand-mark-and-the-wordmark","content":"DS-1061 — The brand mark and the wordmark"},"3588":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/brand-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/brand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/brand#ds-1061--the-brand-mark-and-the-wordmark","content":"The platform is **Nexi**; its mark is `BrandMark` in `@nexus/ui` — a stroked N whose diagonal is a curve, with a dot at its centre, drawn in `currentColor` (the nexiflow\\.ai glyph). The wordmark is **one word whose capital is the glyph**: `BrandWordmark` draws the N at cap height on the baseline and `exi` in the row's bold type (16 px in the shell, 26 px on the doors) — never a mark beside a typed `Nexi`. Expanded shell brand row: the wordmark; NexCore follows it with the app name in tracked uppercase, NexChat ends the row with the Search icon. Collapsed rail: the bare glyph in a 32 px target. The unauthenticated doors (NexCore sign in · sign up · verify · welcome): the wordmark alone as the h1. Every application's favicon: the glyph white on a graphite rounded square (`src/app/icon.svg`). The letter N stays in the DOM, visually hidden, so assistive technology reads \"Nexi\". Applications keep their short names (NexChat · NexCore · NexBI · NexTasks · NexMap · NexCare · NexSales · NexForge · NexGraph); the wordmark is never translated and never written in capitals in copy (`Nexi`, not `NEXI`). Identifiers stay `nexus` (`@nexus/*`, `.nexus-*`, `nexus://`)."},"3589":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","type":"page","content":"Colour","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Foundations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour"},"3590":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","content":"Neutrals, semantic colour, the attention accents, per-application accents and the data palette — in both themes."},"3591":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1001--neutrals","content":"DS-1001 — Neutrals"},"3592":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1002--semantic-colour","content":"DS-1002 — Semantic colour"},"3593":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1003--attention-accents","content":"DS-1003 — Attention accents"},"3594":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1004--per-application-accents","content":"DS-1004 — Per-application accents"},"3595":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1005--data-palette","content":"DS-1005 — Data palette"},"3596":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1001--neutrals","content":"Background, subtle, muted, surface, raised, text (primary · secondary · muted), border (default · strong), focus, and the one accent with its ring and soft tint. Both themes define every neutral; a component names the token, never the hex."},"3597":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-7","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1001--neutrals","content":"Tokens: `--nexus-bg … --nexus-accent-soft`"},"3598":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-8","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1002--semantic-colour","content":"Error, warning, success, info — four values, used sparingly, always with a label or an icon that carries the same meaning. They tint a chip's dot or an inline alert; they never fill a surface."},"3599":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-9","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1002--semantic-colour","content":"Tokens: `--nexus-error · --nexus-warning · --nexus-success · --nexus-info`"},"3600":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-10","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1003--attention-accents","content":"Mint, pink, sky, amber, green, violet, slate, coral, copper, each with a soft tint. They identify an application in the launcher and may mark one running or selected thing on a screen. Never navigation chrome, never a chip, never text colour."},"3601":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-11","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1003--attention-accents","content":"Tokens: `--nexus-accent-mint … --nexus-accent-copper-soft`"},"3602":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-12","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1004--per-application-accents","content":"Each application owns one accent pair (`--nexus-app-<app>-accent` · `-soft`) mapped to an attention accent. A new application claims a free pair in its UAT-0 and the scaffold writes it; two neighbours in the launcher never share a hue."},"3603":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-13","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1004--per-application-accents","content":"Tokens: `--nexus-app-chat-accent … --nexus-app-forge-soft`"},"3604":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-14","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1005--data-palette","content":"Eight categorical hues and one sequential ramp (`--nexus-data-1 … -8`, `--nexus-data-seq-1 … -5`) for things that are *data* — NexForge colour keys, NexBI series, NexMap layers, NexGraph hues — defined once in both themes with ≥ 3:1 against the surface. An app never picks its own chart colour; the attention accents (DS-1003) are not a data palette."},"3605":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour-15","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/colour#ds-1005--data-palette","content":"Tokens: `--nexus-data-1 … --nexus-data-seq-5 (new)`"},"3606":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation","type":"page","content":"Elevation","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Foundations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation"},"3607":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation","content":"Borders separate; two shadows exist; nine layers, each a token."},"3608":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation#ds-1030--surfaces-and-elevation","content":"DS-1030 — Surfaces and elevation"},"3609":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation#ds-1031--layers-and-shadows","content":"DS-1031 — Layers and shadows"},"3610":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation#ds-1030--surfaces-and-elevation","content":"Borders separate; two shadows exist (the composer's and the floating `lg`) and only what floats — the composer, a menu, a dialog, the launcher — may use them. Glass and overlay tokens are the only translucency; the overlay blurs 12 px."},"3611":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation#ds-1030--surfaces-and-elevation","content":"Tokens: `--nexus-surface* · --nexus-glass-* · --nexus-overlay-* · --nexus-shadow-lg · --nexus-composer-shadow*`"},"3612":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation#ds-1031--layers-and-shadows","content":"Nine layers, each a token: raised 1 · sticky 10 · dock 20 · drawer 30 · popover 40 · menu 50 · dialog 60 · toast 70 · skip-link 100 (`--nexus-z-*`); a floating surface names its layer and never a number. Three shadows: `sm` (a hovered row or dragged block) · `md` (a menu, a picker, a popover) · `lg` (a dialog, the launcher) — the literal `0 18px 50px …` that twelve rules carry today becomes `md`."},"3613":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/elevation#ds-1031--layers-and-shadows","content":"Tokens: `--nexus-z-raised … --nexus-z-skip (new) · --nexus-shadow-sm · --nexus-shadow-md (new) · --nexus-shadow-lg`"},"3614":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/icons","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/icons","type":"page","content":"Icons","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Foundations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/icons"},"3615":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/icons-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/icons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/icons","content":"Lucide only, two sizes, always with an accessible name on the control."},"3616":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/icons-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/icons","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/icons#ds-1050--iconography","content":"DS-1050 — Iconography"},"3617":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/icons-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/icons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/icons#ds-1050--iconography","content":"Lucide only, 14 px inside a button or a row, 16 px on its own; always `aria-hidden` — the accessible name is on the control. Status is never an icon alone. No emoji in product UI."},"3618":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion","type":"page","content":"Motion","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Foundations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion"},"3619":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion","content":"One shell transition, one progress pulse, reduced motion honoured."},"3620":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion#ds-1040--motion","content":"DS-1040 — Motion"},"3621":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion#ds-1040--motion","content":"One shell transition (`--nexus-shell-motion`, 200 ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1)); a progress pulse of 600–900 ms on the Pulse strip and the run bar; `prefers-reduced-motion` turns both off."},"3622":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/motion#ds-1040--motion","content":"Tokens: `--nexus-shell-motion`"},"3623":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders","type":"page","content":"Radius and borders","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Foundations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders"},"3624":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders","content":"Seven radii and the shell measures every app shares."},"3625":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders#ds-1020--radius","content":"DS-1020 — Radius"},"3626":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders#ds-1021--shell-measures","content":"DS-1021 — Shell measures"},"3627":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders#ds-1020--radius","content":"Seven radii — `xs` 4 (the inner corner: a chip, a swatch, a focus ring) · `control` 6 (the 34 px input, the 32 px toolbar control, a menu item) · `sm` 8 (button, card) · `md` 12 (panel, floating surface) · `lg` 16 (sheet) · `xl` 20 (dialog, launcher) · `pill` 999 (counter, status chip) — plus the composer's own 26 px. A `border-radius` is one of these names; `--nexus-radius` = `sm`."},"3628":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders#ds-1020--radius","content":"Tokens: `--nexus-radius-xs · -control · -sm … -xl · -pill · --nexus-radius · --nexus-composer-radius`"},"3629":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders#ds-1021--shell-measures","content":"The grid every app shares: 52 px rail, 52 px bar, 248 px sidebar (36 / 34 px rows), a 32 × 44 px collapse handle, 32 px rail buttons, 36 / 28 px button heights, 8 px action gap, 400 px drawer, 440 px confirm, 720 px composer, 800 px content. A screen that needs another measure proposes a token."},"3630":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/radius-and-borders#ds-1021--shell-measures","content":"Tokens: `--nexus-sidebar-* · --nexus-bar-height · --nexus-btn-height* · --nexus-action-gap · --nexus-drawer-width · --nexus-confirm-width`"},"3631":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density","type":"page","content":"Spacing and density","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Foundations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density"},"3632":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density","content":"Ten steps; margins, paddings and gaps name a step, never a number."},"3633":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density#ds-1011--spacing","content":"DS-1011 — Spacing"},"3634":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density#ds-1011--spacing","content":"Ten steps — 2 · 4 · 6 · 8 · 12 · 16 · 20 · 24 · 32 · 48 px (`--nexus-space-1 … -10`): inside a control · icon to label · chip inset · the action gap · a field's gap · section inner · page head · between sections · page padding · the page's foot. Margins, paddings and gaps name a step, never a number; 10 and 14 do not exist (8/12, 12/16). A quiet control that must sit flush with its text uses `.is-flush`; off-screen text uses `.nexus-sr-only`, never a negative margin."},"3635":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/spacing-and-density#ds-1011--spacing","content":"Tokens: `--nexus-space-1 … --nexus-space-10 (new) · --nexus-action-gap = space-4 · --nexus-page-pad · --nexus-section-gap · --nexus-inspector-pad`"},"3636":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type","type":"page","content":"Type","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Foundations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type"},"3637":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type","content":"One family, three weights, seven sizes with one line-height each."},"3638":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type#ds-1010--type","content":"DS-1010 — Type"},"3639":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type#ds-1010--type","content":"One family (`--nexus-font`: Inter, system fallback), three weights (400 · 500 · 600), seven sizes with one line-height each (`--nexus-text-xs … -3xl` = 11 · 12 · 13 · 14 · 16 · 20 · 26): `md` 13 is the workbench body, `lg` 14 the reading body, `2xl` 20 the page title, `xl` 16 the Inspector head and the composer, `sm` 12 chips · labels · hints, `xs` 11 the eyebrow and the counter. No half pixels, nothing under 11, no italic for emphasis, no all-caps except the section title and the eyebrow."},"3640":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/type#ds-1010--type","content":"Tokens: `--nexus-font · --nexus-text-xs … --nexus-text-3xl · --nexus-leading-xs … -3xl · --nexus-composer-font-size · --nexus-composer-placeholder-size`"},"3641":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/viewports","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/viewports","type":"page","content":"Breakpoints and the reference viewport","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Foundations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/viewports"},"3642":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/viewports-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/viewports","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/viewports","content":"Designs are judged at 1440 × 900; one breakpoint matters to the kit."},"3643":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/viewports-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/viewports","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/viewports#ds-1060--breakpoints-and-the-reference-viewport","content":"DS-1060 — Breakpoints and the reference viewport"},"3644":{"id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/viewports-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/foundations/viewports","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/foundations/viewports#ds-1060--breakpoints-and-the-reference-viewport","content":"Designs are judged at 1440 × 900. One breakpoint matters to the kit: under 720 px the Inspector becomes a sheet, the side navigation stacks above its content, and the header line wraps its chips and actions under the title. Below 480 px the shell is NexChat's phone layout."},"3645":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","type":"page","content":"Layout and shell","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell"},"3646":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","content":"One shell, one page frame, one way to go two levels deep, one right-hand panel."},"3647":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2001--the-shell-grid","content":"DS-2001 — The shell grid"},"3648":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2002--the-dock","content":"DS-2002 — The dock"},"3649":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2003--the-launcher","content":"DS-2003 — The launcher"},"3650":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2004--page-frame-widths","content":"DS-2004 — Page frame widths"},"3651":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2005--the-header-line","content":"DS-2005 — The header line"},"3652":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2006--two-levels-never-tabs-under-tabs","content":"DS-2006 — Two levels, never tabs under tabs"},"3653":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-7","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2007--the-inspector-column","content":"DS-2007 — The Inspector column"},"3654":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-8","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2008--the-ask-surface","content":"DS-2008 — The Ask surface"},"3655":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-9","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2009--theme-and-locale-are-attributes-of-html","content":"DS-2009 — Theme and locale are attributes of `<html>`"},"3656":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-10","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2010--settings-and-shortcuts-are-sheets","content":"DS-2010 — Settings and shortcuts are sheets"},"3657":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-11","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","content":"One shell, one page frame, one way to go two levels deep, one right-hand panel. A new application starts from `apps/_template` and inherits every row here without writing layout code."},"3658":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-12","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2001--the-shell-grid","content":"`NexusShell` draws the skip link, the offline strip, `<main>` and the dock. The app's own left navigation (if any) is 248 px with a 52 px rail when collapsed; the collapse handle is centred on the divider (32 × 44 px, 200 ms). With no app navigation the shell draws its own 48 px rail (`dock=\"shell\"`)."},"3659":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-13","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2001--the-shell-grid","content":"Components: `@nexus/app-shell#NexusShell` · `@nexus/app-shell#ShellDock`"},"3660":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-14","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2002--the-dock","content":"Language · Apps · notifications · the user menu (Connected accounts, Settings, Sign out) sit in the `ShellDock` at the bottom of the left navigation (`dock=\"app\"`) or in the shell rail. Menus open upward or beside the rail, follow the WAI-ARIA menu pattern and return focus to their trigger. `Alt+A` opens the launcher suite-wide."},"3661":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-15","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2002--the-dock","content":"Components: `@nexus/app-shell#ShellDock`"},"3662":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-16","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2002--the-dock","content":"*Shown above — open design-system-foundations--layout in the workshop.*"},"3663":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-17","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2003--the-launcher","content":"Static tiles for the applications (Chat · Spin · VibeBan · BI · Graph · Core) and a tile for each module the organization enabled (Map · Care · Forge); a disabled module is absent, never greyed. Each tile carries its app accent (DS-1004) and a one-line description; `resolveAppHref` sends cross-app links to the right origin."},"3664":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-18","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2003--the-launcher","content":"Components: `@nexus/app-shell#AppLauncher` · `@nexus/app-shell#NEXUS_APPS`"},"3665":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-19","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2004--page-frame-widths","content":"Content sits in `PageFrame`: `standard` (max 1320 px — people, settings, detail pages) or `wide` (overview, matrix, audit, executions). 32 px of air above the header line; the body starts 16 px under the tabs."},"3666":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-20","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2004--page-frame-widths","content":"Components: `@nexus/ui/workbench#PageFrame`"},"3667":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-21","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2005--the-header-line","content":"Back arrow (icon, labelled) · title (ellipsis at 46 %) · ≤ 3 chips · Ask bar · ≤ 2 buttons + `⋯` on one 36 px row; under 720 px chips and actions wrap under the title. NexCore and NexChat keep their stacked frame (eyebrow · title · lead) for their own detail pages; every other app renders `layout=\"dense\"`."},"3668":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-22","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2005--the-header-line","content":"Components: `@nexus/ui/workbench#PageLine` · `@nexus/ui/workbench#PageFrame`"},"3669":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-23","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2006--two-levels-never-tabs-under-tabs","content":"The first level of a page is one underline tab row (`UrlTabs` / `LocalTabs`, state in `?tab=`). The second level is a left column of sections (`SideNav` in a `SideNavLayout`, 200 px, `aria-current`). A segmented control may switch views of the same data (list / board) and sits with the filters, never styled as tabs."},"3670":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-24","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2006--two-levels-never-tabs-under-tabs","content":"Components: `@nexus/ui/workbench#UrlTabs` · `@nexus/ui/workbench#LocalTabs` · `@nexus/ui/workbench#SideNav` · `@nexus/ui/workbench#SideNavLayout`"},"3671":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-25","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2007--the-inspector-column","content":"Reading and editing one thing happens in the right-hand `Inspector`: 360–640 px, resizable by a keyboard separator, width persisted per app; Esc closes and focus returns to the opener. Creation opens the same panel empty (`FormInspector`). Under 720 px it becomes a sheet. There is one Inspector on a page."},"3672":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-26","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2007--the-inspector-column","content":"Components: `@nexus/ui/workbench#Inspector` · `@nexus/ui/workbench#FormInspector`"},"3673":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-27","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2008--the-ask-surface","content":"Every app's header line carries the Ask bar: the minimised NexChat composer that sends to chat-api as a Project of that app and offers the hand-off chip and &#x2A;Back to \\<app>* return. An app never builds its own chat input."},"3674":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-28","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2008--the-ask-surface","content":"Components: `@nexus/ui/ask#AskSurface`"},"3675":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-29","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2009--theme-and-locale-are-attributes-of-html","content":"`data-theme` (`light` · `graphite`) and `lang` (`en` · `uk`) are set on `<html>` by the shell from the person's device preference; `THEME_BOOT_SCRIPT` applies the theme before hydration. Graphite ships behind the token audit (`GRAPHITE_ENABLED`); the workshop renders it regardless so the audit has a place to happen."},"3676":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-30","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2009--theme-and-locale-are-attributes-of-html","content":"Components: `@nexus/app-shell#useTheme` · `@nexus/app-shell#THEME_BOOT_SCRIPT` · `@nexus/i18n#LocaleProvider`"},"3677":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-31","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2010--settings-and-shortcuts-are-sheets","content":"Appearance, language, notifications and the keyboard reference open as `SettingsSheet` / `ShortcutsSheet` from the dock — one 400 px drawer, not a settings page per app. App-specific settings live on that app's Settings tab, under the same frame as everything else."},"3678":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-32","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2010--settings-and-shortcuts-are-sheets","content":"Components: `@nexus/app-shell#SettingsSheet` · `@nexus/app-shell#ShortcutsSheet`"},"3679":{"id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell-33","page_id":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/layout-and-shell#ds-2010--settings-and-shortcuts-are-sheets","content":"*No story yet.*"},"3680":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","type":"page","content":"Patterns","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Patterns"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns"},"3681":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"The compositions that cover nearly every screen in the suite."},"3682":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Ten compositions cover nearly every screen in the suite. A new screen names the pattern it follows in its acceptance criteria; a screen that follows none proposes an eleventh."},"3683":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Discovery list → Inspector — A page lists records in a DataTable; selecting a row opens the Inspector on the right with the record's properties and sections; Enter / double-click drills into the record's own p"},"3684":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Create in the Inspector — &#x2A;New …* in the header line opens a FormInspector empty; the form fills it; Submit in the footer creates the record and the panel becomes its detail Inspector."},"3685":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Edit in place — A detail surface reads by default; Edit turns its properties into controls; Save commits and shows *Saved*; Cancel on a dirty form asks inline."},"3686":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Confirmation — Reversible: an ActionPanel where the action was taken, one sentence naming the effect, one primary, Cancel."},"3687":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"The state ladder on every read — A screen's content region renders through DataStateView; loading is text, empty is quiet with ≤ 3 starting points, error and offline retry, denied and not found look alike."},"3688":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-7","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Overview page — A wide frame: the PulseStrip on top, a row of Stats, then Sections with StatusLists and &#x2A;View all →* links."},"3689":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-8","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Settings surface — Settings are a PropertyList: one quiet row per property with the control as the value; grouped by InspectorSection idiom=\"rule\" when there are more than six."},"3690":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-9","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Empty collection — A collection with nothing in it shows the quiet EmptyState in place of the list: one title, the primary action the header line also offers, up to three starting points."},"3691":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-10","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Two-level page — Tabs for the first level, a SideNav column for the second, the content to its right; the active section in the URL."},"3692":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-11","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"List with controls — Above a collection that outgrows one screen: a Toolbar with a SearchField, compact Select filters and the primary action on the right; below the threshold the header line is the wh"},"3693":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-12","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Ask round trip — From any app's Ask bar a question goes to chat-api as that app's Project; the answer appears in the Ask panel with its provenance line; a hand-off opens NexChat with the \\*asked fro"},"3694":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-13","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Link idioms — Three looks for three jobs: an *inline* link in running text (text colour, underlined, hover → secondary); a *row* link — the title cell of a table or row list (no underline, under"},"3695":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-14","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Filter panel — When a list needs more than three filters, they leave the toolbar for a panel above (a wrapping row of labelled compact selects and chips, 12 px label over each) or beside the list"},"3696":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-15","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Form rhythm — Label (12 px · 500 · secondary) · 6 px · control (34 px, 13 px) · 6 px · hint or error (12 px); 16 px between fields; a two-column grid at 16 × 24 for short fields; a titled fields"},"3697":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-16","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Floating surface — One anatomy for everything that floats over the page — a menu, a popover, the composer picker, a select's list: radius 12 · padding 6 · 1 px border · --nexus-shadow-md · items 32 p"},"3698":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns-17","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns","content":"Action rows — Secondary actions under content are a quiet row of links, never a row of buttons: 13 px · 500 · secondary colour · underline on hover · a · between · baseline-aligned under the tex"},"3699":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows","type":"page","content":"DS-7016 Action rows","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Patterns"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows"},"3700":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows","content":"Secondary actions under content are a quiet row of links, never a row of buttons: 13 px · 500 · secondary colour · underline on hover · a · between · baseline-aligned under the tex"},"3701":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows#built-from","content":"Built from"},"3702":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows#rests-on","content":"Rests on"},"3703":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3704":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows","content":"Secondary actions under content are a quiet row of links, never a row of buttons: 13 px · 500 · secondary colour · underline on hover · a `·` between · baseline-aligned under the text, 8 above. *View plan · Pause · Change goal · Stop* under a goal card; *Connect Gmail · Not now* in the sentence that names the obstacle; the footer of an inspector section, a row's expansion, a result line, the recovery line of a state. A bordered button keeps three jobs only — the one primary commit of a surface, a confirmation's pair, the header or toolbar line's named actions. A destructive action in a row is the last link, named by its verb, never red — it confirms by name. One component renders the row (`ActionRow` of `LinkButton tone=\"quiet\"`); nothing app-local."},"3705":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows#built-from","content":"LinkButton · ActionRow · Button · ActionPanel"},"3706":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/action-rows#rests-on","content":"DS-0002 — Typography, spacing and borders over decorative colour · DS-0004 — A control that cannot change anything is not shown · DS-0007 — Reversible asks inline, destructive asks by name · DS-7012 — Link idioms"},"3707":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip","type":"page","content":"DS-7011 Ask round trip","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Patterns"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip"},"3708":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip","content":"From any app's Ask bar a question goes to chat-api as that app's Project; the answer appears in the Ask panel with its provenance line; a hand-off opens NexChat with the *asked fro"},"3709":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip#built-from","content":"Built from"},"3710":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip#rests-on","content":"Rests on"},"3711":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3712":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip","content":"From any app's Ask bar a question goes to chat-api as that app's Project; the answer appears in the Ask panel with its provenance line; a hand-off opens NexChat with the *asked from* chip and &#x2A;Back to \\<app>* returns. The conversation itself is governed by the Conversation Register, not here."},"3713":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip#built-from","content":"`@nexus/ui/ask#AskSurface`"},"3714":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/ask-round-trip#rests-on","content":"DS-2008 — The Ask surface"},"3715":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation","type":"page","content":"DS-7004 Confirmation","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Patterns"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation"},"3716":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation","content":"Reversible: an ActionPanel where the action was taken, one sentence naming the effect, one primary, Cancel."},"3717":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation#built-from","content":"Built from"},"3718":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation#rests-on","content":"Rests on"},"3719":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3720":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation","content":"Reversible: an `ActionPanel` where the action was taken, one sentence naming the effect, one primary, Cancel. Destructive: the same panel with `danger`, a typed name and a `danger` primary. Never \"Are you sure?\"."},"3721":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation#built-from","content":"ActionPanel · Button"},"3722":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/confirmation#rests-on","content":"DS-0007 — Reversible asks inline, destructive asks by name"},"3723":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector","type":"page","content":"DS-7002 Create in the Inspector","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Patterns"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector"},"3724":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector","content":"*New …* in the header line opens a FormInspector empty; the form fills it; Submit in the footer creates the record and the panel becomes its detail Inspector."},"3725":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector#built-from","content":"Built from"},"3726":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector#rests-on","content":"Rests on"},"3727":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3728":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector","content":"*New …* in the header line opens a `FormInspector` empty; the form fills it; Submit in the footer creates the record and the panel becomes its detail Inspector. No separate \"new\" page, no modal."},"3729":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector#built-from","content":"FormInspector · Field · Select"},"3730":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/create-in-the-inspector#rests-on","content":"DS-2007 — The Inspector column"},"3731":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector","type":"page","content":"DS-7001 Discovery list → Inspector","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Patterns"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector"},"3732":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector","content":"A page lists records in a DataTable; selecting a row opens the Inspector on the right with the record's properties and sections; Enter / double-click drills into the record's own p"},"3733":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector#built-from","content":"Built from"},"3734":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector#rests-on","content":"Rests on"},"3735":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3736":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector","content":"A page lists records in a `DataTable`; selecting a row opens the `Inspector` on the right with the record's properties and sections; Enter / double-click drills into the record's own page when it has one. The list keeps its selection and scroll while the panel is open; one Inspector at a time."},"3737":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector#built-from","content":"DataTable · Inspector · InspectorSection · PropertyList · PropertyRow"},"3738":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/discovery-list-inspector#rests-on","content":"DS-2007 — The Inspector column · DS-0005 — Every read has its ladder"},"3739":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place","type":"page","content":"DS-7003 Edit in place","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Patterns"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place"},"3740":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place","content":"A detail surface reads by default; Edit turns its properties into controls; Save commits and shows *Saved*; Cancel on a dirty form asks inline."},"3741":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place#built-from","content":"Built from"},"3742":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place#rests-on","content":"Rests on"},"3743":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3744":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place","content":"A detail surface reads by default; Edit turns its properties into controls; Save commits and shows *Saved*; Cancel on a dirty form asks inline. Switches commit on change without an Edit mode."},"3745":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place#built-from","content":"EditBar · SavedNote · Switch · PropertyList · PropertyRow"},"3746":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/edit-in-place#rests-on","content":"DS-0007 — Reversible asks inline, destructive asks by name"},"3747":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection","type":"page","content":"DS-7008 Empty collection","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Patterns"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection"},"3748":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection","content":"A collection with nothing in it shows the quiet EmptyState in place of the list: one title, the primary action the header line also offers, up to three starting points."},"3749":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection#built-from","content":"Built from"},"3750":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection#rests-on","content":"Rests on"},"3751":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3752":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection","content":"A collection with nothing in it shows the quiet `EmptyState` in place of the list: one title, the primary action the header line also offers, up to three starting points. A table header is never left bare."},"3753":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection#built-from","content":"EmptyState · DataTable"},"3754":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/empty-collection#rests-on","content":"DS-0005 — Every read has its ladder"},"3755":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel","type":"page","content":"DS-7013 Filter panel","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Patterns"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel"},"3756":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel","content":"When a list needs more than three filters, they leave the toolbar for a panel above (a wrapping row of labelled compact selects and chips, 12 px label over each) or beside the list"},"3757":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel#built-from","content":"Built from"},"3758":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel#rests-on","content":"Rests on"},"3759":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3760":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel","content":"When a list needs more than three filters, they leave the toolbar for a panel above (a wrapping row of labelled compact selects and chips, 12 px label over each) or beside the list; the toolbar keeps search and the primary action. Active filters show as removable chips with *Clear all*; a filtered-to-empty list says what it filtered. NexBI's `.nexus-bi-fbar` promoted; DS-7010 stays the ≤ 3 case."},"3761":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel#built-from","content":"Toolbar · showListControls · SearchField · Chip · EmptyState"},"3762":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/filter-panel#rests-on","content":"DS-7010 — List with controls"},"3763":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface","type":"page","content":"DS-7015 Floating surface","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Patterns"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface"},"3764":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface","content":"One anatomy for everything that floats over the page — a menu, a popover, the composer picker, a select's list: radius 12 · padding 6 · 1 px border · --nexus-shadow-md · items 32 p"},"3765":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface#built-from","content":"Built from"},"3766":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface#rests-on","content":"Rests on"},"3767":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3768":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface","content":"One anatomy for everything that floats over the page — a menu, a popover, the composer picker, a select's list: radius 12 · padding 6 · 1 px border · `--nexus-shadow-md` · items 32 px with 8 px inset and radius 8 at 13 px · separators 1 px with 4 px around · captions 12 px secondary; the picker adds a search row and sections, the popover glass. It names its layer (DS-1031), opens from its trigger's corner, closes on Escape and outside click, and returns focus. A select has three sizes — form 34 · toolbar 32 · quiet 26 — and its option hint is a prop, never hidden from outside."},"3769":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface#built-from","content":"Menu · SearchField · Combobox"},"3770":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/floating-surface#rests-on","content":"DS-1031 — Layers and shadows · DS-1020 — Radius"},"3771":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm","type":"page","content":"DS-7014 Form rhythm","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Patterns"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm"},"3772":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm","content":"Label (12 px · 500 · secondary) · 6 px · control (34 px, 13 px) · 6 px · hint or error (12 px); 16 px between fields; a two-column grid at 16 × 24 for short fields; a titled fields"},"3773":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm#built-from","content":"Built from"},"3774":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm#rests-on","content":"Rests on"},"3775":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3776":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm","content":"Label (12 px · 500 · secondary) · 6 px · control (34 px, 13 px) · 6 px · hint or error (12 px); 16 px between fields; a two-column grid at 16 × 24 for short fields; a titled fieldset 24 px from its neighbours. One control height in a form (34), 32 in a toolbar, 40 only on the sign-in card. The focus ring is the accent ring token. \"Wrong\" is said once: the field's border and a `Hint tone=\"danger\"` under it, linked by `aria-describedby`. `.nexus-field` (margin-based) is legacy."},"3777":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm#built-from","content":"Field · Select · Switch · CheckList · SearchField · SecretInput · RadioCard"},"3778":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/form-rhythm#rests-on","content":"DS-1011 — Spacing · DS-0004 — A control that cannot change anything is not shown"},"3779":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms","type":"page","content":"DS-7012 Link idioms","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Patterns"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms"},"3780":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms","content":"Three looks for three jobs: an *inline* link in running text (text colour, underlined, hover → secondary); a *row* link — the title cell of a table or row list (no underline, under"},"3781":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms#built-from","content":"Built from"},"3782":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms#rests-on","content":"Rests on"},"3783":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3784":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms-4","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms","content":"Three looks for three jobs: an *inline* link in running text (text colour, underlined, hover → secondary); a *row* link — the title cell of a table or row list (no underline, underline on hover, the row is the target); a *meta* link at 12 px secondary (*Open source chat*, &#x2A;Why?*). A `<button>` that looks like a link is the inline look over a button with a 24 px target; a fourth tone, *quiet* (13 px · 500 · secondary, underline on hover), is the look of an action row (DS-7016). One class family `.nexus-link` (`.is-row` · `.is-meta`) and `.nexus-link-btn` (`.is-meta` · `.is-quiet`); nothing app-local."},"3785":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms-5","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms#built-from","content":"DataTable · RowList · LinkButton · ActionRow"},"3786":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms-6","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/link-idioms#rests-on","content":"DS-0001 — Black · white · graphite, one accent · DS-0004 — A control that cannot change anything is not shown"},"3787":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls","type":"page","content":"DS-7010 List with controls","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Design system","Patterns"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls"},"3788":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls-0","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls","content":"Above a collection that outgrows one screen: a Toolbar with a SearchField, compact Select filters and the primary action on the right; below the threshold the header line is the wh"},"3789":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls-1","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls#built-from","content":"Built from"},"3790":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls-2","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls#rests-on","content":"Rests on"},"3791":{"id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls-3","page_id":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-system/patterns/list-with-controls#in-the-workshop","content":"In the workshop"},"3792":{