:"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"run storage · 30 days of stdout/code for audit; sandbox outputs 90 days"},"6452":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-76","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"Draft tables, charts, documents"},"6453":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-77","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"editors of the Project"},"6454":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-78","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"Artifacts, versioned, on the Canvas"},"6455":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-79","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"Published artifacts"},"6456":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-80","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"every member, viewers included"},"6457":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-81","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"Artifacts, *published*; pinned as Project sources with a shape hint"},"6458":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-82","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"The notebook"},"6459":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-83","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"stays with the run — the record, not a result"},"6460":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-84","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"Artifacts, never published by the gate"},"6461":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-85","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"Kept datasets (typed copy · normalised · results)"},"6462":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-86","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"members of the Project — shape and provenance to agents, rows to the sandbox of a later run"},"6463":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-87","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"Project datasets with layer *bronze · silver · gold*, technique, Skill version; *Current* or &#x2A;Stale — version of …*"},"6464":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-88","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"The Dataset Card"},"6465":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-89","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"as any document — draft to editors, published to all"},"6466":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-90","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"Artifacts, versioned; grows with later runs"},"6467":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-91","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"Route, gates, criteria, verdicts, reuse / recompute, merge confirmations, Stop / Regenerate"},"6468":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-92","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"audit; the platform's decision dataset"},"6469":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-93","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"decision records with written-back outcomes"},"6470":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-94","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#what-is-kept-and-for-whom","content":"Retention follows the Blueprint's defaults — artifacts 730 days, runs 365, sandbox outputs 90 — and, before any\npurge, the decision records are exported to the governed decision dataset."},"6471":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-95","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#why-not-a-service","content":"A `DataScienceService` would need its own execution path, its own permission checks, its own way to reach models and\nits own idea of \"done\". Every one of those already exists once, generically: Agent Runtime, the Sandbox under a\nprofile, Synapse, the policy decision, the Flow engine's `GoalSpec`. Building the capability as a Flow means a builder\ncan *adapt* it from the Pattern Library — change the criteria, swap the reviewer, add a stage for their domain — and\nthat every improvement to the platform (a faster sandbox, a better coder model, a new approval rule) reaches it\nwithout a release. It also means the boundaries hold by construction: no bespoke code, so no bespoke hole."},"6472":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-96","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#memory-across-runs--reuse-recompute-the-card","content":"Since S5 the pattern remembers. A stage that produced a table calls `nexus.dataset(...)`; the engine registers it as a\n**Project dataset** with its layer, technique and Skill version. On the next question the planner sees those datasets\nin the profile and, where a kept dataset's technique already answers a stage, takes the **reuse** arm — an\n`analysis_reuse` decision with *reuse* and *recompute&#x2A; as its action space, shown in the thread as &#x2A;↺ reused from the\nrun of …*. **Recompute** is the initiator's alone (`POST /chat/flow-runs/{run_id}/recompute`; *409 RUN\\_ACTIVE* while\nthe run is going) and leaves the earlier results in place until it finishes. A dataset whose source file has a newer\nversion reads &#x2A;Stale — version of …*. The **Dataset Card** is the synthesis skill's last output: a document about the\ndata itself that a later run appends to, versioned like any artifact. The layers follow the platform's memory rule\n(Bronze the typed copy, Silver normalised, Gold a result) and every dataset carries where it came from; nothing here\nis a claim in the knowledge graph — findings → NexGraph claims is an open item."},"6473":{"id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist-97","page_id":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agentic-data-scientist#memory-across-runs--reuse-recompute-the-card","content":"What remains open (the work is paused): human review of the four technique skills, subset merges\nin the gate, findings as proposed graph claims, PowerPoint export, and the release candidate. The guide documents only\nwhat runs; where it shows a prototype it says so."},"6474":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","type":"page","content":"Agents, Skills, Tools and Flows","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Technical documentation","Building blocks"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows"},"6475":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-0","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","content":"The four things you build in NexChat, explained with one everyday example — planning a weekend trip."},"6476":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-1","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"The example: a weekend trip"},"6477":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-2","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#why-four-pieces-and-not-one","content":"Why four pieces and not one"},"6478":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-3","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"Where you build each piece"},"6479":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-4","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-same-picture-in-the-architecture","content":"The same picture in the architecture"},"6480":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-5","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","content":"You will meet four words again and again in NexChat: **Agent**, **Skill**, **Tool** and **Flow**. They are\ndeliberately separate, and the separation is what makes what you build reusable, safe and — after a while —\nboring in the best way. This page explains them with one example anyone recognises."},"6481":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-6","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"Every few weeks you plan a short trip for two or three people. It always goes the same way: collect what everyone\nwants, check the weather and the budget, propose a couple of options, argue a bit, decide, and finally put it into\nthe calendar. It is a small job, it repeats, and half of it is looking things up. That is exactly the shape of work\nNexi is made for."},"6482":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-7","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"Here is how the four pieces divide it:"},"6483":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-8","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"Piece"},"6484":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-9","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"In the example"},"6485":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-10","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"One sentence"},"6486":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-11","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"**Skill**"},"6487":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-12","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"*Weekend planning checklist* — how a good proposal looks: dates, place, travel time, cost per person, a plan B for rain, and a question to ask when something is unclear."},"6488":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-13","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"**Skill teaches.** Knowledge and judgement, written once, reviewed by a person, reusable by any agent."},"6489":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-14","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"**Agent**"},"6490":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-15","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"*Trip planner* — the assistant you talk to. It applies the checklist, asks who is coming and what the budget is, and writes the proposals."},"6491":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-16","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"**Agent works.** Instructions + the Skills it applies + the Tools it may use + how it reaches a model."},"6492":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-17","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"**Tool**"},"6493":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-18","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"*Weather forecast* and *Calendar* — look up the forecast for a place and a date; create an event for everyone."},"6494":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-19","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"**Tool acts.** A governed operation on a real system, reached through a Connection with its own credentials."},"6495":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-20","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"**Flow**"},"6496":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-21","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"*Plan the weekend* — every Thursday: gather preferences → planner proposes → repeat until a proposal fits budget and weather → you approve → calendar events are created."},"6497":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-22","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"**Flow orchestrates.** Steps, conditions, loops with a Goal, human approvals; the engine — not the model — decides when it is done."},"6498":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-23","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-example-a-weekend-trip","content":"Read it once as a story: on Thursday evening the Flow starts on its own. The **Trip planner** agent asks the people\nin the Project what they want this time. Inside the loop it writes two proposals, using the **checklist** Skill, and\ncalls the **Weather** Tool for each place. The **Evaluator** — a rule, not the model — checks whether one proposal\nfits the budget and has acceptable weather. If not, the loop runs again, at most three times. When a proposal fits,\nthe Flow pauses and you get an **approval** in NexTasks with the proposal attached. Only after you approve does the\n**Calendar** Tool create the events. Nothing is written anywhere until a person said yes."},"6499":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-24","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#why-four-pieces-and-not-one","content":"You could imagine one \"trip bot\" that does all of this. Nexi splits it on purpose:"},"6500":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-25","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#why-four-pieces-and-not-one","content":"**A Skill owns nothing but knowledge.** The *Weekend planning checklist* has no model, no credentials and no tools.\nThat is why the same Skill can teach a *Team offsite planner* agent next month, and why a person reviews it before\nit is published — you are reviewing judgement, not code."},"6501":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-26","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#why-four-pieces-and-not-one","content":"**An Agent is the one you talk to.** It applies Skills and uses Tools, and it reaches a model only through Synapse —\nso which model, at what cost, with what data leaving the organization, is decided by your administrator, not by\nthe agent."},"6502":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-27","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#why-four-pieces-and-not-one","content":"**A Tool is the only thing that touches the world.** The *Calendar* Tool can create events because a Connection with\nthe right credentials exists and your Project is allowed to use it. The agent cannot invent a new capability; it can\nonly ask for a Tool it has been given."},"6503":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-28","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#why-four-pieces-and-not-one","content":"**A Flow is where completion is decided.*&#x2A; &#x2A;\"Fits budget and weather OK\"* is a **Goal** with a limit of three rounds.\nThe **Evaluator** judges; the loop engine stops. A model never marks its own work as done, and a Flow can never run\nforever or spend without a ceiling."},"6504":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-29","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#why-four-pieces-and-not-one","content":"**A person stays in the loop where it matters.** The approval step is a real pause, visible in NexTasks, with the\nevidence attached. A Flow that changes something outside the conversation always has one."},"6505":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-30","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"Piece"},"6506":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-31","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"Where in NexChat"},"6507":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-32","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"How it starts"},"6508":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-33","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"Agent"},"6509":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-34","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"**Agent Studio** in your Project"},"6510":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-35","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"From one sentence — &#x2A;\"Plan weekend trips for my family within a budget\"* — then refine instructions, attach Skills, allow Tools, test in chat."},"6511":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-36","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"Skill"},"6512":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-37","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"**Skills**"},"6513":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-38","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"Write the instruction and its examples; define what goes in and what comes out; a reviewer publishes it."},"6514":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-39","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"Tool"},"6515":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-40","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"**Tools** (and **Connections** in NexCore)"},"6516":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-41","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"An administrator connects the system once; you pick the Tool for your agent or Flow. Code the model writes runs only in the Sandbox."},"6517":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-42","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"Flow"},"6518":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-43","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"**Flow Studio**"},"6519":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-44","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"Describe the process in plain words and let Nexi draft the Flow, or place the steps yourself; run it and follow it in **Runs**."},"6520":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-45","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#where-you-build-each-piece","content":"Want to do it rather than read about it? The NexChat guide has one chapter per building block with\nthe real screens, starting with Create an Agent from one sentence. Next in this\nsection: how Synapse connects agents to models and systems, and why the ontology matters\nwhen many models and technologies are involved."},"6521":{"id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows-46","page_id":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/agents-skills-tools-flows#the-same-picture-in-the-architecture","content":"The building blocks and their relationships are one view of the architecture model that draws every diagram in this\ndocumentation:"},"6522":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","type":"page","content":"Auto — how Nexi picks the capability","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Technical documentation","Building blocks"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/auto"},"6523":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-0","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto","content":"What happens between a message and its route — the classifier, the deterministic ranker, the three arms, the sticky thread, the fallback, and the Resolver Flow that surveys a Project and proposes a plan when nothing in it fits. Why every route is a decision record, and what is learned from it."},"6524":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-1","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"The pipeline, stage by stage"},"6525":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-2","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"Outcomes are written back"},"6526":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-3","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"The Resolver — a Flow, not a router"},"6527":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-4","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/auto#what-is-tuned-and-by-whom","content":"What is tuned, and by whom"},"6528":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-5","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/auto#what-is-built-and-what-is-not","content":"What is built and what is not"},"6529":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-6","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/auto#where-to-read-more","content":"Where to read more"},"6530":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-7","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto","content":"The Let Auto choose chapter reads Auto from the outside — the route line, &#x2A;Why this\nroute?*, the Resolver card. This page is the inside: the pipeline that runs on every message when the selector is on\n**Auto**, why it is built from a small classifier and a lot of deterministic code, and how the *Resolver* extends it\nwithout adding a service. Two architectural points run through it. **Routing is a decision, not a reasoning trace**:\nthe model classifies, code ranks, the engine records the distribution, and there is nothing to store or show but the\nrecord. **When nothing fits, Nexi does not improvise**: it hands the message to a Flow whose job is to find out\nwhat is missing and ask the right person."},"6531":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-8","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"Stage"},"6532":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-9","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"What it does"},"6533":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-10","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"Why it is built this way"},"6534":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-11","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"**Lexicon pass**"},"6535":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-12","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"Cheap, deterministic signals: a file on the message, an `@agent`, a product name (*Gmail*, *Jira*), verbs of side effect (*send*, *delete*)."},"6536":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-13","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"Signals that should never depend on a model call — a file present is a fact."},"6537":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-14","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"**Platform action**"},"6538":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-15","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"Before discovery and before any model: a verb cue and an object cue that match a command an app declared in the tool registry (*open my inbox*, *create a task … by Friday*, &#x2A;run the Flow …*). The target is resolved through the owning app's door as the person, the PDP confirms `read` on the exact target, and a `client_action` card opens, asks &#x2A;Which one?* or says *Nothing by that name you may open* — identical for missing and not-permitted. Exclusions `asks_how`, `not_a_command`, `foreign_family` keep questions out. A spoken sentence takes exactly this path."},"6539":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-16","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"A command is a fact about the sentence, not an opinion of a model; resolving through the owning app means Auto never grants what the app would not. See Voice, screen context, search and research."},"6540":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-17","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"**Discovery + PDP filter**"},"6541":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-18","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"Lists the Project's capabilities — agents, Flows, arms — and removes what the asker may not use *before* anything is scored."},"6542":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-19","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"An absent capability must not leak into the record; ranking only among the eligible keeps the action space honest."},"6543":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-20","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"**Sticky**"},"6544":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-21","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"If the thread's last positive route (a route the person did not override or regenerate) still matches the topic, it is kept."},"6545":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-22","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"Follow-ups in an analysis thread go to the same agent; the record says *this thread already runs with it*."},"6546":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-23","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"**IntentAnalysis**"},"6547":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-24","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"One call to the `classifier` role via Synapse (prompt `intent_execute.md`) returns a closed-vocabulary structure: intent with per-option probabilities, domain, inputs present, side effects asked, and a `validation.coerced[]` list of anything the model got outside the vocabulary."},"6548":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-25","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"Closed vocabulary makes the output a feature, not free text; coercions are kept because they are training data too."},"6549":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-26","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"**Fallback**"},"6550":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-27","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"Without a classifier model at the Project's classification, the lexicon alone routes — to General or to a specialist by words — and **never starts a Flow**."},"6551":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-28","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"A Flow may have side effects; words alone are not enough evidence."},"6552":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-29","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"**Deterministic ranking**"},"6553":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-30","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"A fixed sum over the eligible candidates: +0.45 intent match · +0.2 domain · +0.1 Project-owned · +0.15 × specificity · −0.15 for a side effect the message did not ask for. Two thresholds: `ambiguity_margin` (ask rather than guess) and `min_specialist_score` (below it, General or the Resolver)."},"6554":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-31","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"The scores are reproducible from the record; a Blueprint tunes the weights (`tuning.auto`), no model does."},"6555":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-32","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"**Arms**"},"6556":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-33","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"Three non-agent answers compete with the agents: **data** (NexBI's governed engine, only when a validated metric matches and its entity has a bound dataset), **knowledge** (NexGraph resolve for a question about documents), **capability** (a product family → &#x2A;General · with ‹product›*, the tools offered this turn, a governed `CapabilityRequest` when a tool needs allowing)."},"6557":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-34","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"An arm is the right answer when a specialist would only add latency and a model's paraphrase of a number."},"6558":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-35","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"**Search arm**"},"6559":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-36","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"A closed en/uk/ru/de search lexicon, or a places/facts question, goes to the `web.search` provider port in core-api: providers in the Blueprint's order, open data first for places and facts, the first that answers wins, nothing leaves above `tuning.web_search.max_classification`. One model call with the results quoted as untrusted data and no tools; `[n]` validated against ranks. A **research cue** goes to the Resolver, which runs the base pack's `web-research` Flow (allow-list approval, HTTP reading plane, report with citations)."},"6560":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-37","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"The web is a source like any other: who answered, from which class, and why is on the card and in two decision records — never the query text."},"6561":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-38","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"**Resolver hand-off**"},"6562":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-39","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"When no specialist reaches the minimum and no arm bids, the message goes to the Project's published copy of the Resolver Flow (below)."},"6563":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-40","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"A \"we cannot do this\" is itself work: find out what is missing and ask the right person."},"6564":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-41","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"**RouteDecision**"},"6565":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-42","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"Written before execution: `decision_id`, kind `route`, tenancy and actor, version pins (policy, prompt template, catalog snapshot), `state_features`, a `state_ref` to the message (never its text), the full `action_space[]` with per-arm features and eligibility, the score distribution, `chosen` with closed `reason_codes[]`, `propensity` (1.0 — there is no exploration), and `cost`."},"6566":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-43","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-pipeline-stage-by-stage","content":"The record is the product: it is what &#x2A;Why this route?* renders and what a future decision model trains on."},"6567":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-44","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"A route is not finished when it is chosen. What the person does next is its label — and it is written to the same\nrecord, never inferred later:"},"6568":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-45","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"The person…"},"6569":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-46","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"Outcome signal"},"6570":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-47","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`label_source`"},"6571":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-48","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"Picks *Try another route*"},"6572":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-49","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`reroute` with the chosen alternative"},"6573":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-50","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`human_explicit`"},"6574":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-51","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"Presses *Regenerate*"},"6575":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-52","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`regenerate`"},"6576":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-53","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`human_implicit`"},"6577":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-54","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"Presses *Not now* on a &#x2A;Run …?* or Resolver card"},"6578":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-55","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`decline`"},"6579":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-56","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`human_explicit`"},"6580":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-57","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"Presses *Stop loop*"},"6581":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-58","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`stop`"},"6582":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-59","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`human_explicit`"},"6583":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-60","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"Accepts a plan, allows a tool, approves a connection"},"6584":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-61","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`approval` with the decision"},"6585":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-62","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`human_explicit`"},"6586":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-63","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"Lets a FlowRun reach a terminal status"},"6587":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-64","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`flow_terminal` with the status"},"6588":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-65","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`engine_deterministic`"},"6589":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-66","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"— an evaluator judges a loop"},"6590":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-67","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`loop_evaluation`"},"6591":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-68","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"`engine_deterministic`"},"6592":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-69","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#outcomes-are-written-back","content":"A model's verdict is never a label: an LLM evaluator's opinion is stored as a *feature* (`llm_proposed`) and refused\nas a training target. No user-facing feedback control exists — *helpful / wrong route* buttons are deferred to a\nfuture UX gate by the owner; everything above is captured from actions people already take."},"6593":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-70","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"The Resolver is the pack Flow `flw_tpl_auto_resolver` from **nexus-base**, published into a Project like any other.\nAuto calls it when the ranking finds nothing; it could equally be run by hand. It is made of the same parts as every\ncapability in Nexi and adds nothing to the platform."},"6594":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-71","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"Part"},"6595":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-72","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"Name"},"6596":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-73","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"What it contributes"},"6597":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-74","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"What it may not do"},"6598":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-75","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"**Agent**"},"6599":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-76","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"need-analyst"},"6600":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-77","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"Turns the message into a `NeedSpec` — goal, constraints (*never send or delete*), cadence, inputs — in a closed schema."},"6601":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-78","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"Hold a tool."},"6602":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-79","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"**Tools**"},"6603":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-80","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"`capability.inventory` · `rights.dryrun` · `state.read`"},"6604":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-81","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"What the Project has (agents, Flows, tools, connections), what the asker may do (core-api's PEP dry run), what exists already (a connection, a pending request). Run **as the asking human** — the survey sees only what they may see."},"6605":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-82","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"Change anything."},"6606":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-83","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"**Agent**"},"6607":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-84","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"resolution-planner"},"6608":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-85","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"Writes a `ResolutionPlan` of at most eight steps, each of a closed kind, preferring what exists in a signed pack, then in the Project, then a draft; each step names who must act."},"6609":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-86","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"Execute a step; mark a right."},"6610":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-87","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"**Gate**"},"6611":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-88","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"`plan.step`"},"6612":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-89","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"The engine attaches the rights chip to every step from the dry run — *you can · needs a Project owner · not possible* — before anyone sees the plan."},"6613":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-90","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"Trust the planner's opinion of rights."},"6614":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-91","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"**Approval**"},"6615":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-92","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"the asker"},"6616":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-93","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"The Propose card. Nothing runs, is created or requested before Accept. *Change* re-plans once. A viewer sees the card without buttons."},"6617":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-94","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"Be decided by anyone but the asker."},"6618":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-95","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"**Loop**"},"6619":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-96","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"Build"},"6620":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-97","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"One step per pass under the Blueprint budget — 8 iterations · 360 s · 60 k tokens · 20 cost units · 3 drafts · 3 requests. Executes **connect** (a connection request raised for the asker in NexCore) and **request\\_tool** (a governed CapabilityRequest to a Project owner); every other kind is *skipped — Nexi cannot do this kind of step yet*. Waits up to 7 days on a person; the same request is not raised twice within 24 h."},"6621":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-98","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/auto#the-resolver--a-flow-not-a-router","content":"Bind a tool, publish a Flow, install anything."},"6622":{"id":"/docs/technical/auto-99","page_id":"/docs/technical/auto","