hnical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#the-applications","content":"Service teams and their customers"},"6712":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-50","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#the-applications","content":"Module — C0 and Telegram approved, S3 preview (guide · how it works)"},"6713":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-51","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#the-applications","content":"**NexForge** · module"},"6714":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-52","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#the-applications","content":"Scenes shaped by hand, sentence or voice, projected as Board · Diagram · 3D · Present; one op engine, versions, a Scene Agent that proposes. `forge-api` over `nexus_forge`."},"6715":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-53","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#the-applications","content":"Architects, analysts, anyone who thinks in pictures"},"6716":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-54","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#the-applications","content":"Module — C0 approved, voice built (guide · how it works)"},"6717":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-55","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#the-applications","content":"**NexGraph**"},"6718":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-56","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#the-applications","content":"Knowledge you can check: sources with pinned versions, the pipeline as a receipt, Graph Studio, the Evidence Workspace, Review with the oracle-or-person gate, Vocabulary. A new version of a document is processed incrementally — unchanged text keeps its vectors, entities merge on their key, claims supersede or contest. NexChat answers from it."},"6719":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-57","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#the-applications","content":"Knowledge teams, everyone who asks"},"6720":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-58","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#the-applications","content":"Available (guide · how it works)"},"6721":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-59","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#the-applications","content":"Agents and Skills are cross-cutting: built once in NexChat, invoked from Chat, Spin, Tasks, BI and Graph — always\nwithin the current application's context and permissions, never with more access than the place you are in grants."},"6722":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-60","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#modules","content":"A module is a pack whose Blueprint layer declares `modules.enabled`. Installing it in NexCore is the whole act: the\nmodule's API opens its gate, the tile appears in every launcher, the content lives in the module's own database.\nRelations come from the NexChat Project the content belongs to; the suite never depends on a module."},"6723":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-61","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#a-message-becomes-an-answer","content":"The same model can replay a scenario step by step. This is what happens between pressing Enter in NexChat and\nreading the reply — and, below it, what happens when the message is spoken and is a command."},"6724":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-62","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#a-message-becomes-an-answer","content":"For inline sequence and flow diagrams inside chapters we use plain Markdown — for example, the same scenario in a\ncompact form:"},"6725":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-63","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#where-the-pictures-come-from","content":"The architecture views are generated from a text model (`architecture/*.c4`) and rendered as interactive\ndiagrams in the page. The model is reviewed like code; there is no drawing tool and no image file to go stale."},"6726":{"id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built-64","page_id":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/how-nexus-is-built#where-the-pictures-come-from","content":"Inline diagrams in chapters are fenced ` ```mermaid ` blocks in the Markdown source, rendered in your browser in\nthe Nexi colours. Each diagram carries a text alternative (*Diagram as text*)."},"6727":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","type":"page","content":"The knowledge graph — how a document becomes knowledge you can check","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Technical documentation","Building blocks"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph"},"6728":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-0","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","content":"Tiers, layers and stores; the six-stage pipeline; the oracle-or-person gate; incremental versions; and how NexChat answers from the graph under the asker's own rights. Continued with the Acme Logistics example."},"6729":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-1","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"Three questions every object answers"},"6730":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-2","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"The objects, from bytes to facts"},"6731":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-3","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"The pipeline: six stages, one receipt"},"6732":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-4","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-gate-oracles-first-people-second-models-never","content":"The gate: oracles first, people second, models never"},"6733":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-5","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#versions-incremental-and-current-only","content":"Versions: incremental, and current-only"},"6734":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-6","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"Rights: the allowed subgraph"},"6735":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-7","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"Answering from the graph: resolve"},"6736":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-8","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#memory-what-flows-produced-as-proposals","content":"Memory: what Flows produced, as proposals"},"6737":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-9","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"Where the pieces run"},"6738":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-10","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-same-picture-in-the-architecture","content":"The same picture in the architecture"},"6739":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-11","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","content":"Ontology ended on a promise: a claim moves from *what was written* to *what a model thinks it means* to\n*what your organization treats as true* only through a gate, and a model can never open that gate itself. NexGraph is\nwhere that promise is kept — for whole documents, at scale, with a pipeline you can read step by step. This page\nexplains the model behind the screens the NexGraph guide walks through: what is stored where, who\nis allowed to write what, and how a question in NexChat comes back with evidence rather than confidence."},"6740":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-12","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","content":"We keep the guide's example: **Acme Logistics**, a Project called *Data science*, a quarterly delivery report with a\nnumeric table and a transport agreement with its carrier *Northwind Traders*."},"6741":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-13","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"Every object in the graph — a page, a fragment, a mention, an entity, a claim — answers three questions, and the\nanswers are independent of each other:"},"6742":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-14","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"Question"},"6743":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-15","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"Answer"},"6744":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-16","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"Values"},"6745":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-17","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"**Whose is it?** — the *tier*"},"6746":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-18","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"Which audience may ever see it."},"6747":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-19","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"**Project** · **Organization** · **Personal** · **Base** (the platform's own documentation, readable by everyone, editable by no one)"},"6748":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-20","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"**How far has it come?** — the *layer*"},"6749":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-21","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"How much interpretation it carries and who did it."},"6750":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-22","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"**Lexical** — literally what was written · **Subject** — what a model proposes it means · **Domain** — what an oracle or a person decided"},"6751":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-23","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"**Where is it kept?** — the *store*"},"6752":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-24","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"The physical shape, all inside PostgreSQL."},"6753":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-25","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"**Bronze** — raw bytes in the object store · **Silver** — fragments, mentions, vectors in pgvector · **Gold** — entities and verified facts in Apache AGE"},"6754":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-26","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#three-questions-every-object-answers","content":"The tier is set once, when a source is bound to a Project, and is **never widened** by anything downstream: not by a\npipeline, not by a Flow that used the document, not by an answer that cited it. The layer is where the gate lives.\nThe store is an implementation detail you meet in Graph Studio's *Datastores* table and nowhere else."},"6755":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-27","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Object"},"6756":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-28","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Layer"},"6757":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-29","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"What it is"},"6758":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-30","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Where the guide shows it"},"6759":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-31","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"**Source binding**"},"6760":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-32","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"—"},"6761":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-33","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"A place NexGraph may read from, bound to one Project: an Upload box, a Server folder, a Google Drive folder. Five states: Connection · Reachability · Content · Access (ACL) · Processing."},"6762":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-34","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Add a source"},"6763":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-35","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"**Source version**"},"6764":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-36","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Bronze"},"6765":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-37","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"One pinned set of bytes with its SHA-256. The identity of a document. A changed file is a *new* version; the earlier one stays, marked superseded."},"6766":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-38","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Sources → Documents (`v1`)"},"6767":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-39","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"**Document item**"},"6768":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-40","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Lexical"},"6769":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-41","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"A heading, paragraph, table, cell, figure, code block or formula on a page — with its span. Produced by the parser."},"6770":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-42","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Read the evidence"},"6771":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-43","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"**Fragment**"},"6772":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-44","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Lexical"},"6773":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-45","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"A chunk of items sized for retrieval, embedded once per (text hash, model)."},"6774":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-46","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Studio → Sources lane"},"6775":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-47","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"**Mention**"},"6776":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-48","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Subject"},"6777":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-49","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"A span the extractor labelled (&#x2A;organization · person · amount · date …*) with a score. &#x2A;A proposal.*"},"6778":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-50","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Evidence panel → *Score 89 % · gliner-x · zero-shot*"},"6779":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-51","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"**Entity · term**"},"6780":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-52","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Subject"},"6781":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-53","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"What mentions resolve to across documents. In Vocabulary, a *term in use*."},"6782":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-54","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Vocabulary"},"6783":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-55","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"**Claim**"},"6784":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-56","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Subject → Domain"},"6785":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-57","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"A numeric statement read from a table cell: metric, value, locator, source assertion. Status *proposed → verified / falsified*; *contested*; *superseded*; *needs re-verification*."},"6786":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-58","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Review claims"},"6787":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-59","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"**Verified fact**"},"6788":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-60","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Domain"},"6789":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-61","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"A claim after the gate, with every verdict in its history."},"6790":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-62","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Studio → Knowledge lane"},"6791":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-63","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"**Evidence span**"},"6792":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-64","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"—"},"6793":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-65","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"The pointer every object carries back to its item, with a precision: *Exact span · Approximate location · Document-level · Unresolved*."},"6794":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-66","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Evidence tab of a claim"},"6795":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-67","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-objects-from-bytes-to-facts","content":"Two of these deserve a sentence. The **source assertion** is kept separately from the **canonical claim** the Project\nagrees on: when a second document states a different figure for the same metric and period, the two assertions stay\nand the canonical claim becomes *contested* — nothing is silently overwritten. And a **mention** is never promoted:\nentities are Subject-layer objects for good; only *claims* cross into Domain, because only claims can be checked."},"6796":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-68","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"Every source version runs through the same six stages. The worker is a **Dagster** code location with one\npartitioned asset per stage and one partition per source version; a sensor scans continuous sources (server folders,\nDrive) about every minute and places an order for each new or changed file."},"6797":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-69","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"Stage"},"6798":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-70","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"Executor"},"6799":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-71","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"Reads"},"6800":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-72","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"Writes"},"6801":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-73","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"Never"},"6802":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-74","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"**Snapshot**"},"6803":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-75","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"Pipeline engine"},"6804":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-76","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"the order"},"6805":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-77","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"the pinned bytes, sanity-checked (size, type)"},"6806":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-78","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"alters the bytes"},"6807":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-79","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"**Structure**"},"6808":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-80","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"Docling (parser)"},"6809":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-81","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"Bronze"},"6810":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-82","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"pages, items, tables with cells, figures; fragments"},"6811":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-83","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"interprets"},"6812":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-84","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"**Extraction**"},"6813":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-85","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"GLiNER-X (extractor)"},"6814":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-86","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"items"},"6815":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-87","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"mentions with label and score; `decision_id` per choice"},"6816":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-88","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"verifies"},"6817":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-89","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"**Subject graph**"},"6818":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-90","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"Pipeline engine"},"6819":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-91","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"mentions, tables"},"6820":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-92","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"entities (resolved on their key), co-mention edges, numeric observations, *proposed* claims"},"6821":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-93","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"decides"},"6822":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-94","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"**Verification**"},"6823":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-95","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"Oracles (`graph-oracle-calc@1.0.0`)"},"6824":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-96","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"claims, cells"},"6825":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-97","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"verdicts *verified / falsified / undecided*; reconciliation with earlier versions"},"6826":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-98","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"uses a model"},"6827":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-99","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"**Index**"},"6828":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-100","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"Qwen3 embedding via Synapse · Knowledge store"},"6829":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-101","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"fragments, entities, facts"},"6830":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-102","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"vectors (reused when the text hash is known), the AGE graph; retires older versions from retrieval"},"6831":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-103","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"embeds twice"},"6832":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-104","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-pipeline-six-stages-one-receipt","content":"The run page in NexGraph renders the worker's own **RunStep** records — executor kind and version, timings, produced\ncounts, structured log lines — so what you read there is the receipt, not a summary. *Retry failed stages* re-runs\nfrom the failed stage against the same bytes and is idempotent: a step that would produce an object that already\nexists recognises it."},"6833":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-105","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-gate-oracles-first-people-second-models-never","content":"Two deterministic **oracles** run over every claim:"},"6834":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-106","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-gate-oracles-first-people-second-models-never","content":"**Transcription** re-reads the value from the parsed cell the claim points at. Equal → *verified*; different →\n*falsified*; cell gone (a new version) → *undecided*."},"6835":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-107","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-gate-oracles-first-people-second-models-never","content":"**Arithmetic** applies to tables with a *Total* row or column: the total must equal the sum of its parts within\nhalf of the last printed digit per part. A total that checks out verifies itself *and* its components; a total that\ndoes not falsifies both; a table without totals leaves the check unrun."},"6836":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-108","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-gate-oracles-first-people-second-models-never","content":"A claim is *falsified* if any check falsifies it, *verified* if transcription verified it and arithmetic verified it\nor did not run, otherwise *proposed* — for a person. In the Acme report the *Shipments*, *On time* and *Late* columns\nsum, so fifteen claims are verified by machine; the *On-time rate* column has a Total row that is a **ratio**, not a\nsum, so the oracle — which knows nothing of ratios — falsifies those five. That is the oracle being honest about the\nlimit of what it can check, and exactly the case a **curator** exists for."},"6837":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-109","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#the-gate-oracles-first-people-second-models-never","content":"A curator (a person with the editor relation) decides within a **named scope**: *transcription + arithmetic — not the\nsupplier's performance*. The decision is an **OracleRun** of type *human\\_review* with a human actor, and a decision\nrecord whose outcome — `label_source = human_explicit` — is written back to the extractor's original `decision_id`.\nAgents and services are refused (`AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN`), whatever relation their owner holds; the Base tier is never\nverifiable by a tenant. Every verdict names its author or oracle version, and nothing is erased: the oracle's\n*falsified* stays as the first line of a claim's history under the curator's *confirmed*."},"6838":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-110","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#versions-incremental-and-current-only","content":"A source version is identified by its bytes. Upload the same report twice and nothing happens; change one paragraph\nand a `v2` appears beside `v1`:"},"6839":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-111","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#versions-incremental-and-current-only","content":"**Structure** re-parses everything (parsing is cheap); **Index** re-embeds only fragments whose text hash has no\nvector yet under the same model — one changed paragraph, one embedding."},"6840":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-112","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#versions-incremental-and-current-only","content":"**Entities** merge on their resolution key, so *Northwind Traders GmbH* in `v2` is the same entity as in `v1`."},"6841":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-113","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#versions-incremental-and-current-only","content":"**Claims** are reconciled: a claim of `v2` with the same locator and value keeps its verdict; a changed value\n*supersedes* the old claim and reopens verification; a *different source* with a different value *contests* both."},"6842":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-114","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#versions-incremental-and-current-only","content":"After a successful Index, `v1` is **retired** from retrieval — its fragments flagged, its vectors removed — so an\nanswer never cites a superseded page. The version itself stays readable, with its provenance, from Sources →\nDocuments."},"6843":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-115","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"NexGraph has no rights of its own. What you see is your **Project relation** — owner, editor, viewer, agent member,\nfetched from NexChat's Projects — intersected with the scope you chose. Three consequences:"},"6844":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-116","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"**Administering is not reading.** An organization administrator without a Project relation sees the operational\nview (bindings, grants, budgets, run health) and no document names, counts of knowledge or content."},"6845":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-117","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"**A wider scope never widens rights.** *All knowledge* is the union of your relations plus the Base tier; it adds\nProjects you already hold, never ones you do not."},"6846":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-118","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"**Every hop is checked.** Graph Studio's neighbourhoods, Review's queue and resolve's candidates are filtered at\ngraph-api's enforcement point object by object; a neighbour you may not read is dropped and *counted* as truncated,\nnever shown by name. The worker runs under its own database role with row-level security and can only read the\nProject its order names."},"6847":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-119","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"Relation"},"6848":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-120","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"May"},"6849":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-121","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"**Viewer / member**"},"6850":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-122","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"Read Overview, Studio, documents, claims, vocabulary; ask (resolve)."},"6851":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-123","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"**Editor / builder**"},"6852":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-124","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"Plus add, pause, resume and revoke sources; upload; retry and pause runs; verify and return claims; propose merges and terms; download; publish datasets."},"6853":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-125","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"**Owner**"},"6854":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-126","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"Plus publish vocabulary snapshots and set the Project's capture policy."},"6855":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-127","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"**Agent / service**"},"6856":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-128","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#rights-the-allowed-subgraph","content":"Read-only within the person's Projects; never create bindings, verify or publish."},"6857":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-129","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"NexChat does not search the graph; it asks graph-api to **resolve** a question into an **evidence bundle** — under\nthe asker's identity, with the question passed *by reference* (a `nexus://chat/message/…` URI graph-api reads under\nthe same rights), never as text. The ladder the *How this was found* drawer shows is the algorithm:"},"6858":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-130","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"Step"},"6859":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-131","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"What it does"},"6860":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-132","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"**Anchoring terms**"},"6861":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-133","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"The question's n-grams are matched to entities — the anchors for a graph hop."},"6862":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-134","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"**Semantic search** · **Keyword search**"},"6863":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-135","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"Dense (pgvector) and lexical (PostgreSQL full-text) retrieval over current fragments."},"6864":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-136","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"**Merging**"},"6865":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-137","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"Reciprocal-rank fusion, with a quota for the dense list."},"6866":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-138","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"**Following the graph**"},"6867":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-139","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"Fragments reached from the anchors' mentions."},"6868":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-140","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"**Verified claims**"},"6869":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-141","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"Up to two Gold claims of the anchored entities, with their verdicts."},"6870":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-142","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"**Access check**"},"6871":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-143","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"Per-candidate enforcement; retired versions dropped; the count of what was excluded is kept."},"6872":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-144","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"**Reranking**"},"6873":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-145","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"A reranker model (Qwen3-Reranker, through the Synapse Model Gateway) scores each candidate against the question; pairs capped by the time budget."},"6874":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-146","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"**Shaping the bundle**"},"6875":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-147","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"Items, claims and up to two figures of the cited sections, each with `why` (arms, ranks, band, hop, anchor)."},"6876":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-148","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"**Sufficiency**"},"6877":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-149","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"*Confident*, *tentative* or *empty*, calibrated on the reranker's scores. A spent budget degrades the bundle; it never empties it."},"6878":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-150","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#answering-from-the-graph-resolve","content":"chat-api then prompts the model with the bundle and streams the reply through a filter that removes any `[n]` the\nbundle cannot back and any image that is not a bundle figure; a *tentative* bundle adds a caution; an *empty* one makes\nthe model say what is missing. The route, the anchoring, the reranking and the sufficiency are each a decision\nrecord; your *Regenerate*, *Stop* or the model's own `[insufficient]` are written back as outcomes."},"6879":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-151","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#memory-what-flows-produced-as-proposals","content":"A Project's **capture policy** (owner-only; *Off · Explicit · Outcomes · Conversation*) decides whether the results of\nAgent and Flow runs — and, if chosen, conversation content — are recorded as *proposed* knowledge. chat-api's outbox\nrelays the completion events to graph-api's inbound door; graph-api records a **capture** under the Project's\nclassification and with the audience of the people who could see the source, never wider. A completed Flow certifies\nnothing: a captured outcome is a Subject-layer claim like any other and reaches Domain only through Review. This\nsurface is documented as a preview in the guide."},"6880":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-152","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"Piece"},"6881":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-153","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"Runs as"},"6882":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-154","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"Talks to"},"6883":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-155","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"**NexGraph** (web)"},"6884":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-156","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"a Next.js application on its own origin, proxying to graph-api, chat-api and core-api"},"6885":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-157","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"the browser never talks to another origin"},"6886":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-158","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"**graph-api**"},"6887":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-159","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"a FastAPI service owning the `nexus_graph` database as role `graph_api` (row-level security applies)"},"6888":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-160","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"core-api for session assertions and Project relations · Synapse for the reranker · NATS for events"},"6889":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-161","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"**graph-worker**"},"6890":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-162","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"a Dagster code location (`dagster dev` on a laptop; a Deployment in Kubernetes) as role `graph_worker`"},"6891":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-163","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"`nexus_graph` · Synapse for embeddings · NexCore's content door for Drive"},"6892":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-164","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"**Specialists**"},"6893":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-165","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"Docling and GLiNER-X inside the worker's process (an opt-in extra of \\~2 GB; without it a *Fixture specialist* stands in)"},"6894":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-166","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"—"},"6895":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-167","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"**Reranker · embedding**"},"6896":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-168","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"models registered in NexCore's Model Fabric (a local `llama-server --reranking`, `qwen3-embedding-0.6b`), reached only through the Model Gateway"},"6897":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-169","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"—"},"6898":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-170","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"**Dagster UI**"},"6899":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-171","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"for operators only, never a Nexi surface; every fact of a run is also in the run page"},"6900":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-172","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"—"},"6901":{"id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph-173","page_id":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/knowledge-graph#where-the-pieces-run","content":"The Deployment guide has the ports and the ladder from laptop to cluster."},"6902":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","type":"page","content":"Modules — packs that add an application","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Technical documentation","Applications"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/modules"},"6903":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-0","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules","content":"How NexMap, NexCare and NexForge are installed per organization as signed packs, how a module API decides whether it may answer at all, where a module takes its relations and data from, and what the suite never depends on."},"6904":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-1","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"A module is a pack resource"},"6905":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-2","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/modules#the-module-gate","content":"The module gate"},"6906":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-3","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-a-module-owns-and-what-it-borrows","content":"What a module owns and what it borrows"},"6907":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-4","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/modules#deployment","content":"Deployment"},"6908":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-5","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-is-deliberately-not-here","content":"What is deliberately not here"},"6909":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-6","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/modules#where-to-read-more","content":"Where to read more"},"6910":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-7","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules","content":"The six suite applications — Home, NexChat, VibeBan, NexBI, NexGraph, NexCore — every organization has. A\n**module** is an application an organization turns on: today **NexMap**, **NexCare** and\n**NexForge**. Nothing about a module is special at runtime — it is a web app, an API, a worker and a\ndatabase like the others — except one thing: it answers only when the organization's Blueprint says so."},"6911":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-8","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"A pack (`packs/nexus-map`, `packs/nexus-care`, `packs/nexus-forge&#x60;) is a signed bundle of agents, skills, flows,\ntemplates, policies and a Blueprint layer — the same artefact NexCore installs for any capability bundle. A module pack\nadds one resource of kind &#x2A;*`module`** (`module/<id>.json`, contract `pack-module`): the module id, the apps and\nservices it brings, where its tile goes (`visibility.launcher.app_id`), its accent token, what it requires of the\nplatform (`requires.platform_tools`, e.g. `task.create`). Its Blueprint layer sets"},"6912":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-9","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"and that field is the whole switch. `Blueprint.modules {enabled[], disabled[]}` is part of the Blueprint contract; a\nProject layer may **disable** a module the organization enabled, never enable one it did not."},"6913":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-10","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"Pack"},"6914":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-11","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"Brings"},"6915":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-12","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"Installs into"},"6916":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-13","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"Guide"},"6917":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-14","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"`nexus-map` 1.0.0"},"6918":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-15","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"Blueprint layer · `map-geofence-notify` Flow template · the vocabulary of positions"},"6919":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-16","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"`apps/map` :3217 · `map-api` :3207 · `nexus_map` (PostGIS)"},"6920":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-17","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"NexMap"},"6921":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-18","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"`nexus-care` 1.0.0"},"6922":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-19","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"1 agent · 4 skills · 3 flows · 3 guardrail profiles · Blueprint layer"},"6923":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-20","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"`apps/care` :3218 · `care-api` :3208 · `care-worker` · `nexus_care`"},"6924":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-21","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"NexCare"},"6925":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-22","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"`nexus-forge` 1.0.0"},"6926":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-23","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"1 agent (Scene Agent) · 1 skill · 5 scene templates · confirmation-level policy · Blueprint layer"},"6927":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-24","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"`apps/forge` :3219 · `forge-api` :3209 · `nexus_forge`"},"6928":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-25","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"NexForge"},"6929":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-26","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#a-module-is-a-pack-resource","content":"The marketplace is deliberately small: **search · import · install · remove**, over a local catalogue of\nsigned files; there is no remote registry. Removing a pack flips the switch back and keeps the module's\ncontent read-only in its database; nothing is deleted."},"6930":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-27","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#the-module-gate","content":"Every module API runs three doors in order on every route:"},"6931":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-28","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#the-module-gate","content":"**Session assertion** — the core-api session, or 401."},"6932":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-29","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#the-module-gate","content":"**Module gate** — `GET {core-api}/blueprints/service/effective?tenant_id=…` as the module's service identity\n(`svc_map_api`, `svc_care_api`, `svc_forge_api`, each with `blueprint.read`). *Enabled* is cached for at most\n**60 s**, *disabled* for at most **5 s*&#x2A;; an absent field, a non-200, an expired cache with core-api\nunreachable all yield &#x2A;*`MODULE_STATE_UNKNOWN`** → 403. There is no \"base pack floor\": an uncertain gate is a\nclosed gate. Reasons are a closed set: `module_not_enabled · module_disabled_by_project · module_forbidden_by_policy\n· module_state_unknown`."},"6933":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-30","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#the-module-gate","content":"**PEP** — the module's own action vocabulary (`MapPepAction` 17, `CarePepAction`, `ForgePepAction` 10) decided\nagainst **Project relations read from chat-api** (`POST /internal/grounding/project-relations`): a module\nhas no membership model of its own; sharing *is* NexChat Project membership. An Organization Admin without a\nrelation gets `NO_PROJECT_RELATION` 403; content of a Project you do not hold answers 404."},"6934":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-31","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#the-module-gate","content":"The web app renders the gate's refusal as one state — *NexMap is not enabled for your organization* / *NexCare isn't\nenabled for this organization* / *NexForge is not enabled here* — with a link to Blueprints & Packs. The App Launcher\ndraws the tile only when the effective Blueprint lists the module; a missing module has no tile at all, never a greyed\none."},"6935":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-32","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-a-module-owns-and-what-it-borrows","content":"Owns"},"6936":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-33","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-a-module-owns-and-what-it-borrows","content":"Borrows"},"6937":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-34","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-a-module-owns-and-what-it-borrows","content":"Its database (`nexus_map` · `nexus_care` · `nexus_forge`), every table keyed `(tenant_id, id)` with row-level security **forced** under the `nexus.tenant_id` GUC"},"6938":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-35","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-a-module-owns-and-what-it-borrows","content":"Identity and session from core-api"},"6939":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-36","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-a-module-owns-and-what-it-borrows","content":"Its API and its action vocabulary"},"6940":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-37","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-a-module-owns-and-what-it-borrows","content":"Relations from the NexChat Project"},"6941":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-38","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-a-module-owns-and-what-it-borrows","content":"Its decision kinds (`MapDecisionKind` 7 · twelve Care kinds · `ForgeDecisionKind` 8) and `decision_records` / `decision_outcomes` tables — with a CHECK that makes `llm_proposed` unrepresentable as a label"},"6942":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-39","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-a-module-owns-and-what-it-borrows","content":"The Model Gateway (NexCare's assistant, NexForge's Scene Agent and dictation)"},"6943":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-40","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-a-module-owns-and-what-it-borrows","content":"Its worker, if any (`care-worker`: SLA clock, channel ingestion, retention export, NexBI datasets)"},"6944":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-41","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-a-module-owns-and-what-it-borrows","content":"Policy, audit sink, the `nexus_app_kernel` package (clock · ids · classification · errors · security · tuning · lexicon)"},"6945":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-42","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-a-module-owns-and-what-it-borrows","content":"Its service identity in `config/security/service-identities.yaml`"},"6946":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-43","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-a-module-owns-and-what-it-borrows","content":"VibeBan for work items (Care cases), NexGraph for knowledge, NexBI for datasets"},"6947":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-44","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-a-module-owns-and-what-it-borrows","content":"Production configuration refuses the development doubles: `SESSION_DRIVER=mock`, `MODULE_GATE_DRIVER=static`,\n`AUTHZ_MODE=embedded` outside dev/test, demo worlds (`MAP_DEMO_WORLD`, `CARE_DEMO_WORLD`, `FORGE_DEMO_WORLD`)."},"6948":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-45","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#deployment","content":"Modules are **profiles**: `deploy/contract.yaml` lists `map-api`, `care-api`, `forge-api` under `profile: map | care |\nforge`; Compose runs `migrate-<module>` + `<module>-api` only with the profile; Helm has `map.enabled`,\n`care.enabled`, `forge.enabled`, all **off by default**, with a NetworkPolicy allowing egress to postgres, core-api and\nchat-api only. The dev stack starts all three (`scripts/dev-stack.sh`). PostGIS joins AGE and pgvector in the one\nPostgreSQL image (`deploy/docker/postgres/Dockerfile` — GPL at the database-process boundary). See\nDeploy for the ladder."},"6949":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-46","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-is-deliberately-not-here","content":"A module cannot enable itself, bind a capability or publish — only a person installing a pack (ADR-0023 §9)."},"6950":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-47","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-is-deliberately-not-here","content":"The suite never imports a module: no `svc_map_api` in graph-api, no Care noun in chat-api's Auto, no Forge\n`ArtifactType` in NexChat. Doors go the other way — *Ask in Chat*, *Open in Graph*, *Open in VibeBan*\n— as links and references, never copies."},"6951":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-48","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#what-is-deliberately-not-here","content":"No remote marketplace, no auto-update, no unsigned import."},"6952":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-49","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#where-to-read-more","content":"Install a module — the chapter."},"6953":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-50","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#where-to-read-more","content":"NexMap · NexCare · NexForge — each module inside."},"6954":{"id":"/docs/technical/modules-51","page_id":"/docs/technical/modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/modules#where-to-read-more","content":"Access rights — the module rows and denied screens."},"6955":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","type":"page","content":"NexBI — governed numbers","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Technical documentation","Applications"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexbi"},"6956":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-0","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi","content":"How NexBI keeps numbers honest — datasets with immutable versions, a semantic model, a closed metric grammar, a governed query engine that compiles typed queries to parameterised SQL with the row policy before aggregation, dashboards as references rendered per viewer, templates and the Advisor as rules, automations as Flows — and where it sits between NexChat, NexGraph and Core."},"6957":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-1","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"The objects"},"6958":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-2","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-governed-query-engine","content":"The governed query engine"},"6959":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-3","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#dashboards-are-references-rendered-per-viewer","content":"Dashboards are references, rendered per viewer"},"6960":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-4","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-studio-a-plan-and-rules-not-a-model","content":"The Studio: a plan and rules, not a model"},"6961":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-5","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#automations-are-flows","content":"Automations are Flows"},"6962":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-6","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#between-the-applications","content":"Between the applications"},"6963":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-7","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#decision-data","content":"Decision data"},"6964":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-8","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#what-is-built-and-what-is-not","content":"What is built and what is not"},"6965":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-9","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#where-to-read-more","content":"Where to read more"},"6966":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-10","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi","content":"The NexBI chapters show the application from the outside. This page is the inside, and makes one point\nthroughout: &#x2A;*a number in Nexi is never a model's output.** A metric is a definition in a grammar the engine can\ncompile; a query is typed and becomes SQL the engine writes; a dashboard is a set of references resolved for the\nreader; certification, publication and revocation are human acts. Where a model appears — the NexChat data arm, the\nStudio's *Ask Nexi*, a proposed dashboard — it chooses *which* metric or template, in a recorded decision, and never\ncomputes."},"6967":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-11","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"Object"},"6968":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-12","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"What it is"},"6969":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-13","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"Immutable?"},"6970":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-14","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"Who changes its state"},"6971":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-15","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"**Dataset** · **DatasetVersion**"},"6972":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-16","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"A governed table in `nexus_bi` with a profile, quality checks (*ok · warnings · failed · no\\_data*) and a row policy. Sources: a CSV/XLSX upload (≤ 64 MiB · ≤ 5 M rows), a NexGraph Gold dataset version, an Agentic Data Scientist result, a Flow output. A **correction** is a new version with a note."},"6973":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-17","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"Every version"},"6974":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-18","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"A human editor publishes; a human owner revokes (a revoked version is never served again, and its dashboards say so)."},"6975":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-19","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"**Semantic model**"},"6976":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-20","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"Entities, dimensions, time dimensions and the row policy over a dataset — what a metric can be defined on."},"6977":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-21","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"Versioned with the dataset"},"6978":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-22","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"Editor."},"6979":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-23","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"**Metric**"},"6980":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-24","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"An `Expr` in the closed grammar — `aggregate · arithmetic · literal · filtered · window` — over one entity; a period default; optional target. Lifecycle *draft → validated → certified → deprecated*."},"6981":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-25","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"Definitions are versioned"},"6982":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-26","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"Editor proposes and validates (a test query must succeed); a **human steward** certifies with *I have reviewed the formula against the dataset schema*; deprecation keeps history."},"6983":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-27","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"**Query record**"},"6984":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-28","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"Every governed run: the BIQuery, the dataset version, the compiled SQL (readable by editors), rows scanned, time, the viewer's row-policy id. &#x2A;How was this calculated?*"},"6985":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-29","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"Yes"},"6986":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-30","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"The engine writes it; nobody edits it."},"6987":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-31","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"**Dashboard** · **DashboardVersion**"},"6988":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-32","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"A draft plus immutable published versions. Blocks are **references**: a KPI to a metric; a chart or table to a Project artifact with a `version_policy` (*follow\\_latest · follow\\_latest\\_approved · pin*); text and section blocks. A block carrying a spec copy is refused (*422 SPEC\\_COPY\\_REJECTED*)."},"6989":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-33","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"Every published version"},"6990":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-34","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"An editor edits the draft; a human with `dashboard.publish` publishes with *I have checked the numbers against their sources*."},"6991":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-35","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"**Template**"},"6992":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-36","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"From the signed **nexus-base** pack: *executive\\_overview · operational\\_control · performance\\_vs\\_target · risk\\_exceptions · data\\_overview*, plus the platform set (*nexus\\_quality · usage · infrastructure · graph · vibeban*). Slots are decision perspectives — *outcome · driver · volume · risk · target · what changed*."},"6993":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-37","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"Pack version"},"6994":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-38","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"Pack release."},"6995":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-39","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"**Automation**"},"6996":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-40","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"A row pointing at a Flow the person owns (`flow_ref`), of kind *refresh · metric\\_alert · subscription*, with schedule and params."},"6997":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-41","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"—"},"6998":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-42","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-objects","content":"The person publishes the Flow in Flow Studio; NexBI reflects its state."},"6999":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-43","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-governed-query-engine","content":"Five properties follow from this shape and are the reason for it:"},"7000":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-44","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-governed-query-engine","content":"**No text-to-SQL.** The only input is a typed `BIQuery`; the SQL is generated from the metric's `Expr` and the\nsemantic model, and every literal is a bound parameter. A model may pick the metric (a `metric_resolution` decision)\nor derive the filters from a sentence (`filter_derivation`); it never writes a clause."},"7001":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-45","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-governed-query-engine","content":"**The row policy is applied before aggregation.** A viewer who may not see *Region = North* gets a *sum* that never\nincluded it — not a filtered total. The same dashboard therefore shows different numbers to different people, by\ndesign, and the query record names the policy that applied."},"7002":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-46","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-governed-query-engine","content":"**Read-only by role, bounded by guards.** Queries run as the database role `bi_query` with no write grant; an\n`EXPLAIN` cost guard, an 8-second timeout and a 1 000-row ceiling bound every run. A dashboard refresh that would\nexceed them fails visibly rather than silently."},"7003":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-47","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-governed-query-engine","content":"**Cache per viewer.** Results are cached keyed by viewer, dataset version and query; a new version or a revocation\ninvalidates; nothing is served across people."},"7004":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-48","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-governed-query-engine","content":"**Every run leaves a record.** The Calculation row on a chart, &#x2A;How was this calculated?* on a KPI, and *View SQL*\nfor editors all read the same `QueryRecord`."},"7005":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-49","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#dashboards-are-references-rendered-per-viewer","content":"A published `DashboardVersion` holds no numbers and no chart specs — only references and layout. Rendering resolves\neach block for the reader: a KPI runs the governed query as them; a chart block resolves the artifact per its version\npolicy (*follow latest · follow latest approved · pin*), and the Updates mode shows which blocks are *behind*; a block\nwhose data the reader may not see **keeps its place and says so**, so two readers see the same shape and their own\nnumbers. The filter bar (period · grain · slices · compare) is state in the URL, applied to every block that can take\nit; a block that cannot says *Not filtered by X*. History lists the immutable versions; Pin freezes a version for a\nreader."},"7006":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-50","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#dashboards-are-references-rendered-per-viewer","content":"Three human acts frame a dashboard: **certification** of the metrics it shows (a steward), **publication** with the\nacknowledgement (a person with `dashboard.publish`), and — from NexChat — **acceptance** of a proposed dashboard\n(`dashboard_proposal`, S6b), which creates a draft and nothing more."},"7007":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-51","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#the-studio-a-plan-and-rules-not-a-model","content":"The Studio's intelligence is deliberately small and inspectable. **Plan**: the decision statement is stemmed and\nmatched against the templates' slot hints; the closest template is chosen and every slot is filled with the best\nvalidated metric or marked *no metric* / *no data* — a `dashboard_plan` decision with all template candidates and\ntheir scores, and the slots you keep or drop written back. **Coverage** compares the draft to the template's slots.\n**Advisor**: nine rules over the draft — *outcome without a driver · no target · no comparison · seasonality risk ·\nconcentration missing · period filter missing · refresh missing · alert missing · subscription missing* — each an\n`advisor_suggestion` decision whose outcome is your Apply or Dismiss, and each editing the **draft only**. *Ask\nNexi* in the Add panel hands a sentence to the NexChat data arm and takes back a draft chart; the Studio never calls a\nmodel itself."},"7008":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-52","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#automations-are-flows","content":"NexBI has no scheduler. *Refresh · Metric alert · Subscription* are Draft Flows instantiated from pack templates\n(`flw_tpl_bi_refresh · flw_tpl_bi_metric_alert · flw_tpl_bi_subscription`) into the Project, owned by the person who\npressed *Create*, published in Flow Studio under Flow rights. Their nodes call back into bi-api's S2S tools\n(`bi.dashboard.describe · bi.alert.evaluate · dataset.describe`) **asserting the owner as the human principal**, so\nevery run is bounded by that person's rights, and an alert or subscription is delivered only into a Project thread.\nAn `action` node is refused for these templates (*422*): they read and post. Each alert evaluation is an\n`alert_evaluation` decision (value · threshold · streak)."},"7009":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-53","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#between-the-applications","content":"**NexChat → NexBI.** The data arm calls the three S2S tools as `svc_chat_api` *asserting the human*; bi-api\nre-checks that human's rights — a service identity never widens what a person may see. The drafts come back to\nchat-api as artifacts (`/internal/artifacts/reference`), so a dashboard can later reference them."},"7010":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-54","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#between-the-applications","content":"**NexBI → NexChat.** Automations are instantiated, run and read through `/internal/flows/*`; events reach chat-api\nby an HTTP outbox relay every 5 s (`/internal/events`), so a dashboard *published* or an alert *fired* appears in the\nProject's activity."},"7011":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-55","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#between-the-applications","content":"**NexGraph → NexBI.** A Gold dataset version can be the source of a NexBI dataset; provenance stays a reference."},"7012":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-56","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#between-the-applications","content":"**Core.** Every operation names one PEP action (`dataset.read · query.run · dashboard.publish · metric.certify …`);\norganization scope (`/bi/organization/…`) maps *admin → owner, member → viewer* and seeds the platform dashboards from\nthe product-metrics measurement; an administrator without a Project relation sees counts and ids, never data\n(*Administering is not reading*)."},"7013":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-57","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#decision-data","content":"Eleven decision kinds are recorded — `intent_resolution · metric_resolution · chart_recommendation · dashboard_plan ·\nadvisor_suggestion · insight_selection · version_policy_default · alert_evaluation · filter_derivation ·\nmodel_proposal · dashboard_proposal` — each with its action space and score distribution, and seventeen outcome\nsignals written back by the actions that exist (accept, dismiss, publish, acknowledge, pin, reroute …). A record with\n`label_source = llm_proposed` as a training target is refused at the API. No feedback control exists in the UI."},"7014":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-58","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#what-is-built-and-what-is-not","content":"Slices 1–6a are approved (semantic layer and metrics · governed query and the data arm · dashboards · Studio ·\nautomations as Flows · organization scope · filter bar). **Dashboards from NexChat** (S6b — the proposal card, *Add to\ndashboard*) is built and presented, not yet accepted. **Insights** — trend · anomaly · comparison · source change — is\na prototype screen over fixture rows; its statistical engine and the `insight.compute` path are not built. The\nrelease image set (compose · Helm) does not yet include bi-api or the NexBI web; the Deploy ladder\nsays where it runs today."},"7015":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-59","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#where-to-read-more","content":"The chapters: Publish a dataset · Define and certify metrics · Read a dashboard · Build a dashboard · Automate a dashboard · Ask your data."},"7016":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-60","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#where-to-read-more","content":"The contract: BI API — 81 operations, tags *datasets · semantic · metrics · queries · dashboards · templates · automations · insights · overview · system*."},"7017":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexbi-61","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexbi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexbi#where-to-read-more","content":"The routing side: Auto — how Nexi picks the capability."},"7018":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","type":"page","content":"NexCare — service operations with a guardrail","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Technical documentation","Applications"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexcare"},"7019":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-0","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexcare","content":"How the Care module serves people outside the organization — a public edge in its own trust zone, an assistant that answers only from verified knowledge, the guardrail port on every turn, one reply authority at a time, Telegram through Synapse, cases as VibeBan work items — and what is still preview."},"7020":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-1","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#two-trust-zones","content":"Two trust zones"},"7021":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-2","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#guardrails","content":"Guardrails"},"7022":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-3","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#one-hand-on-the-reply","content":"One hand on the reply"},"7023":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-4","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#knowledge-agent-studio","content":"Knowledge, agent, Studio"},"7024":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-5","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#channels-telegram-through-synapse","content":"Channels: Telegram through Synapse"},"7025":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-6","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#cases-sla-quality-datasets","content":"Cases, SLA, Quality, datasets"},"7026":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-7","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#contracts-and-api","content":"Contracts and API"},"7027":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-8","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#deployment","content":"Deployment"},"7028":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-9","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#what-is-built-and-what-is-not","content":"What is built and what is not"},"7029":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-10","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexcare","content":"The NexCare chapters show the module from the outside. This page is the inside. NexCare\nis `apps/care`, `care-api`, `care-worker` and the `nexus_care` database, installed per organization as a pack\n(Modules). It is the first part of Nexi that talks to people who are **not members** of the organization,\nand that fact shapes everything: a separate trust zone for them, a guardrail on every turn, and a single hand on the\nreply."},"7030":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-11","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#two-trust-zones","content":"**Suite routes** (`/api/v1/care/*`) are what members use: core-api session assertion, module gate, PEP as\n`svc_care_api` over Care Project relations — the same three doors as every module."},"7031":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-12","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#two-trust-zones","content":"**The public edge** (`/api/v1/care/public/v1/*`) is what the widget and messengers reach, and it is independent of\nthe suite PEP. An anonymous visitor gets a **care session** bearer — `POST /sessions` mints it only when the\nrequest's `Origin` is in the installation's `allowed_origins`; the token is stored hashed, slides 60 minutes, lives\n24 hours at most; every mismatch is the same `403 ORIGIN_NOT_ALLOWED` so nothing can be enumerated. The iframe is\nserved with `Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors <allowed_origins>` per installation. Rate limits are\nper installation (60 sessions/min), per session (12 turns/min) and per client (40/min on a salted hash of the IP — the\nIP is never stored); a turn is at most 4 000 characters. The actor type for a customer is `external`."},"7032":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-13","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#two-trust-zones","content":"The loader (`GET /widget/v1/care.js`, under 10 KB, no framework) draws the launcher and mounts\n`/widget/v1/frame?installation=…`; both are Next routes in `apps/care` — there is no `/widget/v1/*` API."},"7033":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-14","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#guardrails","content":"`platform/guardrails` is a **platform port**, not a Care feature:\n`GuardrailPort.evaluate(stage, profile, subject, features)` with stages `input · retrieval · tool · output`, budgets\n400 ms (input, output) and 1.5 s (retrieval, tool), and every verdict written to the decision sink as a\n`guardrail_verdict`. Checks are deterministic: a forbidden-topic lexicon, PII and secret patterns, prompt-injection\nmarkers, a grounding threshold (`tuning.care.handoff.grounding_min`, 0.6), and a tool allow-list (the `tool` stage\nrejects anything outside the profile's `tools_allowed`). Profiles are pack resources\n(`packs/nexus-care/guardrails/*.json`, contract `guardrail-profile&#x60;): &#x2A;*`internal`*&#x2A; passes through by default,\n&#x2A;*`external_authenticated`*&#x2A; and &#x2A;*`external_public`** **fail closed** on timeout or engine error. The seams\nexist in the Model Gateway and the Agent Runtime; NexCare's public edge is where the external profiles bite today. A\nblock is a handover, not a wall: the customer reads &#x2A;I'm handing this over to a person…*, the desk reads a\n`guardrail-note` naming the rule. A red-team corpus runs in CI (`tests/redteam/corpus.jsonl`; expansion is open)."},"7034":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-15","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#one-hand-on-the-reply","content":"A conversation has a &#x2A;*`HandlerState`** — `AI_ACTIVE`, `HANDOFF_PENDING`, `HUMAN_ACTIVE` — held under a row lock\nExactly one of the assistant or the joined person may send to the customer; a send on a stale version answers\n`409 HANDLER_CHANGED`. **Join** moves authority to the person; **Return** gives it back; **Resolve** needs a reason\ncode from a closed taxonomy (`care-topic-taxonomy`; `422 TOPIC_REQUIRED`) because the reason feeds Quality and the\nNexBI datasets. Handoff is **conversation-based**: the customer asks in words, or policy decides, and the\nconversation waits for a Join — the customer keeps writing meanwhile. \"AI resolved\" is distinguished from \"AI\ncontained\". Customer identity verification is a deterministic code check, and a CRM identity match is a\n**human decision** (`POST …/identity/{link_id}/decide`) — the model never marks anyone verified."},"7035":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-16","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#knowledge-agent-studio","content":"The assistant is a governed **Agent** from the pack; Care Studio's *Assistant* tab is a business-user profile (name,\nlanguages, formality, warmth, brevity, greeting, sign-off, handoff phrase, never-answer topics) that **compiles** into\nan Agent draft a second person reviews before publish — the same rule as every agent. Retrieval reads the Care slice\nof NexGraph with `verified_only` true by default (`GET …/knowledge`, `KNOWLEDGE_SCOPE`); every answer names its\nclaims and versions, and the inspector's *Knowledge* tab shows them. Copilot suggestions to the joined person are\ndecision **features**, never labels."},"7036":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-17","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#channels-telegram-through-synapse","content":"A messenger is a Synapse integration with a `conversation_channel` block: `config/synapse/integrations/telegram.yaml`\ndeclares `auth: api_key`, `egress_hosts: [api.telegram.org]`, `{kind: messaging, ingress: poll}`. The bot token lives\nin the Credential Broker and never reaches care-api; core-api offers `GET /synapse/conversation-channels`,\n`POST /synapse/connections/{id}/channel/receive` and `…/channel/send` under the `channel.use` permission. care-api polls\nevery 3 s (`CARE_CHANNELS_POLL=1`, one poller per deployment — Helm requires 1 replica; webhook ingress and a leased\npoller are S4), finds or creates a `channel_session` per chat for 24 h, and the message lands on the same\ndesk with the chip *Telegram*. There is no Telegram SDK — the adapter in `platform/synapse/nexus_synapse/channels.py`\nspeaks the Bot API over HTTPS (`python-telegram-bot` was rejected as LGPL)."},"7037":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-18","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#cases-sla-quality-datasets","content":"Cases are **VibeBan work items** with a `case_extension`: care-api calls tasks-api's tool door as\n`svc_care_api`; the *Cases* screen is a door to VibeBan and closes when tasks-api is unreachable. Queues carry an SLA\npolicy (business hours, first/next response, resolution, at-risk %, pauses while waiting for the customer)\ndriven by `care-worker`'s clock (`CARE_SLA_CLOCK=1`, `POST /care/studio/sla/tick`). Quality reviews and surveys are\n**contract-only** today (`care-quality-review`, `care-survey`; the screen reads fixtures for now). Nine\ndatasets publish to NexBI through `dataset.publish` from the worker. Retention: messages 365 d, sessions 24 h,\ndecisions exported to the Gold `decision_dataset` before purge."},"7038":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-19","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#contracts-and-api","content":"Eighteen schemas (`care-service-conversation`, `care-message`, `care-widget-installation`, `care-session`,\n`care-external-identity`, `care-identity-link`, `care-handler-transition`, `care-topic-taxonomy`, `care-incident`,\n`care-service-queue`, `care-sla-policy`, `care-case-extension`, `care-quality-review`, `care-survey`,\n`care-channel-session`, `care-events` — 21 `nexus.care.*.v1` events — `guardrail-profile`, `guardrail-decision`),\ncontracts 1.107.0. Routers: public edge (`sessions · turns (JSON or SSE) · verify · handoff · cases · history ·\nknowledge`), conversations (`overview · conversations · transition · messages · topic · topics · studio/installations`),\nchannels (`channels · channels/{id}/pull`), identity, cases/SLA (S3), system. **No `nexus-care-v1.openapi.yaml` is\ncommitted**; FastAPI serves `/docs` on :3208."},"7039":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-20","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#deployment","content":"Web :3218, API :3208, demo host :3219 (`/widget/v1/demo`), worker; database `nexus_care` (Alembic `0001`, RLS FORCE on\nevery tenant table). Compose `docker-compose.care.yml` profile `care`; Helm `care.enabled` (off), `careApi.publicOrigin`,\n`channelsPoll`, Secret `care-client-hash-salt`. Demo: `CARE_DEMO_WORLD=1` seeds the SupplyChain Guru organization,\n*Nova*, two installations and the OTP `482913` — refused in production."},"7040":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexcare-21","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexcare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexcare#what-is-built-and-what-is-not","content":"Approved: C0 (widget · desk · handover · guardrails) and S2 (Telegram). In the tree, **preview**: S3 — cases, identity\ndecisions, queues, SLA. Not yet: quality and survey tables, webhook ingress, Ukrainian and German suite i18n for\n`care.*`, a larger red-team corpus, an OpenAPI file."},"7041":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","type":"page","content":"NexForge — a scene, not a drawing","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Technical documentation","Applications"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexforge"},"7042":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-0","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge","content":"How the Forge module keeps one structured Scene behind four views, compiles every hand — pointer, sentence, voice, agent — into the same closed operations with inverses and versions, lets an agent propose but never apply, treats voice as dictation or command, and records every choice."},"7043":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-1","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#the-object","content":"The object"},"7044":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-2","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#one-edit-language","content":"One edit language"},"7045":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-3","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#the-turn","content":"The turn"},"7046":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-4","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#voice-dictation-is-not-a-command","content":"Voice: dictation is not a command"},"7047":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-5","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#who-may-do-what","content":"Who may do what"},"7048":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-6","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#decision-data","content":"Decision data"},"7049":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-7","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#api-and-tables","content":"API and tables"},"7050":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-8","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#deployment-and-oss","content":"Deployment and OSS"},"7051":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-9","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#what-is-built-and-what-is-not","content":"What is built and what is not"},"7052":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-10","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge","content":"The NexForge chapters show the module from the outside. This page is the inside. NexForge\nis `apps/forge` over `forge-api` and the `nexus_forge` database, installed per organization as a pack\n(Modules). ADR-0056 fixes the object and the engine, ADR-0057 the turn pipeline and the agent. The\nsentence that organises both: **AI proposes, the person applies**."},"7053":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-11","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#the-object","content":"A **Scene** (`nexus://forge/scene/<id>&#x60;) belongs to a NexChat Project and carries one **`SceneSpec` 1.0**: a\ncoordinate system (`unit px|m|cm`, `up_axis z`), `layers[]`, `objects[]`, `relations[]`, `groups[]`, `cameras[]`,\n`views`, a `color_key`, `bindings[]` and `tracks[]`. A **SceneObject** has a `kind` (sticky · text · shape · image ·\nframe · node), a shape, a real **transform** (`position {x, y, z}`, `rotation_deg`) and **geometry** (`width, depth,\nheight`, a primitive box · cylinder · wedge · plane), a `style` (eight hues or none, tint/solid/outline,\nthin/thick/dashed — colour is scene data) and a `semantic.type` from twenty-six closed types. Relations have\nnine kinds; bindings seven (`work_item · flow · artifact · claim · dataset · agent · map_feature`) and are references\nonly. A view is a **projection** of this one spec: switching views is not an operation and the version does not move.\nThe 3D view says *Conceptual* on screen and in every export."},"7054":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-12","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#one-edit-language","content":"Every hand — pointer, keyboard, touch, typed sentence, voice, agent, import — produces **`SceneOp`s**\n(`forge-scene-op.schema.json`): `{op_id, kind, target_ids[], payload, source}` with `source ∈ manual · keyboard · touch\n· typed · voice · agent · import · system` and **26 kinds** (`add · update · move · resize · transform · set_style ·\nset_color_key · connect · disconnect · group · ungroup · set_layer · set_visibility · set_lock · set_semantic ·\nset_property · bind · unbind · set_camera · add_track_step · delete · restore · layout · reorder · undo · redo`). No op\ncarries an utterance or a prompt."},"7055":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-13","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#one-edit-language","content":"The engine (`scenes/engine.py`, pure `apply_batch(spec, ops, limits)`):"},"7056":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-14","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#one-edit-language","content":"validates every op (payload, target exists, nothing locked, `max_objects` 5 000, `ops_per_batch` 500) and applies\n**all or nothing** — `OpsRejected` lists every reason;"},"7057":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-15","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#one-edit-language","content":"computes a per-op **inverse** from the pre-state and stores it; `undo`/`redo` replay the actor's **own** batches\n(depth 100);"},"7058":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-16","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#one-edit-language","content":"makes one batch one immutable &#x2A;*`SceneVersion`** (JSON spec + sha256); `restore {n}` is a *new* version equal to n —\nhistory is append-only;"},"7059":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-17","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#one-edit-language","content":"refuses a batch whose `base_version ≠ current` with `409 SCENE_VERSION_CONFLICT {current_version, since_ops[]}`;\n`(scene_id, request_id)` replays return the original result;"},"7060":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-18","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#one-edit-language","content":"`publish` marks a version for the (future) graph projection."},"7061":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-19","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#one-edit-language","content":"**Confirmation levels** (`packs/nexus-forge/policies/forge-confirmation.json`; a Blueprint may only raise): 1 —\nmove, resize, transform, style, colour key, layer, visibility, lock, camera, undo, redo, reorder apply at once with an\nUndo line; 2 — add, update, connect, group, semantic, property, track step, layout show a card; 3 — delete, ungroup,\ndisconnect, bind, unbind, restore show the exact change; 4 — convert, publish, export, import are **doors**, never\ncompleted by words."},"7062":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-20","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#the-turn","content":"`POST /scenes/{id}/turns` is **one multipart door**: `audio` *or* `text`, a `SceneContextSnapshot`\n(`active_view, selection_ids, pointer_target, viewport, visible_ids, language, captured_at`), `request_id`, `lang`,\noptional `proposal_id` and `dictate`. Order: module gate → PEP `forge.scene.edit` → rate limit (`turn_rpm` 30) →\nsnapshot version check (`SNAPSHOT_STALE`) → \\[audio] transcription through core-api's Gateway → **grammar first**\n(deterministic en/uk; a parse with a unique referent needs no model) → **deixis** (`selection > pointer > name`; a tie\nis a `choice`, never a guess) → the **Scene Agent** → a `SceneProposal`. The SSE stream yields `transcript` first\n(text, language, confidence — never persisted), then one of `proposal | choice | applied | answer | navigate | decline`."},"7063":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-21","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#the-turn","content":"The **Scene Agent** (`nexus://agent/agt_forge_scene`) applies the skill `skl_forge_scene_edit` whose `output_schema`\nis the proposal contract, holds **read tools only** (`forge.scene.read · knowledge.search · graph.query`), is not\nroutable and has no side effects. It is hosted inside forge-api on `nexus_agent_runtime.AgentRuntime` with the\n`core_api_model_port` driver — models only through `POST /synapse/inference/complete`; refusals cross as typed\n`PortError`, never provider text. Its prompt is `prompts/scene_turn.md`. A proposal has `candidates[] {ops,\nsummary, probability}` summing to 1, an optional `needs_clarification {question_key, options ≤ 5}`, a 30-minute TTL,\nand is re-validated against the current version on apply (stale → 409)."},"7064":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-22","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#voice-dictation-is-not-a-command","content":"Voice rides the suite’s voice rails (Voice and screen context) with one addition: the\nsnapshot is **frozen at mic-open**, so a spoken command refers to what the person saw when they started. If an\n`input` or `textarea` outside the composer had focus at mic-open, the mic shows a *T* glyph and the transcript is\ninserted into the field with `dictate=true` — transcript only, **no turn**. `grammar.correction()` keeps the last\nclause after &#x2A;no / no wait / actually / scratch that / ні / тобто…*; `is_affirmation()` applies **only** the\n`proposal_id` on screen (`409 PROPOSAL_SUPERSEDED | EXPIRED` otherwise); `is_negation()` cancels it. Clips are ≤ 2 MB\nand ≤ 30 s, webm/ogg/mp4/wav/mpeg/flac, never stored (`transient://`). Voice adds no rights: the turn and the apply\nare the same `forge.scene.edit`, and the Gateway re-decides model eligibility for the **person's** actor context.\nThe corpus (`tests/voice/corpus/{en,uk}.yaml`) passes 33/33 and 28/28."},"7065":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-23","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#who-may-do-what","content":"Three doors in order (Modules). `ForgePepAction` (10): `forge.scene.read · create · edit · delete ·\nexport · publish_version · convert · forge.template.manage · forge.present · forge.decision.read`; **human-only**:\ndelete, export, convert, publish. Relations are the Project's: `forge.admin (owner) ⊃ forge.edit (editor) ⊃\nforge.view (viewer, agent_member)`. An Organization Admin without a relation gets `NO_PROJECT_RELATION`; a foreign\nscene 404. RLS is forced on every table. `svc_forge_api` holds `session.verify · blueprint.read · pep.check ·\nmodel.invoke` (the last one added most recently, awaiting acknowledgement)."},"7066":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-24","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#decision-data","content":"Eight `ForgeDecisionKind`s, three of them on every turn: `scene_intent` (features `zoom, level, op_kind,\nlanguage, active_view, grammar_hit, input_source, pointer_kind, visible_count, candidate_count, selection_count`; the\nfull action space; propensity; `state_ref = nexus://forge/snapshot/…`), `voice_transcript_pick` (language, media type,\nduration, confidence, candidates, model id — never the words), `deictic_resolution`. Outcomes are written by apply,\ncancel, modify, choose, undo and TTL. Every editor can read the record behind &#x2A;*Why this?**;\n`decision_outcomes` refuses `llm_proposed` by CHECK."},"7067":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-25","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#api-and-tables","content":"`/api/v1/forge`: `GET/POST /scenes` · `GET/PATCH/DELETE /scenes/{id}` · `GET …/objects` · `POST …/ops` · `GET\n…/versions`, `…/versions/{n}`, `…/versions/{a}/diff/{b}` · `POST …/versions/{n}/restore | publish` · `POST …/turns`\n(multipart → SSE) · `GET …/proposals` · `POST …/proposals/{pid}/apply | cancel | choose` · `GET/POST /templates`,\n`DELETE /templates/{id}` · `GET /decisions/{id}` · `GET /health` (`voice_available`). Not yet: `/bindings/live`,\n`/convert/preview`, `/convert`, `/export`, `/import`, `/events`, `/presence`, `/forge/internal/tools/*` (S3–S6). No\nOpenAPI file is committed; FastAPI `/docs` on :3209. Tables (Alembic `0001`, `(tenant_id, id)`, RLS FORCE): `scenes ·\nscene_versions · scene_ops · scene_batches · scene_proposals · scene_templates · decision_records · decision_outcomes ·\naudit_records · outbox`."},"7068":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-26","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#deployment-and-oss","content":"Web :3219 (BFF `/api/forge/*`), API :3209, database `nexus_forge`; profile `forge` in `deploy/contract.yaml`, Compose\nand Helm (`forge.enabled` off; NetworkPolicy egress postgres · core-api · chat-api). Env: `TRANSCRIBER_DRIVER\ncore_api|fixture|none`, `AGENT_DRIVER core_api|none|scripted`, `FORGE_DEMO_WORLD` (refused in production). Voice needs\nthe `asr-local` sidecar behind the Gateway — 18–31 s per clip on a laptop CPU today. **Nothing OSS is imported yet**:\n`SceneCanvas` and `Scene3D` are dependency-free SVG; approved for later slices are LikeC4 `@likec4/*` (MIT) for the\nDiagram view, `dagre` + `d3-force` for layout, three.js in principle if the SVG spike fails; tldraw and `elkjs` were\nrejected, Yjs deferred."},"7069":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexforge-27","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexforge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexforge#what-is-built-and-what-is-not","content":"Approved: C0 — library, the one door in, five templates, Board with palette and handles, the element bar, Inspector,\nfour views, versions and restore, typed turns with grammar + agent, the 409 conflict card. Built, awaiting the owner's\nmicrophone walk: S2 voice. Not yet: the LikeC4 Diagram renderer (the current *Layered layout* is a stand-in),\nconversions and live bindings (S4), exports/imports over the API, presence, graph projection, images, own templates\nover the live API, spoken read-backs, the Voice Dock hand-off."},"7070":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","type":"page","content":"NexMap — where things are, honestly","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Technical documentation","Applications"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexmap"},"7071":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-0","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap","content":"How the map module decides what to draw — server-chosen H3 hexagons or objects over only what you may see — why every position carries how it is known and three timestamps, what the URL holds, how views, zones and uploads work, where PostGIS sits, and what is designed but not yet built."},"7072":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-1","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#level-of-detail-is-a-server-decision","content":"Level of detail is a server decision"},"7073":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-2","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"Data honesty"},"7074":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-3","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#the-url-is-the-view","content":"The URL is the view"},"7075":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-4","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#sources-and-uploads","content":"Sources and uploads"},"7076":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-5","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#who-may-do-what","content":"Who may do what"},"7077":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-6","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"Decision data"},"7078":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-7","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#api","content":"API"},"7079":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-8","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#deployment","content":"Deployment"},"7080":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-9","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#what-is-built-and-what-is-not","content":"What is built and what is not"},"7081":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-10","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap","content":"The NexMap chapters show the module from the outside. This page is the inside. NexMap is\n`apps/map` over `map-api` and the `nexus_map` database with PostGIS; it is installed per organization as a pack\n(Modules). Two rules organise it: **the server decides what is drawn**, and **nothing is drawn that is\nnot known** — no guessed position, no silent (0, 0), no number that reveals an object you may not see."},"7082":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-11","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#level-of-detail-is-a-server-decision","content":"`GET /map/view?c=lon,lat,zoom&t=…&l=…` returns either **cells** or **objects**, never a mix, and the client draws\nwhat it gets. The server computes the H3 resolution for the viewport (r2–r8), counts the **unique permitted\nentities** per cell inside the SQL query — the relation filter is in the `WHERE`, not applied afterwards — drops cells\nunder the Blueprint's `tuning.map.min_cell_count` (suppression drops, never zeroes: `count ≥ 1` is a schema\ninvariant), and switches to objects when at most 400 permitted objects are in view. Every answer carries a\n`lod_selection` decision record: the candidate resolutions, their features, the chosen one, the propensity. The\nstatus line (*Aggregated · H3 resolution 3* / *Objects · 69*) is the record made visible."},"7083":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-12","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#level-of-detail-is-a-server-decision","content":"H3 is computed server-side (`h3` 4.4.1) and stored as `h3_r4 / h3_r6 / h3_r8` columns on `geo_features`; the browser\nuses `h3-js` only to draw cell outlines. MapLibre GL draws the base map (OpenFreeMap vector tiles, OpenStreetMap data,\nODbL attribution; PMTiles self-hosting is S5) and deck.gl the layers; the MapLibre worker is served same-origin from\n`/vendor/maplibre/*` — no CDN."},"7084":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-13","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"Rule"},"7085":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-14","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"Where it lives"},"7086":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-15","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"`position_kind ∈ observed · geocoded · interpolated · estimated`; `interpolated` is valid **only** under a `playback:` URI"},"7087":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-16","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"`map-common`, `map-location-observation` schemas"},"7088":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-17","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"Three timestamps — `observed_at`, `received_at` required; `valid_until` optional — \"honest time\""},"7089":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-18","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"`map-location-observation`"},"7090":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-19","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"`last_position = null ⇒ position_kind = null ∧ freshness = null`; a feature without position is listed, never placed at (0, 0)"},"7091":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-20","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"`map-geo-feature`; the List view; upload results"},"7092":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-21","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"A lane has no geometry — it is a relation between places, drawn as a line from the cell"},"7093":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-22","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"`map-lane`"},"7094":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-23","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"A `MapSpec` (a saved map's definition) cannot carry features, coordinates, counts or HTML"},"7095":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-24","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"`map-spec`"},"7096":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-25","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"Zones are created by people only (`created_by.kind = human`)"},"7097":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-26","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"`map-geo-zone`"},"7098":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-27","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"Now = each object at its last observed position, nothing extrapolated; History = as it was; Playback interpolates moving objects and says so"},"7099":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-28","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"`MapTimeMode`; the time strip"},"7100":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-29","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#data-honesty","content":"Fourteen schemas plus `pack-module` sit in `packages/contracts/schemas/v1/map-*.schema.json`; the vocabulary\n(`PositionKind`, `GeoFeatureKind`, `GeofenceState/TransitionKind` — there is no `exited`, only `left` with a dwell —\n`MapLod`, `MapPepAction` 17, `MapDecisionKind` 7, `MapUploadRejectReason` 16…) is in `vocabulary/v1.json` (ADR-0051 §1)."},"7101":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-30","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#the-url-is-the-view","content":"`/map?c=lon,lat,zoom[,bearing,pitch]&t=<time>&sel=<id>&l=<layers>&hex=<cell>&list&follow`. A **saved view**\nis that address with a name, a Project, *Private* or *Project* sharing and a pinned or floating time\n(`map-saved-view`); `GET/POST /map/views`, `PUT/DELETE /map/views/{id}` under `map.view.save` / `map.view.delete`,\nhumans only, Project views by editors and owners. Because the URL is the state, a copied link, a saved view and a\n*Ask in Chat* hand-off (`context=map:view | map:cell:{h3} | map:{id}`) are the same thing."},"7102":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-31","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#sources-and-uploads","content":"`POST /map/uploads` (`map.upload`, editors and owners, ≤ 64 MiB GeoJSON or CSV) parses rows into observations under\na new source and answers `{placed, without_position, rejected[] {row, reason}}` with sixteen closed reasons\n(*coordinate out of range*, *swapped axes suspected*…). Nothing is placed at (0, 0); the (0, 0) row becomes *without\nposition*. `DELETE /map/uploads/{id}` removes exactly the rows it created. `GET /map/sources` lists the demo world\n(`MAP_DEMO_WORLD=1` on the dev stack: 637 objects on a Silk corridor Lviv → Hamburg, frozen at 2026-09-24 16:00 UTC,\nevery source labelled *fixture*, refused in production) and uploads. Live feeds through Synapse, the `map-worker`,\nthe Dagster `nexus_map` code location and the outbox relay are **not built** (S3)."},"7103":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-32","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#who-may-do-what","content":"Three doors in order on every route — session · module gate · PEP (Modules). Reads need any Project\nrelation; an Organization Admin without one gets `NO_PROJECT_RELATION` 403; an object of a Project you do not hold\nanswers 404. View and upload authoring is human-only (`AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN`); `svc_map_worker` reads tenant-wide,\n`svc_chat_api` reads only, every other service `SERVICE_NOT_ALLOWED`. Every route carries `x-nexus-pep`; audit rows\n`map.module.gate`, `map.view.save`, `map.upload`… go to the audit sink."},"7104":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-33","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"Kind"},"7105":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-34","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"When"},"7106":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-35","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"Outcome"},"7107":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-36","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"`lod_selection`"},"7108":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-37","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"every `/map/view` answer"},"7109":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-38","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"the person's next zoom (implicit)"},"7110":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-39","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"`cell_focus` · `object_pick`"},"7111":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-40","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"a hexagon or object opened"},"7112":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-41","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"Details / Zoom in / Ask"},"7113":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-42","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"`search_ranking`"},"7114":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-43","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"Go to"},"7115":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-44","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"the pick"},"7116":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-45","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"`view_restore`"},"7117":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-46","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"a saved view opened"},"7118":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-47","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"—"},"7119":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-48","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"`upload_row_disposition`"},"7120":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-49","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"every upload row"},"7121":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-50","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"removed / kept"},"7122":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-51","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#decision-data","content":"`POST /map/decisions/{id}/outcomes` assigns `label_source` server-side; `llm_proposed` is unrepresentable in\n`MapLabelSource` — no model is in the loop today, and the schema keeps it that way. No feedback UI."},"7123":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-52","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#api","content":"`map-api` mounts under `/api/v1` (FastAPI `/docs` on :3207): `GET /map/view · /map/entities/{id} · /map/cells/{h3} ·\n/map/search · /map/timeline · /map/unplaced · /map/context · /map/zones · /map/views… · /map/uploads… · /map/sources ·\n/map/decisions/{id}`. The web app reaches it only through its same-origin BFF `/api/map/*`, rewritten to map-api with\nthe person's session when `MAP_API_ORIGIN` is set. **There is no `nexus-map-v1.openapi.yaml` yet** — ADR-0051 §4 fixes\nthe operation list in prose and defers the file; the API reference will carry it when it lands. Declared and not\nimplemented: `/map/entities/{id}/track`, `/map/tiles/*`, `/map/raster/*`, zone writes, `/map/feeds/connect`,\n`/map/export`, `/map/share`, `/map/specs/*`, `/map/internal/tools/*`."},"7124":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-53","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#deployment","content":"Web :3217, API :3207 (Compose host :3307), database `nexus_map` with PostGIS 3.6 created by `postgres`\n(`infra/postgres/init/007-map-database.sql`), Alembic `0001_s1_nexus_map` (GiST on geometry, monthly partitions on\n`location_observations`, RLS FORCE) and `0002_s2_uploads`. Profile `map` in `deploy/contract.yaml`, Compose and Helm\n(`map.enabled` off by default). OSS: MapLibre GL JS 6.11 (BSD-3), deck.gl 9.4 (MIT), h3 / h3-js (Apache-2.0), PostGIS\n(GPL-2.0 at the database-process boundary)."},"7125":{"id":"/docs/technical/nexmap-54","page_id":"/docs/technical/nexmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/nexmap#what-is-built-and-what-is-not","content":"Built and approved: S1 (map · hexagons · objects · Inspector · zones · the gate). Built and presented: S2 (views ·\nsources · uploads). Not built: live position feeds, geofence Flows (the pack ships the template; nothing emits\n`geo_event` yet), raster imagery, the NexChat seam — `ArtifactType.map`, an Auto `map` arm, *Open in NexMap* —\nNexBI dashboards and NexGraph entity capture (design only). The Inspector's *Create task* and &#x2A;Notify me…* are labelled\n*Prototype* on screen. Open questions: risk sources, a remote registry, `task.*` tools."},"7126":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","type":"page","content":"Ontology — why Nexi names everything it uses","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Technical documentation","Building blocks"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/ontology"},"7127":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-0","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology","content":"A shared vocabulary for models, tools, agents, flows and knowledge — and what Nexi can do automatically because everything is described, not just wired. Continued with the weekend-trip example."},"7128":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-1","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"Floor one: the platform vocabulary — what exists and what it can do"},"7129":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-2","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-two-knowledge--what-is-true-in-your-project","content":"Floor two: knowledge — what is *true* in your Project"},"7130":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-3","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/ontology#why-this-matters-more-as-you-add-models-and-technologies","content":"Why this matters more as you add models and technologies"},"7131":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-4","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"Where you meet it today, and what is coming"},"7132":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-5","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/ontology#the-same-picture-in-the-architecture","content":"The same picture in the architecture"},"7133":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-6","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology","content":"The weekend Flow used one model for drafting and a cheaper one for judging, a weather service, your calendar, a\nchecklist Skill and an approval. Behind that sit at least five technologies from five vendors. Ask yourself how the\nFlow drafter knew a *Weather* Tool existed, how Synapse knew which model qualifies as \"good quality, tier ≤ 2\", how\nNexTasks knew that *creating events* needs a person and *reading a forecast* does not — and how, in a year, you would\nfind out which model saw a given conversation."},"7134":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-7","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology","content":"The answer is the same each time: &#x2A;*Nexi describes everything it uses in one vocabulary, and machines read that\ndescription.** That vocabulary is the ontology. It has two floors."},"7135":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-8","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"Every model, tool, connection, agent, skill, flow and project has a **stable identity** and a **machine-readable\ndescription**. Not a label for humans — a description precise enough for Nexi to act on without asking."},"7136":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-9","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"Thing"},"7137":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-10","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"What its description says"},"7138":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-11","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"Who writes it"},"7139":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-12","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"**Model**"},"7140":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-13","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"Roles it can play (draft, judge, embed, transcribe, classify …), tier 0–4, capabilities, languages, licence, measured quality, health right now."},"7141":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-14","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"An administrator registers it in NexCore; Nexi measures it."},"7142":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-15","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"**Tool**"},"7143":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-16","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"What it does, exactly what goes in and what comes out, whether it **changes** something or only reads, which Connection it needs."},"7144":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-17","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"Often imported: an OpenAPI description becomes Tools automatically."},"7145":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-18","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"**Connection**"},"7146":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-19","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"Kind (workspace or your own account), account, scopes in words, status, last used — never the secret."},"7147":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-20","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"An administrator or you, at consent."},"7148":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-21","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"**Skill**"},"7149":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-22","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"Its instruction and examples, and the shape of what it expects and produces. Reviewed by a person before publish."},"7150":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-23","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"A builder."},"7151":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-24","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"**Agent**"},"7152":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-25","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"Which Skills it applies, which Tools it may use, what it needs from a model — not which model."},"7153":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-26","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"A builder, from one sentence onwards."},"7154":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-27","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"**Flow**"},"7155":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-28","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"Steps, conditions, loops with a Goal and its limits, approvals — a document Nexi can check before it runs."},"7156":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-29","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"A builder, or Nexi drafts it from a description."},"7157":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-30","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"**Blueprint**"},"7158":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-31","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"A package of all of the above with what it requires from the organization."},"7159":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-32","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"Whoever ships a capability."},"7160":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-33","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"Because the descriptions share one vocabulary, Nexi can **process them automatically** — which is the whole point:"},"7161":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-34","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-one-the-platform-vocabulary--what-exists-and-what-it-can-do","content":"In the weekend example: the Flow drafter proposed *Weather* and *Calendar* steps because those Tools were described in\nthe Project; the *Calendar* step got an approval because its description says it changes something; Synapse chose a\ntier-2 model because the agent's need and the models' descriptions could be compared; and the trace of one Thursday\nrun links the message, the two model calls, the forecast lookup, your approval and the calendar write with a single id.\nNobody wired any of that by hand. When you register a better model next month, or import a new hotel-booking API,\nthe same machinery picks them up."},"7162":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-35","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-two-knowledge--what-is-true-in-your-project","content":"The second floor is about what your agents **know**, and this is where most systems go wrong: they let a model write\nwhatever it extracts straight into \"the knowledge base\". Nexi refuses to."},"7163":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-36","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-two-knowledge--what-is-true-in-your-project","content":"Only a very small core is fixed — the words needed to talk about truth at all: a **Source** (a message, a file, a\npage), a **Chunk** of it, a **Claim** made about the world, a **Hypothesis**, an **Assumption**, and the record of a\ncheck. Everything else — the entity types and relation names of *your* domain — is not designed up front. It\n**emerges**: agents propose candidate words while they work, people keep the ones that fit, and Nexi periodically\nconsolidates a versioned snapshot of \"how we currently name the world\". A Project's vocabulary is therefore the\nplatform's core, plus what a Blueprint seeds, plus what your own work adds."},"7164":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-37","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-two-knowledge--what-is-true-in-your-project","content":"Every claim then lives in one of three places, and moves between them only through a gate:"},"7165":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-38","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-two-knowledge--what-is-true-in-your-project","content":"**Lexical** is what was literally said or written. Nothing is interpreted yet."},"7166":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-39","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-two-knowledge--what-is-true-in-your-project","content":"**Subject** is what a model *thinks* that means — a Claim with a pointer to its Chunk and Source. It is useful,\nsearchable, and clearly marked as *proposed*."},"7167":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-40","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-two-knowledge--what-is-true-in-your-project","content":"**Domain** is what your organization treats as true. A claim arrives here only through a gate: an automatic check\nagainst a trustworthy source, or a person. &#x2A;*A model can never mark its own claim verified.**"},"7168":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-41","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#floor-two-knowledge--what-is-true-in-your-project","content":"Back to the weekend. Over a few trips the Project accumulates claims: &#x2A;\"Anna avoids drives over two hours\"&#x2A; (Source: a\nchat message in March), &#x2A;\"the cottage in Yaremche allows dogs\"&#x2A; (Source: the booking page), &#x2A;\"budget per person is\n€120\"* (Source: your message last week). The *Trip planner* proposed all three; you confirmed the first and the\nthird, the second was checked against the booking page. Next Thursday the planner **uses only what is trusted*&#x2A;, shows\nthe proposed items as suggestions, and when it says &#x2A;\"Anna prefers short drives\"* you can click through to the message\nwhere she said so. That click — claim → chunk → source — is provenance, and every claim in Nexi carries it."},"7169":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-42","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#why-this-matters-more-as-you-add-models-and-technologies","content":"Each new model, connector or vendor is a new way of describing the same world. Without a shared vocabulary you get\none integration per pair: this model with that tool, this connector with that report — and nobody can answer &#x2A;\"which\nmodel saw this?\"&#x2A; or &#x2A;\"where did that fact come from?\"* With one vocabulary the count stays flat: describe the new\nthing once, and routing, drafting, approvals, policy, packaging, tracing and knowledge gates apply to it on day one."},"7170":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-43","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#why-this-matters-more-as-you-add-models-and-technologies","content":"That is also why the boundaries on the earlier pages exist. Agents cannot install or bind capabilities; they can only\nfile a **capability request** a person decides on. Skills own no tools. Models are described by roles and tiers\nrather than names. Each rule keeps the descriptions honest, so that the automation built on them can be trusted."},"7171":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-44","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"Today"},"7172":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-45","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"Where"},"7173":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-46","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"Models with roles, tiers, capabilities and measured quality; Tools imported from OpenAPI descriptions; Connections described without secrets; Blueprints with requirements"},"7174":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-47","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"NexCore"},"7175":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-48","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"Agents and Skills with declared inputs and outputs; Flows drafted from a description; the `routed to …` chip and Runs with one trace id"},"7176":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-49","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"NexChat"},"7177":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-50","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"Approvals placed automatically on Tools that change something"},"7178":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-51","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"NexTasks"},"7179":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-52","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"Sources with pinned versions; the pipeline as a receipt; Graph Studio; the Evidence Workspace (claim → span → source); Review with the oracle-or-person gate; Vocabulary as *terms in use*"},"7180":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-53","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"**NexGraph**"},"7181":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-54","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"Questions answered *from the knowledge graph* with numbered sources and *How this was found*"},"7182":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-55","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"NexChat"},"7183":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-56","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"Planned"},"7184":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-57","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"Where"},"7185":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-58","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"The ontology registry on top of the vocabulary — managed terms, proposals, merges, versioned snapshots; Memory (captured outcomes of runs as proposed knowledge) beyond preview"},"7186":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-59","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"**NexGraph**"},"7187":{"id":"/docs/technical/ontology-60","page_id":"/docs/technical/ontology","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/ontology#where-you-meet-it-today-and-what-is-coming","content":"To see the vocabulary in use, follow the step-by-step chapters of the NexChat guide — starting with\nCreate an Agent from one sentence. The second floor, at document scale, is\nThe knowledge graph and the NexGraph guide."},"7188":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","type":"page","content":"Synapse — how agents reach models and systems","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Technical documentation","Building blocks"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/synapse"},"7189":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-0","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse","content":"The one gateway between what you build and the outside world — models on one side, your systems and accounts on the other. Continued with the weekend-trip example."},"7190":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-1","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/synapse#two-sides-of-one-gateway","content":"Two sides of one gateway"},"7191":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-2","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/synapse#the-model-gateway-you-say-what-you-need-not-which-model","content":"The Model Gateway: you say what you need, not which model"},"7192":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-3","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/synapse#speech-and-vision-are-gateway-operations-too","content":"Speech and vision are Gateway operations too"},"7193":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-4","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"Connections: the agent never sees a credential"},"7194":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-5","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/synapse#what-this-buys-you-in-one-list","content":"What this buys you, in one list"},"7195":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-6","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/synapse#where-you-meet-synapse","content":"Where you meet Synapse"},"7196":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-7","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/synapse#the-same-picture-in-the-architecture","content":"The same picture in the architecture"},"7197":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-8","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse","content":"In Agents, Skills, Tools and Flows the *Trip planner* agent wrote proposals with a\nmodel, the *Weather* Tool looked up a forecast and the *Calendar* Tool created events in your calendar. None of them\ndid that directly. Everything that leaves Nexi — a request to a model, a call to a weather service, a write into\nyour calendar — goes through **Synapse**. This page explains what Synapse does on each side and why you will be\nglad it is there."},"7198":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-9","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#two-sides-of-one-gateway","content":"Side"},"7199":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-10","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#two-sides-of-one-gateway","content":"What passes through"},"7200":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-11","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#two-sides-of-one-gateway","content":"What Synapse decides"},"7201":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-12","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#two-sides-of-one-gateway","content":"**Model Gateway**"},"7202":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-13","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#two-sides-of-one-gateway","content":"Every model call an Agent, an Evaluator or a Flow step makes."},"7203":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-14","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#two-sides-of-one-gateway","content":"*Which* model answers, from the set your organization allows; what it may cost; that the call is recorded."},"7204":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-15","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#two-sides-of-one-gateway","content":"**Connections**"},"7205":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-16","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#two-sides-of-one-gateway","content":"Every Tool call to a system outside Nexi — an API, a database, a file store, another agent, a webhook."},"7206":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-17","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#two-sides-of-one-gateway","content":"*Whose* credentials are used, that they never reach the agent, that the call is allowed and audited."},"7207":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-18","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#the-model-gateway-you-say-what-you-need-not-which-model","content":"When you build the *Trip planner* you do not pick \"model X, version Y\". You describe the job:"},"7208":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-19","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#the-model-gateway-you-say-what-you-need-not-which-model","content":"> *draft text · good quality · Ukrainian and English · low cost is fine · nothing above tier 2*"},"7209":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-20","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#the-model-gateway-you-say-what-you-need-not-which-model","content":"Synapse turns that into a choice at the moment of the call:"},"7210":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-21","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#the-model-gateway-you-say-what-you-need-not-which-model","content":"**Eligible set.** It starts from every model your organization has registered and keeps only those that fit the\nrole, meet the quality bar, are healthy right now, are allowed for the Project's classification and for your\nBlueprint, and that policy permits *this* agent to use. Each candidate is checked against policy — not the list as a\nwhole."},"7211":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-22","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#the-model-gateway-you-say-what-you-need-not-which-model","content":"**Strategy.** Inside that set it applies the strategy the agent asked for: *cheapest qualified*, *quality first*,\n*local only*, or an explicit model when someone has a reason."},"7212":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-23","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#the-model-gateway-you-say-what-you-need-not-which-model","content":"**Nothing eligible?** The call fails with a clear reason. Synapse never quietly \"upgrades\" to a bigger or a cloud\nmodel to get an answer. A silent upgrade would mean data leaving where it is allowed to be, and a bill nobody agreed\nto."},"7213":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-24","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#the-model-gateway-you-say-what-you-need-not-which-model","content":"**Record.** Every call produces a record — model, tier, tokens, how the decision was made — but **never the prompt\nor the answer text**. That record is what the &#x2A;routed to …* chip under a message shows, what your administrator\nsees in NexCore's model and price reports, and what keeps a Flow's budget honest: tokens are metered by Synapse,\nagents never report their own usage."},"7214":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-25","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#the-model-gateway-you-say-what-you-need-not-which-model","content":"In the weekend example this means the *Trip planner* drafts on a mid-tier local model, the *Evaluator* — a small\njob — runs on the cheapest qualified one, and a frontier cloud model is only used if your organization allowed it\nand the agent asked for that quality. The proportion of work kept off frontier models is a number NexCore shows,\nbecause it is a decision your organization makes on purpose."},"7215":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-26","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#speech-and-vision-are-gateway-operations-too","content":"The Gateway has four operations, not one: **inference**, **transcribe** (`asr` role, floor 0.8),\n**synthesize** (`tts` role, floor 0.7) and **vision**. The same eligible-set rule applies — a *confidential* Project\nmust have a local speech route, and a fitness check enforces it. The local routes are two sidecars inside the\ndeployment, reached by core-api only: `asr-local` (faster-whisper, :8090) and `tts-local` (ukrainian-tts, :8091).\nCloud speech models (`gpt-4o-mini-transcribe`, `gpt-4o-mini-tts`) are tier 4 and eligible up to *confidential*; at\n*secret* a non-Ukrainian answer stays text. Audio is never stored by the Gateway or the sidecars — the record holds the\nmodel, duration and confidence, not the words. NexChat's microphone, Talk mode and NexForge's dictation all use these\noperations; see Voice, screen context, search and research."},"7216":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-27","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#speech-and-vision-are-gateway-operations-too","content":"Two more families reach the outside through Synapse: **web search providers** (`web.search` port — Tavily, Brave,\nMojeek, LangSearch as connections; Wikipedia, Wikidata, OpenStreetMap as open data) and **conversation channels**\n(the Telegram bot NexCare answers in — a connection with a `conversation_channel` block, the bot token in the\nCredential Broker, `api.telegram.org` the only egress host)."},"7217":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-28","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"The *Weather* Tool needs an API key. The *Calendar* Tool needs *your* account. Both are **Connections**, and they are\ndifferent kinds:"},"7218":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-29","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"Kind"},"7219":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-30","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"Example"},"7220":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-31","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"Who sets it up"},"7221":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-32","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"What the agent gets"},"7222":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-33","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"**Workspace connection**"},"7223":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-34","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"*Weather service* — one API key for the whole organization."},"7224":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-35","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"An administrator, once, in NexCore. The key is entered write-only: it can be replaced but never displayed again."},"7225":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-36","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"A Tool that works. The key stays in the credential broker; it is resolved inside Synapse at call time."},"7226":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-37","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"**Your own account**"},"7227":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-38","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"*Calendar* — events created in your calendar, as you."},"7228":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-39","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"You, when a Tool first needs it: a card appears in the conversation, you consent at the provider (Google, your enterprise SSO), Nexi receives a token — never your password."},"7229":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-40","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"A Tool that acts *as you*, within the scopes you granted."},"7230":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-41","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"A Connection is described to the browser and to agents by **what it is, not what it holds**: account, status, scopes\nin words, last used. Secrets never appear in a prompt, a log, an error message or a screen. If the calendar token\nexpires you get *Reconnect*; if you want it gone you *Disconnect* under **Connected accounts** in the user menu, and the\nprovider is told to revoke it."},"7231":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-42","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#connections-the-agent-never-sees-a-credential","content":"Behind a Connection can be many technologies — a REST or OpenAPI service, an MCP tool server, another agent (A2A),\nSQL, files, webhooks, events. For an OpenAPI service the administrator imports its description and Nexi proposes\nthe Tools; reading operations run when an agent asks, **changing operations wait for a person** in NexTasks — the\nsame approval you saw in the weekend Flow, applied automatically to anything that writes."},"7232":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-43","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#what-this-buys-you-in-one-list","content":"**Swap models without touching agents.** Register a new model in NexCore; every agent whose needs it meets can\nstart using it under the same strategy."},"7233":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-44","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#what-this-buys-you-in-one-list","content":"**Cost and data stay where you decided.** Tiers, local-only strategies and per-candidate policy checks make \"which\nmodel saw this\" a governed answer, not a surprise."},"7234":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-45","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#what-this-buys-you-in-one-list","content":"**One place to revoke.** A leaked key or a departed colleague is handled in NexCore or in *Connected accounts* — no\nagent, skill or flow needs to change."},"7235":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-46","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#what-this-buys-you-in-one-list","content":"**One audit trail.** Model calls, tool calls and approvals share the same correlation id, from the message in\nNexChat to the record in NexCore."},"7236":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-47","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#what-this-buys-you-in-one-list","content":"**Outages are typed, not leaked.** If the weather service is down, the Tool returns a clear error to the Flow — with\nno response body from the provider passed on to a model."},"7237":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-48","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#where-you-meet-synapse","content":"You see"},"7238":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-49","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#where-you-meet-synapse","content":"Where"},"7239":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-50","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#where-you-meet-synapse","content":"When"},"7240":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-51","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/synapse#where-you-meet-synapse","content":"*routed to …* chip"},"7241":{"id":"/docs/technical/synapse-52","page_id":"/docs/technical/synapse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"