"},"7308":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-45","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#reading-the-map-top-to-bottom","content":"Module (building)"},"7309":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-46","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#reading-the-map-top-to-bottom","content":"**NexCare** · module"},"7310":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-47","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#reading-the-map-top-to-bottom","content":"Serve customers with an assistant on verified knowledge and people on Join."},"7311":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-48","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#reading-the-map-top-to-bottom","content":"Widget, Telegram, Conversations desk, Cases, Quality, Live, Care Studio"},"7312":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-49","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#reading-the-map-top-to-bottom","content":"Module (building; Telegram live)"},"7313":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-50","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#reading-the-map-top-to-bottom","content":"**NexForge** · module"},"7314":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-51","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#reading-the-map-top-to-bottom","content":"Think, sketch, model; the AI proposes, the person applies."},"7315":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-52","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#reading-the-map-top-to-bottom","content":"Scenes, Board · Diagram · 3D · Present, Scene Agent, Versions, Doors"},"7316":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-53","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#reading-the-map-top-to-bottom","content":"Module (building; voice built)"},"7317":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-54","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#reading-the-map-top-to-bottom","content":"**Modules** are packs that add an application: installing the pack in NexCore › Blueprints & Packs sets\n`modules.enabled` in the organization's Blueprint, the module's API opens its gate and the tile appears in every\nlauncher. Each has its own API, database and worker, uses the same shell, session, Project relations, Synapse, Policy\nand decision data as the suite — and nothing of the suite depends on it. See Modules."},"7318":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-55","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#reading-the-map-top-to-bottom","content":"**Shared runtimes and gateways** are what every application uses and none owns alone. An agent built in NexChat is\nrun by the *Agent Runtime*, reaches a model or a system only through *Synapse*, runs any code it writes in the\n*Sandbox Runtime*, is orchestrated by the *Flow Engine* when it is a step of a Flow, and is told yes or no by\n*Policy* at every step. NexBI uses exactly the same parts — an automation is a Flow on the Flow Engine, a proposed\ndashboard is a Resolver step — NexSpin will call the same agents, NexCare's assistant is an Agent the Studio compiles,\nNexForge's Scene Agent is hosted on the Agent Runtime's model port. This is why agents, skills and flows are called\n*cross-cutting resources*: created in one application, usable from all. Two runtime ports arrived with the modules and\nthe voice work: the **Guardrail port** (input · retrieval · tool · output checks under a profile, used by NexCare and\noffered to the Model Gateway and Agent Runtime) and the Gateway's **speech roles** (`asr`, `tts`) backed by local\nsidecars — see Voice and screen context."},"7319":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-56","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#reading-the-map-top-to-bottom","content":"**State, events and pipelines** is where things are kept. There is one canonical store — PostgreSQL, with pgvector\nfor embeddings, Apache AGE for the graph and PostGIS for NexMap's geometry in the same server — one database per\napplication (`nexus_chat`, `nexus_tasks`, `nexus_bi`, `nexus_graph`, `nexus_map`, `nexus_care`, `nexus_forge`…). NATS\nJetStream carries jobs and events but is never the truth about anything; Dagster runs scheduled data pipelines; every application writes typed audit events that\nNexCore shows."},"7320":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-57","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#inside-nexchat--what-contains-what","content":"Because NexChat is where most people start, here is its own decomposition. A **Project** is the unit of everything:\nit has a classification, members, knowledge, and its own agents, skills and flows. Chats live inside it (or outside,\nas global chats without a Project's knowledge)."},"7321":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-58","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#inside-nexchat--what-contains-what","content":"Read the lines between the four building blocks as the composition rule: &#x2A;Skill teaches. Agent works. Tool acts. Flow orchestrates.* A Skill\nnever owns a Tool; an Agent never owns a Flow; a Tool is never a Skill. That separation is what lets each be reviewed,\nversioned and shared on its own — see Agents, Skills, Tools and Flows."},"7322":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-59","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#how-the-parts-call-each-other","content":"Three things the picture makes visible:"},"7323":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-60","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#how-the-parts-call-each-other","content":"**Nothing reaches a model or a system except through Synapse.** That is where credentials live, where the allowed\nhosts are enforced, and where the model is chosen by role, classification and tier. See Synapse."},"7324":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-61","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#how-the-parts-call-each-other","content":"**A person sits on the path of every side effect** that policy or the binding marks as needing approval — as a card\nin the thread, backed by NexTasks. See Give the agent Tools."},"7325":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-62","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#how-the-parts-call-each-other","content":"**NexCore configures, it does not execute.** It publishes what exists — models, connections, tools, policy bundles —\nand the runtimes enforce it. Administering is not reading: an Organization Admin governs every Project but sees a\nProject's threads only as its member. See Access rights."},"7326":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-63","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#how-the-parts-call-each-other","content":"**Numbers never come from a model.** A data question in NexChat goes to NexBI's governed query engine — a typed\nquery compiled to parameterised SQL, row policy applied before aggregation, the record kept — and the answer is a\ncomputed value with its provenance. See NexBI — governed numbers."},"7327":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-64","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#how-the-parts-call-each-other","content":"**Every choice is a record.** Auto's route, a WIP override in VibeBan, the Studio's template plan, a Resolver plan\nyou accept, the map's level of detail, a Scene Agent's proposal, a guardrail verdict: each is a decision with its\nalternatives, and what you did with it is written back. See Auto — how Nexi picks the capability."},"7328":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-65","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#how-the-parts-call-each-other","content":"**Modules depend on the suite; the suite never depends on a module.** Core answers whether a module is enabled; the\nmodule's API asks before it answers anything and closes when it cannot ask. Relations come from the NexChat Project\nthe content belongs to. See Modules."},"7329":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-66","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#how-the-parts-call-each-other","content":"**Voice adds no rights, and audio is never kept.** A spoken sentence runs the same arm and the same policy checks as a\ntyped one; the clip goes once to the speech model and nowhere else. See\nVoice and screen context."},"7330":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-67","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#where-things-live","content":"The same noun often appears in two applications. This table says who *creates*, who *governs* and what *runs* each\none."},"7331":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-68","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#where-things-live","content":"Thing"},"7332":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-69","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#where-thing