here-things-live","content":"NexChat composer"},"7433":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-170","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#where-things-live","content":"the thread's classification; `retention=session_only`"},"7434":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-171","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#where-things-live","content":"never stored (clip), purged on Remove / 8 h (file), dropped after one vision call (frame)"},"7435":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-172","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#where-things-live","content":"Platform action"},"7436":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-173","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#where-things-live","content":"each app's tool registry entry"},"7437":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-174","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#where-things-live","content":"the policy decision point on the exact target, as the person"},"7438":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-175","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#where-things-live","content":"the owning app's door"},"7439":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-176","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#three-ways-to-read-this-page","content":"**You use Nexi.** Remember NexHome → NexChat → VibeBan: land, work, decide — and NexBI when the question is a\nnumber. Everything else is behind those."},"7440":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-177","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#three-ways-to-read-this-page","content":"**You build agents and flows.** Everything you make lives in a Project in NexChat and runs on the shared runtimes;\nlearn the four nouns in Agents, Skills, Tools and Flows, then follow the\nNexChat chapters."},"7441":{"id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture-178","page_id":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/the-big-picture#three-ways-to-read-this-page","content":"**You run the organization.** NexCore is your application; the runtimes enforce what you publish there. Start with\nAccess rights and How Nexi is built for the four rules and the\narchitecture views."},"7442":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","type":"page","content":"VibeBan — work for people and agents","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Technical documentation","Applications"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/vibeban"},"7443":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-0","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban","content":"How NexTasks became VibeBan — work projects with a board or iterations, items with relations that propagate, milestones, references that link to requirements and tests without copying them, an acceptance gate a human verifies, health derived by a rule — and why an agent never outranks the person it works for."},"7444":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-1","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"The objects"},"7445":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-2","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-acceptance-gate","content":"The acceptance gate"},"7446":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-3","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#wip-limits-are-soft-and-recorded","content":"WIP limits are soft, and recorded"},"7447":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-4","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#who-may-do-what--agent--principal","content":"Who may do what — agent ≤ principal"},"7448":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-5","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"Decision data"},"7449":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-6","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#between-the-applications","content":"Between the applications"},"7450":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-7","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#what-is-built-and-what-is-not","content":"What is built and what is not"},"7451":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-8","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#where-to-read-more","content":"Where to read more"},"7452":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-9","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban","content":"The VibeBan chapters show the application from the outside. This page is the inside. NexTasks began\nas the place a Flow waits for a person — the **approval**. VibeBan grows the same process, `tasks-api` on\nits own database `nexus_tasks`, into work management: what is on your plate, how a team runs a project, and how the\nplatform's own delivery — requirements, criteria, tests, decisions — is tracked against the work. Two rules organise\neverything: **an agent acts within the relation of the human who asked, never beyond it**, and **every place the\napplication ranks or decides for you is a decision record**, not a heuristic."},"7453":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-10","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"Object"},"7454":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-11","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"What it is"},"7455":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-12","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"Notes"},"7456":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-13","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"**WorkProject**"},"7457":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-14","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"A team's project — *not* a NexChat Project. `KEY` of 2–6 capitals; pattern **kanban** (a continuous board) or **iterations**; visibility private or shared; estimation none · points · hours · custom; a classification ceiling. Templates: *simple-kanban*, *software-delivery* (iterations · points · 14-day Monday sprints), *research*."},"7458":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-15","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"Relations `owner · editor · viewer · agent_member` in OpenFGA. Archived → read-only (*409 PROJECT\\_ARCHIVED*)."},"7459":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-16","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"**WorkflowStage**"},"7460":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-17","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"A column with a **category** — *backlog · ready · in\\_progress · review · done · cancelled* — and an optional WIP limit."},"7461":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-18","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"*Blocked* is a condition of an item, never a stage."},"7462":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-19","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"**WorkItem**"},"7463":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-20","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"`KEY-n` (project) or `MY-n` (personal). Types *epic · story · task · bug*; priority *P0–P3*; stage, assignees, owner, due, iteration, milestone, estimate, tags; optimistic `version` with `If-Match` (*409 VERSION\\_CONFLICT*)."},"7464":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-21","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"Personal items are shared person-to-person (viewer · editor) and never enter the work dataset."},"7465":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-22","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"**WorkRelation**"},"7466":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-23","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"*blocks · depends\\_on · relates\\_to · duplicates*. `blocks` propagates the blocked condition; cycles are refused (*409 RELATION\\_CYCLE*)."},"7467":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-24","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"**Iteration**"},"7468":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-25","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"A sprint: one **active** per project (*409 ITERATION\\_ACTIVE*); a **start snapshot** (items · points · people); scope changes tracked against it; completion requires a **disposition** for unfinished items — *return\\_to\\_backlog · move\\_to\\_next* (*422 DISPOSITION\\_REQUIRED*)."},"7469":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-26","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"Start, complete and cancel are human-only."},"7470":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-27","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"**Milestone**"},"7471":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-28","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"A date with a status *open · reached · missed · cancelled*."},"7472":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-29","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"Status is set by a person only — an agent gets *403 AUTHOR\\_NOT\\_HUMAN*."},"7473":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-30","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"**ReferenceObject** · **ReferenceLink** · **ItemReference**"},"7474":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-31","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"A requirement, acceptance criterion, test, test case or decision — as a **link with a label and URI**, never a body (*422 REFERENCE\\_BODY\\_REJECTED*). Imported from the platform's own documentation (its requirement and decision folders) by an `ImportJob` (*preview → apply → job*), or attached by hand."},"7475":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-32","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"A `verifies` link from a person to an acceptance criterion is the act of verification."},"7476":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-33","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"**Health**"},"7477":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-34","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"Derived per project by `health-rule@1`: **at risk** if a P0 is blocked > 3 days, the next milestone is overdue, or any open item is overdue or blocked; **off track** if two of those hold or the trouble ratio ≥ 20 %. An owner may override (*health\\_overridden*)."},"7478":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-35","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"The derivation is a `health_derivation` decision — the rule version is pinned in it."},"7479":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-36","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"**ApprovalRequest**"},"7480":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-37","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"The original noun: a parked side effect or a Flow `approval` node waiting for a person."},"7481":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-38","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-objects","content":"Unchanged contract; deciders, expiry sweep, outbox event."},"7482":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-39","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-acceptance-gate","content":"Done in VibeBan is not a column you drag into. An item's **acceptance** is computed from its references: the\nacceptance criteria linked to it and, for each, whether a human `verifies` link exists. Moving an item to a *done*\nstage with open criteria answers *422 ACCEPTANCE\\_OPEN* — unless the move carries an `override_reason`, in which case the\nmove succeeds and an `acceptance_gate` decision records *moved anyway* with the reason. The board shows this as the\ndoor *n acceptance criteria are not verified — Move anyway · Keep it here · Review criteria*."},"7483":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-40","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#the-acceptance-gate","content":"Why derive rather than store: a stored \"accepted\" flag decays; a derivation from the RTM links stays true as tests and\ncriteria change, and the platform's own coverage — &#x2A;Requirements → AC %*, &#x2A;AC → Tests %* per epic on the References\ntab — is the same computation at project scale."},"7484":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-41","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#wip-limits-are-soft-and-recorded","content":"A move past a stage's WIP limit succeeds. The response carries `wip_exceeded = true`, the board says *Over the WIP\nlimit (6 / 5) — moved anyway*, and a `wip_limit_decision` records the alternatives (*move · keep*) with the outcome\n*moved\\_anyway*. A hard block would teach people to raise the limit; a soft limit with a record teaches the platform\nwhere limits are wrong."},"7485":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-42","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#who-may-do-what--agent--principal","content":"Relation"},"7486":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-43","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#who-may-do-what--agent--principal","content":"Actions"},"7487":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-44","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#who-may-do-what--agent--principal","content":"**viewer**"},"7488":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-45","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#who-may-do-what--agent--principal","content":"view · comment · reference.view · saved\\_view\\.edit"},"7489":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-46","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#who-may-do-what--agent--principal","content":"**editor** and **agent\\_member**"},"7490":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-47","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#who-may-do-what--agent--principal","content":"+ edit · create · move · assign · link · iteration.plan · milestone.edit · reference.attach · project\\_update.write"},"7491":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-48","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#who-may-do-what--agent--principal","content":"**human editor** only"},"7492":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-49","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#who-may-do-what--agent--principal","content":"+ delete · iteration.start / complete / cancel · automation.bind"},"7493":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-50","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#who-may-do-what--agent--principal","content":"**owner**"},"7494":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-51","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#who-may-do-what--agent--principal","content":"+ share · administer · archive · reference.import · work\\_dataset.publish"},"7495":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-52","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#who-may-do-what--agent--principal","content":"An **agent** that is `agent_member` of a project acts only in the intersection of its own relation and the relation of\nthe human it works for — an agent cannot move an item its principal may not move. The **human-only** set is enforced\nbefore OpenFGA and answers *403 AUTHOR\\_NOT\\_HUMAN* to any agent or service: decide an approval; create, share,\nadminister or archive a project; delete or share an item; start, complete or cancel an iteration; import references;\nbind an automation; verify a criterion. An organization administrator without a relation sees **counts only**\n(*Content hidden*). Hidden resources answer *404*; forbidden actions *403 PEP\\_DENIED*; a classification above\nthe project's ceiling *403 CLASSIFICATION\\_CEILING*. Every record carries `allowed_actions[]` decided server-side for\nthe reader — the board never authorises in the browser."},"7496":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-53","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"Kind"},"7497":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-54","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"When"},"7498":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-55","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"Outcome written by"},"7499":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-56","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"`my_work_ranking`"},"7500":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-57","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"every My Work read"},"7501":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-58","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"what you open first (implicit)"},"7502":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-59","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"`wip_limit_decision`"},"7503":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-60","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"a move past a limit"},"7504":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-61","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"*moved\\_anyway*"},"7505":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-62","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"`search_ranking`"},"7506":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-63","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"⌘K and list search"},"7507":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-64","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"the pick"},"7508":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-65","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"`iteration_carryover_default`"},"7509":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-66","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"completing a sprint"},"7510":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-67","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"the disposition chosen"},"7511":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-68","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"`health_derivation`"},"7512":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-69","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"every project read"},"7513":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-70","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"an owner's override"},"7514":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-71","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"`reference_match`"},"7515":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-72","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"import and attach suggestions"},"7516":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-73","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"accept · dismiss"},"7517":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-74","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"`acceptance_gate`"},"7518":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-75","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"a Done move with open criteria"},"7519":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-76","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"*moved anyway* with reason · kept"},"7520":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-77","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#decision-data","content":"Records carry URIs and short labels only — a reference body or an item's description never enters a decision row."},"7521":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-78","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#between-the-applications","content":"**Flows wait here.** An `approval` node or a parked tool call creates an `ApprovalRequest`; the decision emits\n`nexus.tasks.approval.completed.v1` through the outbox and the chat-worker resumes the run exactly once."},"7522":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-79","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#between-the-applications","content":"**NexChat is one Ask bar away.** &#x2A;Ask about ‹project›…* on a project header opens a NexChat thread with the project\nas context; agents read the project through the `task.*` tools when those ship (S5 F, not built)."},"7523":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-80","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#between-the-applications","content":"**The platform documents itself.** The `nexus_docs` importer reads the implementation folders and ADRs, previews the\nreferences it found, and applies them as links; *Re-sync* refreshes without duplicating. This is how the *Nexi\nPlatform* project shows coverage of the platform's own requirements."},"7524":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-81","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#between-the-applications","content":"**Events.** 32 `nexus.tasks.*` channels are declared; automation and work-dataset events are not yet emitted."},"7525":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-82","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#what-is-built-and-what-is-not","content":"S1–S4 (domain and My Work · projects, board, list, realtime · backlog, iterations, milestones · references and the\nimporter) are approved (2026-09-24). S5 A — the acceptance gate — is built; S5 B paging, C inspector leftovers,\nD automation, E a live Inbox and F the `task.*` agent tools are not. The **Inbox** is a prototype on fixtures;\n**Automation** is a contract only; the checklist is not shipped; the work dataset (S6) and hardening (S7) are not\nstarted. The release image set includes tasks-api but not yet the VibeBan web."},"7526":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-83","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#where-to-read-more","content":"The chapters: My Work and the Inbox · Create a project and run the board · Plan an iteration · References and acceptance."},"7527":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-84","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#where-to-read-more","content":"The contract: Tasks API — 87 operations, tags *approvals · work\\_projects · work\\_items · iterations · milestones · references · read\\_models · system*."},"7528":{"id":"/docs/technical/vibeban-85","page_id":"/docs/technical/vibeban","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vibeban#where-to-read-more","content":"Approvals from the Flow side: Decide the approval and read the run."},"7529":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","type":"page","content":"Vocabulary","breadcrumbs":["Nexi Docs","Technical documentation","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary"},"7530":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-0","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"The words Nexi uses, in one sentence each."},"7531":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-1","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"Word"},"7532":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-2","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"Meaning"},"7533":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-3","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Organization**"},"7534":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-4","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"Your company's space in Nexi. It owns people, Projects, models, connections and policies."},"7535":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-5","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Project**"},"7536":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-6","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"Where work happens. Every conversation, file, agent and flow belongs to a Project, and what you can see is decided by your membership in it."},"7537":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-7","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Agent**"},"7538":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-8","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"A configured assistant: instructions, the Skills it applies, the Tools it may use, and how it reaches a model. &#x2A;Agent works.*"},"7539":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-9","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Skill**"},"7540":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-10","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"A portable instruction package with examples, reviewed by a person before it is published. It owns no tools, model or credentials. &#x2A;Skill teaches.*"},"7541":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-11","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Tool**"},"7542":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-12","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"A governed operation — call an API, query a database, run code in the Sandbox — reached through a Connection. &#x2A;Tool acts.*"},"7543":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-13","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Flow**"},"7544":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-14","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"A sequence of steps: agents, tools, conditions, joins, human approvals and loops. &#x2A;Flow orchestrates.*"},"7545":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-15","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Goal**"},"7546":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-16","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"What a loop in a Flow must achieve, with limits on iterations, time and budget. &#x2A;Goal directs.*"},"7547":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-17","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Evaluator**"},"7548":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-18","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"Decides whether a Goal is met. The engine decides; the model never marks its own work as done. &#x2A;Evaluator judges.*"},"7549":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-19","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Sandbox**"},"7550":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-20","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"Where model-generated code runs: isolated, without credentials, without direct network access. &#x2A;Sandbox executes code.*"},"7551":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-21","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Synapse**"},"7552":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-22","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"The Model Gateway and the Connections — the only way agents and flows reach models and external systems. &#x2A;Synapse connects.*"},"7553":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-23","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Connection**"},"7554":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-24","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"A governed link to an external system or model provider, with its own credentials and scope."},"7555":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-25","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Blueprint**"},"7556":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-26","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"A package of agents, skills, flows and their requirements, installed into a Project or an organization."},"7557":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-27","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Approval**"},"7558":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-28","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"A pause in a Flow or an agent action that a person must confirm in VibeBan (NexTasks) before it continues."},"7559":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-29","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Core**"},"7560":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-30","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"NexCore — the application where an organization governs who can see, use, publish and connect what. &#x2A;Core governs.*"},"7561":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-31","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Auto**"},"7562":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-32","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"The default in the composer: a classifier reads the intent, deterministic code ranks the Project's capabilities you may use, and the route is recorded before it runs."},"7563":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-33","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Route · route line**"},"7564":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-34","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"The recorded choice under an answer — *Auto → Analyst · model · runtime* — and the door to &#x2A;Why this route?*, the decision record with every candidate."},"7565":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-35","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Arm**"},"7566":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-36","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"A non-agent answer that competes in Auto: the **data arm** (NexBI's engine), the **knowledge arm** (NexGraph resolve), the **capability arm** (a product's tools)."},"7567":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-37","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Resolver**"},"7568":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-38","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"The Flow Auto hands a message to when nothing in the Project fits: it surveys what exists and what you may do, proposes a plan you accept, change or decline, and asks the right people for connections and tools."},"7569":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-39","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Decision record**"},"7570":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-40","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"Every place Nexi picks among alternatives — a route, a WIP override, a template plan, a Resolver plan — kept with its full action space, scores, the chosen arm and the outcome people gave it."},"7571":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-41","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Module**"},"7572":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-42","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"An application an organization turns on by installing a pack — NexMap, NexCare, NexForge. Its API answers only when the Blueprint lists it; its tile appears only then."},"7573":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-43","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Module gate**"},"7574":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-44","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"The check every module API runs first: is this module enabled for the organization? Unknown is closed."},"7575":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-45","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Platform action**"},"7576":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-46","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"A command an app declares in the tool registry — *open my inbox*, &#x2A;create a task…* — that NexChat runs through the owning app as you, typed or spoken, before any model."},"7577":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-47","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Confirmation level**"},"7578":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-48","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"How much a command needs from you: 1 runs at once · 2 previews, a *yes* required · 3 shows the exact change · 4 is an on-screen door only."},"7579":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-49","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Context snapshot · context chip**"},"7580":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-50","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"A reference to what you are looking at — app, resource, selection, filters — handed over by an Ask bar and shown above the composer, so *this* and *it* point somewhere; verified only after the owning app said you may read it."},"7581":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-51","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"**Spoken**"},"7582":{"id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary-52","page_id":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/technical/vocabulary","content":"The mark under a message that began as speech. The audio is gone; the words stay."},"7583":{"id":"/d