e**; in the acceptance Flow shown here the rejected branch ends on a step called *Held back*, so the list\nitself says what happened. Nothing downstream ran."],[4763,"**✓ Approve*&#x2A; · **⊗ Reject**"],[2412,"**0 · Bootstrap**"],[2417,"**1 · Application**"],[5926,"**12 groups · 2 107 objects in this scope** and the table **Objects in the allowed subgraph** with **Group · Lane ·\nTier · Objects · Verified · Contested · Updated**. Each group tells you what it holds in its name —\n**organization · 107 entities · 1 594 mentions**, **Nexi documentation · 77 documents · 462 pages · 5 726\nfragments** — and its lane and tier. The **claims** group reads &#x2A;*82 %** verified and **0** contested."],[2422,"**2 · Tenant / user**"],[5932,"**2 objects in this view**: **Northwind Traders · organization** and **Northwind Traders GmbH · organization** —\nthe agreement names the company both ways and the resolver, cautious, kept two entities. (Merging them is a\nvocabulary decision — see Vocabulary.) Search narrows the current stage; it does not leave the\ngroup."],[2061,"**3310** — the public origin"],[610,"**403 · humans only** — even the agent that requested it."],[616,"**403 · not a decider** — the card shows &#x2A;Waiting for \\<owner>* without buttons."],[614,"**403 · self-approval** — someone else in the list must decide."],[612,"**409** — an expired request is never approved silently."],[726,"**5 minutes**, then mint a new one"],[495,"**A block you may not see keeps its place.** The dashboard's layout is the same for everyone; the block reads *Not\navailable to you*. Denials are per block, never per dashboard."],[2323,"**A cloud provider.** Put the key in `apps/core-api/.env` as `NEXUS_OPENAI_API_KEY=…` (or `NEXUS_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`)\nand restart the stack. The registry that ships with the stack (`config/synapse/models.yaml`, created from the\nexample on first start) references the key as `env://NEXUS_OPENAI_API_KEY` — the file holds a reference, never the\nkey, so it is safe to read and to commit. Never put a key into `models.yaml` itself: core-api refuses to start when\nit finds a literal secret there."],[6503,"**A Flow is where completion is decided.*&#x2A; &#x2A;\"Fits budget and weather OK\"* is a **Goal** with a limit of three rounds.\nThe **Evaluator** judges; the loop engine stops. A model never marks its own work as done, and a Flow can never run\nforever or spend without a ceiling."],[68,"**A greyed row with a reason**"],[2324,"**A local model, no internet.** Start llama.cpp with the bundled helper, then start the stack in the disconnected\nprofile:"],[1939,"**A model provider.** Nexi answers nothing without a model: a cloud provider key (OpenAI, Anthropic …) *or* a\nlocal OpenAI-compatible server (llama.cpp, Ollama) for the disconnected profile. Every rung shows where the key\ngoes; it never goes into a file you would commit."],[7324,"**A person sits on the path of every side effect** that policy or the binding marks as needing approval — as a card\nin the thread, backed by NexTasks. See Give the agent Tools."],[6504,"**A person stays in the loop where it matters.** The approval step is a real pause, visible in NexTasks, with the\nevidence attached. A Flow that changes something outside the conversation always has one."],[5150,"**A published skill can be pending too.** If you edit a published skill, agents keep applying the last reviewed\nversion and the header reads *Review pending — this version is not applied by agents until approved*."],[65,"**A red note under a form** you were allowed to open"],[6500,"**A Skill owns nothing but knowledge.** The *Weekend planning checklist* has no model, no credentials and no tools.\nThat is why the same Skill can teach a *Team offsite planner* agent next month, and why a person reviews it before\nit is published — you are reviewing judgement, not code."],[62,"**A statement where the content would be** — &#x2A;Your access does not allow this. …*"],[6502,"**A Tool is the only thing that touches the world.** The *Calendar* Tool can create events because a Connection with\nthe right credentials exists and your Project is allowed to use it. The agent cannot invent a new capability; it can\nonly ask for a Tool it has been given."],[6845,"**A wider scope never widens rights.** *All knowledge* is the union of your relations plus the Base tier; it adds\nProjects you already hold, never ones you do not."],[2030,"**About the envelope key.** Until the `kms://` driver lands, `broker-master-key` is a Secrets Manager entry like the\nothers. Protect it accordingly: a separate KMS key for that entry's encryption, restricted resource policy, and a\nbackup outside the account — without it, every stored connection credential is unreadable."],[7610,"**Acceptance gate**"],[5825,"**Access (ACL)**"],[5885,"**Access check**"],[6870,"**Access check**"],[5443,"**Account · Olena Shevchenko · olena\\@northwind.example**, four tabs — **Profile · Security · Sessions ·\nAppearance & language**. Profile: **Name**, **E-mail**, **Role** *Organization Owner*, **Classification**\n*Secret* (her clearance), **Joined** *Sep 19, 2026*, **Identities** *Nexi account* — the provider she signs\nin with. The hint: &#x2A;Role and clearance are set by your organization's administrators.* **Edit** changes the\ndisplay name only."],[4442,"**Across the Project**"],[5786,"**Add knowledge source** with the sentence that governs it: &#x2A;NexGraph defines the scope. Synapse connects. NexCore\nchecks rights.* Four radio cards:"],[5578,"**Add model** — and the header reads *7 configured · 1 healthy*. The new row **Team Qwen (local) · Ollama ·\n127.0.0.1:11434 · Local · Healthy · chat · Confidential** is selected and its inspector open: **Enabled** on,\n**Health Healthy** (Core probed the provider on registration), and the sentence that bounds Core's role —\n&#x2A;Core does not replace Model Fabric routing — it only narrows what routing may choose.* Because this is the\norganization's own model, **Delete model** is offered."],[6844,"**Administering is not reading.** An organization administrator without a Project relation sees the operational\nview (bindings, grants, budgets, run health) and no document names, counts of knowledge or content."],[6855,"**Agent / service**"],[368,"**agent member**"],[6509,"**Agent Studio** in your Project"],[6491,"**Agent works.** Instructions + the Skills it applies + the Tools it may use + how it reaches a model."],[229,"**Agent**"],[5201,"**Agent**"],[6388,"**Agent**"],[6392,"**Agent**"],[6396,"**Agent**"],[6489,"**Agent**"],[6598,"**Agent**"],[6606,"**Agent**"],[6622,"**Agent**"],[7151,"**Agent**"],[7537,"**Agent**"],[6417,"**Agentic Data Scientist** (template 1.6.1)"],[4586,"**Agents → New agent**, one sentence: &#x2A;Read the accommodation offers we received and turn them into one comparison\ntable: place, price for two nights, driving time, whether the dog is welcome, what is included. Never invent a\nnumber.* Rename the draft to **Offer reader** and save."],[5267,"**Agents**: **General** (*everyday knowledge work in the Project*), **Analyst** (*extraction, classification and\ncomparison with provenance*), **Writer**, **Reviewer** (*grounded answers and comparisons — citations\nmandatory*) and **Governance** (*classifies events for the administrators' flow; never decides*). These are the\nagents you met in the NexChat guide; the General agent is the one that answered the first conversation."],[5604,"**AI proposes, the person applies.** A sentence goes first through a deterministic grammar (*add a note X* needs no\nmodel); otherwise the **Scene Agent** returns a proposal, drawn as a ghost with &#x2A;*Apply · Modify · Cancel · Why\nthis?**. Small changes apply at once; adding, deleting and the doors to other apps wait for you. Agents hold read\ntools only."],[5736,"**All knowledge · 2 projects · platform knowledge** first, then your Projects with their classification and chat\ncount, then **Manage projects in NexCore**. Projects are made and staffed in NexChat and NexCore; NexGraph only reads\nthe relation you already hold."],[5730,"**All knowledge**"],[6279,"**All my work** lists the items on your name, grouped **Critical · In progress · Waiting · Ready · Later**. The\norder inside a group is a ranking VibeBan records as a decision (`my_work_ranking`) with the alternatives it\nconsidered — so a later model can learn from what you actually opened first."],[2534,"**An accessible name.** Every interactive element has one — text, a label, or `aria-label` on an icon-only control.\nAn icon is decoration (`aria-hidden`); the name is on the control."],[6501,"**An Agent is the one you talk to.** It applies Skills and uses Tools, and it reaches a model only through Synapse —\nso which model, at what cost, with what data leaving the organization, is decided by your administrator, not by\nthe agent."],[389,"**An editor cannot publish.** Taras, editor of *Autumn catalogue*, can author a new agent and a new flow, run\nthem as drafts, and hand them to Olena; the *Publish* button is refused for him. This is the review gate, not a\nlimitation to work around."],[390,"**An organization administrator cannot write in a Project from outside.** Olena can add or remove members of\nany Project, archive it, or approve what waits in it — but cannot send a message or run a flow there unless she\nis also owner or editor. (Reading is the one part of that rule not yet closed in this build; see\nHow Nexi decides.)"],[6389,"**Analysis planner**"],[5867,"**Anchoring terms**"],[6860,"**Anchoring terms**"],[5446,"**Appearance & language** is the one tab that is purely this device's: **Theme** &#x2A;System · Light · Graphite\n(arriving with the next release)* — *a preference for this device; System follows your operating system* —\nand **Language** *English · Українська*."],[1969,"**Application Load Balancer** via the **AWS Load Balancer Controller** + **ACM** certificate + **Route 53**"],[7272,"**Applications** are what people open. Each has one job and its own nouns:"],[5627,"**Applied: Added Review with security · Undo · Why this?**. The note is a real object (*STICKY · GENERIC* in the\nInspector), the version chip moved on, History shows the batch with the source *typed*. **Undo** replays the\nstored inverse of your own batch — up to a hundred deep."],[4914,"**Approval by policy** / **Always requires approval**"],[5149,"**Approval is pinned to a version.** The moment anyone saves a change on any tab, the skill is *v0.1.4* and the\nreview of *v0.1.3* no longer counts — the header falls back to *Review pending*."],[4753,"**APPROVAL NEEDED** · *Agentic result for Plan the weekend — review before publishing*"],[4952,"**Approval**"],[6614,"**Approval**"],[7557,"**Approval**"],[7479,"**ApprovalRequest**"],[5146,"**Approve this version**"],[387,"**Approve** — decide an approval request a run is parked on (see below)."],[6069,"**Arithmetic**"],[6835,"**Arithmetic** applies to tables with a *Total* row or column: the total must equal the sum of its parts within\nhalf of the last printed digit per part. A total that checks out verifies itself *and* its components; a total that\ndoes not falsifies both; a table without totals leaves the check unrun."],[7565,"**Arm**"],[6555,"**Arms**"],[2119,"**Artifacts**"],[4506,"**Ask anything about Acme shipments · Project context applies automatically.** Above the composer, a chip:\n&#x2A;*sample\\_dataset.xlsx · 44.4 MB · confidential · ✕**. While it uploads the chip reads &#x2A;Reading…* then\n&#x2A;Uploading…*; you can type meanwhile — only **Send*&#x2A; waits. The hint under the composer: *@ to pick an agent · /\nto use a skill · + to add sources*."],[5542,"**Audit** answers the same way: &#x2A;Your access does not allow this. Only an Owner or Admin can read the\norganization's audit log.* Two more facts were written while he looked."],[5464,"**Audit** shows *Signed in* and *Revoked sessions* rows for each of those acts."],[5551,"**Audit** then carries **Viewed payloads · Allow** for the administrator, with Reason `2:completion,input_messages`."],[306,"**Auditor**"],[5002,"**Auto → Direct answer · engine:nexbi**: the number is computed by the governed query engine as you, and the\nmodel is never given the rows. Drafts of a chart and a table follow. The data arm bids only when a validated\nmetric matches the words *and* its entity has a bound dataset — the *Why* panel shows the two ticks. The full walk\nis in the NexBI guide: Ask your data from NexChat."],[5006,"**Auto → General · with Gmail.** The capability arm recognised a product family and offered the mail tools; the\nanswer carries a **capability card** — *Connect Google Workspace* — because the tool needs a connection you have\nnot made. Connecting happens in NexCore under your consent; nothing is read before. If the Project's owner has not\nallowed the tool, the card reads *Ask a Project owner to allow mail search* and the request goes to them as a\ngoverned **CapabilityRequest** — agents never bind tools themselves. Details in\nGive the agent Tools."],[7561,"**Auto**"],[4992,"**Auto** is the default in every NexChat composer. It reads your message and the Project it is in and picks *how* to\nanswer: a plain reply from General, a specialist agent, a Flow, a computed number from NexBI, an answer from the\nknowledge graph — or, when nothing in the Project can do what you asked, a **Resolver** run that surveys what is\nmissing and proposes a plan. Every choice is written down before it runs and is readable afterwards. This chapter\nwalks the routes you will meet and how to read each one."],[3958,"**Auto** is ticked — &#x2A;Nexi picks the capability and Synapse picks the smallest qualified model; the answer\nnames both.* Below it the models this Project may use, each with a one-line note (*Recommended for this\nProject*, *Faster, lower cost*, *Approved local deployment*), and the footer *Model availability is controlled\nby Project policy*."],[6995,"**Automation**"],[7633,"**Automation**"],[1994,"**AWS Load Balancer Controller**"],[2151,"**Back up.** Three named volumes hold everything: `pgdata` (all four databases), `natsdata` (in-flight jobs; safe to\nlose, unpleasant to lose mid-run) and `broker-secrets` (the sealed credential store). Back up Postgres logically and\nthe credential store with its master key:"],[6311,"**Backlog** on the left, the chosen iteration on the right — **Sprint 1 · 5 items · 13 pts · 1 people**, its goal,\nand the note *active — additions count as a scope change*. **Add** moves a row into the iteration, **Remove**\nsends it back; nothing else about the item changes — its stage, assignees and rank inside the backlog are kept.\nUp to 200 items can be planned at once."],[441,"**Base-tier knowledge is nobody's to verify.** The platform documentation every organization receives is\nread-only; its claims have no *Verify* button for anyone, and it can be hidden for an organization but never\nedited."],[1981,"**Bedrock** as a Tier-4 provider (planned) · a provider key in Secrets Manager · **a GPU node group** with vLLM/llama.cpp"],[6424,"**Blueprint**"],[7157,"**Blueprint**"],[7555,"**Blueprint**"],[5285,"**Blueprints & Packs › Overview** shows two layers, seven active restrictions and zero conflicts; the **Matrix**\nnames the layer behind every effective value; **Packs** shows *Nexi Base · signed · Installed*."],[5657,"**Board**: the same objects on a free canvas with the tool rail on the left; the Inspector stays open; the selection\nsurvives. **3D**: the five objects as solids on a grid in perspective (&#x2A;28° · 32°*), presets **Perspective · Iso ·\nPlan · Front · Right**, *Snap · 10 px*, *Measure*, the chip **Conceptual** — a reminder that this is a model of\nideas, not an engineering drawing. **Front** gives an orthographic elevation (&#x2A;5° · 0°*) where heights are\ncomparable. **Present**: the scene full-bleed with *1 / 1* and previous/next; steps are the scene's cameras,\n`←` `→` `Space` move, `Esc` leaves. Switching views is not an edit; the version chip never moves."],[2125,"**Bootstrap secrets**"],[5718,"**Bronze · Silver · Gold**"],[7685,"**Bronze · Silver · Gold**"],[6753,"**Bronze** — raw bytes in the object store · **Silver** — fragments, mentions, vectors in pgvector · **Gold** — entities and verified facts in Apache AGE"],[315,"**Builder**"],[5339,"**Builder**"],[7003,"**Cache per viewer.** Results are cached keyed by viewer, dataset version and query; a new version or a revocation\ninvalidates; nothing is served across people."],[5282,"**Capabilities** lists the pack's five agents, ten skills and nine patterns as *Organization · Published*; the\nsame list appears for a plain member."],[309,"**Capability Admin**"],[5335,"**Capability Admin**"],[7701,"**Capture policy**"],[5739,"**Capture: Off**. The select offers **Off** (&#x2A;Nothing is captured.*), **Explicit** (&#x2A;only when a person says \"save as\nproposed knowledge\"*), **Outcomes** (*results of canonical Agent/Flow runs, as proposed claims*) and\n**Conversation** (*also conversation content, under the Project's classification*). The facts beside it are the\npromises that hold whichever mode you choose: **Audience — Never widened — the people who could see the source**,\n**Layer — Subject · proposed until reviewed**, the Project's **Classification** and the **Retention**. Below,\n**Recent outcomes** with the tabs *All · Agent run · Flow run · Artifact · Message* — empty here: &#x2A;No captured\noutcomes yet.*"],[7654,"**Care session**"],[7662,"**Care Studio**"],[4147,"**Certify** is disabled until the acknowledgement is ticked; as an editor the button is absent and the API answers *403*."],[7258,"**Channels** — a Telegram bot with its health"],[725,"**Chat API** (`/api/v1/chat/…`), **Tasks API** (`/api/v1/tasks/…`) and **Graph API** (`/api/v1/graph/…`)"],[4467,"**Cheapest qualified** — the smallest model that clears the quality floor (default). *Quality first* — best score for the role, cost second. *Inside the contour* — never leaves the deployment; no cloud tier. *Pinned model* — developer mode: bypasses routing; the organization's Blueprint may refuse it, in which case the pin is ignored and recorded."],[5724,"**Claim**"],[6783,"**Claim**"],[7691,"**Claim**"],[6841,"**Claims** are reconciled: a claim of `v2` with the same locator and value keeps its verdict; a changed value\n*supersedes* the old claim and reopens verification; a *different source* with a different value *contests* both."],[5583,"**Classification ceiling Confidential · Explicit selection — · Auto routing Allowed · Fallback allowed Enabled\n· Max cost units / day No limit · Rate limit No limit**, and the formula: &#x2A;Effective availability = provider\nenabled ∩ organization ∩ project ∩ agent ∩ user ∩ classification ∩ Blueprint.* This is where a model is\nnarrowed to Projects or groups, given a daily budget or a rate, or made pinnable by name (*Explicit\nselection*) — each a tightening of what routing may choose, never a widening."],[4944,"**Classification ceiling**"],[242,"**Clearance.** Every person has a **clearance** (*Public · Confidential · DSK · Secret · Top secret*), set by the\nadministrators in People; every Project, file, agent and run has a **classification**. A person reads and acts\nonly at or below their clearance. Olena, with *Secret*, may open a *Confidential* Project; a member cleared to\n*Confidential* never sees a *Secret* one, whatever their role."],[4761,"**Comment (optional)** · *A note for the audit trail*"],[6413,"**Confidential analytics sandbox**"],[7577,"**Confirmation level**"],[7061,"**Confirmation levels** (`packs/nexus-forge/policies/forge-confirmation.json`; a Blueprint may only raise): 1 —\nmove, resize, transform, style, colour key, layer, visibility, lock, camera, undo, redo, reorder apply at once with an\nUndo line; 2 — add, update, connect, group, semantic, property, track step, layout show a card; 3 — delete, ungroup,\ndisconnect, bind, unbind, restore show the exact change; 4 — convert, publish, export, import are **doors**, never\ncompleted by words."],[7246,"**Connected accounts**"],[5816,"**Connection**"],[7145,"**Connection**"],[7553,"**Connection**"],[7204,"**Connections**"],[5822,"**Content**"],[7579,"**Context snapshot · context chip**"],[2538,"**Contrast.** Text and the borders that carry meaning hold 4.5 : 1 against their surface in Light and Graphite; the\ndata palette holds 3 : 1 against both."],[7012,"**Core.** Every operation names one PEP action (`dataset.read · query.run · dashboard.publish · metric.certify …`);\norganization scope (`/bi/organization/…`) maps *admin → owner, member → viewer* and seeds the platform dashboards from\nthe product-metrics measurement; an administrator without a Project relation sees counts and ids, never data\n(*Administering is not reading*)."],[7559,"**Core**"],[7233,"**Cost and data stay where you decided.** Tiers, local-only strategies and per-candidate policy checks make \"which\nmodel saw this\" a governed answer, not a surprise."],[7695,"**Curator**"],[4303,"**Customer**: the person and company, channel, language, verification state, previous conversations and the\naccount fields — *read from the CRM through Synapse, not stored in Care*. **Knowledge**: the verified claims the\nassistant used (*SOP-OPS-02 v2 — Зміна ETA/ETD*, the client tariff), each linking into NexGraph, and the retrieval\npolicy of the guardrail profile. **Case*&#x2A; &#x2A;(preview)*: the VibeBan work item linked to this conversation, or\n**Create case** when the work will outlive the chat. **Activity**: the audit trail — assistant turns, handoff\nrequested, joined, reply sent — with times and actors."],[6898,"**Dagster UI**"],[7627,"**Dashboard · version**"],[6987,"**Dashboard** · **DashboardVersion**"],[5733,"**Data science · Knowledge of this Project · confidential** and the posture line **Knowledge operational**. The\n**Knowledge pulse** reads left to right the way knowledge is made: **Sources 2 → Documents 8 → Claims → Verified**,\nwith *fragments*, *pages*, *contested* and *proposed* counted underneath. Four counters (**Documents ingested**,\n**Claims verified**, **Contested open**, **Runs · 24 h**). Then two tables side by side: **Sources** (the\nProject's *Uploads* and the read-only *Nexi documentation* of the **Base** tier) and **Datastores** — *Bronze ·\nobject store · raw captures*, *Silver · pgvector · fragments & vectors*, *Gold · Apache AGE · entities & verified\nfacts* — each with its volume and state. Below, **Pipeline · last 24 h** lists the six stages with *done · running\n· failed* counts, and **Knowledge by tier** shows how much of what you see is your Project's and how much is base.\nThe sidebar: **Overview**; **Knowledge** — Graph Studio, Sources, Vocabulary; **Operations** — Pipeline, Review."],[6397,"**Data scientist**"],[4177,"**Data** lists the dataset as *v1 · OK · Certified*."],[7617,"**Dataset · version**"],[6971,"**Dataset** · **DatasetVersion**"],[6081,"**Decided** counts **28**; searching the queue for `On-time rate` shows five **Falsified** rows."],[7569,"**Decision record**"],[385,"**Delete · administer · export** — archive the Project, add and remove members, change its governance, export\ncontent (an export of *DSK* or above also needs a stated purpose)."],[5092,"**Description**"],[6552,"**Deterministic ranking**"],[235,"**Device**"],[7670,"**Dictation**"],[6540,"**Discovery + PDP filter**"],[1936,"**Docker** (Docker Desktop or Engine 24+) on every rung, including the laptop — Postgres and Keycloak run in it and\nthe sandbox uses it."],[6767,"**Document item**"],[7167,"**Domain** is what your organization treats as true. A claim arrives here only through a gate: an automatic check\nagainst a trustworthy source, or a person. &#x2A;*A model can never mark its own claim verified.**"],[4841,"**Done**"],[7672,"**Door**"],[695,"**Doors that exist in a contract but are not served yet** — the BI *Insights* 