roject_id}/studio/landscape` (`getLandscape`), `GET …/studio/clusters/{cluster_id}/members`,\n`GET …/studio/objects/{uri}/nearby` (`getNearby`), `GET …/objects/{uri}` (`getObject`), `GET …/objects`\n(`listObjects` — the List twin and the search box: `q`, `scope`, `tier`, `layer`, `status`, `kind`, `cluster_id`),\n`GET …/objects/{uri}/figure` (an authenticated door for figure images). Across Projects: `GET\n/graph/studio/landscape`. Try them on Graph API › Graph Studio."],[6108,"`GET /graph/projects/{project_id}/vocabulary/in-use` (`listTermsInUse`) aggregates entities of the allowed subgraph\nwith their mention and source counts — the same entities Studio shows, projected as a list. Types are the resolver's\nclosed set — &#x2A;Organization · Person · Role · Location · Amount · Date · Product · Technology · Document (named)*. The\nregistry endpoints — `…/vocabulary/terms` (managed terms), `…/vocabulary/proposals`, `…/vocabulary/snapshots` — and a\ncurator's `POST …/entities/{entity_id}/merge-proposals` exist in the contract; their screens follow their release\ngate. Across Projects: `GET /graph/vocabulary/in-use`."],[6109,"`GET /graph/projects/{project_id}/vocabulary/in-use`, `GET /graph/vocabulary/in-use` (`listTermsInUseAll`), `GET\n/graph/projects/{project_id}/vocabulary/terms` (`listTerms`), `…/vocabulary/proposals`, `…/vocabulary/snapshots`,\n`POST …/entities/{entity_id}/merge-proposals`. Try them on Graph API › Vocabulary."],[2494,"`GET /health` (internal)"],[2497,"`GET /idp/health/ready` on the management port (internal)"],[7082,"`GET /map/view?c=lon,lat,zoom&t=…&l=…` returns either **cells** or **objects**, never a mix, and the client draws\nwhat it gets. The server computes the H3 resolution for the viewport (r2–r8), counts the **unique permitted\nentities** per cell inside the SQL query — the relation filter is in the `WHERE`, not applied afterwards — drops cells\nunder the Blueprint's `tuning.map.min_cell_count` (suppression drops, never zeroes: `count ≥ 1