kspace`; `service` (administrators only)"],[3513,"`page` · `inline` · `url` · `surface-legacy`"],[2212,"`password`"],[3085,"`plain` · `hint` · `error` · `required` · `textarea`"],[6611,"`plan.step`"],[7033,"`platform/guardrails` is a **platform port**, not a Care feature:\n`GuardrailPort.evaluate(stage, profile, subject, features)` with stages `input · retrieval · tool · output`, budgets\n400 ms (input, output) and 1.5 s (retrieval, tool), and every verdict written to the decision sink as a\n`guardrail_verdict`. Checks are deterministic: a forbidden-topic lexicon, PII and secret patterns, prompt-injection\nmarkers, a grounding threshold (`tuning.care.handoff.grounding_min`, 0.6), and a tool allow-list (the `tool` stage\nrejects anything outside the profile's `tools_allowed`). Profiles are pack resources\n(`packs/nexus-care/guardrails/*.json`, contract `guardrail-profile&#x60;): &#x2A;*`internal`*&#x2A; passes through by default,\n&#x2A;*`external_authenticated`*&#x2A; and &#x2A;*`external_public`** **fail closed** on timeout or engine error. The seams\nexist in the Model Gateway and the Agent Runtime; NexCare's public edge is where the external profiles bite today. A\nblock is a handover, not a wall: the customer reads &#x2A;I'm handing this over to a person…*, the desk reads a\n`guardrail-note` naming the rule. A red-team corpus runs in CI (`tests/redteam/corpus.jsonl`; expansion is open)."],[183,"`POLICY_CONNECTION_NOT_OWNED` · `CONNECTION_ADMINISTER_DENIED` · `CREDENTIAL_READ_DENIED`"],[180,"`POLICY_MODEL_NOT_ENTITLED` · `POLICY_TOOL_NOT_ENTITLED`"],[151,"`POLICY_UNAVAILABLE`"],[3337,"`populated-connected` · `populated-native` · `empty-setup-door` · `org-admin-d423` · `loading` · `error` · `denied` · `offline`"],[3288,"`populated` · `empty` · `loading` · `error` · `not_found` · `offline`"],[2887,"`populated` · `few` · `many` · `reader` · `empty_writer` · `empty_reader` · `loading` · `error` · `offline` · `empty_search`"],[3025,"`populated` · `selectable` · `empty` · `loading` · `error` · `wrapping` · `bare-header-forbidden`"],[3327,"`populated` · `selected` · `with-meta` · `empty` · `loading` · `error`"],[7086,"`position_kind ∈ observed · geocoded · interpolated · estimated`; `interpolated` is valid **only** under a `playback:` URI"],[4088,"`POST /bi/projects/{project_id}/automations {kind, target_ref, schedule, params}` calls chat-api\n`POST /internal/flows/instantiate` with the template URI, the parameters and the caller's identity; the resulting\nFlow id is stored on the **Automation** row (`flow_ref`). `POST …/automations/{id}/run` → chat-api\n`/internal/flows/run`; `POST …/automations/{id}/sync` → `/internal/flows/reference` to refresh the Flow's state and\nlast run. The Flow's tool nodes call back into bi-api's S2S tools (`bi.dashboard.describe`, `bi.alert.evaluate`,\n`dataset.describe`) asserting the automation owner as the human principal — so the rights checked are the owner's,\nnever a service's. Events: `nexus.bi.alert.fired.v1`, `nexus.bi.alert.acknowledged.v1`."],[4149,"`POST /bi/projects/{project_id}/metrics` creates the draft from the expression (the model-facing door\n`…/metrics/propose` accepts only a frozen query or artifact reference — never a sentence — and marks the draft as\nagent-created). `POST …/metrics/{metric_id}/validate` compiles and runs a query with `purpose = metric_validation`\nunder the read-only role; `POST …/certify {acknowledge: true}` requires `metric.certify` and a human principal;\n`POST …/deprecate` flips the lifecycle and emits the event. Resolution for NexChat is `POST …/metrics/resolve` — the\nclassifier's short terms in, ranked candidates and the chosen one out, recorded as a `metric_resolution` decision with\nits whole candidate list. `GET …/metrics/{metric_id}/usage` is the *Used by* of a metric."],[4119,"`POST /bi/projects/{project_id}/plans {decision_statement, template_ref?}` returns the plan (slots, matched metrics,\nreasons) and its `decision_ref`; `POST …/plans/{plan_id}/instantiate` creates the Dashboard and its draft.\n`PUT …/dashboards/{dashboard_id}/draft` replaces the whole draft (blocks are references; the Block schema has\n`additionalProperties: false`); `POST …/blocks` is the Canvas' *Add to dashboard*. `GET …/coverage` and\n`GET …/suggestions` feed the two panels; `POST …/suggestions/{id}/apply | dismiss` write the outcome.\n`POST …/publish {acknowledge: true, note?}` requires `dashboard.publish` and a human, freezes a DashboardVersion and\nemits `nexus.bi.dashboard.published.v1`. Templates come from the signed **nexus-base** pack (`GET /bi/templates`); the\n*Nexi itself* templates read the platform's own product metrics."],[4567,"`POST /chat/projects/{project_id}/attachments` (`createAttachment`), `GET /chat/attachments/{attachment_id}`, `POST\n/chat/threads/{thread_id}/messages` (`sendMessage`, `attachment_uris[]` ≤ 8), `GET /chat/routes/{route_id}` (the\ndecision record), `GET /chat/flow-runs/{run_id}` · `…/steps` · `…/iterations`, `POST …/pause` · `…/resume` ·\n`…/loop/stop` · `…/cancel`, `GET /chat/projects/{project_id}/artifacts`, `GET /chat/artifacts/{artifact_id}` ·\n`…/versions`, `GET /chat/artifacts/{artifact_id}/export?format=docx|pdf|md|xlsx|csv|ipynb`, `GET/POST\n/chat/projects/{project_id}/context` (pinned sources), `GET /chat/projects/{project_id}/datasets`,\n`GET /chat/datasets/{dataset_id}` · `…/schema`, `POST /chat/flow-runs/{run_id}/recompute`, `GET /chat/agents/runs/{run_id}`. See the\nAPI reference."],[4060,"`POST /chat/projects/{project_id}/threads/{thread_id}/messages` · `GET /chat/routes/{route_id}` ·\n`POST /chat/messages/{message_id}/reroute` — Chat API · `POST /bi/projects/{project_id}/queries` ·\n`GET /bi/projects/{project_id}/queries/{query_id}` · `POST …/dashboards/{dashboard_id}/blocks` — BI API."],[5505,"`POST /chat/projects` (NexChat's dialog) creates the Project in the caller's workspace — any workspace member may —\nand writes its creator as **owner**; the Project inherits the organization's classification and Blueprint. Core\nreads `GET /chat/projects` and, where allowed, `GET /chat/projects/{id}/members` (metadata by reference). The\nlist is already filtered by the server to Projects the caller holds a relation in; a `GET /chat/projects/{id}` by a\nnon-member is refused as `404 NOT_FOUND`, so existence is never confirmed to outsiders."],[5509,"`POST /chat/projects` `{ name, instructions?, accent?, classification?, idempotency_key }` (201), `GET /chat/projects`,\n`GET /chat/projects/{id}` (404 for non-members), `GET /chat/projects/{id}/members`, `POST /chat/projects/{id}/members`\nand `PUT …/members/{subject_id}` `{ subject_id, subject_type, relation }` (owner or admin; 403 otherwise),\n`DELETE …/members/{subject_id}`, `GET /chat/projects/{id}/archive-impact`. See the API reference."],[5021,"`POST /chat/threads/{thread_id}/messages` (`sendMessage`) · `GET /chat/routes/{route_id}` (`getRouteDecision`) ·\n`POST /chat/routes/{route_id}/confirm` · `POST /chat/messages/{message_id}/reroute` · `POST /chat/messages/{message_id}/regenerate` ·\n`GET /chat/projects/{project_id}/capabilities` · `GET /chat/flow-runs/{run_id}` · `GET /chat/capability-requests` —\nChat API. Route outcomes (`/chat/routes/{id}/outcomes`) and the rights dry run (`/pep/dryrun`) are\ninternal in this slice and not yet in the published contract."],[5020,"`POST /chat/threads/{thread_id}/messages` runs the Auto pipeline in chat-api — lexicon pass → discovery + PDP filter →\nsticky → *IntentAnalysis* from the `classifier` role via Synapse (prompt `intent_execute.md`) → deterministic\nranking → arms (data · knowledge · capability) → Resolver hand-off — and writes a **RouteDecision**\n(`GET /chat/routes/{route_id}`): state features, every candidate with its features and eligibility, the score\ndistribution, the chosen arm with closed reason codes, propensity 1.0, cost. *Try another route* is\n`POST /chat/messages/{message_id}/reroute`; *Run* on a card is `POST /chat/routes/{route_id}/confirm`. Reroute,\nregenerate, decline, Stop and card decisions are written back as outcomes keyed by the decision id — the record is\ntraining-grade decision data; no request text is stored in it. The Resolver is the pack Flow `flw_tpl_auto_resolver`,\npublished into the Project (`POST /chat/projects/{project_id}/flows/instantiate`), with the Blueprint budget\n`tuning.auto.resolver` — 8 iterations · 360 s · 60 k tokens · 3 drafts · 3 requests · 7-day wait — and a\n`tuning.auto.resolver.enabled` switch. Rights chips come from core-api's `POST /pep/dryrun` as the asker;\nconnection requests raised for you are `connection-requests/on-behalf` in NexCore."],[7720,"`POST /chat/voice/speech` derives **one sentence server-side** from the settled turn: a card speaks its result\n(&#x2A;Opening Inbox.* · &#x2A;Which one: A or B?* · &#x2A;Task created — MKT-1.*); a text answer is spoken as a **gist** — one\n`chat_fast` call with `prompts/voice_spoken_gist.md`, ≤ 35 words, first sentence as fallback — preceded by an\nacknowledgement (&#x2A;Let me look.* · &#x2A;One moment.* · &#x2A;On it.&#x2A;) the moment the words are understood. The **`tts`\nrole** (floor 0.7) is served by `ukrainian-tts` (Tetiana) for Ukrainian and `gpt-4o-mini-tts` for en/ru/de up to\n*confidential*; at *secret* a non-Ukrainian answer stays text. One `SpeechPlayer` per tab; the strip offers **Stop** and\n**Text only** (sessionStorage — no `synthesize` call leaves); `+` → *Turn voice answers off*. Tapping the mic over\nspeech is barge-in."],[7122,"`POST /map/decisions/{id}/outcomes` assigns `label_source` server-side; `llm_proposed` is unrepresentable in\n`MapLabelSource` — no model is in the loop today, and the schema keeps it that way. No feedback UI."],[7102,"`POST /map/uploads` (`map.upload`, editors and owners, ≤ 64 MiB GeoJSON or CSV) parses rows into observations under\na new source and answers `{placed, without_position, rejected[] {row, reason}}` with sixteen closed reasons\n(*coordinate out of range*, *swapped axes suspected*…). Nothing is placed at (0, 0); the (0, 0) row becomes *without\nposition*. `DELETE /map/uploads/{id}` removes exactly the rows it created. `GET /map/sources` lists the demo world\n(`MAP_DEMO_WORLD=1` on the dev stack: 637 objects on a Silk corridor Lviv → Hamburg, frozen at 2026-09-24 16:00 UTC,\nevery source labelled *fixture*, refused in production) and uploads. Live feeds through Synapse, the `map-worker`,\nthe Dagster `nexus_map` code location and the outbox relay are **not built** (S3)."],[5424,"`POST /organizations/join-requests` `{ organization }` (201; 403 `JOIN_DOMAIN_NOT_ALLOWED`; 404 unknown handle),\n`GET /organizations/join-requests/mine`, `GET /organizations/{id}/join-requests` (administrators; 403 otherwise), `POST /organizations/{id}/join-requests/{request}/approve` with `{ role }` and `…/decline`,\n`PATCH /organizations/{id}` with `{ domains }`. See the API reference."],[5361,"`POST /organizations` (201; 409 `ALREADY_IN_ORGANIZATION`), `GET /organizations/{id}`,\n`GET|POST /organizations/{id}/invitations` (records only — never the token), `GET /organizations/{id}/members`,\n`GET /session/context` (tenant, clearance and memberships of the current session). See the\nAPI reference."],[7062,"`POST /scenes/{id}/turns` is **one multipart door**: `audio` *or* `text`, a `SceneContextSnapshot`\n(`active_view, selection_ids, pointer_target, viewport, visible_ids, language, captured_at`), `request_id`, `lang`,\noptional `proposal_id` and `dictate`. Order: module gate → PEP `forge.scene.edit` → rate limit (`turn_rpm` 30) →\nsnapshot version check (`SNAPSHOT_STALE`) → \\[audio] transcription through core-api's Gateway → **grammar first**\n(deterministic en/uk; a parse with a unique referent needs no model) → **deixis** (`selection > pointer > name`; a tie\nis a `choice`, never a guess) → the **Scene Agent** → a `SceneProposal`. The SSE stream yields `transcript` first\n(text, language, confidence — never persisted), then one of `proposal | choice | applied | answer | navigate | decline`."],[6261,"`POST /tasks/projects` · `GET /tasks/projects/{project_id}/stages` · `GET /tasks/projects/{project_id}/items` ·\n`POST /tasks/items` · `POST /tasks/items/{item_id}/move` · `POST /tasks/items/{item_id}/assign` ·\n`POST /tasks/items/{item_id}/relations` · `POST /tasks/projects/{project_id}/updates` ·\n`GET /tasks/projects/{project_id}/activity` — Tasks API."],[6359,"`POST /tasks/references` · `POST /tasks/items/{item_id}/references` · `GET /tasks/items/{item_id}/acceptance` ·\n`GET /tasks/items/{item_id}/reference-suggestions` · `POST /tasks/projects/{project_id}/references/import` ·\n`GET /tasks/projects/{project_id}/references/coverage` · `POST /tasks/items/{item_id}/move` (`override_reason`) —\nTasks API."],[7728,"`POST /v1/audio/speech&#x60;, loopback **:8091**"],[7727,"`POST /v1/audio/transcriptions&#x60; (OpenAI-shaped), loopback **:8090**"],[2138,"`POSTGRES_IMAGE` · `NATS_IMAGE`"],[1961,"`postgres.mode: external`, `postgres.host`, `postgres.sslmode: require`"],[2072,"`postgres`"],[4942,"`project.read`"],[6648,"`prompts/intent_execute.md` in chat-api"],[7060,"`publish` marks a version for the (future) graph projection."],[177,"`PURPOSE_REQUIRED`"],[3057,"`quiet` · `quiet-with-reason` · `inline` · `card-legacy`"],[3055,"`quiet` (default): one line of title, one primary action, ≤ 3 starting points as plain links, a `body` only when a permission or dependency explains the emptiness. `inline`: the one-line version for a table body, column or Inspector section. `card` (dashed, options chips) is legacy."],[3046,"`read` · `read-cannot-edit` · `editing` · `error` · `dirty-cancel`"],[7514,"`reference_match`"],[6575,"`regenerate`"],[168,"`RELATION_MISSING`"],[2370,"`RELEASE.json`"],[2005,"`RELEASE.json` is the manifest each release publishes — every image by digest. Nodes pull from ECR with their node\nrole; no `imagePullSecret` is needed inside the account. Turn on ECR image scanning and immutable tags on the\