"1"],[2690,"1"],[2702,"1"],[2706,"1"],[2718,"1"],[2722,"1"],[2726,"1"],[2251,"1 · Developer laptop"],[704,"1 · From this portal (recommended for the playground)"],[6922,"1 agent · 4 skills · 3 flows · 3 guardrail profiles · Blueprint layer"],[6926,"1 agent (Scene Agent) · 1 skill · 5 scene templates · confirmation-level policy · Blueprint layer"],[1435,"1.101.0 (e): the Project **owner** restores a retired type — its entities are read again, the label is offered again. Idempotent. `nexus.graph.vocabulary.type.restored.v1`."],[1432,"1.101.0 (e): the Project **owner** retires a type for this Project — L0 shipped or a stored L1/L2 term alike. An overlay, never a deletion: the entities of the type stay rows, but every read of the Project (in-use terms · landscape · search · neighbourhood) leaves them out and counts them as hidden; the type leaves `entity_label_choices` and the worker drops it from new runs' detector labels. Idempotent. `nexus.graph.vocabulary.type.retired.v1`."],[1071,"1.121.0 ((3)) — the person's answer to a completed `web-research` run's `outputs.proposed_source` (*Add to knowledge · Not now*). `add` creates the Project's `web` binding through graph-api's normal source route **as the person** (graph-api's PEP decides `binding.create`; a twin the Project already reads is found, not doubled); `not_now` changes nothing. The hosts and URLs are the run's own outputs — the body carries only the choice. Either answer is one `research_source_proposal` decision (both arms, propensity 1.0) with its `human_explicit` outcome `source_added` · `source_dismissed` (rule 85). A person only — 403 `ACTOR_NOT_HUMAN` for an agent; 409 `RUN_NOT_COMPLETED` · `NO_SOURCE_PROPOSAL`; 403 `SOURCE_ADD_DENIED` when graph-api refuses the person; 503 `GRAPH_API_UNAVAILABLE`."],[1529,"1.124.0 (c): what references the connection — flows (scheduled or not) and agents from chat-api, knowledge sources from graph-api, datasets from bi-api — aggregated over bearer service edges. Owner of a `user` connection or administrator; `unavailable[]` names the edges that did not answer."],[1051,"1.13.0 — clears the pause flag and re-publishes `nexus.jobs.run.continue.v1` for every id in current_node_ids (attempt 1, msg id dedupes a double click). Only `paused` runs (a `waiting` run with the flag set just drops the flag). PepAction=invoke + relation owner|editor."],[1050,"1.13.0 — cooperative pause. Sets pause_requested_by; the worker finishes the *current* step and schedules nothing; status becomes `paused` with current_node_ids = the nodes that would have run next. A waiting run stays `waiting` with the flag set and pauses when it is woken. PepAction=invoke + relation owner|editor."],[1073,"1.14.0 — human stop of the active loop container. Sets FlowRun.loop_stop_requested_by; the current body attempt finishes, the open pass closes with exit_reason=human_stop / stopped_by and the run follows the loop's when=needs_human edge (never silently completes the goal). PepAction=invoke + relation owner|editor. Cooperative — the response shows the flag set, the exit arrives with the next step."],[1072,"1.14.0 — loop-container iterations of a run (badge \"3 / 10\", goal progress, criteria results, budget). Read from the durable flow_loop_iterations rows (the loop's state — never reconstructed from the bus); body node attempts remain in /steps with their `iteration`. Same visibility as GET /chat/flow-runs/{run_id}."],[1741,"1.148.0 ( A4) — the templates *New project* offers: the three built-ins first, then the tenant's installed pack templates (`PackResourceKind tasks.project_template`, read from core-api's service door, cached ≤ 60 s). Any signed-in human; nothing of a tenant's content."],[1355,"1.152.0 ( A4): the owner shares the source with the whole organization (`tier: organization`) or takes it back (`project`). The binding, its versions and their Lexical records (items · chunks · page renders · embeddings · datasets) move to the tier; the origin project_id stays; entities and claims remain the origin Project's. Owner-only; operable from the origin Project alone (404 elsewhere). Emits binding.shared.v1. Idempotent."],[974,"1.18.0 — BlobMeta of one stored blob (media type, size, sha256, classification, who / what wrote it, retention class). PepAction=read on the owning Project and clearance for the blob's classification — 404 otherwise (no existence leak). Never a location."],[969,"1.18.0 — export a Notebook artifact as .ipynb (nbformat 4) generated server-side from the canonical nexus-notebook-v1 body (own exporter; forbidden MIME outputs refused, classification banner as the first markdown cell). PepAction=export on the Project (READ is not enough). Stored as a blob (retention_class=export, Notebook.export.ipynb_ref) on first export and re-used for the same version."],[1177,"1.18.0 — export a Notebook artifact as .ipynb (nbformat 4) generated server-side from the canonical nexus-notebook-v1 body (own exporter; forbidden MIME outputs refused, classification banner as the first markdown cell). PepAction=export on the Project (READ is not enough). Stored as a blob (retention_class=export, Notebook.export.ipynb_ref) on first export and re-used for the same version."],[975,"1.18.0 — stream the bytes of a blob. PepAction=read on the owning Project and clearance for the blob's classification; the digest is re-checked while streaming (mismatch → 500 BLOB_CORRUPT + audit, never partial trust). Served as an attachment with the sniffed media type — never rendered inline as HTML / script. This is the ONLY way bytes leave the store; there is no presigned or public URL. (finding 7): a blob that is an execution's code / stdout / stderr (the record's code_ref / stdout_ref / stderr_ref) follows the …/output rule — owner | editor; a viewer gets 403 SANDBOX_OUTPUT_RESTRICTED (metadata too)."],[1176,"1.18.0 — the bounded, redacted stdout or stderr of an execution as text (what stdout_ref / stderr_ref point to). Redacted by nexus_security before 