0,"2\\. Every API checks policy before it acts"],[1784,"3"],[2586,"3"],[2602,"3"],[2622,"3"],[2626,"3"],[2650,"3"],[2674,"3"],[2686,"3"],[2710,"3"],[2730,"3"],[2734,"3"],[706,"3 · From a script, with the cookie"],[2154,"3 · Kubernetes"],[6671,"3\\. Models and external systems are reached only through Synapse"],[2014,"32 random bytes, base64"],[2017,"32 random bytes, base64"],[2067,"3300 · 3301 · 3304"],[2070,"3303"],[2082,"3307 (map, loopback) · — · —"],[2064,"3320 (loopback)"],[5890,"38 → 8 · 288 ms"],[5887,"39 → 39 · 5 ms"],[1789,"4"],[2570,"4"],[2614,"4"],[2634,"4"],[2646,"4"],[2662,"4"],[2666,"4"],[2694,"4"],[2698,"4"],[2762,"4"],[2766,"4"],[2786,"4"],[2822,"4"],[1945,"4 · AWS — reference architecture"],[5896,"4 → 4 · 2 ms"],[2090,"4 vCPU and 8 GB RAM are comfortable for the stack itself; the disconnected model server wants more (see step 5)."],[6672,"4\\. What you compose"],[5878,"42 → 31 · 2 ms"],[2590,"5"],[2618,"5"],[2678,"5"],[2826,"5"],[2830,"5"],[2834,"5"],[2838,"5"],[2073,"5533"],[2566,"6"],[2594,"6"],[2598,"6"],[2658,"6"],[2738,"6"],[2758,"6"],[2778,"6"],[2814,"6"],[2818,"6"],[5869,"6 → 2 · 9 ms"],[2562,"7"],[2654,"7"],[2670,"7"],[2782,"7"],[2746,"8"],[2750,"8"],[2794,"8"],[2798,"8"],[6641,"8 · 360 s · 60 k · 20 · 3 · 3 · 7 d · 24 h"],[5893,"8 → 4 · 4 ms"],[2554,"9"],[6563,"A \"we cannot do this\" is itself work: find out what is missing and ask the right person."],[4900,"a **binding** — attaching a tool to an agent — never gives anyone more than they already have;"],[5935,"A **CO\\_MENTION** relation is a *Subject*-layer edge: the two entities were mentioned in the same fragment. It is a\nproposal about relatedness, not a verified fact — which is what the **Proposed** state on every entity says."],[5832,"A **continuous** binding shows more here: a **Sync** section (*Last sync · Result · Files: n seen · new or changed\n· missing · settling · Next sync · Permissions*), **Pause** and **Resume** beside **Revoke** (&#x2A;Pausing stops the\nsync and new runs; a running job finishes. Revoking stops for good and deletes nothing.*), and when something is\nwrong, a **next action** in plain words — &#x2A;The folder is not reachable from the worker. Check the mount and the\npath, then wait for the next sync.* or &#x2A;Re-authorize the connection to resume.* with a **Re-authorize** button."],[4394,"A **Draft** exists only for the builders of the Project: nobody can pick it in chat, and *Test in chat* is the only way to talk to it. **Published** means it is in the `@` picker for everyone in the Project. (Two more states exist: *Disabled* and *Archived* — the agent stays in history but cannot be used.)"],[5071,"A **Draft** is visible only to the Project's builders and cannot be attached to any agent. **Published** puts it in the agent's Skills tab for everyone in the Project. (A third state, *Disabled*, keeps the skill in history but it can be neither reviewed nor published.)"],[4806,"a **Goal** is a measurable target with limits — *budget\\_fit ≥ 0.9, at most 6 passes, at most 60 minutes*;"],[3951,"A **Grounding** drawer opens on the right with three sections. **Sources** — the Project material the answer\nused (none yet: the Project has no knowledge attached). **Graph facts** — verified facts from the organization's\nknowledge graph (none yet). **Run** — the model that answered, a run reference you can quote when asking for\nhelp, and the time. The footer states the rule the whole platform follows: &#x2A;Claims are verified only by the\noracle or a human reviewer — never by the model.*"],[4541,"A **member** sees the same card without **Publish**: &#x2A;Ask the Project owner to publish.* — **Keep as drafts** stays\navailable. The owner is notified (*Approval assigned to you*) in the Notifications inbox."],[4131,"A **metric** is a named, versioned definition — &#x2A;Late delivery rate = SUM(late\\_deliveries) / SUM(shipments)* — over an\nentity of the Project's semantic model. Dashboards, alerts and NexChat's direct answers resolve metrics by name, so a\nnumber means the same thing everywhere. This chapter walks the lifecycle **draft → validated → certified →\ndeprecated** on the six metrics of the Logistics Project."],[291,"a **Project relation** — *owner, editor, viewer, operator* — what a person is **inside one Project**. It says what\nthey may do with that Project's threads, files, agents, flows and approvals."],[5625,"A **proposal card**: *Added Review with security · Text* with &#x2A;*Apply · Modify · Why this?**; the sticky is drawn\ndashed on the canvas as a ghost. The sentence went first to a deterministic **grammar** (*add a note X* with no\nambiguous referent needs no model); where the grammar is not enough the **Scene Agent** proposes. Adding is a\nlevel-2 change, so it waits for you. A sentence that moves or recolours (level 1) applies at once with an **Undo**\nline; deleting, ungrouping and the doors (levels 3–4) always wait."],[7053,"A **Scene** (`nexus://forge/scene/<id>&#x60;) belongs to a NexChat Project and carries one **`SceneSpec` 1.0**: a\ncoordinate system (`unit px|m|cm`, `up_axis z`), `layers[]`, `objects[]`, `relations[]`, `groups[]`, `cameras[]`,\n`views`, a `color_key`, `bindings[]` and `tracks[]`. A **SceneObject** has a `kind` (sticky · text · shape · image ·\nframe · node), a shape, a real **transform** (`position {x, y, z}`, `rotation_deg`) and **geometry** (`width, depth,\nheight`, a primitive box · cylinder · wedge · plane), a `style` (eight hues or none, tint/solid/outline,\nthin/thick/dashed — colour is scene data) and a `semantic.type` from twenty-six closed types. Relations have\nnine kinds; bindings seven (`work_item · flow · artifact · claim · dataset · agent · map_feature`) and are references\nonly. A view is a **projection** of this one spec: switching views is not an operation and the version does not move.\nThe 3D view says *Conceptual* on screen and in every export."],[5034,"A **search answer card**: *via OpenStreetMap · open data · places&#x2A;, two results as external links with host and\nsnippet (*\\[1] Spaces Khreshchatyk — coworking, 5 Khreshchatyk Street&#x2A;, *\\[2] Khreshchatyk — street in Kyiv*),\n**Providers tried: 3** (Wikipedia skipped, Wikidata skipped, OpenStreetMap answered) and the foot &#x2A;Titles and\nsnippets are the provider's text, shown as found — nothing in them was run.* The answer cites \\[1] and \\[2]; a\ncitation that points at no result is dropped. Footer: *Auto → General · web search*. For places and facts open data\ngoes first; for the rest the Blueprint's order (Tavily → LangSearch → open data → own index by default); the first\nprovider that answers wins; at most ten results."],[6241,"A **stage** is yours to name. Every stage maps to a **category** — *backlog · ready · in progress · review · done ·\ncancelled* — and it is the category that My Work, the counters and the health rule read, so you can rename\n*Review* to *QA* without breaking anything. *Blocked* is not a stage: it is a condition an item is in while another\nopen item **blocks** it."],[5014,"A **viewer** of the Project reads the plan with its steps and chips but without Accept, Change or Not now, and the\nline &#x2A;Waiting for the person who asked to accept, change or decline the plan.* Only the asker decides."],[498,"A **work project** in VibeBan is not a NexChat Project; it carries its own relations — `owner · editor · viewer ·\nagent_member` — granted by its owner, and personal items (`MY-n`) are shared person-to-person as viewer or editor.\nThe rule that makes VibeBan different: **an agent never outranks its principal**. An `agent_member` acts within the\nintersection of its own relation and the relation of the human it works for, and the sensitive actions are refused to\nany agent or service before OpenFGA is asked."],[3169,"A `<button>` or `<a>` that reads as a link — the inline look (DS-7012) over a 24 px target — in three tones: `inline` (text colour, underlined), `meta` (12 px secondary), `quiet` (13 px · 500 · secondary, underline on hover: the goal card's actions). `ActionRow` lays its children on one baseline with an `aria-hidden` `·` between, wraps, and is the only container for secondary actions under content (DS-7016). Replaces the seven app-local link-button classes and the ≈ 40 `*-actions` containers of the audit."],[6471,"A `DataScienceService` would need its own execution path, its own permission checks, its own way to reach models and\nits own idea of \"done\". Every one of those already exists once, generically: Agent Runtime, the Sandbox under a\nprofile, Synapse, the policy decision, the Flow engine's `GoalSpec`. Building the capability as a Flow means a builder\ncan *adapt* it from the Pattern Library — change the criteria, swap the reviewer, add a stage for their domain — and\nthat every improvement to the platform (a faster sandbox, a better coder model, a new approval rule) reaches it\nwithout a release. It also means the boundaries hold by construction: no bespoke code, so no bespoke hole."],[3416,"a `fieldset` with a legend; native radios; the button label changes with the choice"],[2953,"a `fieldset` with a visually hidden legend"],[3193,"a `form` labelled by its title; the summary takes focus on open; the required field is announced on submit; Esc returns focus to the opener; the ladder is the `role=status` of the write"],[2917,"a `main` with one `h1`; the form's first field takes focus; errors are `role=alert` next to the field"],[7094,"A `MapSpec` (a saved map's definition) cannot carry features, coordinates, counts or HTML"],[3251,"a `menu` opened from the Project name button; the count is text, not a badge alone"],[2888,"a `table` with a caption per day group; the row menu is a named `menu` opened from a labelled `⋯` button; *Show more* is a button that announces the new count"],[7475,"A `verifies` link from a person to an acceptance criterion is the act of verification."],[3800,"A `wide` frame: the `PulseStrip` on top, a row of `Stat`s, then `Section`s with `StatusList`s and &#x2A;View all →* links. Monochrome; no pie, no dashboard tiles with their own colours."],[3163,"A <button> or <a> that reads as a link — the inline look (DS-7012) over a 24 px target — in three tones: inline (text colour, underlined), meta (12 px secondary), quiet (13 px · 50"],[4980,"A binding is a row on the agent's version — tool id, tool version, an optional connection and an approval mode that\nmay only be stricter than the tool's own. When the agent proposes a call, Nexi evaluates it against everything at once:\nis the tool enabled and cleared for the Project's classification; is it bound to this agent and this operation; does the\n*person* hold the permission the tool requires; is the connection healthy and theirs; does policy allow it here and\nnow. Any *no* is a typed refusal you can read in *Technical details*. Side effects in a test are refused; side effects\nin a real chat with *Always requires approval* — or when policy says so — are **parked**: the call is recorded, an\napproval request is opened in NexTasks for the Project's owners, and the runtime waits. A decision re-enters exactly\nthat call with the grant attached; an expiry ends it with *nothing changed*. Connected tools additionally run inside\ntheir integration's **egress allow-list** — a call to any other host fails as `egress_denied` even if the model asks for\nit. None of this is in the prompt; it is the shape of the runtime."],[4456,"A binding may also be created for you: when a **capability request** (an agent asked for a tool it did not have, a\nperson approved) is granted, the tool appears here with the note *Bound by … from a capability request*."],[4202,"A block is a **reference**, not a number: a KPI references a *metric*; a chart or table references an *artifact*\n(a chart produced in NexChat or in the Studio) with a **version policy** — *follow latest* (the newest version of\nthe artifact), *follow latest approved* (the newest version a person published), or *pin* (exactly this version).\nThe dashboard version is immutable; what moves is what the references resolve to, and the policy says how far\nthey may move. A block you may not read — its metric above your clearance, its dataset outside your relation —\nkeeps its place in the grid with *Not available to you*, so two readers see the same layout and different numbers.\n*Not filtered by Carrier* on a block means that block's entity has no such dimension."],[7601,"A board column and what it means — *backlog · ready · in progress · review · done · cancelled*; *blocked* is a condition, not a stage."],[6260,"A board is `GET /tasks/projects/{project_id}/items` (paged, with the stages from `…/stages`) plus one server-sent\nevent stream per project; a move is `POST /tasks/items/{item_id}/move {stage_ref}` — tasks-api checks\n`work_item.move` at its enforcement point, writes the new stage and rank, sets `completed_at` when the target category\nis *done* (and clears it when an item leaves *done*), evaluates the WIP limit and records the decision, and emits\n`nexus.tasks.item.moved.v1`. Health is derived by the rule `health-rule@1` from the open items on every read of the\nOverview and My Work, and each derivation is a `health_derivation` decision; an owner's update with a health writes\nthe outcome `health_overridden` on it. Nothing in VibeBan runs a Flow on a move today — the `on_stage_enter`\nbinding exists in the contract for a later slice."],[3301,"A bordered choice with a title and a one-line description, 16 px radio in the first column, 10 px gap; the card is the label."],[3307,"A bordered choice with a title and a one-line description, 16 px radio in the first column, 10 px gap; the card is the label. Promoted from VibeBan's `.nexus-tasks-radio` (UX-AUDIT); the only way to offer two to five explained options — never a `Select` for that."],[5929,"A breadcrumb appears — **← Back · Landscape › organization** — and the status line **Entered organization · 107\nobjects on stage**. The table now lists **objects**: **Object · Kind · Lane · Tier · State**, each row an entity\nwith its type after a dot (**Google · organization**, **Keycloak · organization**) and its **State — Proposed**.\nThe line above the table is precise about scope: *107 objects in this view · not the whole organization*."],[6250,"A bug in *Fixing*, P0 · Critical, assigned to *Me*. Priorities are **P0 Critical · P1 High · P2 Normal · P3 Low*&#x2A;;\nthe red &#x2A;‼&#x2A; chip on the card is a P0, &#x2A;!* a P1."],[5552,"A Builder opening **Executions** or **Audit** reads *Your access does not allow this*, and the **Deny** filter\nafterwards shows *Administer · connection \\_all · Deny · NOT\\_AN\\_ADMINISTRATOR* for each attempt."],[7153,"A builder, from one sentence onwards."],[7156,"A builder, or Nexi drafts it from a description."],[7150,"A builder."],[4361,"A card &#x2A;Opening Inbox…* and, without a click, the shell lands in **VibeBan › Inbox** (*All 5 · Approvals 2 ·\nAssignments 1*). What happened: the sentence hit the **platform-action arm** — verb cue plus object cue matched\n`tasks.open_inbox` in the registry — before any model ran; the target was resolved through VibeBan's own door as\nyou; the policy decision point confirmed `read`; the href came from the registry's template, never from your\nwords. Level-1 actions (open, view) run at once; the route footer reads *Auto → Open Inbox · command*."],[4818,"A card appears while the draft is being saved."],[7588,"A card that says which provider answered (search API · open data · the platform's index), the results as found, and why that route."],[6070,"A cell in a **Total** row (or column) must equal the sum of the other cells of its column (row), within half of the last printed digit per part."],[5855,"A chat inside the Project whose sources you processed — here **Data science**. Open the Project in NexChat and\nstart a new chat there."],[5521,"A chat turn feels like a conversation. Underneath it is a **run**: an agent was started on someone's behalf, a\nmodel was called with a prompt built from the Project's context, an answer came back, and each of those facts was\nwritten down with a **correlation id** that ties them together. Core is where an administrator reads that record —\nnot the conversation, the *record of it*."],[4446,"A checklist of the skills the agent may apply. Two rules, both visible on the screen:"],[6773,"A chunk of items sized for retrieval, embedded once per (text hash, model)."],[6789,"A claim after the gate, with every verdict in its history."],[6072,"A claim is **Falsified** if *any* check falsifies it; **Verified** if transcription verified it and arithmetic\nverified it or did not run; otherwise it stays **Proposed** for a person."],[6836,"A claim is *falsified* if any check falsifies it, *verified* if transcription verified it and arithmetic verified it\nor did not run, otherwise *proposed* — for a person. In the Acme report the *Shipments*, *On time* and *Late* columns\nsum, so fifteen claims are verified by machine; the *On-time rate* column has a Total row that is a **ratio**, not a\nsum, so the oracle — which knows nothing of ratios — falsifies those five. That is the oracle being honest about the\nlimit of what it can check, and exactly the case a **curator** exists for."],[6559,"A closed en/uk/ru/de search lexicon, or a places/facts question, goes to the `web.search` provider port in core-api: providers in the Blueprint's order, open data first for places and facts, the first that answers wins, nothing leaves above `tuning.web_search.max_classification`. One model call with the results quoted as untrusted data and no tools; `[n]` validated against ranks. A **research cue** goes to the Resolver, which runs the base pack's `web-research` Flow (allow-list approval, HTTP reading plane, report with citations)."],[2201,"A cluster with a CNI that **enforces** NetworkPolicy (Calico, Cilium, most managed CNIs). kind's default CNI only\nstores the policies; the local script offers a Calico cluster config for that reason."],[2243,"A cluster without internet takes the release from a mirror and answers with a model it hosts itself:"],[3158,"A collapsible JSON view: keys muted, values typed by weight and a monospace face (never colour), containers with a count and a toggle; copy per node."],[3752,"A collection with nothing in it shows the quiet `EmptyState` in place of the list: one title, the primary action the header line also offers, up to three starting points. A table header is never left bare."],[3748,"A collection with nothing in it shows the quiet EmptyState in place of the list: one title, the primary action the header line also offers, up to three starting points."],[7460,"A column with a **category** — *backlog · ready · in\\_progress · review · done · cancelled* — and an optional WIP limit."],[7576,"A command an app declares in the tool registry — *open my inbox*, &#x2A;create a task…* — that NexChat runs through the owning app as you, typed or spoken, before any model."],[6539,"A command is a fact about the sentence, not an opinion of a model; resolving through the owning app means Auto never grants what the app would not. See Voice, screen context, search and research."],[3565,"A component that does not exist yet goes through the register, not around it."],[7538,"A configured assistant: instructions, the Skills it applies, the Tools it may use, and how it reaches a model. &#x2A;Agent works.*"],[4972,"A connected tool's passport has more lines than a platform tool's: **Protocol rest**, **Permissions**\n`suppliers_api.write`, **Classification ceiling ≤ confidential**, **Approval: Always requires approval**,\n**Egress hosts** `suppliers.acme-test.example` — the only host this tool may ever call — and **Integration**\n*Suppliers API · workspace*, the Synapse integration and the connection scope it uses. When an integration has\nseveral healthy connections, **Add** first asks you to choose one; with one it binds silently."],[7243,"A connection card"],[2437,"A connection credential (Tier 2)"],[7230,"A Connection is described to the browser and to agents by **what it is, not what it holds**: account, status, scopes\nin words, last used. Secrets never appear in a prompt, a log, an error message or a screen. If the calendar token\nexpires you get *Reconnect*; if you want it gone you *Disconnect* under **Connected accounts** in the user menu, and the\nprovider is told to revoke it."],[6080,"A contested claim is never resolved by the pipeline: the two source assertions stay, and a person confirms one as\nthe canonical claim (or returns both). A **new version** of either source reopens the claim as **Needs\nre-verification**; the oracle runs again and, if the value moved, the old verdict is **Superseded**."],[7260,"a conversation channel connected in NexCore › Synapse"],[7034,"A conversation has a &#x2A;*`HandlerState`** — `AI_ACTIVE`, `HANDOFF_PENDING`, `HUMAN_ACTIVE` — held under a row lock\nExactly one of the assistant or the joined person may send to the customer; a send on a stale version answers\n`409 HANDLER_CHANGED`. **Join** moves authority to the person; **Return** gives it back; **Resolve** needs a reason\ncode from a closed taxonomy (`care-topic-taxonomy`; `422 TOPIC_REQUIRED`) because the reason feeds Quality and the\nNexBI datasets. Handoff is **conversation-based**: the customer asks in words, or policy decides, and the\nconversation waits for a Join — the customer keeps writing meanwhile. \"AI resolved\" is distinguished from \"AI\ncontained\". Customer identity verification is a deterministic code check, and a CRM identity match is a\n**human decision** (`POST …/identity/{link_id}/decide`) — the model never marks anyone verified."],[6351,"A criterion has one of four states. **Verified** — the requirements trace in the documentation carries the\nevidence mark for it (the importer reads it; nobody sets it in VibeBan). **Accepted** — a person attached the\ncriterion to this item with the relation *verifies*: their name and time are on the link, and the count becomes\n*1 of n verified*. **Open** — criteria exist and tests are linked, but nobody has accepted it. **No test** — the\ncriterion has no test linked at all. An agent's or a model's judgment never becomes *accepted*; only a human\nattaches *verifies*. Detaching the link is a second explicit action and is recorded."],[4164,"A CSV with a header row. Ours has seven columns — `month · carrier · region · shipments · revenue · late_deliveries ·\nfreight_cost` — 189 rows for three carriers, three regions and 21 months."],[6837,"A curator (a person with the editor relation) decides within a **named scope**: *transcription + arithmetic — not the\nsupplier's performance*. The decision is an **OracleRun** of type *human\\_review* with a human actor, and a decision\nrecord whose outcome — `label_source = human_explicit` — is written back to the extractor's original `decision_id`.\nAgents and services are refused (`AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN`), whatever relation their owner holds; the Base tier is never\nverifiable by a tenant. Every verdict names its author or oracle version, and nothing is erased: the oracle's\n*falsified* stays as the first line of a claim's history under the curator's *confirmed*."],[6075,"A curator with the right relation sees an enabled **Verify** on a *Proposed* or *Contested* claim. The panel below\nis from the platform's own review fixtures (a Project called *Контроль постачань* — \"delivery control\" — with a\nUkrainian corpus; the interface is the same)."],[56,"A customer from a page that is not allowed"],[7424,"a customer through the widget or Telegram; Care Studio"],[6890,"a Dagster code location (`dagster dev` on a laptop; a Deployment in Kubernetes) as role `graph_worker`"],[4100,"A dashboard in NexBI starts from a **decision**, not from a blank grid: &#x2A;Which carrier contracts to renegotiate to bring\nlate deliveries under control.* The planner matches the sentence to the closest **template** — a set of decision\nperspectives (*outcome · driver · volume · risk · target · what changed*) — and tells you before anything is created\nwhich slots the Project's metrics can fill. This chapter builds *Carrier performance* that way, then reads the Studio."],[7471,"A date with a status *open · reached · missed · cancelled*."],[7607,"A date with a status only a person sets — *open · reached · missed · cancelled*."],[2202,"A default StorageClass for Postgres and NATS volumes (in-cluster mode) and for core-api's credential store."],[7622,"A definition in a closed grammar — *draft → validated → certified → deprecated*; a human steward certifies."],[4145,"A deprecated metric **stays resolvable** for the dashboards that already show it — with a badge — so nothing\nbreaks silently; it disappears from the pickers for new blocks and from NexChat's resolution. Nothing is deleted."],[3740,"A detail surface reads by default; Edit turns its properties into controls; Save commits and shows *Saved*; Cancel on a dirty form asks inline."],[3744,"A detail surface reads by default; Edit turns its properties into controls; Save commits and shows *Saved*; Cancel on a dirty form asks inline. Switches commit on change without an Edit mode."],[5727,"A deterministic check. *Transcription* re-reads the value from the cell; *arithmetic* checks a Total against the sum of its parts."],[7694,"A deterministic, versioned check — transcription re-reads the cell, arithmetic checks a Total against its parts. Never a model."],[4526,"A document that leads with **What stands out**, then how the data is organised, the suggestions, data quality — and cites every artifact. The chat answer under the run is that first section."],[7518,"a Done move with open criteria"],[6988,"A draft plus immutable published versions. Blocks are **references**: a KPI to a metric; a chart or table to a Project artifact with a `version_policy` (*follow\\_latest · follow\\_latest\\_approved · pin*); text and section blocks. A block carrying a spec copy is refused (*422 SPEC\\_COPY\\_REJECTED*)."],[5797,"A Drive folder and everything under it, through the Google connection *you* authorised in NexCore."],[6887,"a FastAPI service owning the `nexus_graph` database as role `graph_api` (row-level security applies)"],[4401,"A fifth element appears only when needed: a **governance pill**. NexCore may review agents; the states are *Not\nreviewed*, *Under review*, *Approved* and **Blocked**. A blocked agent shows *Blocked by NexCore governance* with the\nreason; *Publish* and *Test in chat* are disabled and the agent is hidden from the picker until the block is lifted.\nIf the governance service cannot be reached at all, NexChat tells you &#x2A;Governance checks are temporarily\nunavailable. Nothing was changed.* — it never guesses."],[4503,"A file: `.xlsx`, `.csv`, `.tsv`, `.parquet` (up to **64 MB**), or notes, JSON and e-mail up to 1 000 000\ncharacters. Our example is a workbook of service incidents, `sample_dataset.xlsx`: two sheets, 20 061 rows × 57\ncolumns, the second sheet a legend of field definitions."],[4534,"A finished run now **reads as an answer** first: the report's *What stands out* section is lifted into the thread as\ntext, then one line — &#x2A;Analysis report · Document · v1 · Published · Open in Canvas · Export ▾* — then *N artifacts\npublished · notebook*, and the staged card you watched above is folded under **Show the stages & drafts**. A second\nline names the **Dataset card · v1 · Open in Canvas**."],[6553,"A fixed sum over the eligible candidates: +0.45 intent match · +0.2 domain · +0.1 Project-owned · +0.15 × specificity · −0.15 for a side effect the message did not ask for. Two thresholds: `ambiguity_margin` (ask rather than guess) and `min_specialist_score` (below it, General or the Resolver)."],[4733,"A Flow has parked on “Review results”. Find it, read what it is asking and who may answer, approve or reject with a note for the audit trail, follow both endings, start the same Flow from a chat, and read the History. About fifteen minutes."],[6551,"A Flow may have side effects; words alone are not enough evidence."],[7590,"A Flow that plans, asks which hosts it may read, reads them, and reports with citations and a proposed source you may add."],[5019,"A Flow with side effects never runs from Auto without a &#x2A;Run …?* card."],[31,"A form that opens for everyone and refuses on submit"],[6017,"A full-width workspace: the app sidebar collapsed to icons, a header **← Sources · northwind-framework-agreement-\n2027.pdf · v1 · 2 pages** and, right, &#x2A;*PDF 1 / 2 · printed —** (the printed page number, when the document has\none). Left rail: **PAGES** (*PDF 1 — Framework Transport Agreement*, *PDF 2 — 6. Payment*, each with its first\nheading), **OBJECTS** with counts (**Tables 1 · Figures 0 · Mentions 80 · Entities 59 · Fragments 8**),\n**COVERAGE 2 / 2 done**, **PIPELINE · Completed · 22.09 23:50**."],[7651,"A geographic area a person defined (a corridor, a port, a warehouse) that objects are inside of and geofence Flows will react to."],[7554,"A governed link to an external system or model provider, with its own credentials and scope."],[7542,"A governed operation — call an API, query a database, run code in the Sandbox — reached through a Connection. &#x2A;Tool acts.*"],[6972,"A governed table in `nexus_bi` with a profile, quality checks (*ok · warnings · failed · no\\_data*) and a row policy. Sources: a CSV/XLSX upload (≤ 64 MiB · ≤ 5 M rows), a NexGraph Gold dataset version, an Agentic Data Scientist result, a Flow output. A **correction** is a new version with a note."],[7618,"A governed table with immutable versions — from a file, the knowledge graph, an analysis or a Flow — with quality checks, a row policy, corrections and revocation."],[5191,"A hands-free way to say, hear and confirm — with the same rights, the same cards and the same records as typing.\nNext: Act from anywhere — what a spoken command can do."],[3938,"A header with the Project name and its chevron, a **Confidential** tag, and four places on the right:\n**Chats · Agents · Skills · Flows**. The sidebar shows the Project selected with &#x2A;No chats in this Project yet —\nstart one above.* The centre reads &#x2A;Ask anything about Weekend trips — Project context applies automatically.*"],[6769,"A heading, paragraph, table, cell, figure, code block or formula on a page — with its span. Produced by the parser."],[7111,"a hexagon or object opened"],[1321,"A HUMAN curator's verdict: creates an OracleRun {oracle.type=human_review, actor.kind=human} and moves the claim to verified|falsified; the verdict scope codes are mandatory. Agents and services get 403 AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN. Writes a curator_verdict GraphDecisionRecord. When the Blueprint requires it the decision is parked as a NexTasks approval and 202 is returned."],[6974,"A human editor publishes; a human owner revokes (a revoked version is never served again, and its dashboards say so)."],[7393,"a human steward certifies; deprecation"],[7409,"a human verifies an acceptance criterion"],[5421,"A join request (`POST /organizations/join-requests` with `{ organization: \"<handle>\" }`) is accepted only if the\ncaller's verified e-mail domain is in the organization's `domains`; otherwise the API answers `403\nJOIN_DOMAIN_NOT_ALLOWED` and nothing is stored (an unknown handle is a plain 404) — the answer names the\norganization and its handle, never its members, projects or settings. An organization may also switch `auto_join`\non, in which case a request from a listed domain goes straight in. A stored request carries the requester's\nidentity and the time; the requester's browser polls `GET /organizations/join-requests/mine`. **Approve** (`POST …/join-requests/{id}/approve`\nwith the chosen role) creates the membership exactly like an accepted invitation does — role from the decision,\nclearance from the organization — marks the request decided by whom and when, sends the decision mail and writes\nthe audit event; **Decline** records the decision without a membership. Requests and invitations are administrator\nresources: `GET …/join-requests` and `GET …/invitations` return 403 to members, which is why Kate's People screen has\nno Requests block."],[95,"A join request to an organization that does not accept your e-mail domain is refused on the form, with the way in:\n*ask an administrator for an invitation*."],[5118,"A JSON Schema object with `\"type\": \"object\"`. Leave empty for free-form."],[1956,"A Kubernetes cluster with enforced NetworkPolicy"],[7092,"A lane has no geometry — it is a relation between places, drawn as a line from the cell"],[4556,"A later question — **Top 10 organisations by score** — is answered in 3 s: &#x2A;Grouped by the canonical organisation\nname from the entities dataset; the four largest carry 61 % of the score. &#x2A;*Nothing was re-read from the\nworkbook.*** Under the draft, the **reuse line*&#x2A;: **↺ Reused from the run of 21 Sep 15:02: Column roles ·\nOrganisation name spellings · Recompute**. Below, **DATASETS KEPT IN THE PROJECT · 3** — each with its name,\n**layer** (*Bronze · typed copy*, *Silver · organisations normalised*, *Gold · duplicate groups*), shape, the\ntechnique that made it, the Skill and its version, and **Current** — or &#x2A;Stale — version of …* once the source file\nchanged."],[7609,"A link — never a copy — from an item to a requirement, acceptance criterion, test or decision; imported from the platform's own documentation."],[7673,"A link from one application into another — *Ask in Chat*, *Open in Graph*, *Open in VibeBan*, Forge's Backlog · Flows · Knowledge — always a reference, never a copy."],[2087,"A Linux server or a laptop with **Docker Engine 24+ / Docker Desktop** and the Compose plugin (`docker compose version`)."],[4451,"A list of **bindings** — the tools this agent may call. The line at the top is the security model of the whole tab:\n&#x2A;Tools are atomic capabilities. At run time the agent can only use what you, the Project and policy all allow — a\nbinding never elevates anyone.*"],[3944,"A list of agents with a one-line purpose each: **General** (ticked — *Everyday knowledge work in the\nProject*), **Analyst**, **Writer**, **Reviewer** (*citations mandatory*), **Governance**. These are the agents\nyour organization provides to every Project; the ones you build later appear here too."],[4053,"A list of the Project's dashboards you may edit, and **New dashboard**. The block is added to the dashboard's\n**draft** as a *reference* to this artifact with the default version policy (`follow_latest_approved`; a\n`version_policy_default` decision) — publishing it is the dashboard owner's step, in NexBI. If the dashboard has\na period filter, the block follows it from then on; the chip *Not filtered by X* on the dashboard tells you when a\nblock cannot."],[3319,"A list of things that are not a grid — conversations, layers, threads, inbox items: 36 px rows (44 with a second meta line), 12 px inset, a 2 px accent rail for the selected row, h"],[3325,"A list of things that are not a grid — conversations, layers, threads, inbox items: 36 px rows (44 with a second meta line), 12 px inset, a 2 px accent rail for the selected row, hover `bg-subtle`, the whole row a target. Replaces `.nexus-tasks-row`, `.nexus-care-row`, `.nexus-care-chat-row`, `.nexus-map-layer-row` (UX-AUDIT,) — four app rows that are one thing with four sets of numbers."],[3850,"A list that fits on one screen (12 rows at 1440 × 900) has no search, filter or view toggle; the row returns once the collection outgrows it and stays while a control is in use. A disabled control that can never be enabled is replaced by a sentence that says why (`Restriction`)."],[617,"A listed decider"],[4529,"A living document about the *data itself*: shape, column roles, how it was cleaned, the findings so far, the techniques run and their Skills, open suggestions. It is versioned like any document and grows with later runs."],[5572,"A local OpenAI-compatible runtime you can point at — the chapter uses Ollama at `http://127.0.0.1:11434`. (In\nthe review fixture the endpoint is answered by a stand-in; see the screenshot note.)"],[5502,"A member of the organization who holds no relation in the Project sees an empty **Projects** list and *not found*\nat the Project's address."],[615,"A member of the Project who is not on the decider list"],[6673,"A message becomes an answer"],[7036,"A messenger is a Synapse integration with a `conversation_channel` block: `config/synapse/integrations/telegram.yaml`\ndeclares `auth: api_key`, `egress_hosts: [api.telegram.org]`, `{kind: messaging, ingress: poll}`. The bot token lives\nin the Credential Broker and never reaches care-api; core-api offers `GET /synapse/conversation-channels`,\n`POST /synapse/connections/{id}/channel/receive` and `…/channel/send` under the `channel.use` permission. care-api polls\nevery 3 s (`CARE_CHANNELS_POLL=1`, one poller per deployment — Helm requires 1 replica; webhook ingress and a leased\npoller are S4), finds or creates a `channel_session` per chat for 24 h, and the message lands on the same\ndesk with the chip *Telegram*. There is no Telegram SDK — the adapter in `platform/synapse/nexus_synapse/channels.py`\nspeaks the Bot API over HTTPS (`python-telegram-bot` was rejected as LGPL)."],[5178,"A microphone the browser may use."],[6320,"A milestone is a **date that matters** — a gate, a demo, a release — independent of iterations. Each row: due date,\n**Status** (*Open · Reached · Missed · Cancelled* — a human sets it), **Health** (*On track* until an attached open\nitem is overdue or the date passes), **Progress** (done over attached items), **Edit**, **Attach** (items attach here\nor from the Inspector). *Carrier onboarding complete* has one item (the EDI epic); *Q4 dashboards published* two;\n*Release 2026.11* none yet. The next open milestone's date is what the project health rule watches."],[868,"A model drafts a metric from a frozen query/artifact (refs only) — lifecycle=draft, created_by.kind=agent, bi.metric_resolution record."],[2315,"A model provider — see step 4. Without one the stack starts, but every chat turn ends with *model unavailable*."],[5525,"A model the Project may use — the deployment's seed models are enough (the review fixture answers for them)."],[6592,"A model's verdict is never a label: an LLM evaluator's opinion is stored as a *feature* (`llm_proposed`) and refused\nas a training target. No user-facing feedback control exists — *helpful / wrong route* buttons are deferred to a\nfuture UX gate by the owner; everything above is captured from actions people already take."],[193,"A module adds one refusal of its own before all the others: the **module gate**."],[6949,"A module cannot enable itself, bind a capability or publish — only a person installing a pack (ADR-0023 §9)."],[548,"A module has **no membership model of its own**: it reads your relation in the NexChat Project its content belongs to\n(from chat-api, as its own service identity) and, before that, asks NexCore whether the organization enabled the\nmodule at all. Three doors in order on every route — session · module gate · PEP — and two constants: an\nOrganization Admin without a relation gets `403 NO_PROJECT_RELATION` (administering is not reading), and content of a\nProject you do not hold answers `404`. Voice adds no rights anywhere: a spoken edit or command is the same action as\na typed one."],[6904,"A module is a pack resource"],[6722,"A module is a pack whose Blueprint layer declares `modules.enabled`. Installing it in NexCore is the whole act: the\nmodule's API opens its gate, the tile appears in every launcher, the content lives in the module's own database.\nRelations come from the NexChat Project the content belongs to; the suite never depends on a module."],[52,"A module the organization has not enabled"],[7503,"a move past a limit"],[7484,"A move past a stage's WIP limit succeeds. The response carries `wip_exceeded = true`, the board says *Over the WIP\nlimit (6 / 5) — moved anyway*, and a `wip_limit_decision` records the alternatives (*move · keep*) with the outcome\n*moved\\_anyway*. A hard block would teach people to raise the limit; a soft limit with a record teaches the platform\nwhere limits are wrong."],[2869,"a named `alertdialog`; *Used by* is a list; Archive is the primary, Cancel first in Tab order"],[3270,"a named `alertdialog`; the knowledge line is `role=status`; Publish is the primary, Cancel first in Tab order"],[3214,"a named `dialog`; focus lands in the composer; Esc cancels and returns focus to *New artifact*"],[3309,"a native `input[type=radio]` inside a `label`; the group has a `fieldset`/`legend`"],[3571,"A new application is created from the suite's application scaffold: the shell, the kit, both languages, the\ncomposition stories, and the fitness baseline at zero arrive together, and the application claims its accent pair\nin the launcher. Until the scaffold ships, a new application starts from the kit and the shell by the same rules."],[4616,"A new chat opens with your message as the first turn and, under it, a **run card*&#x2A;: **✓ Compare cottage offers ·\n4 steps**. **Outputs** is expanded — `table` is the Canvas address of the new artifact and `summary` reads &#x2A;3\noffers. Old Mill is the cheapest (350 EUR) but the farthest and takes no dogs; Lakeside cabin is the only one that\nwelcomes the dog outright.* The footer, **Flow Runtime · confidential**, says who produced this turn and at which\nclassification. Click the table's address."],[4146,"A new draft appears in the Overview's *Needs attention*; validating it removes the row."],[6274,"A Nexi account in an organization. On the documentation stack: **Alex Rivera**, member of three work projects."],[233,"A Nexi component talking to another (chat-api parking a run on tasks-api, core-api publishing a revocation)."],[6884,"a Next.js application on its own origin, proxying to graph-api, chat-api and core-api"],[4840,"A NexTasks item for the *Project owner*. The Flow waits."],[7566,"A non-agent answer that competes in Auto: the **data arm** (NexBI's engine), the **knowledge arm** (NexGraph resolve), the **capability arm** (a product's tools)."],[4741,"A note on the screenshots"],[5259,"A note on the screenshots"],[5396,"A note on the screenshots"],[5434,"A note on the screenshots"],[5478,"A note on the screenshots"],[5519,"A note on the screenshots"],[5567,"A note on the screenshots"],[7692,"A numeric statement read from a table cell — metric, value, locator — *proposed* until an oracle or a person decides; *contested* when sources disagree; *superseded* by a newer version."],[6785,"A numeric statement read from a table cell: metric, value, locator, source assertion. Status *proposed → verified / falsified*; *contested*; *superseded*; *needs re-verification*."],[5725,"A numeric statement read from a table cell: metric, value, locator. Status **Proposed** → **Verified** / **Falsified** by an oracle or a person; **Contested** when two sources disagree; **Superseded** by a newer version; **Needs re-verification**."],[4543,"A one-turn answer this time: the collapsed line **› Ran code in the sandbox · 4.2 s · confidential-analytics**,\nthe sentence &#x2A;Stacked by direction over the verified-date month; 9 directions, 14 months. The three largest\ndirections …* and **NEW DRAFT · 1 — Score by month and direction · Chart · v1 · Draft** with the chart. The route\nline reads **Auto → Data scientist · qwen3-8b · local · Agent Runtime**, and &#x2A;*Why this route?** shows **Intent\nAnalyse data (0.90) · Selected Data scientist · agent · Why ✓ this thread already runs with it ✓ required tools\navailable ✓ you may run it ✓ classification allowed · Model qwen3-8b · local — selected by Synapse · Candidates\nconsidered: 3**."],[6911,"A pack (`packs/nexus-map`, `packs/nexus-care`, `packs/nexus-forge&#x60;) is a signed bundle of agents, skills, flows,\ntemplates, policies and a Blueprint layer — the same artefact NexCore installs for any capability bundle. A module pack\nadds one resource of kind &#x2A;*`module`** (`module/<id>.json`, contract `pack-module`): the module id, the apps and\nservices it brings, where its tile goes (`visibility.launcher.app_id`), its accent token, what it requires of the\nplatform (`requires.platform_tools`, e.g. `task.create`). Its Blueprint layer sets"],[7556,"A package of agents, skills, flows and their requirements, installed into a Project or an organization."],[7158,"A package of all of the above with what it requires from the organization."],[3736,"A page lists records in a `DataTable`; selecting a row opens the `Inspector` on the right with the record's properties and sections; Enter / double-click drills into the record's own page when it has one. The list keeps its selection and scroll while the panel is open; one Inspector at a time."],[3732,"A page lists records in a DataTable; selecting a row opens the Inspector on the right with the record's properties and sections; Enter / double-click drills into the record's own p"],[3897,"A password of **at least 12 characters** if you choose the e-mail route."],[5794,"A path under a root the operator approved for this deployment."],[7558,"A pause in a Flow or an agent action that a person must confirm in VibeBan (NexTasks) before it continues."],[47,"A person tries to verify what a model wrote"],[7696,"A person with the editor relation who confirms a claim within a named scope or returns it for clarification."],[6282,"A personal item can be **shared** with one person as viewer or editor from its Inspector — that is the only\nsharing a personal item has; moving it into a project is a separate, explicit action."],[4778,"A picker with the Project's **Published** Flows — *Plan the weekend · 1 inputs* — and the rule in one line: &#x2A;A