r open NexBI with `?project=<id>`)."],[4809,"A Project you own or edit. The screenshots use **Family weekends**, a fresh Project; **Weekend trips** from the\nearlier chapters works just as well."],[5778,"A Project you own or edit. We use **Data science**, which every organization gets from the Nexi Base blueprint."],[86,"A Project, thread, file or approval outside your organization — or one you were removed from — opens on the\nplatform's *Not found* page, is absent from the Project switcher, and never appears in **Search**. Nexi does not\ndistinguish *does not exist* from *not yours*: that difference would itself be information."],[4502,"A Project. Every organization gets **Data science** from the base blueprint — its description reads &#x2A;Attach a\nworkbook or CSV and ask — the Agentic Data Scientist profiles it, plans the analysis with you, runs pandas in the\nconfidential sandbox and leaves the tables and charts as drafts.* Any other Project works too: the Flow is\ninstalled into every Project on creation."],[4580,"A Project. We use **Family weekends** again — fresh here, but the one from Build your first Flow\nworks too."],[6879,"A Project's **capture policy** (owner-only; *Off · Explicit · Outcomes · Conversation*) decides whether the results of\nAgent and Flow runs — and, if chosen, conversation content — are recorded as *proposed* knowledge. chat-api's outbox\nrelays the completion events to graph-api's inbound door; graph-api records a **capture** under the Project's\nclassification and with the audience of the people who could see the source, never wider. A completed Flow certifies\nnothing: a captured outcome is a Subject-layer claim like any other and reaches Domain only through Review. This\nsurface is documented as a preview in the guide."],[2880,"A Project's artifacts as the builders' rows grouped by day (DS-3035 rows, DS-3019 toolbar, DS-7010): title · type · origin · status pill · by whom · when."],[2885,"A Project's artifacts as the builders' row