ledge live together; the people in a\nProject see the same things. The accent is only the dot next to the name in the sidebar. Your organization's\ndefault classification (here *Confidential*) is applied automatically — you will see it as a tag in the Project\nheader."],[4927,"A small table opens under the row. It is the tool's passport — the facts NexCore holds about it, not something the\nagent or a prompt can change:"],[4581,"A small text file with a few offers. Ours is `cottage-offers-autumn.txt` — three e-mails pasted one after another:"],[7603,"A soft ceiling on a stage; a move past it succeeds, says so, and is recorded as *moved anyway*."],[6838,"A source version is identified by its bytes. Upload the same report twice and nothing happens; change one paragraph\nand a `v2` appears beside `v1`:"],[5721,"A span of text the extractor labelled (*organization*, *amount*, *date* …) with a score. A proposal."],[6777,"A span the extractor labelled (&#x2A;organization · person · amount · date …*) with a score. &#x2A;A proposal.*"],[7688,"A span the extractor labelled with a type and a score. A proposal."],[7605,"A sprint with a start snapshot, points and scope changes; one active at a time; finished with a disposition for what is left."],[7468,"A sprint: one **active** per project (*409 ITERATION\\_ACTIVE*); a **start snapshot** (items · points · people); scope changes tracked against it; completion requires a **disposition** for unfinished items — *return\\_to\\_backlog · move\\_to\\_next* (*422 DISPOSITION\\_REQUIRED*)."],[4548,"A stopped run still offers what it made: the drafts list ends with **Analysis report (partial) · Document**, and\nthe review card reads &#x2A;*Will be published (7)** — you may publish a partial result knowingly."],[6246,"A table of all **112 items** — Key · Title · Type · Priority · Stage · Assignees · Due · Flags — sortable by rank,\npriority, due or updated, groupable by stage, type, assignee or epic. Tag chips (`epic-001 +1`) come from the\nseeding script; on the NEXUS Platform project the tags mirror the epic folders in the repository."],[3242,"a table with a caption; the board link says *opens in NexTasks* to a reader; the empty state's one action is a real link; the unavailable line is plain text, not an error"],[7457,"A team's project — *not* a NexChat Project. `KEY` of 2–6 capitals; pattern **kanban** (a continuous board) or **iterations**; visibility private or shared; estimation none · points · hours · custom; a classification ceiling. Templates: *simple-kanban*, *software-delivery* (iterations · points · 14-day Monday sprints), *research*."],[7597,"A team's project in VibeBan — a `KEY`, a pattern (continuous board or iterations), stages, types, members — not a NexChat Project."],[3441,"A thin monochrome line over a series, last point marked; decorative — the number sits next to it."],[7229,"A Tool that acts *as you*, within the scopes you granted."],[7225,"A Tool that works. The key stays in the credential broker; it is resolved inside Synapse at call time."],[4902,"a tool with a **side effect** can be made to wait for a person, and in a test chat it does not run at all."],[24,"A tool you may not bind"],[5550,"A trace shows a **Timeline** of five records with sizes (*44 chars*, *70 chars*), not text; **Payloads** shows\nthe input messages and the completion with sizes and a *Confidential* chip; **Summary** shows *Records 5 · Model\ncalls 1 · Payloads Full capture*."],[7624,"A typed query compiled by the engine to parameterised SQL — never text-to-SQL — with the row policy applied before aggregation and a record you can read."],[5310,"A verified person who belongs to no organization lands on **Welcome to Nexi**, with the only two ways forward.\n**Create an organization** — *you become its owner; a default project and Blueprint are set up for you* — or\n**Join an existing organization** — by an invitation from the e-mail, or by asking with the organization's\nhandle (the next chapter). Choose 