h the run: Analysis notebook (code) · sandbox\noutputs*&#x2A; — &#x2A;*! Viewers will see published artifacts only. Drafts and code stay with the run.** — **Publish** ·\n**Keep as drafts**."],[5919,"Above the stage: &#x2A;*Search objects…**, the scope (**Project only**), the view switch **Space · Lanes · List** and\n**Save view**. The heading **Landscape** and a frank line: &#x2A;The landscape shows the first groups; narrow the scope\nto see the rest.* On the stage, one sphere per **group**, sized by its members and coloured by its lane — the\nlegend underneath: **Sources · Claims · Knowledge · Base**, a green &#x2A;*verified share (ring)** and grey *volume\nbetween groups*. You can read the two documents of &#x2A;*Uploads (2)** on the right, the &#x2A;*Nexi documentation (77)**\nbelow, the entity groups by type — **product 716 · document 436 · technology 286 · role 195 · amount 132 ·\norganization 107 · location 65 · person 32 · date 31** — and, small and green-ringed, **claims 28**. Lines between\nspheres are volume: how many mentions connect one group to another."],[4390,"Above the tabs, the header is the same on every tab and tells you four things:"],[4965,"Above the thread, *Testing · Trip planner v5 (Draft) · Exit test*. The answer contains a **tool-call row** —\n`task.create`, a duration, a state — that you can expand; **Technical details** shows the invocation id, an\n**error\\_code**, a digest of the input and a **Trace** line with *Copy correlation id*. In a test, side effects are\nrefused on purpose: a draft agent must not create real tasks while you are still shaping it. (In the review\nenvironment shown here NexTasks is not wired to this deployment at all, so the call failed typed with\n`TOOL_PROTOCOL_UNSUPPORTED`; in your organization the same row reads *Side effects are not executed while testing\nan agent*.) Either way the row is honest about what happened, and the correlation id is what you paste into a\nsupport request."],[4947,"Above this the tool