e caller holds a relation on (the PEP's set, never a client list) plus the platform's `base` tier. Read-only; edits stay on the Project routes. The Evidence Workspace read model opened from the All view — same checkpoints as getDocumentView."],[1365,"additive — the **All knowledge** view ( `project_plus_org`, c): no Project in the path = every Project the caller holds a relation on (the PEP's set, never a client list) plus the platform's `base` tier. Read-only; edits stay on the Project routes. Versions across the caller's Projects, newest first (query: binding_id)."],[1265,"additive — the Evidence Workspace read model of one SourceVersion in one call: version · binding · last run · outline (pages, sections, tables, figures as previews, never text) · counts · coverage · the bounded mention list (each with `pdf_page`) · the entities they resolve to. Text leaves only through listPageItems. Denied and foreign-tenant alike → 404; clearance below the version's classification → 404."],[1266,"additive — the Silver text of one page (query: page; or offset/limit over the document) with the evidence spans and mentions that sit on the returned items. This is checkpoint 5 for the page sheet: PEP `object.read` on the version + classification clearance; the per-item listDocumentItems/getItemText pair stays for clients that need one item."],[2260,"Address"],[2308,"admin console `http://127.0.0.1:3220/idp/admin/` (operators only)"],[2065,"admin console `http://localhost:3320/idp/admin/`; users sign in through `web` at `/signin`"],[397,"admin without relation"],[451,"admin without relation"],[504,"admin without relation"],[553,"admin without relation"],[298,"administrator"],[301,"administrator"],[304,"administrator"],[1527,"Administrator creates a `workspace` / `service` connection with a `credential_ref` (never a value). `owner_kind=user` is refused (422)."],[7251,"administrators register models and connections and read the reports"],[1511,"Admit knowledge source"],[5589,"After **Add model** (Ollama, local endpoint) the header counts one more, the row reads *Healthy*, and NexChat's\nmodel catalogue lists it for this organization."],[4787,"After **Approve** the card reads *Approved by you*, the step is **Done**, the run **Completed** on the *Approved*\narrow; after **Reject**, the same on the *Rejected* arrow — also **Completed**."],[5419,"After **Approve** with a role, the roster shows the person with that role; the requester's card changes without\na re-login; the decision mail arrives."],[4116,"After **Create draft** the Dashboards registry shows the dashboard under *drafts*; after **Publish** under *published · v1*."],[5354,"After **Create organization** the ready screen lists exactly three things, and **Set up in Core** opens the\nOverview of your organization without another sign-in."],[4084,"After **Create**, NexChat's Flow list shows a Draft named after the automation, owned by you."],[5592,"After **Delete model**, the row and the catalogue entry are gone; **Audit** lists *Registered model*, the\nBuilder's *Deny*, and *Deleted model*."],[4562,"After **Publish**, a viewer of the Project sees exactly the eight published artifacts and not the notebook."],[5503,"After a grant, **Members** lists the person with the relation you chose, the list counts them, and their own\n**Projects** list shows the Project — and nothing they are not in."],[5461,"After a second sign-in from another browser, **Sessions** lists two rows with browser · system · last seen and\n*this device* on one of them."],[6842,"After a successful Index, `v1` is **retired** from retrieval — its fragments flagged, its vectors removed — so an\nanswer never cites a superseded page. The version itself stays readable, with its provenance, from Sources →\nDocuments."],[4719,"After adding, the Tools tab shows one row: *Project search — Search the current Project's pinned sources,\nattachments and threads*, tagged *Read-only*, with **Posture** (how the tool behaves for this agent) and\n**Remove**. The line above says it plainly: *a binding never elevates anyone* — the agent can search only what\nthe person using it could search themselves."],[4148,"After deprecating *Freight cost*, the KPI block that shows it keeps rendering with a *deprecated* badge; the Studio's *From Nexi* picker no longer lists it."],[7242,"after every model call"],[252,"After Olena grants her *viewer* on *Autumn catalogue*, Kate sees exactly that Project — and still not *General*,\nof which she is not a member:"],[4085,"After publishing, **Run now** on the Refresh produces a *Last run · just now · ok* within a few seconds and the dashboard header's *Updated* time moves."],[4700,"After the dialog closes you land in the new Project. In the Project header on the right, press **Agents**."],[4833,"Agent"],[6508,"Agent"],[7343,"Agent"],[554,"agent · service"],[450,"agent (data arm, for the person)"],[933,"Agent detail (READ on the owning Project; 404 when invisible)"],[396,"agent member"],[7342,"Agent Runtime"],[7346,"Agent Runtime"],[4322,"Agent Studio, tab by tab"],[4372,"Agent Studio, tab by tab"],[918,"Agents"],[6721,"Agents and Skills are cross-cutting: built once in NexChat, invoked from Chat, Spin, Tasks, BI and Graph — always\nwithin the current application's context and permissions, never with more access than the place you are in grants."],[7175,"Agents and Skills with declared inputs and outputs; Flows drafted from a description; the `routed to …` chip and Runs with one trace id"],[287,"Agents are not people with fewer rights"],[931,"Agents of this Project (project-scoped + workspace-level, PEP-filtered)\n\nDefault (`include=published`) is the picker view — published, governance ≠ blocked. `include=all` is the\nmanagement view (Agents list screen) and also returns drafts, disabled and blocked agents with their\ngovernance projection; it requires `can_edit` on the Project."],[6474,"Agents, Skills, Tools and Flows"],[6365,"Agents, Skills, Tools and Flows — the four things you build and why they are\nseparate, with the weekend-trip example."],[4489,"Agents, their versions, tool bindings and the inference policy are resources of the NexChat API under a Project.\nSee the API reference — the pages are generated from the published contracts once the reference is\npublished."],[6440,"Aggregates it computed (counts, shares, ranges; ≤ 3 example values per field in prose)"],[932,"AI-first create — intent → draft (status=draft)\n\nBody is `AgentDraftRequest`: `intent` alone is enough — a first-party \"Draft agent\" Skill produces name /\npurpose / instructions (deterministic fixture drafter until the Agent Runtime lands in S6). Explicit fields\noverride the draft. Nothing is published without an explicit `publish`; no tools are bound by a create.\nThe definition is owned and written by NexChat (`nexus://agent/<id>`). NexCore does not author agents\n(403 for non-human / NexCore identities): it attaches a governance record\n(`core.agent_governance`) that the PEP enforces on invoke and publish. Idempotent on `idempotency_key`."],[1189,"AI-first create — intent → SKILL.md draft package (origin=project, status=draft, 0.1.0)"],[1036,"AI-first create — natural-language intent → Create Flow Skill → validated draft WorkflowSpec + plan + questions. Nothing is published or executed. PepAction=create on project (relation can_edit). Idempotent via body.idempotency_key."],[1930,"ALB + ACM certificate"],[869,"Alias/term → metric candidates with scores for the data arm (1032); certified wins over draft; ambiguity ⇒ needs_clarification, never a guess; bi.metric_resolution record."],[4009,"All chapters use one Project seeded on the documentation stack for the persona **Alex Rivera**: **Logistics**, with the\ndataset *Shipments 2025–2026* (189 rows · three carriers · three regions · 21 months), six metrics in every lifecycle\nstate, the published dashboard *Carrier performance* and three draft automations."],[5674,"All chapters use the same small corpus, so you can follow along from the first to the last. The persona is **Alex\nRivera**, owner of the Project **Data science** in the organization **Acme Logistics** (a logistics company with hubs\nin Rotterdam, Warsaw, Lyon and Kyiv). Two documents:"],[6204,"All chapters use the same three work projects, seeded on the documentation stack for the persona **Alex Rivera**:\n**NEXUS Platform** (the platform's own delivery, a continuous board), **NEXUS Operations** (a bug-triage board with a\nWIP limit) and **Acme Q4 delivery** (an iterations project with two sprints and three milestones)."],[5508,"All Core frames are live captures on the review fixture with the three Northwind accounts. The **New project**\ndialog is the NexChat frame from the first NexChat chapter — the fixture stacks of the two apps do not share\ndata, so the same dialog could not be shown with the Northwind name. Membership was granted with the API\ndescribed in step 4; the two forms that should do it — Core's **Members › Edit** and a members dialog in NexChat —\nare recorded as open items for the owning teams."],[5467,"All frames are live captures on the review fixture with Olena's account; the second browser is a Playwright\ncontext with a Safari user agent, which is why the row reads *Safari · macOS*. Sign-in cards are Core's own in\nAPI mode (the provider's forms are behind *Continue with work e-mail*); in a deployment with Keycloak they look as\nin Create your organization. Two things are recorded as open items for the NexCore\nteam: **Change password** and **Set up two-factor** open panels drawn for the prototype (a sample QR and manual\nkey) that are not connected to the identity provider, so they are not shown here; and **Profile › Edit** saves\nthe display name only to the browser store. The reset mail is written to the fixture's outbox and not shown."],[5289,"All frames are live captures on the review fixture with the Northwind accounts; nothing was changed in the\norganization. Step 5 has no Core