· loading · error-state · planned · done · empty · loading · error · denied · offline"],[3140,"Also: with-tabs · live"],[2984,"Also: written · contact · busy · in-the-inspector · in-the-inspector-form"],[6806,"alters the bytes"],[1905,"Amazon RDS (external) — RDS has pgvector and PostGIS but **not Apache AGE**: `nexus_graph` needs an in-cluster or self-managed PostgreSQL; `nexus_map` may stay on RDS"],[1082,"Amend goal"],[1415,"amendment: authz_mode (engine|embedded), bundle_ok, bundle_version, bundle_key_id, verified_at, staleness_allowed_s. Fails closed: with AUTHZ_MODE=engine and no valid bundle every other operation returns 503 POLICY_UNAVAILABLE."],[7495,"An **agent** that is `agent_member` of a project acts only in the intersection of its own relation and the relation of\nthe human it works for — an agent cannot move an item its principal may not move. The **human-only** set is enforced\nbefore OpenFGA and answers *403 AUTHOR\\_NOT\\_HUMAN* to any agent or service: decide an approval; create, share,\nadminister or archive a project; delete or share an item; start, complete or cancel an iteration; import references;\nbind an automation; verify a criterion. An organization administrator without a relation sees **counts only**\n(*Content hidden*). Hidden resources answer *404*; forbidden actions *403 PEP\\_DENIED*; a classification above\nthe project's ceiling *403 CLASSIFICATION\\_CEILING*. Every record carries `allowed_actions[]` decided server-side for\nthe reader — the board never authorises in the browser."],[4808,"an **approval** is a step where the Flow waits for a person — in a test it is simulated, in a real run it waits."],[4363,"An **Auto · action** proposal: *Title Developer portal chapters · Due Fri, Oct 9, 2026 · Europe/Kiev · Visible to\nOnly you and this board's members*, then &#x2A;*Which one?** with the boards you may write to — *NEXUS Platform · NEXUS\nOperations · Acme Q4 delivery*. Pick a board; the card asks &#x2A;*Create this task?** with **Confirm · Change · Cancel**\nand the hint &#x2A;Say or type \"yes\" to confirm — or say what to change.* A *yes* binds to this proposal and its version;\na correction voids it; it expires after ten minutes. Confirm → *Task created — PLT-42 · Open PLT-42*, created through\ntasks-api as you, with an idempotency key so a repeated yes cannot create twice. Assigning or moving (level 3)\nshows the exact change and waits; &#x2A;run the Flow…* starts a Flow run the same way."],[290,"an **organization role** — what Core › People gives a person when they are invited: &#x2A;Owner, Admin, Builder,\nMember …*. It says what the person may do **to the organization**."],[3289,"an `article` named after the document; embedded tables are real tables with headers; the offline banner is `role=status`"],[6980,"An `Expr` in the closed grammar — `aggregate · arithmetic · literal · filtered · window` — over one entity; a period default; optional target. Lifecycle *draft → validated → certified → deprecated*."],[584,"an `external` actor with a care session for an allowed origin; the guardrail profile decides what may be disclosed"],[6542,"An absent capability must not leak into the record; ranking only among the eligible keeps the action space honest."],[6516,"An administrator connects the system once; you pick the Tool for your agent or Flow. Code the model writes runs only in the Sandbox."],[41,"An administrator opens a dashboard without a Project relation"],[45,"An administrator opens Graph Studio without a Project relation"],[7147,"An administrator or you, at consent."],[7141,"An administrator registers it in NexCore; Nexi measures it."],[37,"An administrator without a project relation"],[53,"An administrator without a Project relation"],[7224,"An administrator, once, in NexCore. The key is entered write-only: it can be replaced but never displayed again."],[621,"An agent added to a Project reads what the Project offers and acts through the person who started it. Three\nthings are closed to it by identity, whatever relation it holds: **authoring** (it cannot create, change, publish or\ndelete agents, skills, tool bindings or flows — it may only *request* a capability, which a human grants),\n**approving** (it can neither decide nor read an approval it did not cause), and **payloads** (it never reads what a\nmodel was told or answered). Above *Confidential* an agent must also be able to name the person it acts for, or it\nis refused outright."],[369,"An agent added to the Project, acting for a person"],[4804,"An agent answers when you ask. A **Flow** works when it is time — every Thursday, when a file arrives, when someone\npresses *Run*. In this chapter you build the Flow from The example: *plan the weekend — propose,\nkeep improving until it fits the budget, let a person approve, then act*. You will not draw anything; you describe it\nin one sentence and Nexi drafts the steps. Then you do what a builder always does with a draft: read the plan,\ncorrect the two things the machine guessed wrong, test it with nothing at stake, and publish."],[5167,"An agent applies a skill by *uri* — instructions only. Nothing in the skill can grant a tool, a model, a piece of\nknowledge or a permission; the composition rule *Skill teaches · Agent works · Tool acts* is enforced by the shape of\nthe data, not by a checkbox. The full vocabulary and its diagram are in\nAgents, Skills, Tools and Flows."],[238,"An agent is not a person with fewer rights; it is a different identity with a person behind it. That is why an\naudit row for a run names the agent *and* the human it acted for, and why an agent can never publish a skill or\napprove its own request (see Roles and relations)."],[164,"An agent or a service tried to do something only a person may — create, publish, decide."],[609,"An agent or a service tries to decide"],[7376,"an agent or the Sandbox"],[39,"An agent tries a human-only action"],[55,"An agent tries to apply, delete, publish or join"],[7655,"An anonymous visitor's bearer, minted only for an allowed origin, hashed, 60 min sliding, 24 h at most."],[27,"An answer you are not allowed to have"],[7572,"An application an organization turns on by installing a pack — NexMap, NexCare, NexForge. Its API answers only when the Blueprint lists it; its tile appears only then."],[80,"An approval card in a chat shows the same steps to everyone in the Project — but the **Approve / Reject** buttons only\nto the people who may decide. Everyone else sees *Waiting for approval · Waiting for a Project owner*."],[6557,"An arm is the right answer when a specialist would only add latency and a model's paraphrase of a number."],[1983,"An AWS account with a VPC that has public subnets (for the ALB) and private subnets in at least two AZs (for\nnodes and RDS), NAT for outbound traffic, and the subnets tagged for the Load Balancer Controller\n(`kubernetes.io/role/elb`, `kubernetes.io/role/internal-elb`)."],[6990,"An editor edits the draft; a human with `dashboard.publish` publishes with *I have checked the numbers against their sources*."],[5504,"An Editor or Viewer who tries to change membership is refused."],[4600,"An empty canvas with only **Start*&#x2A;. From here you add the nodes with the &#x2A;*+** palette on the left exactly as in\nBuild your first Flow, or describe them in the box at the bottom (*e.g. add a Spin notification\nafter approval*). Whichever way, the result to aim for is below."],[4646,"An empty list with a **New skill** button. Skills your organization provides appear below under **Platform** —\n*Create Flow*, *Summarize sources*, *Pin to context* — already published and usable with `/` in the composer.\nYou can open them to read how they are written; they are the same kind of thing you are about to make."],[4812,"An empty page with one promise: &#x2A;Describe an automation in one sentence — Nexi drafts the steps, you review the\nplan, then test and publish.* That is the whole method of this chapter, in order. Press **New