t contract; a\nProject layer may **disable** a module the organization enabled, never enable one it did not."],[606,"Answer"],[6743,"Answer"],[1098,"Answer an open question or a *Continue · Finish · Stop* choice \n\n1.140.0 ( S1). PEP: OpenFGA on (project, actor) and the goal's owner — outside the\nactor's Projects the goal is 404, never 403 (the thread idiom); service and agent identities are refused on every\nwrite (403, recorded). No request text in any payload.\nThe pick idiom's answer for a goal in `waiting_user`: a closed `choice` or a bounded `text` (the only free text —\nwritten to the board as `origin: person`). Wakes the supervisor run."],[6735,"Answering from the graph: resolve"],[6415,"Anything else."],[642,"API"],[7078,"API"],[7049,"API and tables"],[628,"API reference"],[1465,"App registry"],[3677,"Appearance, language, notifications and the keyboard reference open as `SettingsSheet` / `ShortcutsSheet` from the dock — one 400 px drawer, not a settings page per app. App-specific settings live on that app's Settings tab, under the same frame as everything else."],[5081,"Appears only on skills provided by the organization; every field is disabled."],[6677,"Application"],[7273,"Application"],[3989,"Applications"],[2390,"Apply"],[796,"Apply suggestion"],[824,"Apply to the DRAFT only (never a published version) → new draft + outcome suggestion_applied (human_explicit)."],[4839,"Approval"],[7359,"Approval"],[4953,"Approval by policy"],[1573,"Approvals"],[4793,"Approvals are NexTasks resources: `GET /tasks/approvals/{id}` (200 for a decider or the requester, 404 for everyone\nelse) and `POST /tasks/approvals/{id}/decide` with `{ decision: \"approve\" | \"reject\", comment? }` — 403 for a\nnon-decider or self-approval, 409 once decided or expired. Runs: `GET /chat/flow-runs/{run}` and `…/steps`. See the\nAPI reference."],[7528,"Approvals from the Flow side: Decide the approval and read the run."],[7177,"Approvals placed automatically on Tools that change something"],[100,"Approvals still appear as the cards in NexChat shown above, with the same codes (`NOT_DECIDER`, `SELF_APPROVAL`,\n`AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN`) returned as `403` by the Tasks API. The work-management screens add\ntwo walls of their own."],[1579,"Approvals visible to the actor — the inbox read model behind the thread card, the Studio run view and *Needs your decision*. PepAction=read: records where the actor is a decider or the `on_behalf_of` human (services: the tenant's); a record above the reader's clearance is left out (a `confidential` approval is invisible to an `internal` clearance). RLS on tenant_id — another tenant's records never appear. Newest first."],[1817,"Approvals: requests, decisions, evidence — and, behind `TASKS_WORK_DOMAIN`, VibeBan's work projects, items, iterations, milestones and references. Tells chat-api what was decided."],[339,"Approve"],[618,"Approve or reject, with a note; the run continues or ends; the decision is immutable and audited."],[7069,"Approved: C0 — library, the one door in, five templates, Board with palette and handles, the element bar, Inspector,\nfour views, versions and restore, typed turns with grammar + agent, the 409 conflict card. Built, awaiting the owner's\nmicrophone walk: S2 voice. Not yet: the LikeC4 Diagram renderer (the current *Layered layout* is a stand-in),\nconversions and live bindings (S4), exports/imports over the API, presence, graph projection, images, own templates\nover the live API, spoken read-backs, the Voice Dock hand-off."],[7040,"Approved: C0 (widget · desk · handover · guardrails) and S2 (Telegram). In the tree, **preview**: S3 — cases, identity\ndecisions, queues, SLA. Not yet: quality and survey tables, webhook ingress, Ukrainian and German suite i18n for\n`care.*`, a larger red-team corpus, an OpenAPI file."],[6715,"Architects, analysts, anyone who thinks in pictures"],[1746,"Archive (HUMAN owner). Read-only for every relation, listed under *Archived*, automations disabled; emits `nexus.tasks.project.archived.v1`."],[961,"Archive (reversible)\n\n1.139.0 ( door, contract fixed in S1). Sets `status = archived`, `archived_at · archived_by ·\narchived_by_label · status_before_archive`; emits `nexus.chat.artifact.archived.v1`. Rights: a draft needs\nProject WRITE, a published artifact needs ADMINISTER; humans only. Idempotent (200 on a repeat). A caller\nwithout the right is 404 — never 403 with a reason. Every write on an archived artifact afterwards is\n409 ARTIFACT_ARCHIVED; reads and exports continue; consumers keep resolving."],[811,"Archive (status archived; versions stay readable; automations unbound)."],[947,"Archive artifact"],[2768,"Archive artifact dialog"],[2860,"Archive artifact dialog"],[783,"Archive dashboard"],[1139,"Archive project"],[1217,"Archive this chat — never deleted (1.17.0)\n\nThe chat's creator, or anyone with ADMINISTER on the enclosing Project (global chats: the creator only);\nhumans only (403 `ARCHIVE_HUMAN_ONLY`, audited). Sets `archived_at`; the chat leaves RECENT, the Project's\nlist, the drawers and search, and refuses new turns (409 `THREAD_ARCHIVED`); GET by id still answers\n(read-only, with *Restore*). 409 `PROJECT_ARCHIVED` if the whole Project is archived — its chats go with\nit and come back with it. Emits `nexus.chat.thread.archived.v1`. No body: archiving is not versioned\nagainst concurrent edits — a chat has none."],[1153,"Archive this Project — NexChat never deletes (1.17.0)\n\nADMINISTER on the Project (owner / workspace admin) **and a human actor** — agents and services get 403\n`ARCHIVE_HUMAN_ONLY`, audited. Sets `status = archived` + `archived_at`. Everything inside is hidden *by\nderivation*: chats, agents, skills, flows, pins and attachments are not mutated, every list endpoint,\nthe sidebar, drawers, search and composer pickers leave them out because their Project is archived, and\nevery write into them answers 409 `PROJECT_ARCHIVED`. Members may still GET the Project and its content by\nid (read-only