m through Synapse"],[4010,"Chapter"],[4313,"Chapter"],[5200,"Chapter"],[5219,"Chapter"],[5680,"Chapter"],[5741,"Chapter"],[6205,"Chapter"],[3874,"Chapters"],[4005,"Chapters"],[4214,"Chapters"],[4311,"Chapters"],[5217,"Chapters"],[5599,"Chapters"],[5668,"Chapters"],[6112,"Chapters"],[6200,"Chapters"],[1955,"Chart setting"],[7339,"Chat / thread"],[646,"Chat API"],[2487,"chat-api"],[6878,"chat-api then prompts the model with the bundle and streams the reply through a filter that removes any `[n]` the\nbundle cannot back and any image that is not a bundle figure; a *tentative* bundle adds a caution; an *empty* one makes\nthe model say what is missing. The route, the anchoring, the reranking and the sufficiency are each a decision\nrecord; your *Regenerate*, *Stop* or the model's own `[insufficient]` are written back as outcomes."],[4059,"chat-api's **data arm** calls bi-api's S2S tools as `svc_chat_api` asserting the asking human:\n`POST /bi/tools/project.describe` (which datasets and metrics exist for the Project), `POST /bi/tools/metrics.resolve`\n(an `intent_resolution` + `metric_resolution` decision — every candidate metric with its score), then\n`POST /bi/tools/dataset.query` with a typed **BIQuery**. bi-api compiles it to parameterised SQL (never text-to-SQL),\nruns the PEP checkpoints (tenancy → metric read → dataset read + classification → row policy before aggregation) under\nthe read-only `bi_query` role (8 s, 1000 rows, EXPLAIN cost guard), and returns the rows and the query record. chat-api\nwrites the answer text and registers the chart and table artifacts (`POST /internal/artifacts/reference`), so NexBI\ndashboards can reference them. The route itself is a `RouteDecision` (`GET /chat/routes/{id}`) with the data arm as one\nof the candidates."],[5903,"chat-api's Auto adds a **knowledge arm** to every route decision — one candidate beside the agents, scored on whether\nthe question names the platform, asks how to do something, or asks about the Project's data; it never competes with a\nFlow. When it wins, the `KnowledgeAnswerResponder` calls graph-api `POST /graph/resolve` with `purpose = knowledge` (k =\n8, a 6 s budget) under **your** identity — passing a *reference* to your message, not its text; graph-api reads the\nquestion itself under the same rights. graph-api runs the ladder above, checks every chunk at its enforcement point,\ndrops retired versions (only the current version of a source is ever retrieved), and returns an **EvidenceBundle**\nwhose every item carries `why` (arms, ranks, band, hop, anchor) and whose `explanation.steps[]` are what the drawer\nrenders. chat-api reads the items by reference, prompts the model with the bundle, streams the reply through a filter\nthat removes any `[n]` the bundle cannot back and any image that is not a bundle figure, and records the provenance\n(`sources[kind=knowledge]`, `grounding{status, decision_id}`, `evidence_bundle_ref`). The route, the anchoring, the\nreranking and the sufficiency decision are each a **decision record**; your *Regenerate*, *Stop* or the model's own\n`[insufficient]` are written back as **outcomes** — the graph learns from being asked."],[2288,"chat-worker — Flow runs, approvals resumer, outbox"],[6686,"Chats and Projects; Auto and the Resolver; Agent Studio, Flow Studio, Skills and Knowledge. Agents and Flows are created here and can be used from every other application."],[4310,"Chats, Projects, Agent Studio, Flow Studio, Skills and Knowledge — one task per chapter, with the real screens."],[6535,"Cheap, deterministic signals: a file on the message, an `@agent`, a product name (*Gmail*, *Jira*), verbs of side effect (*send*, *delete*)."],[4039,"Check"],[4067,"Check"],[4096,"Check"],[4127,"Check"],[4157,"Check"],[4188,"Check"],[4496,"Check"],[4574,"Check"],[4738,"Check"],[4800,"Check"],[4895,"Check"],[4988,"Check"],[5256,"Check"],[5297,"Check"],[5393,"Check"],[5431,"Check"],[5475,"Check"],[5516,"Check"],[5564,"Check"],[5772,"Check"],[5849,"Che