ning application decides whether you may read it — a document you lost access to shows as\n*not available to you*, not as its old title."],[5590,"Choosing a cloud provider shows an **API key** field with the vault hint and a *Confidential* cloud ceiling."],[4626,"Choosing a file in a `file` input does two governed things in one request: the browser uploads the text to the\nProject as an **attachment** (`POST /chat/projects/{project}/attachments` — filename, media type, text; the\nserver records size and a SHA-256 and gives it a `nexus://chat/attachment/…` address) and pins that address as a\n**context item** of kind `file` with the Project's classification. The Flow Engine then passes the *address* to the\nagent step; the Agent Runtime resolves it to the text only when the run's principal — you — may read that Project,\nso a well-formed address of another Project's file yields nothing. `artifact.create_table` is a platform Tool: the\nagent produced data, the Tool wrote the artifact, and the run's outputs carry the artifact's address — the agent\nnever writes into the Canvas by itself."],[5892,"Chose the items, the claims, the figures."],[7383,"Claim"],[6625,"Claim a step done the engine did not record."],[6824,"claims, cells"],[160,"clearance"],[286,"Clearance and classification"],[6317,"Click **ACME-11**."],[5652,"Click **Customer**."],[5933,"Click **Northwind Traders**."],[6103,"Click **Northwind Traders**."],[5985,"Click **northwind-framework-agreement-2027.pdf · Uploads**."],[5991,"Click **Verify** under **Verification**."],[6056,"Click **Warsaw · Shipments**."],[6242,"Click a card — here the epic **NEXUS-11 · Epic 003**."],[6161,"Click a hexagon near Hamburg."],[4713,"Click at the end of the text and add:"],[3940,"Click into the composer and type, in your own words, what you want. Ours:"],[6027,"Click the **Entity** link."],[4856,"Click the **Review results** node too."],[4852,"Click the **Trigger** node."],[5811,"Click the **Uploads** row."],[4846,"Click the header of the **Goal loop** container."],[6024,"Click the underlined **Northwind Traders GmbH** in the preamble."],[5575,"Clicking a seed row opens its inspector: **Overview · Policy · Usage** — and no **Delete model** button; the\n**Enabled** switch is read-only. The deployment's models are the operator's; the organization reads them."],[6548,"Closed vocabulary makes the output a feature, not free text; coercions are kept because they are training data too."],[2411,"Cloud"],[1986,"Cluster provisioning itself is your platform team's concern: the chart installs on any conformant cluster and\ndoes not ship Terraform. The steps below name what the cluster must have."],[1390,"Clusters + flows of the caller's ALLOWED objects for the scope (query: scope, tier, layer, q). Counts are computed after the PEP filter; truncation is reported with counts. Never the tenant graph."],[133,"Code"],[153,"Code"],[3589,"Colour"],[3575,"Colour — Neutrals, semantic colour, the attention accents, per-application accents and the data palette — in both themes."],[3574,"Colour, type, radius, the shell's measures, surfaces and motion — 101 tokens in eight groups, read from `tokens.css` by the workshop so the page can never drift from the CSS."],[3573,"Colour, type, spacing, radius, elevation, motion and icons — every number is a token."],[4172,"Column · Label · Type · Unit · **Role** — *time dimension · dimension · measure*. The note says the dataset is\n*modelled in the Project's semantic layer as entity shipments\\_2025\\_2026; metrics are defined over it*. Two\ndoors: **Propose a model** asks Nexi for a semantic model of the table (entity, dimensions, time dimension, roles —\na *proposal* you review and apply; nothing is applied silently), and **Dashboard from this table** starts a\ndashboard plan over it. Without a semantic model there are no metrics and no dashboards — the model is what turns\ncolumns into things a question can name."],[2732,"Combobox"],[2965,"Combobox"],[5099,"Comma-separated labels for finding the skill later: `procurement, risk`."],[4371,"Commands that run through the right app with your rights, a chip that says what the assistant is pointing at, and a\nway to show or hand Nexi something without it entering the organization's memory."],[1717,"Comments, oldest first."],[3466,"Compact name · meta · status rows on an overview (Models, Connections); hover reveals `detail`; rows may link."],[3461,"Compact name · meta · status rows on an overview (Models, Connections); hover reveals detail; rows may link."],[872,"Compile + run a test query (purpose metric_validation) → lifecycle validated with validation_query_ref."],[7394,"compiled by the governed query engine"],[1608,"Complete (HUMAN editor+) with a disposition per unfinished item; writes `iteration_carryover_default` decisions and history rows; publishes the work dataset; emits `nexus.tasks.iteration.completed.v1` (counts + decision ids)."],[1598,"Complete iteration"],[7509,"completing a sprint"],[2548,"Component"],[2544,"Components"],[2522,"Components — one page per component: contract, states, accessibility, stories."],[3664,"Components: `@nexus/app-shell#AppLauncher` · `@nexus/app-shell#NEXUS_APPS`"],[3659,"Components: `@nexus/app-shell#NexusShell` · `@nexus/app-shell#ShellDock`"],[3678,"Components: `@nexus/app-shell#SettingsSheet` · `@nexus/app-shell#ShortcutsSheet`"],[3661,"Components: `@nexus/app-shell#ShellDock`"],[3676,"Components: `@nexus/app-shell#useTheme` · `@nexus/app-shell#THEME_BOOT_SCRIPT` · `@nexus/i18n#LocaleProvider`"],[3674,"Components: `@nexus/ui/ask#AskSurface`"],[3672,"Components: `@nexus/ui/workbench#Inspector` · `@nexus/ui/workbench#FormInspector`"],[3666,"Components: `@nexus/ui/workbench#PageFrame`"],[3668,"Components: `@nexus/ui/workbench#PageLine` · `@nexus/ui/workbench#PageFrame`"],[3670,"Components: `@nexus/ui/workbench#UrlTabs` · `@nexus/ui/workbench#LocalTabs` · `@nexus/ui/workbench#SideNav` · `@nexus/ui/workbench#SideNavLayout`"],[1893,"Compose"],[2385,"Compose"],[2409,"Compose"],[2456,"Compose"],[2056,"Compose is the first rung on which you run **the product as it ships**: the same signed images every other target\ninstalls, started as containers on one machine. Nothing is built locally, nothing hot-reloads. It is the right\ntarget for a trial, a demo, a small team on one server, and — with the disconnected profile — a site without\ninternet."],[2147,"Compose publishes plain HTTP on 3310. For anything people reach by name, put a reverse proxy in front — Caddy,\nnginx, Traefik — that terminates TLS for `nexus.example.com` and forwards to `127.0.0.1:3310`, then set\n`NEXUS_PUBLIC_URL=https://nexus.example.com` and restart (`docker compose up -d`). Every URL the platform emits —\nOAuth callbacks, sign-in redirects, e-mail links — is built from that one variable, and Keycloak is told that it\nsits behind a proxy (`xforwarded`). Forward `/` as a whole; `/api/v1/*` and `/idp/*` are routed inside `web`."],[2111,"Compose pulls the images, starts Postgres and NATS, waits for Postgres to be healthy, runs the four database\ninitialisations and the three `migrate-*` one-shot services, then starts the APIs, waits for their health probes,\nand finally starts `web`. On a fresh machine this takes two to four minutes; the images are around 2 GB together."],[2150,"Compose re-runs the `migrate-*` services with the new images before the new APIs start; nothing else is needed.\nDowngrades are not supported once a migration has run — take a backup first."],[2812,"Composer-line door"],[2977,"Composer-line door"],[7057,"computes a per-op **inverse** from the pre-state and stores it; `undo`/`redo` replay the actor's **own** batches\n(depth 100);"],[2428,"Configuration files hold **references** — `env://NAME`, `vault://mount/path#key`, `nexus://…` for broker-managed\nrows — never values. core-api refuses to start if it finds a literal secret in a registry file."],[1164,"Confirm route"],[1207,"Confirm route"],[3686,"Confirmation — Reversible: an ActionPanel where the action was taken, one sentence naming the effect, one primary, Cancel."],[2851,"Confirmation · Action rows"],[2944,"Confirmation · Action rows"],[5240,"Connect a system (Connections)"],[7367,"Connection"],[1518,"Connection health history"],[1569,"Connections of a tool in the caller's tenancy (health + classification; never endpoint values)."],[7193,"Connections: the agent never sees a credential"],[1908,"container"],[2057,"Container"],[1902,"container (`nexus/postgres`: AGE + pgvector + PostGIS)"],[1903,"container + named volume (`POSTGRES_IMAGE`)"],[1898,"containers"],[3665,"Content sits in `PageFrame`: `standard` (max 1320 px — people, settings, detail pages) or `wide` (overview, matrix, audit, executions). 32 px of air above the header line; the body starts 16 px under the tabs."],[987,"Context and knowledge"],[276,"Continue with Roles in an organization, relations in a Project."],[5795,"Continuous"],[5798,"Continuous"],[7026,"Contracts and API"],[3535,"controls are labelled buttons with `aria-keyshortcuts`; the layers panel is a dialog that returns focus; the status line is `role=status`"],[2828,"Conversation parts"],[2987,"Conversation parts"],[1195,"Conversations — global or inside a Project."],[1048,"Cooperative cancel — status=cancelled for queued/waiting; running step finishes its attempt then stops (no new dispatch). Pending approval task in NexTasks is withdrawn. Completed external writes are NOT undone automatically (see compensation)."],[3536,"Copy and language"],[2523,"Copy and language — how the suite speaks, in two languages."],[2245,"Copy the model weights (a GGUF file) into a PVC named in `modelServer.modelPvc`."],[274,"Core › Audit"],[271,"Core › Blueprints & Packs (organization layer) and Core › Projects › Governance (tighten only)"],[265,"Core › People › Invite — the clearance is chosen with the role and travels with the invitation"],[262,"Core › People (invite, or edit the person)"],[268,"Core › Projects › Members