able that turns them into *yes* or\n*no*."],[980,"Effective Blueprint for the Project (base → domain → regulatory → organization → project merged by NexCore). Drives \"Default capabilities inherited from …\", default Goal Loop, tool/model/sandbox defaults in pickers. Read-only projection of GET /blueprints/effective on core-api."],[1475,"Effective profile for a tenancy / project / optional flow — the tightest of Blueprint → Project → Flow → node. Used by the Sandbox Manager before every execution; PEP re-checks classification of inputs ≤ profile.classification_max."],[7066,"Eight `ForgeDecisionKind`s, three of them on every turn: `scene_intent` (features `zoom, level, op_kind,\nlanguage, active_view, grammar_hit, input_source, pointer_kind, visible_count, candidate_count, selection_count`; the\nfull action space; propensity; `state_ref = nexus://forge/snapshot/…`), `voice_transcript_pick` (language, media type,\nduration, confidence, candidates, model id — never the words), `deictic_resolution`. Outcomes are written by apply,\ncancel, modify, choose, undo and TTL. Every editor can read the record behind &#x2A;*Why this?**;\n`decision_outcomes` refuses `llm_proposed` by CHECK."],[3604,"Eight categorical hues and one sequential ramp (`--nexus-data-1 … -8`, `--nexus-data-seq-1 … -5`) for things that are *data* — NexForge colour keys, NexBI series, NexMap layers, NexGraph hues — defined once in both themes with ≥ 3:1 against the surface. An app never picks its own chart colour; the attention accents (DS-1003) are not a data palette."],[2364,"Eight images"],[7038,"Eighteen schemas (`care-service-conversation`, `care-message`, `care-widget-installation`, `care-session`,\n`care-external-identity`, `care-identity-link`, `care-handler-transition`, `care-topic-taxonomy`, `care-incident`,\n`care-service-queue`, `care-sla-policy`, `care-case-extension`, `care-quality-review`, `care-survey`,\n`care-channel-session`, `care-events` — 21 `nexus.care.*.v1` events — `guardrail-profile`, `guardrail-decision`),\ncontracts 1.107.0. Routers: public edge (`sessions · turns (JSON or SSE) · verify · handoff · cases · history ·\nknowledge`), conversations (`overview · conversations · transition · messages · topic · topics · studio/installations`),\nchannels (`channels · channels/{id}/pull`), identity, cases/SLA (S3), system. **No `nexus-care-v1.openapi.yaml` is\ncommitted**; FastAPI serves `/docs` on :3208."],[681,"Either it does not exist or it is not in your organization — the answer is the same on purpose."],[3900,"Either press **Continue with Google** and pick your work Google account in the window that opens, or press\n**Create account** to use a work e-mail and password."],[3606,"Elevation"],[3579,"Elevation — Borders separate; two shadows exist; nine layers, each a token."],[7013,"Eleven decision kinds are recorded — `intent_resolution · metric_resolution · chart_recommendation · dashboard_plan ·\nadvisor_suggestion · insight_selection · version_policy_default · alert_evaluation · filter_derivation ·\nmodel_proposal · dashboard_proposal` — each with its action space and score distribution, and seventeen outcome\nsignals written back by the actions that exist (accept, dismiss, publish, acknowledge, pin, reroute …). A record with\n`label_source = llm_proposed` as a training target is refused at the API. No feedback control exists in the UI."],[951,"Embed artifact citations"],[965,"Embed the answer's citations into a document artifact (documented in 1.139.0)"],[4252,"Embed the widget"],[4220,"Embed the widget — the host page, the launcher, a first conversation as a customer, verification, handover, language."],[2303,"Embedding model · reranker"],[6831,"embeds twice"],[3690,"Empty collection — A collection with nothing in it shows the quiet EmptyState in place of the list: one title, the primary action the header line also offers, up to three starting points."],[2692,"EmptyState"],[3048,"EmptyState"],[3753,"EmptyState · DataTable"],[3481,"Enable / disable — the change is the commit; the caller shows the saved note."],[1558,"Enable tool"],[4949,"Enabled"],[4950,"Enabled"],[4842,"End"],[7723,"Engine"],[1299,"Engine log lines (query: level, stage, cursor)."],[4524,"Engine, from computed metrics — *every column has a role*, *a grouping found&#x2A;, *≥ 3 insights&#x2A;, *≥ 3 suggestions&#x2A;, *≥ 4 charts*, *data-quality errors counted*."],[4530,"Engine: card saved."],[4527,"Engine: report saved."],[4521,"Engine: reviewer verdict recorded."],[4518,"Engine: the copy exists."],[4271,"Enter the e-mail and the code."],[5944,"Entering **organization** and searching **Northwind** finds the two entities; the Inspector of *Northwind Traders*\nlists **8 relations**."],[6820,"entities (resolved on their key), co-mention edges, numeric observations, *proposed* claims"],[893,"Entities bound to datasets, dimensions and time dimensions — what metrics and filters are built on."],[7620,"Entities, dimensions, time dimensions and row policies over a dataset — what a metric can be defined on."],[6976,"Entities, dimensions, time dimensions and the row policy over a dataset — what a metric can be defined on."],[2007,"Entry"],[2486,"environment, drivers, identity mode"],[1686,"Epics, stories, tasks and bugs: create, move, assign, relate, comment; acceptance criteria and the Done gate."],[6068,"Equal → *verified*. Different → *falsified*. Cell gone (new version) → *undecided*."],[3061,"error and offline carry Retry; denied names who may grant access when the screen knows; notFound doubles as the other-tenant answer."],[3598,"Error, warning, success, info — four values, used sparingly, always with a label or an icon that carries the same meaning. They tint a chip's dot or an inline alert; they never fill a surface."],[2696,"ErrorState"],[3060,"ErrorState"],[1501,"Evaluation suites shipped with the platform (role, operation, sample count, languages)"],[5056,"Evaluations"],[4836,"Evaluator"],[5901,"Every `[n]` in the text has an entry in **Sources**; **How this was found** lists ten steps."],[7108,"every `/map/view` answer"],[5016,"Every answer in an Auto thread has a route line, and &#x2A;*ⓘ** opens a record with *Candidates considered: n ≥ 1*."],[5569,"Every answer in NexChat is produced by a model, and every model an agent may use is a row in **Models**. Northwind\nstarts with what the deployment provides; in this chapter Olena adds the organization's own — a small Qwen served\nby Ollama on a machine inside the company network — and you follow it from the form to NexChat's picker, to the\npolicy that governs it, to the refusal a Builder gets when he tries the same, and to the audit line left behind\nwhen it is deleted. Along the way: what a **cloud** model asks for instead, and why the key you type never comes\nback."],[3673,"Every app's header line carries the Ask bar: the minimised NexChat composer that sends to chat-api as a Project of that app and offers the hand-off chip and &#x2A;Back to \\<app>* return. An app never builds its own chat input."],[3864,"Every application mounts `NexusShell` with the shared App Launcher, header, organization · project context and Ask surface. An app does not invent its own navigation chrome, theme switch or locale switch."],[4538,"Every artifact now carries a **Published** pill; the notebook stays **Draft**. The card became a recorded line:\n**HUMAN REVIEW — Published 8 artifacts · Alex Owner · 17:41**."],[5659,"Every batch of edits is already a version (the chip counts them); **Save version** names one you want to come back\nto. **Restore v1** later creates a *new* version equal to v1 — history is append-only. The `⋯` menu offers\n**Objects list** (the keyboard path to every element), **Export glTF · Export OBJ · Import glTF** (client-side) and\n**Delete scene** (owner; typed name). Back in **Scenes** the library shows the card with a footprint thumbnail,\n*6 objects · v2* and *Can edit*; the New-scene door moved to the header."],[6253,"Every change, by whom, when: &#x2A;reference\\_attached · NEXUS-104 · Epic 011 …*. Filter by **Who** (a person, an agent,\nthe importer) and by **Kind**. An agent's actions carry the agent's name; nothing an agent does is attributed to\nthe person it works for."],[4312,"Every chapter in this guide is one task you can do yourself, step by step, with the screens you will see. All of\nthem use the same everyday example so you can follow along from the first chapter to the last:\n**Plan a weekend trip** — who does what, and what the finished Flow looks like."],[6055,"Every claim of the report first, then the agreement's: **Warsaw · Shipments · Verified · acme-q3-2026-delivery-\nreport.md**, **Rotterdam · Late · Verified**, **Total · Shipments · Verified** … and, lower, **Total · On-time\nrate · Falsified**, **Kyiv · On-time rate · Falsified**. The **Item** is *row label · column label* of the cell;\n**Kind** is the verdict; **Context** the document."],[7164,"Every claim then lives in one of three places, and moves between them only through a gate:"],[2248,"Every code execution an agent asks for becomes a Job in `nexus-sandbox`. The manager is the only identity that can\ncreate it; the Job runs the `sandbox-python` image as a non-root user on a read-only root filesystem with a\ndeny-all NetworkPolicy — it cannot reach the APIs, the database, the internet or another sandbox. A ResourceQuota\ncaps how many can run at once. With a gVisor RuntimeClass (`sandbox.runtimeClassName: gvisor`) the kernel is\nisolated too, which is what the strictest data-classification profiles require; without it the platform simply\nrefuses to run those profiles rather than running them less safely."],[2545,"Every component of the kit: its contract, its states, its accessibility and its stories."],[5177,"Every composer in NexChat has a microphone. One tap, speak, pause: no stop button, no hold-to-talk. The recording goes\nonce to the speech model behind the Model Gateway — on this stack the local **faster-whisper** sidecar — and comes back\nas text that becomes your message, marked *Spoken*. The answer is read back in one sentence by the local **Ukrainian\nTTS** or a hosted voice, while the screen already shows the full text."],[2442,"every current session assertion expires within five minutes; users stay signed in through their cookie"],[3299,"every decision is a button on the card; the language switch is a `tablist` with roving tabindex; the golden-case receipt is `role=status` with pass/fail as text, not colour"],[692,"Every error body carries a `correlation_id`. Administrators find the request in **NexCore › Audit** by that id —\nsee Read the audit trail of a run."],[6481,"Every few weeks you plan a short trip for two or three people. It always goes the same way: collect what everyone\nwants, check the weather and the budget, propose a couple of options, argue a bit, decide, and finally put it into\nthe calendar. It is a small job, it repeats, and half of it is looking things up. That is exactly the shape of work\nNexi is made for."],[5197,"Every few weeks you plan a short trip for two or three people. It always goes the same way: collect what everyone\nwants, check the weather and the budget, propose a couple of options, decide, and put it into the calendar. Small,\nrepetitive, half of it is looking things up — exactly the kind of work Nexi is for. The chapters in this guide build\nit piece by piece."],[3525,"every glyph is `role=img` with an `aria-label` and a `title`; the fields are labelled inputs; a fact carries `aria-label` *label: value*; an unparsable value is `aria-invalid` with a `role=alert` line"],[6984,"Every governed run: the BIQuery, the dataset version, the compiled SQL (readable by editors), rows scanned, time, the viewer's row-policy id. &#x2A;How was this calculated?*"],[7054,"Every hand — pointer, keyboard, touch, typed sentence, voice, agent, import — produces **`SceneOp`s**\n(`forge-scene-op.schema.json`): `{op_id, kind, target_ids[], payload, source}` with `source ∈ manual · keyboard · touch\n· typed · voice · agent · import · system` and **26 kinds** (`add · update · move · resize · transform · set_style ·\nset_color_key · connect · disconnect · group · ungroup · set_layer · set_visibility · set_lock · set_semantic ·\nset_property · bind · unbind · set_camera · add_track_step · delete · restore · layout · reorder · undo · redo`). No op\ncarries an utterance or a prompt."],[2505,"Every image runs as a **non-root user** (`uid 10001`; the sandbox as `65532`), on a **read-only root filesystem**\nwith a small `/tmp&#x60; tmpfs, with &#x2A;*`no-new-privileges`**, and `tini` as pid 1 for clean signal handling."],[2372,"every image with its digest — what `mirror.sh` copies and what you archive with a deployment"],[3858,"Every interactive element has an accessible name; focus is visible (`:focus-visible`, 2 px); tabs, menus, switches, trees and separators use the WAI-ARIA pattern; the target is WCAG 2.2 AA and the workshop fails a story with a serious or critical axe violation."],[4200,"Every KPI gains a delta — &#x2A;Late deliveries 2 016 ▲ +13,3 %*, &#x2A;Revenue 5 002 410 EUR ▲ +18,1 %*, &#x2A;Late delivery rate\n▼ −3,6 %* — computed by running the same query for the comparison window; the arrow's colour follows the metric's\n**direction** (*lower is better* for a late rate). *Previous year* aligns the window a year back instead. The status\nline reads *Filtered to Year to date · Month · previous period*."],[3023,"Every list of records: a real `<table>`, 36 px sticky header, 42 px rows, one border; click / Space selects (`aria-selected`), Enter / double-click drills in. The body owns `loading`, `error` (with Retry) and `empty` — a header over nothing is a defect."],[3017,"Every list of records: a real <table>, 36 px sticky header, 42 px rows, one border; click / Space selects (aria-selected), Enter / double-click drills in."],[6456,"every member, viewers included"],[7202,"Every model call an Agent, an Evaluator or a Flow step makes."],[7135,"Every model, tool, connection, agent, skill, flow and project has a **stable identity** and a **machine-readable\ndescription**. Not a label for humans — a description precise enough for Nexi to act on without asking."],[6930,"Every module API runs three doors in order on every route:"],[7500,"every My Work read"],[3870,"Every name, number, address and document in the workshop and the catalogue is invented; nothing is copied from a tenant, a customer or a real person. The publication scan fails on a secret or a real-looking identifier."],[2517,"Every Nexi application is built from one kit and one set of rules. This section is that system, written once: the\npages are generated from the Design System Register, and every component is shown as it really renders, in the\n**component workshop** — a living catalogue of every component in every state, in Light and Graphite, in English and\nUkrainian."],[3562,"Every number on the screen is a token — spacing, type, radius, control height, layer, shadow, data colour. A raw\ncolour, a px radius, an off-scale size or a `z-index` literal in an application stylesheet fails the fitness check."],[6741,"Every object in the graph — a page, a fragment, a mention, an entity, a claim — answers three questions, and the\nanswers are independent of each other:"],[734,"Every operation on the reference pages has an **Authorization** row under the request line. Expand it and paste the\nvalue in the form the header takes — the word `Bearer`, a space, the token:"],[5251,"Every organization starts with a signed pack — agents, skills, flow patterns, tools and one Blueprint. Read the registry in Core, open one agent and see what Core governs about it, then read the Blueprint chain, the settings matrix and the pack card to understand where the ceilings come from and why a Project can only tighten them. Fifteen minutes of reading, no changes."],[1753,"Every Overview number (1173): deterministic counts, health (owner-set or derived — a `health_derivation` decision), active iteration, next milestone, reference coverage. An org administrator without a relation gets `content_visible=false` counts."],[636,"Every page in this section is generated at build time from the contract files the platform ships, so what you\nread is exactly what the API accepts. Every operation has a **playground**: fill the fields, press *Send*, read the\nreal answer of a real Nexi — yours."],[620,"Every person carries a **clearance**, every resource a **classification** — *Public · Confidential · DSK · Secret\n· Top secret*. A relation never overrides clearance: an owner cleared to *Confidential* is refused their own\nProject the day it is reclassified *Secret*. A Project's classification is set at creation and may be tightened,\nnever loosened below the organization's default; cloud models are capped by the Blueprint (*Confidential* in the\nbase pack), so a *Secret* Project can only ever use local models."],[7570,"Every place Nexi picks among alternatives — a route, a WIP override, a template plan, a Resolver plan — kept with its full action space, scores, the chosen arm and the outcome people gave it."],[2480,"Every process answers a health probe with a body that names its drivers — the same body the smoke report collects:"],[7512,"every project read"],[6989,"Every published version"],[547,"Every record carries `allowed_actions[]` decided server-side for the reader; a stale edit answers `409\nVERSION_CONFLICT`; an archived project is read-only (`409 PROJECT_ARCHIVED`); a hidden project is `404`."],[74,"Every refusal is also written to the organization's audit log as a **Deny** row with a reason code — the same codes\nlisted at the end of this page. Screens below are the real ones, taken from the fixture\norganizations *Mission A* and *Northwind Traders*."],[22,"Every refusal state Nexi shows — in NexChat, NexCore, on approval cards and in the API — with the reason code behind it and the person who can change it."],[5554,"Every request NexChat makes carries a **correlation id**; the runtime stamps it on the turn, the agent run, the\nmodel invocation and the audit records it writes, so one id is the whole story. **Executions** is chat-api's\n`GET /chat/observability/traces` (`kind`, `status`, `project_id`, `since`, `limit`): the tenant's latest agent\nand flow runs by reference, allowed only for the tenant administrator (`core.tenant` READ). A **trace** is\n`GET /chat/trace/{correlation_id}` — the tenant admin reads any; a human who is *owner* of **every** Project the\ntrace touches reads that one; anyone else is answered **404**, so the id itself reveals nothing. The Payloads tab\nasks again with `?include=payloads`, which passes a second gate (`observability.payload` READ — a human with\n*administer* on the Project, or the tenant admin) and writes a `payload_viewed` audit record naming the payload\nkinds. Payload text is redacted by policy before it is stored, and a Project may be configured for *metadata only*,\nin which case the trace carries sizes and ids and no text. **Audit** is core-api's\n`GET /organizations/{id}/audit` (`since`, `limit`, `action`) — Owner or Admin only, **403** for a member, **404**\nfor a stranger; the store is append-only. Core's shell decides whether to *offer* the administrators' screens by\nprobing an *administer* action, which is why a member's refused visit is recorded as *Administer · connection\n\\_all · Deny · NOT\\_AN\\_ADMINISTRATOR*."],[220,"Every request that reaches Nexi — a click in NexChat, a page in Core, a call from a script, a Tool an agent wants\nto use — is answered by the server with one of three things: the result, **403 · you may not**, or **404 · there\nis nothing here**. This page explains how that answer is made, in the order it is made, so that when you see a\ndenied screen you know which wall you hit and who can move it."],[4843,"Every run ends here — approved or rejected, the run is recorded."],[5688,"Every run: six stages, the execution tree step by step, who executed each step, what it produced, its log."],[5153,"Every save creates a snapshot; the list is newest first, each row with the version, its status, an optional change\nsummary, the time and the author."],[4486,"Every save on any tab creates the next version, newest on top, with a short note on what changed — *Draft created*,\n*Overview edited*, *Tool bound: project.search* — the time and the author. Nothing is ever overwritten: if a colleague\nsaved while you were editing, your save is refused and you reload to see their version first."],[4792,"Every screen in this chapter was captured on the review fixture except the two **decided** states (steps 4 and 5),\nwhich come from the platform's acceptance evidence of the approval step. On the fixture stack that draws the portal,\nNexTasks currently refuses a person's decision (*Your session is not valid*) because its session-verification feed\ndoes not start in test mode — recorded as an open item; the frames will be re-captured on *Plan the weekend* when\nit is fixed."],[3852,"Every screen renders loading · empty · error · denied · offline · not found before its content, through the kit's `DataStateView`. Denied and not found look the same (the UI cannot tell \"missing\" from \"not yours\"); error and offline carry Retry; a spinner never sits over stale content."],[5958,"Every source version goes through the same **pipeline**: six stages, about twenty steps, each executed by a named\nspecialist and each leaving a record of what it produced. This chapter reads the Pipeline screen, opens the run that\nprocessed `northwind-framework-agreement-2027.pdf`, and follows it step by step — so that when a run fails or a claim\nlooks odd you know exactly where to look."],[6796,"Every source version runs through the same six stages. The worker is a **Dagster** code location with one\npartitioned asset per stage and one partition per source version; a sensor scans continuous sources (server folders,\nDrive) about every minute and places an order for each new or changed file."],[4750,"Every step so far is **Done** with its node id, duration and the worker that ran it; the agent step also names the\nagent run behind it (`nexus://agent/run/…`) so the trace can be followed further. Then **Waiting · Review\nresults**, and inside it the **approval card**:"],[2542,"Every story in the workshop is also a test: it renders, its interaction runs, and an accessibility engine checks the\nresult — a serious or critical finding fails the build. The *Accessibility* panel in the workshop shows the same\nfindings interactively for any story, in any theme or language."],[3538,"Every string is a key"],[3854,"Every string is a key (uk = en); copy never names a mechanism, never invents a value, and says the same thing for not-found and not-yours. One card, one progress, one receipt per action — the conversation register's honesty rules apply to every surface, not only to chat."],[4373,"Every tab and every field of the agent screen — what it means, what it changes, and what it can never do — with the real screen for each."],[5047,"Every tab and every field of the skill screen — what a skill carries, what it never carries, and how the human review gate works — with the real screen for each."],[5168,"Every tab maps to the Chat API › Skills: Get skill\nreturns what the Studio shows, Update skill is Save,\nReview skill records the human review and\nPublish skill is refused without it. Try them from the reference with your\nown session (how to authenticate)."],[7205,"Every Tool call to a system outside Nexi — an API, a database, a file store, another agent, a webhook."],[4901,"every tool has a **Posture** you can read before you attach it: what it touches, what it may reach, who reviewed it;"],[2242,"Every upgrade renders three new migration Jobs (`-r<revision>`), the new API pods wait for them, the old pods keep\nserving until then. `helm rollback` restores the previous images and configuration, **not** the schema — migrations\nare forward-only. Take a database backup before an upgrade and treat a rollback as an emergency measure, never as a\nroutine."],[7120,"every upload row"],[6973,"Every version"],[7771,"Every voice door is PEP-checked on the exact thread before any byte moves; Mallory gets 404; agents and services get\n403 on person-only doors. Targets resolve through the owning app as the person; writes carry their own PEP and\nidempotency key; access is re-checked on every Confirm and every hands-free turn. Level 4 never completes by voice.\nVoice is not authentication and VAD is never speaker identification. Frames, files, snippets and pages are quoted\ndata — a frame or file turn offers no tools; the search call has no tools and flattens results so a snippet cannot\nforge `[n]`; the research model picks link ids only. Forbidden by fitness checks: voice adding\nrights; a Source or claim from a frame or session file without the separate route; product nouns in arm code;\ntranscript text in decision rows; audio or frames in JetStream, logs, traces or backups; persistent capture without a\nfresh gesture; a results page in a headless browser; CAPTCHA solving or residential proxies."],[6683,"Everyone"],[4976,"Everything a person needs, in one place: **Via** the connection · the **Account** the call would use · **Why** —\n&#x2A;This tool changes data outside Nexi — policy asks a person to approve it first.* · **Requested by** the agent\n*on behalf of* the person who asked · the **Arguments** as a key/value list (`supplier_id: sup_42`) · an optional\n**Comment** for the audit trail · **Approve** and **Reject**, and a countdown until the request expires — after which\nnothing happens and the card says so. Approve, and the call runs with your decision recorded; the thread continues with *Continues the\nanswer above*. Reject, and the runtime writes &#x2A;Nothing changed.* A member who is not an owner sees the same card\nwith *Waiting for a Project owner* and no buttons."],[2051,"Everything after the install — releases, mirroring, upgrades, rotation, backups, health — is on Operations. The chart itself is described rung by rung on Kubernetes."],[299,"Everything an Admin can, and the organization itself: settings, Blueprint binding, pack installation; the Owner is the one member who cannot be removed. One per organization — the person who created it."],[239,"Everything belongs to exactly one **organization** (the *tenant*): people, Projects, agents, models, connections,\nruns, audit. The first check on every request is whether the actor and the thing asked for belong to the same\norganization. When they do not, the answer is **404** — not 403 — so that an outsider cannot even learn that the\nthing exists. A Project id from another organization, a thread, a file, an approval: *Not found*, every time."],[5436,"Everything in Core so far was about the organization. **Account** is about you: your name and e-mail, the role and\nclearance the administrators gave you, where you are signed in, your theme and language. The part that matters\nfor safety is **Sessions**: every browser that currently holds a session for you is a row, and you can sign the\nothers out from the one you trust — a laptop you left open at home, a shared machine you forgot."],[3972,"Everything in this chapter is one call each in the Chat API, and you can run them from\nthe reference with your own session (how to authenticate):"],[4161,"Everything NexBI computes stands on a **dataset**: a governed table with **immutable versions**. A version is\npublished once and never edited; a correction is a new version with a note; a version that must not be shown any\nmore is *revoked* and stops rendering everywhere at once. This chapter uploads the *shipments* CSV into the\n**Logistics** Project, publishes it, and reads the four tabs of the dataset page."],[2359,"Everything on this page applies to every target above the laptop. Where Compose and Kubernetes differ, both\ncommands are given."],[4419,"Everything on this tab is about **reading**. The line at the top is the rule that makes the tab safe to use: &#x2A;Sources\nare always filtered by the Project and by your access at run time.* Whatever you allow here, the agent can never show a\nperson something that person could not open themselves."],[3527,"Everything that floats over NexMap's WebGL canvas and is DOM, not map: the kind glyphs (shipment · vessel · aircraft · hub by kind), the status line (cursor · zoom band · what is o"],[3532,"Everything that floats over NexMap's WebGL canvas and is DOM, not map: the kind glyphs (shipment · vessel · aircraft · hub by kind), the status line (cursor · zoom band · what is on screen · loading), the map controls (layers · zoom · reset north — `IconButton`s in a dock), the layers panel (a floating surface, DS-7015, with one switch per layer and the unplaced count as a door), the keyboard sheet (`?`) and the hover tooltip (feature · cell · zone · event · lane — one grammar, `role=presentation`, never focusable). Layers and dock tokens: `--nexus-z-dock` · `--nexus-z-popover`; the canvas itself is not a story (WebGL) — UAT-3 compares the running workspace to these. Not a kit duplicate: the kit has no map, no layers and no hover card."],[2462,"everything: organizations, users, chats, agents, flows, approvals, audit, sealed credentials"],[1247,"Evidence"],[1307,"Evidence bundles"],[6778,"Evidence panel → *Score 89 % · gliner-x · zero-shot*"],[6794,"Evidence tab of a claim"],[1259,"Evidence Workspace structure (query: kind, page, cursor). Text arrives as previews; full text by item text_ref through getItemText."],[7219,"Example"],[5055,"Examples"],[6609,"Execute a step; mark a right."],[5342,"Execute approved capabilities."],[1171,"Executions of model-generated code and their output."],[1470,"Executions of model-generated code and their output."],[6798,"Executor"],[888,"Explain query"],[6643,"Exploration"],[5692,"Explore Graph Studio"],[5750,"Explore Graph Studio"],[5905,"Explore Graph Studio"],[2549,"Export"],[955,"Export artifact"],[1174,"Export artifact"],[793,"Export dashboard"],[1460,"Export pack"],[1464,"Export the organisation's intelligence / process layer as a signed `.nexuspack` — templates, agents, skills, tool definitions, policies, evaluations, sandbox profiles, UI config. Connections are replaced by `requires.connections`; tenancy and secrets are stripped and re-scanned before the archive is signed. PepAction=export."],[1506,"External systems Synapse can reach."],[1434,"f: the Project **owner** lifts every type control of the Project — the reverse of `retireAllTerms`. `nexus.graph.vocabulary.type.restored.v1` per type, `bulk: true`."],[1433,"f: the Project **owner** retires every type of the chosen layers for this Project in one door — the owner's *remove all layers of ontology*. Default `levels: [L1, L2]` (candidates + published); `L0` only when named. The same reversible overlay as `retireTerm`, one control per type (types already retired are left as they are). `nexus.graph.vocabulary.type.retired.v1` per type, `bulk: true`."],[2624,"Facts · Fact"],[3071,"Facts · Fact"],[1532,"Facts through a connection (listings, changes, permissions) — normalised JSON, never a credential. Service principals with `connection.read` only."],[1886,"faster-whisper (`large-v3-turbo`, \\~1.6 GB) behind `POST /v1/audio/transcriptions`; the Gateway's local `asr` route. Compose profile `asr-local`, Dockerfile `deploy/docker/asr-local.Dockerfile`, no published port."],[7724,"faster-whisper / CTranslate2 (MIT), `deepdml/faster-whisper-large-v3-turbo-ct2` (\\~1.6 GB)"],[6655,"Feature flags: chat-api `NEXUS_FEATURES=auto,data_arm,capability_arm`; web `NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURES=AUTO_ROUTING,\nPATTERN_LIBRARY,DATA_ANALYSIS`."],[2489,"features on, `job_bus_driver`, `sandbox.driver`, flow-runtime counters (`handled`, `failed`, `expired_capabilities`)"],[1865,"Features, observations, H3 aggregation, zones, saved views, uploads; the module gate; decision records. Owns `nexus_map` — **PostGIS** required (the `nexus/postgres` image carries PostGIS 3.6 next to AGE and pgvector). Demo world only with `MAP_DEMO_WORLD=1`, refused in production."],[2588,"Field"],[3078,"Field"],[4459,"Field"],[4590,"Field"],[5086,"Field"],[5113,"Field"],[5125,"Field"],[5312,"Field"],[3777,"Field · Select · Switch · CheckList · SearchField · SecretInput · RadioCard"],[4079,"Fields: the metric, a comparison (&#x2A;> · ≥ · \\< · ≤*), the threshold, the period (*last 7 days* by default) and a\n**streak** — *fire after n consecutive evaluations over the line* (×2 in the registry row means two in a row). The\nFlow (`flw_tpl_bi_metric_alert`) evaluates `bi.alert.evaluate` on the schedule; every evaluation is an\n`alert_evaluation` decision with the value, the threshold and whether the streak was reached. When it fires, the\nalert posts into the Project thread you name, with &#x2A;How was this calculated?* attached; **Acknowledge** on the\nautomation's page records who saw it and stops repeat posts until the next crossing."],[5861,"Figures are rendered through an authenticated door of NexChat — never a public link; if you may not see the page a\nfigure is on, its place reads &#x2A;This figure is not available to you.*"],[6434,"File name and path; sheet names; column names and types; row and column counts; the legend sheet's definitions"],[7765,"filename, sha, pages"],[4507,"Files are accepted only in Project chats, and the server decides the type from the bytes, not the name — a PDF\nrenamed `.xlsx` is refused with *We can read .xlsx · .csv · .tsv · .parquet · .json · .txt · .md*. A large CSV is\nnot refused: it becomes a dataset (stored, profiled) rather than inline text. Up to eight files per message."],[3908,"Fill in the form and press **Create organization**."],[4020,"Filter by period and grain, compare with the previous period, read a KPI's version policy, open History and Updates, understand what a viewer does and does not see."],[2964,"Filter panel"],[3695,"Filter panel — When a list needs more than three filters, they leave the toolbar for a panel above (a wrapping row of labelled compact selects and chips, 12 px label over each) or beside the list"],[99,"Filtering the log to *Deny* is the fastest way for an administrator to see who hit which wall today\n(Read the audit trail of a run)."],[3966,"Finally press **New chat** in the sidebar."],[6123,"Find and inspect an object"],[6120,"Find and inspect an object — Go to, the list, the Inspector, and what the actions do today."],[6131,"Find one shipment — *Cable drums · SHP\\_0163*, delayed near Hamburg — and read everything the map knows about it, with\nthe provenance of each fact."],[4338,"Find the run that needs you, read the card, see it as an editor, approve and reject with a note, read History, start the Flow from a chat."],[5013,"Finished, as the Project owner **Dana*&#x2A; sees it after allowing the tool: **✓ Resolver · 2 of 3 steps · 7 s ·\nComplete — 2 of 3 steps done**; ✓ *Connect your mailbox — connected — reads with your permission only*; ✓ *Ask to\nallow mail search — a Project owner allowed it*; ~~Triage the mail~~ *skipped — Nexi cannot do this kind of step\nyet*. **CREATED 2** — the Connection *Connected* and the Request *Allowed*, each with **Details**. The report is\nthe run's own narrator's text; nothing in it is claimed done that the engine did not record."],[641,"Five APIs, one sign-in. Which credential each one reads — and how to pass it in the playground, curl or code — is\non Authenticate your API calls."],[5374,"Five cards. **Nexi Base** is *Installed* — the layer every organization has. **NexCare**, **NexForge** and\n**NexMap** read &#x2A;Available · provides module …* with what each contains: a NexCare pack brings one agent, four\nskills, three flows and a Blueprint layer; NexForge one agent, one skill and five templates; NexMap a Blueprint\nlayer, a geofence Flow template and the vocabulary of positions. The filters above the cards — *Layer*,\n*Provides*, *Status* — narrow a longer catalogue; *Provides → module* shows only packs that add an application."],[216,"Five checks, in order"],[4584,"Five entries. **Attach file** and **Add source** are the two that concern knowledge; **Choose agent**, **Use\nskill** and **Project context** you met before. Choose **Add source**."],[6999,"Five properties follow from this shape and are the reason for it:"],[2094,"Flag"],[2976,"Floating surface"],[3205,"Floating surface"],[3697,"Floating surface — One anatomy for everything that floats over the page — a menu, a popover, the composer picker, a select's list: radius 12 · padding 6 · 1 px border · --nexus-shadow-md · items 32 p"],[7128,"Floor one: the platform vocabulary — what exists and what it can do"],[7129,"Floor two: knowledge — what is *true* in your Project"],[6517,"Flow"],[7355,"Flow"],[7358,"Flow Engine"],[7402,"Flow Engine"],[4821,"Flow Studio opens on the **Design** tab. Click the name in the breadcrumb and rename the draft **Plan the weekend**\n(the drafter named it from your words)."],[7401,"Flow Studio publish; the owner's rights"],[1007,"Flows and runs"],[4887,"Flows are resources of the Chat API › Flows:\nCreate flow draft drafts from an intent,\nSave flow draft saves the canvas,\nValidate flow, Publish flow,\nStart flow run starts a test or real run and\nList flow runs fills the Runs tab. Approvals are\nTasks API › Approvals. Run them from the reference with your own session\n(how to authenticate)."],[1035,"Flows of a Project (screen 15) — PepAction=view on project; returns latest version per workflow_id with status + last run summary"],[5689,"Follow a pipeline run"],[5747,"Follow a pipeline run"],[5948,"Follow a pipeline run"],[6545,"Follow-ups in an analysis thread go to the same agent; the record says *this thread already runs with it*."],[4544,"Follow-ups in the same thread stick to the Flow's own **Data scientist** agent — *this thread already runs with\nit*. Expand the *Ran code* line for **Show code** and **Open notebook**: &#x2A;Python on the run's prepared dataset; no\nnetwork, no credentials. The code is in the analysis notebook.* Charts are native, editable chart artifacts (bar ·\nline · area · pie · scatter · metric); an unsupported kind becomes the nearest one and the answer says so."],[4963,"For **http** the list says &#x2A;*No more tools match.** Raw *HTTP request* and *MCP invoke* are builder escape hatches\nand are never offered in this dialog — a business user's agent reaches systems only through named, reviewed tools.\nThe footer offers &#x2A;*Import from OpenAPI…** for owners and editors; that wizard is a chapter of its own."],[2029,"For `nexus-service-tokens`, `nexus-idp` and `nexus-provider-keys` write two short `ExternalSecret` manifests of your\nown (the chart maps only the three above today) with `dataFrom: [{ extract: { key: nexus/prod/idp } }]`, which turns\neach JSON field into a Secret key. Apply them before the chart; they refresh on ESO's interval, so rotating a value in\nSecrets Manager reaches the pods on their next restart."],[2074,"for `psql` and backups"],[4627,"For a chat turn, the Agent Runtime assembles **pinned context** from the Project's approved sources, filtered by\nyour access, and records what it used in the turn's **AnswerProvenance** — that record is what the Grounding drawer\nshows. Nothing on it is written by the model."],[4662,"For a conversational skill like this one you can leave both as they are, or clear the output schema so the agent\nanswers in prose following the *Output format* section. Schemas matter when another step — a Flow, a Tool, an\nEvaluator — has to read the result by field rather than by eye."],[2203,"For a real cluster: an ingress controller, a TLS certificate (cert-manager or your PKI), a mail relay, and — for\ndisconnected sites — a registry mirror with the release copied into it."],[3552,"For builders"],[2525,"For builders — how to add a component, write its story, and keep a new application inside the\nsystem."],[4959,"For connected tools: the only hosts the tool may reach. Anything else is refused as *egress denied*."],[6724,"For inline sequence and flow diagrams inside chapters we use plain Markdown — for example, the same scenario in a\ncompact form:"],[6899,"for operators only, never a Nexi surface; every fact of a run is also in the run page"],[6180,"For step 5, a CSV with `name, lat, lon` columns. The walk used `depots.csv` — five rows: a Lviv depot, a row without\ncoordinates, one with the axes swapped, one at (0, 0) and one out of range."],[5619,"For step 6 a microphone and the `asr-local` sidecar running behind the Model Gateway (the dev stack starts it when\ninstalled). Without them the mic says &#x2A;Voice is not configured for this workspace — text still works.*"],[4234,"For the last step, a Telegram bot token from BotFather. The documentation stack has none, so that step shows the\nstate before a channel is connected and describes the rest."],[2003,"For the sandbox's kernel isolation (`sandbox.runtimeClassName: gvisor`) EKS managed node groups do not ship gVisor;\nuse a self-managed node group with the gVisor containerd shim or leave `runtimeClassName` empty — the platform then\nrefuses the strictest data-classification sandbox profiles instead of running them less isolated. A GPU node group\n(`g5`/`g6` instances) is optional and only needed for models you host yourself."],[4478,"For the Trip planner the defaults are right. If you build an agent that only sorts messages into three folders,\nchoose *Router* or *Classifier* and cap it at *Tier 1* — it will run on a tiny local model for almost nothing."],[4444,"For the Trip planner, *Project default* everywhere is right: it reads the booking pages and last year's notes you pin,\nand remembers the conversation."],[1884,"forge-api, core-api"],[2954,"Form rhythm"],[3310,"Form rhythm"],[3384,"Form rhythm"],[3696,"Form rhythm — Label (12 px · 500 · secondary) · 6 px · control (34 px, 13 px) · 6 px · hint or error (12 px); 16 px between fields; a two-column grid at 16 × 24 for short fields; a titled fields"],[5782,"Formats NexGraph reads: PDF; Word, RTF, OpenDocument text, EPUB; PowerPoint and OpenDocument slides; Excel,\nOpenDocument sheets, CSV; plain text, Markdown, MDX, HTML, AsciiDoc, LaTeX, JSON, XML; e-mail (`.eml`, `.msg`),\ncalendar (`.ics`); PNG, JPEG, TIFF, WebP, BMP images. **Up to 50 MB per file** (the operator may set another\nlimit)."],[2680,"FormInspector"],[3087,"FormInspector"],[3729,"FormInspector · Field · Select"],[5868,"Found the entities the question names."],[3572,"Foundations"],[2519,"Foundations — colour, type, spacing and density, radius and borders, elevation, motion, icons,\nviewports. Every number is a token; the workshop reads the live values."],[4198,"Four **KPI** blocks, each with the metric's value, the **dataset version** it was computed on (`dsv_…`) and its\n**version policy** — *Follow latest approved* — plus *cached* when the number came from the per-viewer cache.\nTwo timelines (*Late delivery rate by carrier*, *Revenue by carrier*) and a **text** block *How to read this*,\nwritten by the author for the reader."],[6277,"Four counters on one line. **Today** — items due today and how many are overdue. **Critical** — P0 items on your\nname in any project. **In progress** — items in an *in progress* or *review* stage across your projects, with how\nmany are yours. **Completed** — done items across your projects, and how many were yours. Each counter's small\nline tells you what it counts, so the numbers are never a guess."],[3909,"Four fields. **Organization name** — how it appears everywhere (here *NovaBank*). **Organization handle** — a\nshort lowercase identifier proposed from the name; you can edit it. **Work domain** — optional; people whose\ne-mail ends in this domain can *request* to join (they still need approval). **Region** — where the\norganization's data lives; this cannot be changed later, so pick the region your company requires. The note\nsays it: &#x2A;Only the essentials. Security, models and Blueprints are configured later in Core.*"],[214,"Four kinds of identity"],[213,"Four kinds of identity, one organization boundary, five checks in a fixed order, and one rule that surprises administrators — administering an organization is not reading its content. With the screens each answer produces."],[4601,"Four nodes in a line. **Start** is a manual trigger with two **inputs**: `offers` of type **file** (required) and\n`weekend` of type string (optional). The **Offer reader** agent step receives `$.inputs.offers` — the document\nitself, not its name — and is asked for a `table` and a `summary`. **Save comparison table** is the platform tool\n`artifact.create_table`: it takes the agent's table and writes it into the Canvas under the title *Cottage\noffers — autumn weekend*. **Table ready** ends the run with the artifact's address and the summary as outputs.\nThe **Valid** check is green. Press **Publish**."],[6668,"Four rules, four views"],[4109,"Four sources. **From Nexi** — a KPI of a *validated or certified* metric, a text note, a section header. **From\nartifacts** — a chart or table that already exists in the Project (made in NexChat or in an earlier Studio session),\nadded as a **reference** with a version policy. **From data** — pick a dataset, a measure and a breakdown; NexBI\nruns the governed query and creates the chart artifact for you. **Ask Nexi** — describe the block; the answer comes\nback as a draft chart you accept. A block never carries a copy of a spec: adding one that does is refused\n(*422 SPEC\\_COPY\\_REJECTED*), because a dashboard is references all the way down."],[4817,"Four things in that sentence become four things in the Flow. **Every week on Thursday** → a schedule trigger.\n**Keep improving … until** → a loop with a Goal. **budget\\_fit >= 0.9** → the Goal's success criterion, written\nas *metric, comparison, number* — write it that way and the drafter can read it. **I review** → an approval\nstep for the Project owner. *Two options* and *the calendar* are for the agent to understand; nothing in the\nFlow's structure depends on them."],[4707,"Four things to notice. The pill **Draft** — the agent exists but nobody can pick it in chat yet. The **Purpose**\nis your sentence; it is the one line shown in the agent picker later. **Model** says &#x2A;Project default (chat ·\ncheapest qualified)* — the agent does not own a model; the Project's policy chooses the cheapest model that\nqualifies for the classification (see Synapse if you want to know why). And\n**Governance: Not reviewed** — NexCore has not looked at this agent yet; it may block it later, and you would\nsee that here."],[7100,"Fourteen schemas plus `pack-module` sit in `packages/contracts/schemas/v1/map-*.schema.json`; the vocabulary\n(`PositionKind`, `GeoFeatureKind`, `GeofenceState/TransitionKind` — there is no `exited`, only `left` with a dwell —\n`MapLod`, `MapPepAction` 17, `MapDecisionKind` 7, `MapUploadRejectReason` 16…) is in `vocabulary/v1.json` (ADR-0051 §1)."],[6867,"Fragments reached from the anchors' mentions."],[6829,"fragments, entities, facts"],[5143,"Free text, up to 2 000 characters, stored with the decision so the next reader knows what was checked."],[1758,"From a laptop to Docker Compose, to Kubernetes, to AWS — the same images and the same definitions on every target; only the configuration changes."],[5292,"From an empty sign-up page to an organization with two people — create the account, verify the e-mail, create “Northwind Traders”, read what Nexi set up for you, invite a colleague with a role, and follow the invitation from the mail to the roster. About twenty minutes for two people."],[3708,"From any app's Ask bar a question goes to chat-api as that app's Project; the answer appears in the Ask panel with its provenance line; a hand-off opens NexChat with the *as