udWatch). No secret is ever written to a log — a redaction failure is a bug to report."],[755,"Long-running integrations should not borrow a person's session. Nexi distinguishes **service identities** from\npeople: a service token names a service, not a user, and the server decides what a service may do from that type\n(for example, only services create approval requests; a person can only decide them). Today service tokens are\nissued for the platform's own services; **self-service API clients for your organization are not available yet** —\nwhen they ship, they will appear in *NexCore › Access & Policies* and on this page. Until then, automate through\nFlows and webhooks, which run as the Flow's publisher under\nthe Project's rules, with no token to keep."],[6374,"Looking for *how to do* something? That is the User guide: one task per chapter, with the real screens."],[4086,"Lower the alert threshold below the current value and **Run now** twice: the second run posts the alert into the thread (streak ×2)."],[5100,"Lowercase letters, digits or hyphens, up to 20 tags."],[3617,"Lucide only, 14 px inside a button or a row, 16 px on its own; always `aria-hidden` — the accessible name is on the control. Status is never an icon alone. No emoji in product UI."],[3615,"Lucide only, two sizes, always with an accessible name on the control."],[2312,"macOS or Linux; **Docker Desktop** (or Docker Engine) running."],[1977,"Mail for sign-up and reset"],[2309,"Mailpit"],[5232,"Make a group, add people, give the group a Project instead of each person."],[5645,"Make a scene and understand that it is one thing seen four ways. The walk starts from the &#x2A;*System landscape (C4)**\ntemplate so there is something to look at in every view."],[6410,"Makes drafts visible to the Project."],[7058,"makes one batch one immutable &#x2A;*`SceneVersion`** (JSON spec + sha256); `restore {n}` is a *new* version equal to n —\nhistory is append-only;"],[5246,"Manage your account — where you are signed in"],[5425,"Manage your account — where you are signed in"],[1038,"Manual edit from Flow Studio (screen 17) — full WorkflowSpec for the current draft version. Rejected with 409 if the target version is published (create a new draft instead). `layout` is stored as-is; execution fields are re-validated."],[1045,"Manual start or \"Test flow\" (test_mode=true — mutating nodes stubbed, no external writes, no approvals created; outputs marked simulated). PepAction=invoke. Server writes FlowRun + first FlowRunStep in one transaction, then publishes `nexus.jobs.run.start.v1` via outbox (1.13.0; was `nexus.jobs.flow.step.ready.v1`). Duplicate idempotency_key returns the existing run (200)."],[7307,"Map (hexagons · objects), Inspector, Time, Views, Zones, Sources"],[7419,"Map view · upload · zone"],[2282,"map-api · care-api · forge-api (modules) · care-worker"],[1869,"map-api, core-api, the tile server"],[1626,"Mark inbox read"],[776,"Mark proposal reviewed"],[1637,"Mark read (own inbox). Writes outcome `accepted` (human_implicit) on the ranking when the entry was the top one."],[7586,"Material Nexi reads for this session only — a text file, one frame of a window — never a Source, never kept; saving is a separate, confirmed act."],[6848,"May"],[134,"Meaning"],[669,"Meaning"],[4423,"Meaning"],[4435,"Meaning"],[4591,"Meaning"],[4911,"Meaning"],[5114,"Meaning"],[5709,"Meaning"],[7532,"Meaning"],[310,"member"],[313,"member"],[316,"member"],[319,"member"],[322,"member"],[325,"member"],[6462,"members of the Project — shape and provenance to agents, rows to the sandbox of a later run"],[6447,"members of the Project; the sandbox, read-only"],[6687,"Members, Builders"],[6691,"Members, Teams, Approvers"],[1156,"Memberships projection (owner/editor/viewer/agent_member)"],[1269,"Memory"],[5667,"Memory (preview)"],[6382,"Memory across runs — reuse, recompute, the Card"],[6736,"Memory: what Flows produced, as proposals"],[6815,"mentions with label and score; `decision_id` per choice"],[6819,"mentions, tables"],[2568,"Menu"],[3194,"Menu"],[3769,"Menu · SearchField · Combobox"],[1108,"Messages"],[1113,"Messages of a thread in order (creator or can_view on its Project)"],[7391,"Metric"],[4134,"Metric · Status · **Formula** · Data · **Target** · Owner. The six metrics of Logistics: four **Certified** (*Late\ndeliveries · Late delivery rate · Revenue · Shipments*), *Freight cost* validated (the list shows it as\n**Proposed** — validated but not yet certified), *Gross margin* **Draft**. Each row carries the key and version\n(`late_rate · v1`). *4 of 6 certified* above the table is what the Overview's pulse strip counts."],[866,"Metric registry (all lifecycles; deprecated badged)."],[854,"Metrics"],[2393,"Migrations"],[1611,"Milestones"],[1617,"Milestones with derived health."],[742,"Mint a new token; send `Authorization: Bearer <token>` exactly."],[3600,"Mint, pink, sky, amber, green, violet, slate, coral, copper, each with a soft tint. They identify an application in the launcher and may mark one running or selected thing on a screen. Never navigation chrome, never a chip, never text colour."],[843,"Mirror a NexGraph DatasetVersion BY REFERENCE: rows are read through graph-api's PEP with the caller's context and materialised by the Dagster asset; the version keeps the graph refs."],[5789,"Mode"],[7363,"Model"],[901,"Model a dataset: derive one entity from the dataset's current version — every column a field, string columns dimensions, the first period/date column the time dimension — and merge it into the Project's model (created when none exists; an entity of the same name is replaced; version += 1). The one door the Data and Metrics screens use before a first metric; the full PUT remains for hand-authored models."],[897,"Model dataset"],[1481,"Model Fabric — registered models, providers and evaluations."],[2335,"Model registry and connections (references only)"],[2418,"model-provider keys, connection credentials, OAuth client secrets"],[1494,"Model