 | care |\nforge`; Compose runs `migrate-<module>` + `<module>-api` only with the profile; Helm has `map.enabled`,\n`care.enabled`, `forge.enabled`, all **off by default**, with a NetworkPolicy allowing egress to postgres, core-api and\nchat-api only. The dev stack starts all three (`scripts/dev-stack.sh`). PostGIS joins AGE and pgvector in the one\nPostgreSQL image (`deploy/docker/postgres/Dockerfile` — GPL at the database-process boundary). See\nDeploy for the ladder."],[3618,"Motion"],[3580,"Motion — One shell transition, one progress pulse, reduced motion honoured."],[535,"Move an item past a WIP limit"],[541,"Move an item to Done with unverified criteria"],[1213,"Move chat to a Project (governed)\n\n/007. Server checks: actor is editor+ on target AND owner/editor on source (or thread owner);\nOPA: target classification ≥ effective thread classification (no downgrade), source compatibility\n(pinned sources/attachments allowed in target), purpose. Deny → ThreadMoveResponse with coarse\nblockers (`classification_downgrade`, `target_access`, `source_incompatible`, `policy`) and\n`user_message_key`. `require_approval` → NexTasks approval task; thread stays in place until decided.\nAudit event `nexus.chat.thread.moved.v1` (allow) or `nexus.core.audit.recorded.v1` (deny) after commit."],[5906,"Move from the landscape of the Project's knowledge to one group, to one object and the network around it — in Space, Lanes and List — and read the Inspector. About twenty minutes."],[5751,"Move from the landscape to a group, to one object and its network — in Space, Lanes and List — and read the Inspector."],[1698,"Move item to project"],[6171,"Move the map into the past and replay it, save a view for yourself or a Project, read the Sources catalogue and upload a CSV of positions with an honest result. About fifteen minutes."],[1200,"Move thread"],[1711,"Move to a stage and position. Server-side authorisation; WIP soft (`wip_exceeded`); entry into `done` completes. Writes a stage transition (dataset), `moved` activity, emits `nexus.tasks.item.moved.v1 {from/to stage + category, wip_exceeded}`; may fire bindings (`automation_trigger_match` decision). Approval projections do not exist as items."],[1693,"Move work item"],[6258,"Moving a card and pressing the browser's back button leaves the card where you moved it — moves are server state, not view state."],[6357,"Moving a story with open criteria to *Done* without a reason is refused; with a reason the Activity tab records the move with your reason and the `acceptance_gate` decision carries *gate\\_overridden*."],[1635,"My Work (1113; ≤ 600 ms incl. the ranking write): personal items + assignments across readable projects, grouped Today · Critical · In progress · Waiting · Later · Completed, ordered by a `my_work_ranking` decision. Humans and agents (an agent sees its assignments)."],[6208,"My Work and the Inbox"],[6262,"My Work and the Inbox"],[6292,"My Work is one read model: `GET /tasks/my-work` returns the counters, the projects with their derived health and the\nranked items, computed server-side under your relations — tasks-api asks NexCore's enforcement point for every project\n(`work_project.view`) and never returns a project you hold no relation to. Personal items are stored with a `MY`\nkey sequence per person and an FGA tuple naming you as owner; a share adds one tuple for one other person. Creating an\nitem is `POST /tasks/items` with an `Idempotency-Key`, so a retried request never creates a duplicate."],[6289,"My Work shows **3** projects in the table and your items grouped under **Critical** and **In progress**."],[7287,"My Work, Inbox, Work projects (board · iterations), Work items, Milestones, References, Acceptance gate, Approvals"],[1622,"My Work, search and other ranked views built for the reader."],[2162,"Name"],[6385,"Name"],[6595,"Name"],[5199,"Name in the example"],[4091,"Name the decision, let the planner pick the closest template, create the draft, add blocks from Nexi, artifacts and data, read Coverage and the Advisor, save, and publish with the acknowledgement. About twenty minutes."],[4136,"Name, **key** (unique in the Project — `gross_margin`), the **entity**, and the **expression**. The grammar is\ndeliberately small: an aggregation over a measure — `SUM(x)`, `COUNT(x)`, `COUNT_DISTINCT(x)`, `AVG(x)`, `MIN(x)`,\n`MAX(x)` — arithmetic between aggregations: `SUM(revenue) - SUM(freight_cost)`,\n`SUM(late_deliveries) / SUM(shipments)` — numeric literals, a reference to another metric, a *filtered*\nsub-expression (`SUM(shipments) WHERE region = 'North'`) and a *time window* (the same aggregate over the previous\nperiod). No free SQL, no functions the engine cannot parameterise; an invalid\nexpression is refused *with the position* (*422 EXPRESSION\\_INVALID*). Optional **unit** (currency, percent,\ncount) and **direction** (*higher is better · lower is better*) decide how a KPI and a comparison are rendered."],[2179,"Namespace"],[6623,"narrator"],[1906,"NATS"],[2297,"NATS JetStream"],[2471,"NATS store"],[2341,"NATS store, local model weights, Dagster home"],[1992,"NATS volume, core-api credential store"],[6599,"need-analyst"],[2049,"Network policy enforcement confirmed: a pod in `nexus-sandbox` cannot reach RDS or the internet"],[2182,"NetworkPolicies"],[3590,"Neutrals, semantic colour, the attention accents, per-application accents and the data palette — in both themes."],[374,"never"],[414,"never"],[432,"never"],[438,"never"],[468,"never"],[480,"never"],[486,"never"],[602,"never"],[6801,"Never"],[474,"never — `403 AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN`"],[525,"never — `403 AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN`"],[566,"never — `AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN`"],[408,"never — text leaves graph-api to people only"],[596,"never — the agent proposes, the person applies"],[5107,"Never put an API key, a password, an email address or a customer's name in here. The text is shown to every builder\nin the Project and travels with the skill wherever it goes."],[7434,"never stored (clip), purged on Remove / 8 h (file), dropped after one vision call (frame)"],[7754,"never stored or logged anywhere; sidecars log counts"],[2760,"New artifact dialog"],[3206,"New artifact dialog"],[799,"New draft — blank, from a template, from a plan or duplicated (references, never specs)."],[2441,"New Ed25519 seed **and** a new `SESSION_SIGNING_KID` (`compose-1` → `compose-2`; `keycloak.signingKid`)"],[968,"New immutable version (Canvas save / Ask NEXUS rewrite result)\n\nWRITE on the Project. `base_version` must equal `current_version`, otherwise 409 (someone else saved first). Body type must match the artifact type (422). An archived artifact is 409 ARTIFACT_ARCHIVED (1.139.0)."],[40,"NexBI"],[4003,"NexBI"],[3994,"NexBI — governed datasets, certified metrics, dashboards recomputed per reader, the Studio, automations as Flows, and data questions answered in NexChat."],[6955,"NexBI — governed numbers"],[6370,"NexBI — governed numbers — datasets with immutable versions, a closed metric grammar, the governed\nquery engine (typed query → parameterised SQL, row policy before aggregation), dashboards as references rendered\nper viewer, automations as Flows."],[7400,"NexBI → Automations, as a Draft Flow"],[7388,"NexBI → Data (a file, a graph dataset version, an analysis result, a Flow output)"],[7392,"NexBI → Metrics"],[7396,"NexBI → Studio; proposed from NexChat"],[109,"NexBI applies *administering is not reading* to numbers, and adds a wall no other application has: a block you may\nnot see keeps its place."],[4139,"NexBI compiles the expression against the model and **runs a test query** on the current dataset version. The\nquery record is kept with the metric (`validation_query_ref`), so *how was this validated* is always answerable.\nSuccess moves the metric to **validated**; a compile error tells you which name the model does not know."],[4071,"NexBI has no scheduler of its own. When you press **New automation**, NexBI creates a **Draft Flow** in your name from a\ntemplate in the signed *nexus-base* pack — *Refresh · Metric alert · Subscription* — and hands you to Flow Studio to\npublish it. The automations registry then shows the Flow's state and its last run. This chapter sets up all three for\n*Carrier performance*."],[7008,"NexBI has no scheduler. *Refresh · Metric alert · Subscription* are Draft Flows instantiated from pack templates\n(`flw_tpl_bi_refresh · flw_tpl_bi_metric_alert · flw_tpl_bi_subscription`) into the Project, owned by the person who\npressed *Create*, published in Flow Studio under Flow rights. Their nodes call back into bi-api's S2S tools\n(`bi.dashboard.describe · bi.alert.evaluate · dataset.describe`) **asserting the owner as the human principal**, so\nevery run is bounded by that person's rights, and an alert or subscription is delivered only into a Project thread.\nAn `action` node is refused for these templates (*422*): they read and post. Each alert evaluation is an\n`alert_evaluation` decision (value · threshold · streak)."],[4031,"NexBI is under construction. Built so far — the semantic layer and metrics, the governed query engine and\nthe NexChat data arm, dashboards, the Studio, automations as Flows, the organization scope and the filter bar — are\napproved. **Dashboards from NexChat** (S6b) is built and awaiting acceptance. **Insights** (trend · anomaly · comparison\n· source change) is a prototype screen on fixture rows; its statistical engine is not built. Where a chapter shows a\nprototype it says so."],[4168,"NexBI reads the header and **profiles** the columns — name, label, detected type (*period · string · integer ·\ndecimal · date · boolean*) and a suggested role. The upload is **staged**: nothing is published yet and nothing is\ncomputed over it. Check the types (a `2025-01` column should be *period*, an amount *decimal*), then **Publish** —\nthis creates **v1**, runs the quality checks and makes the version the current one. A staged upload you abandon is\ndiscarded."],[445,"NexBI reads the person's relation in the Project that owns the data and applies it at every checkpoint of a governed\nquery — tenancy, metric, dataset and classification, then the **row policy before aggregation** — so two people with\nthe same relation and different clearances see different totals of the same dashboard. Two capabilities sit above the\nrelations: `bi_publish` (share and publish dashboards — owners hold it) and `metric_steward` (certify metrics,\nacknowledge a revocation — owners hold it until a steward is named)."],[2270,"NexBI web"],[4212,"NexCare"],[6924,"NexCare"],[7018,"NexCare — service operations with a guardrail"],[4000,"NexCare — service operations: a website widget and Telegram, an assistant on verified knowledge, one Conversations desk with Join/Return, Care Studio."],[7259,"NexCare › Care Studio"],[4216,"NexCare is an **optional module** an Organization Owner installs from NexCore (Install a module).\nIt has two faces:"],[2988,"NexCare's conversation: the timeline (customer · agent · assistant · tool · system entries, each labelled by who said it and whether the customer saw it — internal entries are visi"],[2993,"NexCare's conversation: the timeline (customer · agent · assistant · tool · system entries, each labelled by who said it and whether the customer saw it — internal entries are visibly internal), the handoff summary card (what the assistant checked as a tick list, its reason codes, the sentiment labelled *model-inferred* — rule 85, a feature never a verdict), the composer (reply vs internal note as one segmented choice; the assistant's draft carries its provenance into the send) and the conversation Inspector (identity · facts · case · journey; one primary — *Create case*). Not a kit duplicate: `TurnCard` (DS-5xxx) is NexChat's own turn; a care timeline has two parties and a tool lane."],[23,"NexChat"],[4309,"NexChat"],[7176,"NexChat"],[7182,"NexChat"],[7336,"NexChat"],[3992,"NexChat — chats, Projects, Auto and the Resolver, agents, skills, flows, knowledge, data analysis."],[7340,"NexChat (also NexSpin, planned)"],[7344,"NexChat → Agent Studio"],[7356,"NexChat → Flow Studio"],[7348,"NexChat → Skill Studio; Packs"],[3997,"NexChat also carries the suite's voice and hands: Speak to Nexi,\nAct from anywhere, Search the web and research a question."],[7432,"NexChat composer"],[6857,"NexChat does not search the graph; it asks graph-api to **resolve** a question into an **evidence bundle** — under\nthe asker's identity, with the question passed *by reference* (a `nexus://chat/message/…` URI graph-api reads under\nthe same rights), never as text. The ladder the *How this was found* drawer shows is the algorithm:"],[3930,"NexChat is open: from the App Launcher (the **◉ Nexi** mark, top left of any Nexi app) choose **Chat**, or open\n`/chat` on your Nexi host."],[5301,"NexChat needs an organization around it: people, roles, a Project, a Blueprint that says what is allowed. This\nchapter is the very first ten minutes of a company on Nexi. Olena, who will own the organization, creates her\naccount and **Northwind Traders**; then she invites Taras as a **Builder**, and we follow Taras from the e-mail to the\nroster. Along the way you see what Nexi creates for you without asking, and what it deliberately leaves for later."],[5579,"NexChat noticed at once: the Composer's model catalogue for Northwind now lists &#x2A;*Team Qwen (local)** as\n*allowed · local · tier 2 · chat*. Nothing was restarted; the catalogue is the registry read as this\norganization."],[4723,"NexChat opens a chat inside the Project with a banner at the top — *Testing · Trip planner v4 (Draft) — Exit\ntest&#x2A; — and the agent already attached to the composer as the chip **@ Trip planner**. The sidebar lists it as\n*Test · Trip planner* under the Project. This test chat behaves exactly like a real one, with the draft version\nyou just saved; nobody else sees the draft. Under every answer a &#x2A;*Why this answer?** link shows which model was\nused,