wn placeholder · the mic · ↑ (send) / Stop while running; the panel toggle w"],[29,"NexCore"],[5215,"NexCore"],[7174,"NexCore"],[7250,"NexCore"],[7373,"NexCore"],[3996,"NexCore — people, groups, projects, capabilities, models, connections, access, audit — and installing a module."],[7560,"NexCore — the application where an organization governs who can see, use, publish and connect what. &#x2A;Core governs.*"],[7369,"NexCore (health, scope, owner)"],[7353,"NexCore (review, enable, ceiling)"],[7365,"NexCore (tier, classification, who)"],[7352,"NexCore → Capabilities; imported from OpenAPI in NexChat"],[7368,"NexCore → Connections"],[7364,"NexCore → Models"],[7337,"NexCore → Projects"],[7345,"NexCore governance (block / approve)"],[5218,"NexCore is where an organization is set up and governed: who is in it, what they may do, which models and systems\nthe agents may reach, and what happened. Every chapter is one task, step by step, on one running example — a\ncompany called **Northwind Traders** that Olena creates on day one."],[5324,"NexCore opens on the **Overview** of Northwind Traders. Three things to notice on the first visit:"],[2264,"NexCore web"],[5597,"NexForge"],[6928,"NexForge"],[7041,"NexForge — a scene, not a drawing"],[7774,"NexForge — dictation vs command on the same rails."],[4001,"NexForge — think, sketch, model: scenes projected as board, diagram, 3D and presentation; edit by hand, by sentence or by voice; the AI proposes, you apply."],[7428,"NexForge (a person; the Scene Agent proposes)"],[5601,"NexForge is an **optional module** an Organization Owner installs from NexCore (Install a module).\nIts object is a **Scene** — not a drawing. A scene is a structured set of objects, relations, layers, cameras and a\ncolour key, which NexForge **projects** four ways: **Board** (free canvas), **Diagram** (layered C4-style layout),\n**3D** (the same objects as solids with a real camera) and **Present** (steps over the cameras). Switching the view\nchanges nothing in the scene."],[7665,"NexForge's object: objects, relations, layers, cameras and a colour key — not a drawing — projected as Board, Diagram, 3D and Present."],[44,"NexGraph"],[5661,"NexGraph"],[3995,"NexGraph — sources, the pipeline, Graph Studio, evidence, claims and their review, vocabulary — and how NexChat answers from the knowledge graph."],[7380,"NexGraph → Sources (upload, server folder, Google Drive)"],[1826,"NexGraph adds four processes and two small models. They run on the laptop now. The Compose\nfile and the Helm chart are prepared for them — the PostgreSQL image they need is selectable through\n`POSTGRES_IMAGE` (`nexus/postgres`: PostgreSQL 16 with **Apache AGE** and **pgvector**, built from\n`deploy/docker/postgres/Dockerfile`; the stock `postgres:16` stays the default until the family ships), the chart\ncreates the database roles, and chat-api's settings already point at `graph-api` — but the process definitions\nthemselves arrive in a coming release. Plan capacity for them now."],[118,"NexGraph draws the *administering is not reading* rule more visibly than any other application, because an\nOrganization Admin has legitimate work there — bindings, grants, run health — without any right to the knowledge\nitself."],[6843,"NexGraph has no rights of its own. What you see is your **Project relation** — owner, editor, viewer, agent member,\nfetched from NexChat's Projects — intersected with the scope you chose. Three consequences:"],[391,"NexGraph holds no rights of its own: it asks for the person's relation in the Project that owns the knowledge and\nturns it into the action table below. Two rules from the rest of the platform hold here word for word. *Administering\nis not reading*: an Organization Owner or Admin without a relation sees bindings, grants and run health as ids,\nkinds, states and counts — never a document name, a knowledge count or a page. And *a model never decides*: a\nclaim becomes *verified* or *falsified* through one door only, an oracle or a human curator."],[5669,"NexGraph is where a Project's documents become **knowledge you can check**. You hand it a source — a file, a folder on\nan approved server, a Google Drive folder — and a pipeline turns every page into fragments, mentions, entities and\nnumeric claims, keeps the exact span each of them came from, and lets a deterministic check or a person decide what is\ntrue. NexChat then answers questions from that graph and shows you which sources it used and how it found them."],[2267,"NexGraph web"],[2329,"NexGraph's pipeline needs three things a chat does not: a parser for documents, a detector for mentions, and an\nembedding model; an answer from the knowledge graph also wants a reranker. All of them run on the laptop, none\nleaves it, and each is optional — the stack detects what is installed and writes the choice into the worker's\n`.env` (`SPECIALISTS_DRIVER`, `EMBEDDER_DRIVER`) on every start."],[6675,"Nexi — formerly NEXUS; the applications keep their names — is a suite of separate applications that share one shell,\none identity and one policy. The pictures on this page\nare not drawings: they are **views of a single architecture model** kept next to the documentation. When the model\nchanges, every view changes with it. Click an element to read its description; double-click a layer to drill in."],[7270,"Nexi (the platform formerly named NEXUS) is not one application. It is a **suite**: several applications with one shell, one sign-in and one set of\nagents, standing on **one governed runtime** — and a set of **modules**, applications an organization turns on from\nNexCore when it needs them (NexMap, NexCare, NexForge). The map below is the whole thing, top to bottom. Click an item to read\nwhat it is; the arrow takes you to the page that explains it."],[7263,"Nexi decomposed on one page — the applications, what each one contains, the runtimes they all share and the state underneath — with the map you can click through."],[253,"Nexi distinguishes *you may not* from *there is nothing here*, and its screens say which."],[137,"Nexi does not know who is calling — authenticate."],[4411,"Nexi drafts a *Role* line from your sentence and five *Rules* that every drafted agent starts with:"],[4657,"Nexi gives you the shape — a heading, a *Goal* from your text, a numbered **Procedure** and an **Output\nformat** — but the procedure it drafts is a generic analysis skeleton. Replace it with the real method. For the\nchecklist:"],[6663,"Nexi in one picture"],[2360,"Nexi is **built once, by the project's CI, and installed from a registry** — no target builds its own images. Each\nrelease consists of:"],[1767,"Nexi is built to be deployed **once, the same way, everywhere**. One set of signed container images, one Helm\nchart, one Compose file and one environment contract cover every target — your laptop, a single server, an on-prem\ncluster, a managed cloud cluster. What differs between them is *only* configuration: where the database lives,\nwho holds the secrets, how the public edge terminates TLS. Agents, Skills, Flows, policies and connections you\nbuild on one target run unchanged on the next."],[6676,"Nexi is not one big application. Each product owns its own screens and its own API; the shared shell gives them\none launcher, one header, one workspace context and one design language. Planned applications are drawn with a\ndashed border; **modules** — applications an organization enables from Blueprints & Packs — with a dotted one; the\ngovernance application carries the accent."],[5306,"Nexi itself does not hold your password. **Create account** hands you to the organization's identity provider\n— the registration form below is that provider's, in Nexi clothing."],[678,"Nexi knows the resource exists and you may not do this to it."],[1953,"Nexi needs"],[714,"Nexi never takes a password over the API. You sign in **once, in NexCore**, and everything else derives from that\nsession — in the browser, in the playground on these pages, in a script."],[2322,"Nexi reaches every model through the Synapse Model Gateway; the laptop offers two ways to feed it."],[58,"Nexi refuses in four different voices, and each one tells you something different:"],[2406,"Nexi separates *who bootstraps the system* from *what the system stores for its users*. Getting the tiers right is\nmost of the security work of a deployment."],[5370,"Nexi ships six applications every organization has — Home, NexChat, VibeBan, NexBI, NexGraph, NexCore — and a\ngrowing set of **modules**: applications an organization turns on when it needs them. Today there are three:\n**NexMap** (where things are), **NexCare** (service operations with a website widget) and **NexForge** (a creative\nstudio of scenes). A module is a **pack** like any other — agents, skills, flows, a Blueprint layer — whose Blueprint\nlayer declares `modules.enabled`. Installing the pack is the whole act: the module's API starts answering, the tile\nappears in every App Launcher, and the module's own guide applies. This chapter installs all three."],[222,"Nexi tells four kinds of actor apart, and several checks below depend on which one is asking."],[6110,"NexMap"],[6920,"NexMap"],[7070,"NexMap — where things are, honestly"],[3999,"NexMap — where things are: hexagons and objects, honest time and position, saved views, zones, uploads."],[6953,"NexMap · NexCare · NexForge — each module inside."],[7420,"NexMap (a person)"],[6114,"NexMap is an **optional module** — an Organization Owner installs it from NexCore (Install a module)\nand a **Map** tile appears in every App Launcher. The map is the page: no dashboard around it, an *Ask / go to* pill as\nthe second focus, a time strip along the bottom, and a thin rail with **Map · Views · Zones · Sources**."],[2276,"NexMap web · NexCare web · NexForge web (modules)"],[1860,"NexMap, NexCare and NexForge are **profiles**: `deploy/contract.yaml` lists their APIs under `profile: map | care |\nforge`; Compose starts `migrate-<module>` and `<module>-api` only with the profile; the chart has `map.enabled`,\n`care.enabled` and `forge.enabled`, all off, with a NetworkPolicy that lets a module API reach postgres, core-api and\nchat-api and nothing else. Installing the pack in NexCore does not start a process — the operator turns the profile\non, then the Owner installs the pack; the module's web app shows *not enabled* in between. The laptop stack runs all\nthree."],[4002,"NexSpin is a planned application; its guide appears when it does."],[7261,"Next in this series: **why the ontology matters** — how Nexi describes every model, tool and technology it uses,\nand what it can automate because it does."],[2250,"Next rung: AWS — the same chart with RDS, Secrets Manager and an ALB around it. Releases, mirroring, backups and rotation for every cluster: Operations."],[2348,"Next rung: Docker Compose — the same processes as signed containers, one `.env`, one public port. What the processes are and why they are separated: How Nexi is built."],[2153,"Next rung: Kubernetes — the same images from the Helm chart, with migrations as Jobs, a deny-all network and the sandbox as isolated Jobs. Day-2 topics for this rung: Operations."],[7178,"NexTasks"],[7362,"NexTasks"],[6198,"NexTasks · VibeBan"],[7361,"NexTasks; policy on who decides"],[3612,"Nine layers, each a token: raised 1 · sticky 10 · dock 20 · drawer 30 · popover 40 · menu 50 · dialog 60 · toast 70 · skip-link 100 (`--nexus-z-*`); a floating surface names its layer and never a number. Three shadows: `sm` (a hovered row or dragged block) · `md` (a menu, a picker, a popover) · `lg` (a dialog, the launcher) — the literal `0 18px 50px …` that twelve rules carry today becomes `md`."],[744,"No `nexus_session` cookie reached NexCore — you are signed in on another host name, or in another browser."],[5008,"No capability in the Project scores high enough — so Auto hands the message to the **Resolver Flow**, and its\nanswer is a plan, not a guess: **Nexi · Resolver · Plan · 3 steps**, the summary *Each morning, flag the mailbox\nmessages that need you — nothing is sent or deleted*, then the steps, each with a **rights chip** — *you can* ·\n*needs a Project owner* · *not possible* — and a dependency (*after step 1*): **Connect your mailbox** · **Ask to\nallow mail search** · **Triage the mail*&#x2A;. Buttons: **✓ Accept** · **Change** · **Not now** · **Details**, and the\nfootnote &#x2A;Nothing runs, is created or requested before you accept.* Route line: **Auto → Resolver · Flow Runtime**."],[5581,"No endpoint this time; an **API key** field instead, and the hint under it: &#x2A;Stored in the credential vault;\nCore keeps the reference only and clears this field on Add.* The key goes to the Credential Broker, the\nregistration keeps a reference, and neither Core, NexChat nor any agent ever reads the key back — the\nregistration list shows only `has_credential: true`. The **Classification ceiling** carries a second hint:\n&#x2A;Cloud models are capped at Confidential by Nexi Base (Blueprint, tighten-only)* — the ceiling you read in\nthe Blueprint matrix, applied at the moment it matters. She cancels."],[741,"No header, malformed header (`Bearer` missing), or the token is older than five minutes."],[2506,"No image contains a shell you can reach from the product: there is no exec path from a chat to a container."],[4359,"No microphone needed — everything here works typed; spoken is the same path (Speak to Nexi)."],[2290,"no port"],[3862,"No raw colour, radius, shadow or font outside `packages/ui/src/tokens.css`. A screen that needs a new value proposes a token. Light and Graphite are one token contract; a component that hard-codes a colour breaks the Graphite audit."],[6951,"No remote marketplace, no auto-update, no unsigned import."],[108,"No screen — the refusal never reaches a person's screen because an agent cannot open one. Starting or completing an\niteration, setting a milestone's status, verifying an acceptance criterion, deciding an approval, sharing or archiving a\nproject, importing references and binding an automation answer `403 AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN` to any agent or service\nprincipal, before OpenFGA is even asked. A move to *Done* with unverified criteria answers `422 ACCEPTANCE_OPEN`\nunless a person supplies an override reason."],[117,"No screen: **Publish**, **Certify**, **New automation** and **Stop serving** are absent for a viewer, and the API\nanswers `403 PEP_DENIED` (`dashboard.publish`, `metric.certify`, `automation.create`, `dataset.revoke_ack`). Publishing\nand certification are also **human-only** — a service or agent principal receives `403 AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN`. A dashboard\nblock that carries a spec copy instead of a reference is refused with `422 SPEC_COPY_REJECTED` regardless of rights."],[191,"No valid session or token reached the server."],[675,"No valid session, or the token in the field is not one the portal can refresh."],[4823,"Node"],[1047,"Node attempts in order (timeline / debugging). 1.29.0 (hotfix 2026-09-19) — each node's newest completed row carries `output` (the payload `output_ref` points to), redacted per `policy.sensitive_outputs` for non-owners like `FlowRun.outputs`; readable by whoever may read the run (Project READ, classification ≤ clearance)."],[1932,"none (source)"],[4957,"None declared"],[4958,"None declared"],[2398,"none for `web`, `chat-api`, `tasks-api` at ≥2 replicas; brief for `core-api` (one replica)"],[6645,"none; propensity 1.0"],[5480,"Northwind Traders has three people now. This chapter gives them somewhere to work together: a **Project** —\nNexi's unit of shared context, membership and policy. You will create it where Projects are created (NexChat),\nfind it a second later where Projects are governed (NexCore), read what Core knows about it, and give Taras and\nKate a **relation** in it. Along the way you will see the rule that makes Projects the boundary they are: &#x2A;*a person\nwho holds no relation in a Project does not see that it exists.**"],[2450,"Not a routine rotation: everything sealed under the key must be re-sealed. Plan it as a maintenance with a backup; treat compromise of this key as a re-onboarding of every stored credential"],[960,"Not allowed — there is no delete of an artifact; the only exits are `archive` and `restore`"],[751,"Not an authentication problem: see roles and relations."],[5541,"Not an empty table — a statement: &#x2A;*Your access does not allow this. Executions are visible to organization\nadministrators only. Project owners review their runs from the thread or flow run.** The list was requested\nand refused by the server; the screen repeats the refusal and does not pretend the organization is idle."],[28,"Not found"],[7751,"Not kept"],[4954,"Not required"],[5800,"Not yet available; the card is disabled."],[143,"Not yours, or nowhere — deliberately the same answer."],[1990,"Note"],[952,"Note artifact version"],[5110,"Note how it names the parameters it honours (`length`, `audience`), gives sizes (\"3–8 short bullets\") and states its\none hard rule first: &#x2A;Work only from the given material; never add facts, numbers or names that are not in it.*"],[2059,"Notes"],[2363,"Notes"],[7455,"Notes"],[1824,"nothing"],[4810,"Nothing else. The drafted Flow uses the Project's general agent; you do not need the Trip planner for this chapter."],[4697,"Nothing else. The example needs no connected systems — that comes with the Tools chapter."],[5372,"Nothing else. The three packs ship with the platform and are listed as **Available** until you install them."],[5841,"Nothing is deleted by **Revoke**: the binding stops syncing and running, the documents and everything derived from\nthem stay with a *revoked source* mark on their provenance."],[4667,"Nothing is published. Instead the **Evaluations** tab opens: &#x2A;How this skill is judged before it may teach an\nagent. A person must read and approve the exact current version; any edit asks for a new review.* **Human\nreview** is *Review pending*; **Evaluation suite** is *None yet* — automatic evaluations arrive with packaged\nskills. Below: **Review notes**, **Request changes** and **Approve this version**."],[3544,"Nothing is written into a component. Every label, hint, empty state and error is a key in the shared locale files,\npresent in **English and Ukrainian** at the same time — a string that exists in one language only does not ship. The\nworkshop renders every story in both, so a label that overflows in Ukrainian is caught before a screen is built."],[4765,"Nothing on the card is a summary written by the agent. What the loop produced is above, in the Goal panel and the\nagent step; the card only carries the request and its provenance."],[1951,"Nothing on this page is AWS-specific *inside* Nexi. The chart from the Kubernetes rung\nis installed unchanged; what AWS provides is the ground it stands on — the cluster, the database, the secret store,\nthe public edge, the registry. This page maps each of those onto a managed AWS service and gives you the values to\nwrite."],[5303,"Nothing. This chapter starts before you have an account. You need two e-mail addresses you can read — one for\nthe owner, one for the invitee — or a colleague who follows the second half with you."],[4653,"Notice what is **not** here: no model to choose, no tools to bind, no files to attach. A skill is portable text;\nthe agent that applies it brings everything else and stays within its own permissions."],[4276,"Nova answers: &#x2A;*I'm handing this over to a person on our team so you get a proper answer. They'll see this\nconversation and continue from here.** Pricing is a blocked topic in the *External* profiles; the guardrail port\nstopped the turn at the input stage and turned it into a handover. The team sees a *guardrail note* in the timeline\nsaying which rule fired; the customer sees a polite handover, never a refusal wall and never a guess."],[4270,"Nova says shipment details are shared only with the account holder and offers a 6-digit code; the inline step\n&#x2A;*Confirm it's you — Enter the e-mail on your order. We'll send a 6-digit code.** with an e-mail field, **Send\ncode** and **Not now**. The guardrail profile switched from *External · public* to *External · verified customer*\nonly after the code — the assistant cannot mark anyone verified; the code check is deterministic."],[4876,"Now **Run flow** is available too. Choose it."],[7098,"Now = each object at its last observed position, nothing extrapolated; History = as it was; Playback interpolates moving objects and says so"],[4848,"Now click the **Goal chip** in the toolbar."],[5634,"Now click the **title field** first, then press the mic and speak."],[4588,"Now the **Knowledge** tab."],[6073,"Now the report. Its **Shipments**, **On time** and **Late** columns add up — *7 210 + 5 180 + 3 640 + 2 390 = 18\n420* — so those fifteen claims, totals included, are **Verified**. The **On-time rate** column has a **Total** row\ntoo, &#x2A;94.1 %*, but a percentage in a Total row is a *ratio*, not a sum: *96.0 + 89.0 + 95.1 + 97.9 = 378.0 ≠\n94.1*. The arithmetic oracle, which knows nothing about ratios, falsifies the total **and its four components**.\nFive **Falsified** verdicts — *Total · On-time rate*, *Rotterdam*, *Warsaw*, *Lyon* and *Kyiv · On-time rate*."],[2161,"Object"],[6443,"Object"],[6755,"Object"],[6967,"Object"],[7453,"Object"],[7144,"Often imported: an OpenAPI description becomes Tools automatically."],[4301,"Oksana's message — the container released, a trucker booked for 09:00 — appears under her name; the inbox row\nupdates its last activity. The customer sees it in the widget at once."],[5407,"Olena adds `northwind.example` to the organization's domains."],[5441,"Olena clicks her name at the bottom of the sidebar."],[5531,"Olena clicks the first correlation id."],[5437,"Olena does exactly that in this chapter: she signs in from a second browser, sees both rows, revokes the other,\nand watches that browser be turned away on its next click with a sentence that says why. Then she signs out\nherself, asks for a password reset link from the sign-in card, and reads the four audit lines those actions left."],[5493,"Olena grants two relations: **Taras · Editor** — he will build the catalogue's Agents and Flows — and **Kate ·\nViewer** — she needs to read what comes out, not change it."],[5580,"Olena opens **Add model** again and picks **Anthropic · Cloud** — to look, not to submit."],[5487,"Olena opens **Autumn catalogue**."],[5275,"Olena opens **Blueprints & Packs**."],[5265,"Olena opens **Capabilities**."],[5270,"Olena opens **General**."],[5536,"Olena opens **Governance › Audit**."],[5573,"Olena opens **Models**."],[5547,"Olena opens **Overview**."],[5411,"Olena opens **People**."],[5526,"Olena opens **Runtime › Executions** before anyone has used NexChat."],[5273,"Olena opens **Tools**."],[5576,"Olena presses **Add model**."],[5352,"Olena reloads **People**: *2 active · 0 invited*; the invitation reads **Accepted**; the roster has **Taras\nBondar · Builder · Active**. Click his row."],[5586,"Olena selects &#x2A;*Team Qwen (local)** and presses **Delete model**; a confirmation asks once. The row is gone,\nthe header is back to *6 configured*, and NexChat's catalogue no longer offers it — with the same immediacy as\nit appeared. Then she opens **Audit**."],[5458,"Olena signs in again and opens **Governance › Audit**."],[5484,"Olena switches to NexChat and presses **+ New project** in the sidebar."],[5543,"Olena, back in **Audit**, switches **All decisions** to **Deny**."],[2304,"Ollama `:11434` · `llama-server --reranking :8081`"],[6637,"on (provisional, base pack)"],[4102,"On **Dashboards**, press **New dashboard**."],[6252,"On a board with eight open bugs and one critical, **Current priorities** lists the P0 and P1 items with their\nstage — the same list the on-call person would want first. Health is *On track* because nothing is blocked or\noverdue; a P0 blocked for more than three days would turn it *At risk*."],[2244,"On a connected machine: `deploy/scripts/mirror.sh --release RELEASE.json --to registry.example.internal/nexus`\ncopies the eight images and the chart by digest and verifies their signatures\n(Operations → Releases)."],[4863,"On a draft, **Run flow** is grey and **Run with test data** is available. A draft cannot run for real; it can\nalways be tested."],[4144,"On a metric that should no longer be used, press **Deprecate**."],[5860,"On a Project question the list looks the same with **Project** instead of *Base knowledge*, and the entries are\npassages of your documents, **claims** with their status badge — **VERIFIED**, *contested*, *proposed* — and\nentities with **Open in Studio**. A **claim** source is the graph vouching for a number: a verified rate from the\nagreement's table arrives with the badge the oracle gave it."],[6350,"On an item you edit, open **Acceptance** and press **Accept** on a criterion."],[6295,"On an iterations project — rank the backlog, plan Sprint 1 and Sprint 2 in the planning pane, start a sprint, read points and scope change, complete a sprint with an explicit disposition for every unfinished item, and attach items to milestones. About twenty minutes."],[6316,"On an iterations project the board has an iteration selector — **Sprint 1 · Active** — and shows only that sprint's\nitems across the stages. ACME-4 in *Backlog* is planned into the sprint but not yet started; the ⏱ **1** on its card\nis a *blocked by* count (ACME-3 blocks it). Cards show **Me**, the estimate in **pts** and the due date."],[5447,"On another browser — Safari, say — Olena signs in again with the same account and opens Core. Back on the\nfirst, she opens **Sessions** and refreshes."],[2509,"On Compose: only `web` and the loopback admin ports are published; `sandbox-manager` is the only container with the\nDocker socket, and the sandbox containers it starts have no network."],[2508,"On Kubernetes: default-deny NetworkPolicies with exactly the contract's edges; `nexus-sandbox` under Pod Security\n*restricted* with deny-all and a ResourceQuota; the manager's Role can create Jobs and read logs, never read\nSecrets or exec."],[693,"On the **fixture (E2E) stack** the Tasks API answers `401 UNAUTHENTICATED` to every person, token or not: that\nstack does not start the key feed tasks-api needs to verify a human's assertion (a known platform gap, being fixed\nby the NexTasks team). Try the Tasks API against the development stack or a real deployment."],[3906,"On the **Welcome to Nexi** page keep **Create an organization** selected and press **Continue**."],[5384,"On the Packs tab a module's card offers **Remove**."],[1530,"On-demand probe (owner of a user connection or administrator). OAuth connections are probed through the token (refresh if due) before any endpoint."],[3916,"Once you are signed in, Get session context in the Platform\nAPI tells you who Nexi thinks you are — try it from the reference with your own session\n(how to authenticate). Creating an account and an organization is the identity\nprovider's job and is not part of the published API; the organization and membership endpoints are documented\nwhen their contract is published."],[3225,"one `h1` per page; the back link is labelled"],[3764,"One anatomy for everything that floats over the page — a menu, a popover, the composer picker, a select's list: radius 12 · padding 6 · 1 px border · --nexus-shadow-md · items 32 p"],[3768,"One anatomy for everything that floats over the page — a menu, a popover, the composer picker, a select's list: radius 12 · padding 6 · 1 px border · `--nexus-shadow-md` · items 32 px with 8 px inset and radius 8 at 13 px · separators 1 px with 4 px around · captions 12 px secondary; the picker adds a search row and sections, the popover glass. It names its layer (DS-1031), opens from its trigger's corner, closes on Escape and outside click, and returns focus. A select has three sizes — form 34 · toolbar 32 · quiet 26 — and its option hint is a prop, never hidden from outside."],[1580,"One ApprovalRequest (the card's source of truth; the browser polls it every 2 s while pending). PepAction=read: a human in `deciders.user_ids` or the `requested_by.on_behalf_of` human, with clearance ≥ the record's classification — otherwise 404, never 403 (no existence leak); other Project members see the card through chat-api's projection (tasks-api owns no Project membership). Service callers (core-api verifying an approval before it executes) read with their service token and see the un-redacted digest, never the raw arguments — those exist nowhere."],[1356,"One binding with states, lags, grant and allowed_actions."],[6547,"One call to the `classifier` role via Synapse (prompt `intent_execute.md`) returns a closed-vocabulary structure: intent with per-option probabilities, domain, inputs present, side effects asked, and a `validation.coerced[]` list of anything the model got outside the vocabulary."],[4195,"One card per dashboard: the title, *Published · v1*, the **decision statement** it supports (*Which carrier\ncontracts to renegotiate to bring late deliveries under control*), live headline numbers, *6 blocks · 2 timelines*,\nwhen and by whom. The filter row switches between published and drafts; **New dashboard** starts the\nStudio."],[6344,"One card per epic with its status line straight from the documentation (*Done — UAT-0…UAT-4 verified 2026-09-02*)\nand six figures: stories, requirements, acceptance criteria, tests, decisions, and two **coverage** ratios —\n**Requirements → AC** (how many requirements have at least one acceptance criterion) and **AC → Tests** (how many\ncriteria have at least one test). Red is below the threshold. One epic reads 56 % / 100 %: every criterion has a\ntest, about half the requirements have a criterion. These figures are the same for everyone; they do not depend on\nyour rights."],[3988,"One chapter per task, for each Nexi application, with the real screens."],[2160,"One chart, one `values.yaml` whose defaults *are* the environment contract, and one small values file per kind of\ncluster. The chart installs exactly the same processes Compose starts, with three things Kubernetes does better:\nmigrations become Jobs the Deployments wait for, the network becomes default-deny with only the contract's edges\nopen, and the sandbox becomes Jobs in their own locked-down namespace."],[6239,"One column per stage with its count. The filter row: **Board / List**, **Stage**, **Assignee**, **Type**,\n**Priority**, **Blocked only** and a search box; the **Live** dot says the board follows server events (it says\n*Polling* when the stream is down and the page falls back to refreshing). *Done* is collapsed to a strip with\nits count — expand it with the chevron."],[2252,"One command starts everything with hot reload — Postgres, Keycloak and a mail catcher in Docker; the APIs, the web apps and the knowledge pipeline as host processes."],[2092,"One command, one file. `compose-init.sh` copies the annotated example to `deploy/compose/.env`, generates every\nbootstrap secret — database passwords, the two master keys, the Keycloak client secrets, the session signing key —\nand sets the file to mode 600. The file is the **bootstrap tier** of secrets and lives only on this machine. It is\nidempotent: an existing `.env` is never overwritten unless you pass `--force`, which rotates every key."],[3495,"One component renders every executor — agent · knowledge · data · search · research · Flow · resolver · goal — from one contract."],[3500,"One component renders every executor — agent · knowledge · data · search · research · Flow · resolver · goal — from one contract. The header line is &#x2A;‹title› · ‹who/what› · ‹elapsed or when›*, the title an executor's label and never an id. A plain answer is prose in the thread with no frame; work longer than the threshold shows **one** folded progress line that unfolds into the staged view and becomes the receipt with the result beneath it; a turn has at most one progress indicator. The eight states are closed, one copy class and one visual each; an unknown state renders `failed`, never blank. `waiting_on_you` carries the decision inline in the same idiom for every executor. Typography and borders only; no second colour. S8: the card has a `lead` slot — what it already holds about the ask, rendered first in every state, before the progress line and any wait; the goal fills it with its Situation strip (DS-5002), no other executor uses it yet."],[2219,"one credential per process, presented on service-to-service calls"],[845,"One dataset head."],[1245,"One DatasetVersion with rows and cell-level provenance."],[7044,"One edit language"],[1504,"One evaluation run (other tenants' runs are 404)"],[1263,"One EvidenceSpan with precision and page labels."],[3639,"One family (`--nexus-font`: Inter, system fallback), three weights (400 · 500 · 600), seven sizes with one line-height each (`--nexus-text-xs … -3xl` = 11 · 12 · 13 · 14 · 16 · 20 · 26): `md` 13 is the workbench body, `lg` 14 the reading body, `2xl` 20 the page title, `xl` 16 the Inspector head and the composer, `sm` 12 chips · labels · hints, `xs` 11 the eyebrow and the counter. No half pixels, nothing under 11, no italic for emphasis, no all-caps except the section title and the eyebrow."],[3637,"One family, three weights, seven sizes with one line-height each."],[3935,"One field and one sentence: &#x2A;Nexi will create a Project workspace for chats, files and shared AI context.*\nThe accent dots only colour the dot next to the name in the sidebar."],[5791,"One file per upload, into the Project's upload box."],[1531,"One folder of a connection as the signed-in person sees it (1b, the folder picker) — names and kinds, folders first, trashed items left out; never bytes, never a credential. The person's own `user` connection, or a Shared one available to 