 changed file is a new version; the earlier one stays, marked superseded."],[7680,"One pinned set of bytes with its SHA-256; the identity of a document. A changed file is a new version, the old one stays."],[6765,"One pinned set of bytes with its SHA-256. The identity of a document. A changed file is a *new* version; the earlier one stays, marked superseded."],[3503,"one polite live region per thread announces a state change once; the progress line is `role=progressbar` with `aria-valuetext` = the copy (—: it has no accessible name yet, (c)); every inline decision is reachable by Tab from the composer and runs on Enter; Esc does nothing destructive"],[1744,"One project with its stage/type refs, members (owner/editor/viewer see them) and `allowed_actions` for this reader. Hidden → 404."],[1672,"One reference: id, title, status, epic, origin (path/sha/last sync), version, counts. Follow `target_uri`/`origin` to read the source under your own PEP."],[4166,"One row per dataset: **Version** (the current one), **Quality** (*OK · warnings · failed · no data* — computed at\npublish), **Source** (*CSV / XLSX upload · NexGraph · analysis · flow*), **Semantic layer** (*Modelled* when the\ndataset is an entity of the Project's semantic model), **Certification** (*Certified* = published and quality OK),\n**Updated**. The line above reads *1 datasets · 1 certified*."],[5451,"One row remains — **Chrome · macOS · this device** — and **Revoke other sessions** is disabled again: there\nis nothing else to revoke. The Safari row is gone from the list because core-api marked that session revoked;\nthe browser holding its cookie does not know yet."],[3,"One rule to remember"],[1296,"One run with stages, coverage and engine logs (closed codes, never document text)."],[5660,"One scene, four views, a saved version, and the shape of the editor: a header line, the element as the menu, the\nInspector as a door. Next: Edit by hand and by words."],[6485,"One sentence"],[7595,"One sentence"],[7616,"One sentence"],[7639,"One sentence"],[7676,"One sentence"],[3621,"One shell transition (`--nexus-shell-motion`, 200 ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1)); a progress pulse of 600–900 ms on the Pulse strip and the run bar; `prefers-reduced-motion` turns both off."],[3866,"One shell transition (200 ms ease-out) and one progress pulse (600–900 ms); everything respects `prefers-reduced-motion`; nothing bounces, slides in from the edge or fades for decoration."],[3619,"One shell transition, one progress pulse, reduced motion honoured."],[3646,"One shell, one page frame, one way to go two levels deep, one right-hand panel."],[3657,"One shell, one page frame, one way to go two levels deep, one right-hand panel. A new application starts from `apps/_template` and inherits every row here without writing layout code."],[6620,"One step per pass under the Blueprint budget — 8 iterations · 360 s · 60 k tokens · 20 cost units · 3 drafts · 3 requests. Executes **connect** (a connection request raised for the asker in NexCore) and **request\\_tool** (a governed CapabilityRequest to a Project owner); every other kind is *skipped — Nexi cannot do this kind of step yet*. Waits up to 7 days on a person; the same request is not raised twice within 24 h."],[7264,"One suite, several applications, one runtime"],[3008,"One switch for the ladder: loading · empty · error · denied · notFound · offline · ready."],[3013,"One switch for the ladder: loading · empty · error · denied · notFound · offline · ready. Every screen reads through it."],[6287,"One table, filtered by kind: **Approvals** (a Flow or an agent asks you to allow something — deciding happens in\nNexChat or NexCore; VibeBan links you there), **Assignments**, **Mentions** (`@you` in a comment),\n**Reviews** (you are a reviewer of an item that reached *review*), **Due**, **Blocked** (an item of yours became\nblocked by another), **Agent results** (an agent finished a run on an item of yours), **Shared** (someone shared a\npersonal item with you). Unread rows carry a dot; the bell in the rail counts them."],[4712,"One text area, **Main instructions**: a *Role* line built from your sentence and five *Rules*. The rules are the\nsame for every drafted agent and are worth reading once — ground answers in the Project's sources and cite them;\nnever present a proposed claim as verified; stay within the classification; use only the tools bound to you;\nreturn structured findings. The note under the box says the important thing: &#x2A;Tools and skills are configured on\ntheir own tabs — not here.* Instructions are *how the agent thinks*; what it may *do* is decided elsewhere and\ncannot be talked into being."],[4410,"One text area, **Main instructions**. This is the agent's character and its rules — what it should do first, what it\nshould ask, how it should answer. What it is **not** is a place for permissions: the hint under the box says it\nplainly, &#x2A;Tools and skills are configured on their own tabs — not here.* Writing \"you may search the web\" in the\ninstructions gives the agent nothing; binding a tool does. Equally, writing \"never delete files\" is a good instruction\nbut not a guarantee — the guarantee comes from not binding a tool that deletes files."],[4814,"One text box, three example sentences you can try later (a weekly supplier price report, a contract review, a\nMonday digest), and a quiet **Start with an empty canvas** for the day you want to draw by hand. Notice the shape\nof the examples: *when* it runs, *who* does what, *what* comes out, and *who approves*. A good sentence for a Flow\nhas the same four parts."],[6134,"One text field: a place, an object name or identifier, or coordinates. Enter flies the map there. The last row of\nthe results is always &#x2A;*Ask NexChat: \"…\"** — the same words sent to NexChat with the map as context. Type\n*SHP\\_0163* and press Enter."],[5438,"One thing to know before you start: **passwords and second factors belong to the identity provider**, not to\nCore. Core keeps sessions and shows you the door to the provider; it never sees your password."],[1500,"One ToolInvocation of the caller's tenancy"],[1572,"One ToolInvocation of the caller's tenancy"],[3505,"One underline tab row — 36 px, 600 weight when active, a 2 px accent line, no fill, optional counts."],[3511,"One underline tab row — 36 px, 600 weight when active, a 2 px accent line, no fill, optional counts. `UrlTabs` keeps state in `?tab=`; `LocalTabs` in the parent (`layout=\"page\"` or the compact `inline` for an Inspector). `variant=\"surface\"` is the legacy pill."],[813,"One version (blocks as references)."],[849,"One version with columns, quality and cell provenance (rows via getDatasetVersionRows)."],[1392,"One-hop neighbours grouped by NeighbourKind (query: kinds=sources,claims,entities,checks; limit per kind ≤ 50). Every hop is PEP-checked; a hidden intermediate node drops the path and is counted in `truncated`."],[5792,"One-time"],[7163,"Only a very small core is fixed — the words needed to talk about truth at all: a **Source** (a message, a file, a\npage), a **Chunk** of it, a **Claim** made about the world, a **Hypothesis**, an **Assumption**, and the record of a\ncheck. Everything else — the entity types and relation names of *your* domain — is not designed up front. It\n**emerges**: agents propose candidate words while they work, people keep the ones that fit, and Nexi periodically\nconsolidates a versioned snapshot of \"how we currently name the world\". A Project's vocabulary is therefore the\nplatform's core, plus what a Blueprint seeds, plus what your own work adds."],[4431,"Only facts that passed the verify gate (an oracle check or a person). When you pick this, a second field **Domain** appears: *domain:\\<name> — only verified facts of that Domain graph*."],[5740,"Only the Project **owner** may change the policy; a change that would widen the audience is refused by the server.\nA completed Flow never certifies its content: a captured outcome is a *proposed* claim like any other and goes through\nReview. This screen is documented as a preview — its walk-through follows its release gate."],[2225,"only when `coreApi.vault.addr` points at an OpenBao/Vault (a read-only token)"],[2228,"only when images come from a private registry (also copied into `nexus-sandbox`)"],[7126,"Ontology — why Nexi names everything it uses"],[6368,"Ontology — why Nexi names everything it uses, and what it automates because of that."],[6739,"Ontology ended on a promise: a claim moves from *what was written* to *what a model thinks it means* to\n*what your organization treats as true* only through a gate, and a model can never open that gate itself. NexGraph is\nwhere that promise is kept — for whole documents, at scale, with a pipeline you can read step by step. This page\nexplains the model behind the screens the NexGraph guide walks through: what is stored where, who\nis allowed to write what, and how a question in NexChat comes back with evidence rather than confidence."],[6306,"Open **Acme Q4 delivery**."],[4112,"Open **Advisor**."],[4239,"Open **Assistant**."],[4074,"Open **Automations** in the rail."],[6308,"Open **Backlog**."],[6345,"Open **Board** and click a story — **NEXUS-11 · Epic 003**."],[6238,"Open **Board**."],[6315,"Open **Board**."],[4235,"Open **Care Studio**."],[4247,"Open **Channels**."],[4292,"Open **Conversations**."],[4194,"Open **Dashboards**."],[4165,"Open **Data** in the rail."],[6054,"Open **Decided 28**."],[4243,"Open **Guardrails**, then **Knowledge**."],[6286,"Open **Inbox** in the rail."],[6312,"Open **Iterations**."],[4306,"Open **Live**, then **Quality**, then **Cases**."],[4133,"Open **Metrics**."],[6319,"Open **Milestones**."],[6247,"Open **NEXUS Operations** → **Board**."],[6251,"Open **NEXUS Operations** → **Overview**, then **Activity**."],[6342,"Open **NEXUS Platform** → **References**."],[6235,"Open **NEXUS Platform** from the rail."],[6249,"Open **OPS-2**:"],[4245,"Open **Queues