057,"Signed in as a viewer with a row policy on *Region*, the same question yields fewer rows scanned — and a different\n*Highest* if the hidden region changes it."],[5420,"Signed in as the new member, **People** shows the roster but no **Requests** block."],[5439,"Signed in to Core as anyone — the chapter uses Olena, Owner of **Northwind Traders**."],[729,"Signed in to NexCore, open this address in the same browser (replace the host with yours):"],[34,"Signed out from elsewhere"],[7372,"signed outside; installed in NexCore → Blueprints & Packs"],[5971,"Silver (Lexical)"],[5974,"Silver (Subject, proposed)"],[5977,"Silver (Subject)"],[5983,"Silver + Gold"],[6472,"Since S5 the pattern remembers. A stage that produced a table calls `nexus.dataset(...)`; the engine registers it as a\n**Project dataset** with its layer, technique and Skill version. On the next question the planner sees those datasets\nin the profile and, where a kept dataset's technique already answers a stage, takes the **reuse** arm — an\n`analysis_reuse` decision with *reuse* and *recompute&#x2A; as its action space, shown in the thread as &#x2A;↺ reused from the\nrun of …*. **Recompute** is the initiator's alone (`POST /chat/flow-runs/{run_id}/recompute`; *409 RUN\\_ACTIVE* while\nthe run is going) and leaves the earlier results in place until it finishes. A dataset whose source file has a newer\nversion reads &#x2A;Stale — version of …*. The **Dataset Card** is the synthesis skill's last output: a document about the\ndata itself that a later run appends to, versioned like any artifact. The layers follow the platform's memory rule\n(Bronze the typed copy, Silver normalised, Gold a result) and every dataset carries where it came from; nothing here\nis a claim in the knowledge graph — findings → NexGraph claims is an open item."],[4652,"Six tabs — **Overview · Instructions · Input / Output · Examples · Evaluations · Versions** — and a header\nthat already tells the story of this chapter: **Draft**, version **v0.1.0**, **Review pending**, and instead of a\nPublish button a black **Review before publishing**. The one-line rule at the top of the tab is the definition\nyou should remember: &#x2A;A skill teaches a method. It carries instructions, input/output schemas, examples and an\nevaluation — never tools, a model, knowledge or permissions. The agent that applies it brings those.*"],[6511,"Skill"],[7347,"Skill"],[1190,"Skill detail (platform skills are visible to everyone in the tenant)"],[4328,"Skill Studio, tab by tab"],[5046,"Skill Studio, tab by tab"],[1178,"Skills"],[4380,"Skills"],[1188,"Skills for `/` picker — platform + project (+ installed once lands)"],[4683,"Skills, their versions, examples and the human-review record are resources of the\nChat API › Skills: Create skill draft,\nUpdate skill, Review skill and\nPublish skill — the last is refused without an approved review of the\ncurrent version. Try them from the reference with your own session\n(how to authenticate)."],[1874,"SLA clock, retention export to the Gold decision dataset, NexBI dataset publishing."],[7014,"Slices 1–6a are approved (semantic layer and metrics · governed query and the data arm · dashboards · Studio ·\nautomations as Flows · organization scope · filter bar). **Dashboards from NexChat** (S6b — the proposal card, *Add to\ndashboard*) is built and presented, not yet accepted. **Insights** — trend · anomaly · comparison · source change — is\na prototype screen over fixture rows; its statistical engine and the `insight.compute` path are not built. The\nrelease image set (compose · Helm) does not yet include bi-api or the NexBI web; the Deploy ladder\nsays where it runs today."],[6122,"Slices S1 (map · hexagons · objects · Inspector · zones) and S2 (saved views · sources · uploads) run on the live stack;\nS2 is presented and awaiting approval. Live position feeds, geofence Flows, raster imagery and the NexChat map seam\n(*Open in NexMap* from an answer) are designed and not yet built — the chapters say so where it matters."],[2050,"Smoke report archived with the release version"],[4899,"So far the **Trip planner** answers from what it knows. In this chapter it gets two hands: **Project search**, so it\ncan read the booking pages and last year's notes you pin to the Project, and **Create task**, so it can leave a\nNexTask for whoever books the cottage. On the way you learn the three ideas that make tools safe in Nexi:"],[4578,"So far the agent knew only what you typed. This chapter gives the Project something to *read*: a text file with\nthree accommodation offers for the autumn weekend. You will see where a Project keeps its knowledge (**Pinned\nsources** in the Context drawer), what an agent's **Knowledge** tab promises, and the one path that puts a document\ninto a Project today — a Flow whose input is a **file**. The Flow reads the offers with a small agent, writes them as\na **table in the Canvas**, and leaves the file behind as a source every later answer in the Project is grounded on."],[5066,"So there is no Tools tab, no Models tab and no Permissions tab here — on purpose. A skill is a portable piece of\nknow-how: you can export it, review it, and attach it to any agent, and it can never quietly widen what that agent\nis allowed to do. The agent's own Permissions and Models tabs remain the only place\nwhere reach is decided."],[1710,"Soft-delete (HUMAN editor/owner): disappears from every view and search, history kept, key never reused. Emits `nexus.tasks.item.deleted.v1`. 204."],[94,"Some screens do not refuse; they omit. **People** as a member has no *Requests* and no *Invitations* section — join\nrequests and invitations are administrators' business. (This build still draws an **Invite** button; the server\nrefuses it — a known gap.)"],[227,"Someone signed in through the organization's identity provider; a session in a browser."],[362,"Someone who watches runs and reads results — the relation scheduled and triggered runs are attributed to"],[7379,"Source · version"],[2784,"Source chip"],[3427,"Source chip"],[1327,"Sources"],[6766,"Sources → Documents (`v1`)"],[7075,"Sources and uploads"],[4427,"Sources only. Good for agents that must not lean on inferred facts."],[1348,"Sources registry rows with five states each. Administrators without a Project relation see binding ids, kinds, states and lags — no titles."],[7179,"Sources with pinned versions; the pipeline as a receipt; Graph Studio; the Evidence Workspace (claim → span → source); Review with the oracle-or-person gate; Vocabulary as *terms in use*"],[661,"Sources, pipeline runs, the graph, evidence, claim review, vocabulary, evidence bundles"],[7299,"Sources, Pipeline, Graph Studio, Evidence Workspace, Review, Vocabulary; Memory (preview)"],[5662,"Sources, the pipeline, Graph Studio, evidence, claims and their review, vocabulary — and how NexChat answers from the knowledge graph. One task per chapter, with the real screens."],[3631,"Spacing and density"],[3577,"Spacing and density — Ten steps; margins, paddings and gaps name a step, never a number."],[1264,"Spans, source versions, contributing sources and the deciding OracleRun of a claim — the Inspector's Evidence tab. Derived-conclusion rule: the caller must be allowed on ALL derived_from_source_refs unless an independently allowed source suffices; otherwise 404."],[2704,"Sparkline"],[3437,"Sparkline"],[5169,"Speak to Nexi"],[7671,"Speaking into a field: the words land there and no turn runs. A command speaks to the scene."],[7192,"Speech and vision are Gateway operations too"],[7254,"speech in and out through the asr and tts roles"],[7732,"Speed"],[7431,"Spoken clip · session file · shared frame"],[7758,"Spoken sentence"],[1590,"Sprints of an Iterations project — plan, start, complete with dispositions, cancel."],[4513,"Stage"],[5963,"Stage"],[6531,"Stage"],[6797,"Stage"],[844,"Stage a CSV/XLSX (≤ 64 MiB) and infer typed columns (T15). Returns an upload_ref that publishDatasetVersion consu