ts right; the active section in the URL. Never a tab row inside a tab panel."],[3820,"Tabs for the first level, a SideNav column for the second, the content to its right; the active section in the URL."],[4910,"Tag"],[2367,"Tags"],[4288,"Take one conversation from the assistant, answer the customer and give it back. The desk is one screen for every\nchannel — widget, Telegram, later e-mail — and one rule: **exactly one hand writes at a time**. The walk is in the\nSupplyChain Guru demo as **Oksana Bondar**, a service agent."],[7302,"Talk as a team, with agents in the room."],[1800,"Talks to"],[1829,"Talks to"],[1849,"Talks to"],[1863,"Talks to"],[6882,"Talks to"],[5170,"Tap the microphone, say what you want, pause — the end of speech is detected, the words become your message, the answer is spoken back. Turn voice answers off, or go hands-free with Talk. About ten minutes."],[5530,"Taras asked NexChat the same question from his side — `GET /chat/observability/traces` with his session — and\nwas answered **403 · RELATION\\_MISSING**. The list is for the organization's administrators; a member reads\ntheir own thread in NexChat."],[5349,"Taras has no account, so the link first takes him to **Create account** — the same page Olena saw in step 1,\nbut Nexi remembers where he was going (`next=/welcome?invite=…`). He registers with the invited address,\nverifies the e-mail, signs in."],[5351,"Taras lands in Nexi Chat — the default project **General** is his to use — and Core shows him Northwind Traders\ntoo, read-only where his role stops. If he opens the mail link again he is simply sent into the organization:\nthe token was spent when he joined."],[5584,"Taras, a Builder, opens **Models** — he sees &#x2A;*Team Qwen (local)** like everyone — and presses **Add model**."],[5279,"Taras, an Editor of *Autumn catalogue*, drafts an agent there in Studio — **Catalogue copywriter**, *writes\nproduct texts for the autumn catalogue from the supplier sheet*. Olena, the Owner, publishes it."],[5540,"Taras, signed in as himself, opens **Executions**."],[654,"Tasks API"],[4968,"Tasks are not wired in the review environment, so to *see* an approval we borrow the fixture the platform's own\nacceptance tests use: a **Suppliers API** connected through Synapse, in a Project **Supplier directory**, with a small\nagent **Supplier steward** whose only tool is `suppliers.delete`. Everything below is the same mechanism you will meet\nwith your own connected systems — a CRM, a booking system, a ticket queue."],[2490,"tasks-api"],[1852,"tasks-api, core-api"],[6702,"Team rooms and threads with contextual agents (`@agent` mentions)."],[6703,"Teams"],[6360,"Technical documentation"],[981,"Template → instance (built in, consumed by S9). Resolves `requires` against the Project's bindings (the effective Blueprint once lands), applies its policies and returns a draft WorkflowSpec 1.2 (template.is_template=false, `template.source_*` set) for Flow Studio. When `pattern_id` is given the template is the pattern's and `origin.pattern_uri` / `origin.pattern_version` are stamped. Unresolved requirements → `origin.open_questions[]` on the draft (P0 templates have none) or 422 `unresolved_binding` when `strict=true`. Idempotent per key. Never publishes or runs."],[1056,"Template → instance (built in, consumed by S9). Resolves `requires` against the Project's bindings (the effective Blueprint once lands), applies its policies and returns a draft WorkflowSpec 1.2 (template.is_template=false, `template.source_*` set) for Flow Studio. When `pattern_id` is given the template is the pattern's and `origin.pattern_uri` / `origin.pattern_version` are stamped. Unresolved requirements → `origin.open_questions[]` on the draft (P0 templates have none) or 422 `unresolved_binding` when `strict=true`. Idempotent per key. Never publishes or runs."],[908,"Templates and plans"],[3682,"Ten compositions cover nearly every screen in the suite. A new screen names the pattern it follows in its acceptance criteria; a screen that follows none proposes an eleventh."],[3634,"Ten steps — 2 · 4 · 6 · 8 · 12 · 16 · 20 · 24 · 32 · 48 px (`--nexus-space-1 … -10`): inside a control · icon to label · chip inset · the action gap · a field's gap · section inner · page head · between sections · page padding · the page's foot. Margins, paddings and gaps name a step, never a number; 10 and 14 do not exist (8/12, 12/16). A quiet control that must sit flush with its text uses `.is-flush`; off-screen text uses `.nexus-sr-only`, never a negative margin."],[3632,"Ten steps; margins, paddings and gaps name a step, never a number."],[1502,"Tenant-scoped evaluation runs, newest first"],[1498,"Tenant-scoped ModelInvocation records, newest first (retention 90 days by default)\n\nAudit / metering projection — metadata only (role, operation, tier, model, provider, tokens, latency, routing,\nstatus); never prompt text, inputs or outputs. Filters combine with AND. `run_id` / `agent_id` accept the bare id\nor the full `nexus://agent/run/…` / `nexus://agent/…` URI. Records of other tenants are never listed."],[1499,"Tenant-scoped ToolInvocation records, newest first \n\nTrace / audit projection — decision, status, connection, digests, duration, error code and user-message key;\nnever arguments, output or headers. Filters combine with AND. Records of other tenants are never listed (RLS)."],[1571,"Tenant-scoped ToolInvocation records, newest first \n\nTrace / audit projection — decision, status, connection, digests, duration, error code and user-message key;\nnever arguments, output or headers. Filters combine with AND. Records of other tenants are never listed (RLS)."],[1429,"Terms by level/tier/status with usage counts (query: level, tier, status, q, cursor). Base (L0) terms are read-only."],[1418,"Terms in use and the ontology registry — managed terms, proposals, snapshots."],[2328,"Tests run per app and never touch your stack's databases: `npm run test:chat-api`, `npm run test:core-api`,\n`npm run test:tasks-api`, `npm run test:graph-api`, `npm run test:bi-api`, `npm run test:graph-worker`,\n`npm run test:chat`; the Postgres-backed variants (`test:*:pg`) use throw-away `*_test` databases on `:5433`."],[7756,"text + facts, 1 h if unsent, then the message"],[4582,"Text formats only in this version: `.txt`, `.md`, `.csv`, `.tsv`, `.json`, `.eml` — up to a million characters."],[3180,"Text only, `role=status aria-live=polite`; no spinner colour."],[3175,"Text only, role=status aria-live=polite; no spinner colour."],[3316,"Text that explains a restriction (`Restricted by <policy>`) — never a bare disabled control (DS-0004)."],[3312,"Text that explains a restriction (Restricted by <policy>) — never a bare disabled control (DS-0004)."],[7170,"That is also why the boundaries on the earlier pages exist. Agents cannot install or bind capabilities; they can only\nfile a **capability request** a person decides on. Skills own no tools. Models are described by roles and tiers\nrather than names. Each rule keeps the descriptions honest, so that the automation built on them can be trusted."],[6346,"The **Acceptance** section — *0 of 85 verified* — lists the acceptance criteria attached to this epic and its\nstories, each with *Open* and the number of tests linked (*AC-A2A-001 · agent card → tools → call · Open · 3 tests*).\nThe **References** section (further down) lists the requirements, decisions and documents. The importer attaches\neach reference to the item whose story id it belongs to; references with no matching story land on the epic."],[5898,"The **Access check** row is the one to remember: *Outside your access and left out: 1* means retrieval found a\ncandidate you may not read and the answer never saw it. The **Sufficiency** row decides the tone of the reply —\n*confident*, *tentative* (the model is told to treat the evidence as not answering unless it plainly does), or\n*empty*, in which case the answer says what is missing instead of guessing."],[4718,"The **Add a tool** dialog lists what your organization allows, each with a short description and tags: **Read-only**\nor **Side effects**, **Approval by policy*&#x2A; when a person must confirm each use, and a classification ceiling\nsuch as *≤ top\\_secret*. Tools that exist but are not available to this Project are listed greyed out with the\nreason — so you know what to ask for."],[92,"The **Add model** panel is drawn for every member; the refusal arrives when a non-administrator presses **Register**,\nin red, under the form, naming the roles that may:"],[4520,"The **Analysis planner** agent (no tools) reads what each column *is* from its values and picks the techniques this dataset supports — segments by a category, distributions and outliers, correlations, patterns over time, candidate clusters, recurring words in free text; duplicate candidates or unit spellings only when the values repeat or vary — 3–10 stages, each with a *why*, plus proposed indices; the **Reviewer** agent checks that every criterion is covered and every stage is grounded in the profile. If the reviewer objects, a gate asks &#x2A;Proceed despite reviewer concerns?*"],[4617,"The **Canvas** opens on the right with **Cottage offers — autumn weekend**: five columns, three rows, units in\nthe headers (*EUR*, *min*), &#x2A;by flow:flw\\_…* as the author. It is a first-class artifact of the Project — versioned\n(*v1 · Saved*), editable (*double-click a cell*), sortable (*click a header*), and it will appear in the Project's\nartifacts for everyone who may read the Project."],[4291,"The **Care pulse**: *Assistant answering 2 · People answering 4 · Waiting for a person 1 · SLA at risk 5*, today's\ncounts, **3 need attention**, and a link to analytics in NexBI. The rail lists Overview, Conversations, Cases,\nQuality, Live, the doors to other apps (Knowledge → NexGraph, Automation → Flow Studio, Channels → NexCore,\nAnalytics → NexBI) and **Care Studio**."],[6057,"The **claim Inspector**: **Warsaw · Shipments · 5 180**, the line **Domain · Verified · Project** (its layer, its\nstatus, its tier), &#x2A;*Open evidence →** and four tabs. **Claim** shows **WHAT THE SOURCE STATES** — *Warsaw ·\nShipments = 5 180* — and the facts: **Metric** shipments · **Value** 5 180 · **Method** table-cells\\@1 (the engine\nthat read it, versioned) · **Locator** acme-q3-2026-delivery-report.md · r1c1 (row 1, column 1 of the table) ·\n&#x2A;*Source assertion ≠ canonical claim (kept separately)**."],[3939,"The **Confidential** tag is your organization's default classification, applied to every new Project. You did not\nchoose it and, as a member, you cannot raise it; it is what decides which models and tools the Project is allowed\nto use (how access is decided). The four places are the four kinds of\nthing a Project owns — the rest of the guide visits each."],[4585,"The **Context** drawer is the Project's memory shown to you: **Scope** (this Project), the default **Agent**\nand **Model** for new chats, the **Classification** — *confidential*, inherited by everything pinned here — and\n**Pinned sources**: &#x2A;No sources pinned to this Project yet.* This drawer is where every source you add will be\nlisted, whichever way it arrived. It is read-only on purpose: a source enters a Project through a governed\naction, never through a drag into a side panel. Close it."],[4558,"The **Context** drawer now lists them beside the files: &#x2A;*PINNED SOURCES — FILES (1) · DATASETS (1)** —\n*epoints\\_sample 2 — organisations normalised · confidential*. Say *Keep the cleaned table for later questions* and\nthat is what happens; agents in later threads see its shape, never its rows."],[4553,"The **Context** drawer: &#x2A;*Pinned sources — Files (1) · Artifacts (3)**. Publishing pinned the table, the chart and\nthe report as **sources of the Project**: every later turn in any thread of the Project lists them — as a *shape\nhint* only (*table · v1 · published · columns … · N rows*), never their content."],[5072,"The **description** line"],[6013,"The **Evidence Workspace** is where every object of the graph meets the text it came from. It shows a document as\nthe pipeline read it — page by page, with every **mention**, **entity** and **claim** anchored to its exact span —\nand, beside the page, the facts about the document itself: its version, its hash, its parser, its run. This chapter\nopens the transport agreement and follows one claim down to its cell and one mention up to its entity."],[4369,"The **file bar**: &#x2A;File: ‹name› · N pages · Kept until … — Remove now deletes it at once. Not added to NexGraph.*\nThe answer is a bounded card — *From ‹name› · N pages read*, citation chips *Temporary source · p. N* with exact\nquotes (a quote not in the file is dropped), and &#x2A;The file doesn't say:* for what it did not cover. The file is\nparsed in-process, is never a Source, an attachment or an index, and is gone after eight hours or **Remove now**.\nSaving is a separate, confirmed act: *save this answer* (a Project artifact) or *add this to the project knowledge*\n(NexGraph, level 3). PDF and Office files are refused with a typed reason — nothing is stored."],[4620,"The **Grounding** drawer is the receipt of the answer. **Sources → Pinned context** lists the two files the\nagent was given; **Graph facts** says none were used; **Run** names the model, the **run reference** an\nadministrator can trace, and the time. The last sentence is the platform's rule: &#x2A;Claims are verified only by\nthe oracle or a human reviewer — never by the model.*"],[5863,"The **Grounding** drawer, **HOW THIS WAS FOUND**: &#x2A;The answer is grounded in 4 items from the knowledge graph;\nevery \\[n] in the text is one of them.* Then the ladder of steps, each with **in → out** counts and its time:"],[4847,"The **Inspector** docks on the right. A loop is a small thing with a big description: **Label**, **Description**\n(&#x2A;Loop Container: work → evaluate. Every exit leads to review.*), then the **Objective** — your sentence, which is\nwhat the agent reads each pass — the **Success criteria** *budget\\_fit ≥ 0.9*, and the **Guardrails** *Max\niterations 10 · Max duration 60 minutes · Token budget*."],[5934,"The **Inspector** opens on the right: **Northwind Traders · Entity · Claims · Base**, the button **Expand\nnearby**, then the facts — **Group** organization · **Kind** Entity · **Tier** · **Type** organization · **State ●\nProposed**. Under **NEARBY**, **Entities 8**. Under **RELATIONS · 8*&#x2A;, each relation with its direction and kind:\n**← CO\\_MENTION Taras Bondar · France · 15 November · Acme Logistics · Petra Lindqvist*&#x2A;, **→ CO\\_MENTION Managing\nDirector · 92 % · Poland**. These are the things the agreement mentions in the same passages as the carrier — the\npeople who signed, the countries of its lanes, the service level. The status line reads **Focused Northwind\nTraders · 8 relations**."],[5330,"The **Invite a person** panel opens on the right. The **Role** list is the organization's vocabulary of trust,\nfrom the widest to the narrowest:"],[4559,"The **merges gate**. Ask *Analyse this dataset and ask me before merging organisation names*, and the\n*Duplicate candidates* stage stops at **waiting for your decision** with an approval card — kicker **ORGANISATION\nNAMES** — &#x2A;*Merge 23 probable duplicate names?** &#x2A;The duplicate-candidates stage found names that look like the\nsame organisation written differently. Confirm to count them together in the normalised dataset; keep them apart\nto leave them as they are. The original values stay in the typed copy either way.* The top pairs with their\nsimilarity (*Organisation E ↔ Organization E · 83 % similar*), *and 19 more pairs — Review in Canvas shows them\nall&#x2A;, the note **! Confirmed merges are recorded as your decision; nothing here is verified by the model*&#x2A;, and\n**✓ Merge all 23** · **Keep apart** · **Review in Canvas**. The gate appears when the Blueprint enables it and the\nnumber of uncertain pairs is at or above its threshold (20 by default); your answer is a `merge_confirmation`\ndecision and the *only* way a merge happens."],[5940,"The **organization** group fades to the background — *107* — and **Northwind Traders** is lit with its eight\nneighbours drawn in blue: *Petra Lindqvist*, *Taras Bondar*, a long line to *Acme Logistics*. Hovering shows a\ncard with &#x2A;*Details →**. The legend explains the colours — *Coloured by what they co-occur with: other 83 · with\nLocation 6 · with Product 4 · with Role 4 · with Amount 3 · with Document (named) 3 · with Person 2 · with Date 1\n· with Technology 1* — and the reading rule: &#x2A;Lit — the object and its 1-hop · faded — the rest of the group, in\nplace · beside it — neighbours from other groups · Double-click a neighbour — its network · Esc — back.*"],[5488,"The **Overview**: the classification chip and status under the name, **Open in Chat** to go to the work itself,\nand five tabs — **Overview · Members · Capabilities · Runtime · Governance**. The counters are honest zeros:\none member, no capabilities, models or connections yet. The block that matters on day one is **Effective\npolicy** — *Classification Confidential · Cloud ceiling Allowed up to Confidential · External writes Approval\nrequired · Sharing Organization only · Publishing Project Owner approval* — and its last line, *Inherited from:\nNorthwind Traders*. Nobody set these for the Project; they are the organization's rules, and the Project may\nmake them stricter, never looser."],[5353,"The **person inspector**: General (status, joined, last active, classification), **Access**, **Security**,\n**Activity**, and **Edit*&#x2A; for the name and the role. &#x2A;(In this build the Identity line still reads “No identity\nlinked yet — the invitation has not been accepted” after the join; the roster and the Accepted row are the truth.\nRecorded as an open item.)*"],[7743,"The **platform-action arm** (`chat_api/auto/platform_action_arm.py`) runs **before any model**: verb cue ∧ object cue\n→ candidates → target resolved **through the owning app's door as the person** (`SearchService`, `tasks.list_projects`)\n→ PDP `read` on the exact target → a `client_action` message with status `resolved` (auto-navigates once if newest and\n≤ 15 s), `choice` (2…8 targets with kinds) or `not_found` (identical for missing and not-permitted). Hrefs\ncome from registry templates filled from the resolved resource, never from the sentence. Exclusions `foreign_family`,\n`not_a_command`, `asks_how` keep questions and other systems' nouns out. **Confirmation levels** (ADR-0052 §2): 1 runs\nat once; 2 previews and reads back, a *yes* required (`task.create`, `flow.start`, `answer.save`); 3 shows the exact\nchange and waits (`task.assign`, `task.move`, `knowledge.add_session_file`); 4 is an on-screen door only\n(`access.change`). A *yes* binds to `proposal_id` + `version`; a correction voids it; TTL 600 s. Writes go\nthrough tasks-api, graph-api and the Flow Runtime with their own PEP and `idempotency_key = request_id`. No action is\n`agent_bindable`."],[4395,"The **purpose** line"],[5993,"The **RECORD** section under each step (collapsed) holds the step's structured record with **Copy JSON** — the same\ndata the API returns; nothing is shown in the page that is not in the record."],[6355,"The **References** tab's stamp changes after **Re-sync** if the documentation commit changed; otherwise it keeps the SHA and updates the time."],[4613,"The **Run flow from this chat** sheet: the same two inputs as the Studio dialog, plus &#x2A;*Message (optional)** —\n*Shown as your turn in the thread; the flow does not read it* — and a **Test with data** checkbox that would\nsimulate the side effects instead of doing them. The message is for the people reading the chat later, not for\nthe Flow: the Flow gets exactly its declared inputs and nothing else."],[4868,"The **Runs** tab opens on this run."],[4883,"The **Runs** tab shows two runs: a *Test* that **Completed** with the approval *simulated*, and a real run\n**Waiting for approval: Review results**."],[4608,"The **Runs** tab with the run selected. Four steps, all **Done**; the agent step names the **agent run** behind\nit (`nexus://agent/run/…`), the tool step the Synapse invocation (`synapse: ti_…`). **Budget** counts one model\ncall and one tool call. **Inputs** (collapsed) holds the attachment's address and *10–12 October*; **Outputs*&#x2A;\nthe table's address and the summary. &#x2A;(On the review fixture the model answers an agent step with the example\nfrom its output schema — that is why the durations read 0 ms; with a real model the same run takes a few\nseconds and the numbers come from your file.)*"],[7063,"The **Scene Agent** (`nexus://agent/agt_forge_scene`) applies the skill `skl_forge_scene_edit` whose `output_schema`\nis the proposal contract, holds **read tools only** (`forge.scene.read · knowledge.search · graph.query`), is not\nroutable and has no side effects. It is hosted inside forge-api on `nexus_agent_runtime.AgentRuntime` with the\n`core_api_model_port` driver — models only through `POST /synapse/inference/complete`; refusals cross as typed\n`PortError`, never provider text. Its prompt is `prompts/scene_turn.md`. A proposal has `candidates[] {ops,\nsummary, probability}` summing to 1, an optional `needs_clarification {question_key, options ≤ 5}`, a 30-minute TTL,\nand is re-validated against the current version on apply (stale → 409)."],[667,"The **server** menu at the top of each playground has two entries. *Through this portal* is the default and needs no\nconfiguration. *A Nexi deployment directly* sends the request from your browser to the origin you type — that\ndeployment must list this portal in its `CORS_ORIGINS`, otherwise the browser refuses before Nexi answers."],[6020,"The **sha256** is the identity of this version. If someone hands you a copy of the file, its hash either matches\nthis one or it is a different version."],[4370,"The **share bar**: *Screen: Window · title · This session only · Not added to NexGraph · Stop sharing · End and\nclear*. **One frame per question** (optionally cropped on the preview) goes to one vision call and the bytes are\ndropped; the answer reads &#x2A;I see: … · I don't see: …* with regions drawn in your tab only. A frame or a file turn\noffers the model **no tools** and cannot propose an action: what you show Nexi is quoted data, never instructions."],[4729,"The **Versions** tab shows every save you made, oldest to newest."],[5410,"The **waiting card**: the request went to Northwind Traders' administrators. Kate can close the tab; when she\ncomes back she lands on this card, not on the choice — and if she leaves it open, it updates itself the moment a\ndecision is made."],[688,"The *Body* panel shows every field; required ones are marked."],[444,"The *Effective rights for this object* block at the bottom of a claim's Verification tab shows the decision for the\nobject you are looking at — *Read the claim · Open the evidence · Verify claims* — with the line &#x2A;Why you see\nthis: your own Project relation.* Denials from the API come as `403 NOT_EDITOR`, `403 NOT_OWNER`,\n`403 AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN` or `403 PEP_DENIED` with a `user_message_key`, never policy text; a policy outage is\n`503 POLICY_UNAVAILABLE`, never a yes."],[7217,"The *Weather* Tool needs an API key. The *Calendar* Tool needs *your* account. Both are **Connections**, and they are\ndifferent kinds:"],[4807,"the &#x2A;*engine, never the model,** decides whether the goal is met, and stops at the limits;"],[2468,"the `.env` file, stored like a password"],[3201,"The `⋯` for secondary actions. Items may be `danger` (opens a destructive confirmation) or `disabled`; Esc and an outside click close it."],[2876,"The `⋯` of an artifact row (DS-3005 menu): Open · Open source chat · Publish · Add to dashboard · Rename · Archive… · Restore in sections, each item present only when the rights and the origin allow it — a reader sees Open and Open source chat; an owner of an archived chart sees Restore; a published document the person did not write offers no Rename. Nothing is disabled: an item that cannot run is not there."],[2394,"the `migrate-*` services run again before the APIs start"],[2011,"the `nexus` role's password"],[2213,"the `nexus` role's password"],[1846,"The `tasks-api` image already ships and now carries the **work domain** (`TASKS_WORK_DOMAIN`) in the same database\n`nexus_tasks`; the VibeBan web and the whole NexBI pair are laptop processes for now. Their definitions join the Compose\nfile and the chart in a coming release; the chart will need one more database and role."],[2198,"the `VOICE_*` keys in `configmaps.yaml`, the `LIVEKIT_API_SECRET` seam"],[7747,"The `web.search` **provider port** lives in core-api (`POST /synapse/web-search/{providers,query}`), adapters in\n`platform/synapse/nexus_synapse/web/search.py&#x60;. Four classes: &#x2A;*`api`** Tavily · Brave · Mojeek · LangSearch (keys as\nSynapse connections, `config/synapse/integrations/web-search-*.yaml&#x60;); &#x2A;*`open_data`*&#x2A; Wikipedia · Wikidata ·\nOpenStreetMap; &#x2A;*`own`** `nexus_index&#x60; (Project knowledge only); &#x2A;*`model_native`** OpenRouter `web` plugin (off by\ndefault). **SearXNG and Oxylabs are rejected** and there is no SERP-in-a-browser. Order is the\nBlueprint's `tuning.web_search.providers` (default Tavily → LangSearch → open data → own; a layer may only narrow),\nopen data first for `places`/`facts`, first answer wins, ≤ 10 results. **Classification ceiling**\n`tuning.web_search.max_classification = confidential`: on a *secret* thread no query leaves. Auto hears a closed\nen/uk/ru/de lexicon (`chat_api/auto/search.py`); one model call with results **quoted as untrusted data, no tools**\n(`prompts/search_answer.md`), `[n]` validated against ranks. No provider → *No web answer* + a typed reason + **Ask the\nadministrator** (one `CapabilityRequest` on `web.search`). Queries leave only through core-api's door as the person,\nand `session_only` content never routes to a provider whose retention is not `none`."],[2507,"The `web` image bakes the API origins as the contract's service names; the browser never receives a service\naddress."],[3195,"The ⋯ for secondary actions."],[2871,"The ⋯ of an artifact row (DS-3005 menu): Open · Open source chat · Publish · Add to dashboard · Rename · Archive… · Restore in sections, each item present only when the rights and "],[7445,"The acceptance gate"],[2853,"The account's activity stream (amended 2026-10-11): the log composer (DS-6107) at the top, then **Next** — planned interactions and open follow-ups in one list, soonest first — and"],[2857,"The account's activity stream (amended 2026-10-11): the log composer (DS-6107) at the top, then **Next** — planned interactions and open follow-ups in one list, soonest first — and **History**, done interactions newest first. One row grammar for both: a glyph (open = planned or follow-up, filled = done) · when · kind or title · outcome chip · who · with whom · the summary · the next step with its follow-up door. The stream is the *Activity* view of the page; Deals · Quotes · Documents are its sibling views (`LocalTabs`, DS-2006). The source chip (DS-6101) on the page line says where these came from; when the source is unavailable the list stays, marked as the last copy. Not a kit duplicate: no kit export shows a dated sequence with a planned/done glyph."],[176,"The action is for the organization's Owner or Admin."],[179,"The action needs a stated purpose and none was given."],[1640,"The actor's views plus the project's shared views (`project_ref`)."],[3894,"The address of your Nexi installation (for example `https://app.your-company.example`). Your IT team or the\nperson who invited you has it."],[167,"The agent has no human behind this turn, or the tool is not delegated to it."],[4441,"The agent keeps the thread of one conversation."],[4443,"The agent may recall what it learned in other chats of the same Project — again filtered by what the asking person may see."],[4593,"The agent reads what the Project has pinned — nothing of its own. There is no per-agent upload; an agent has no private library."],[4488,"The agent record is a small, typed document: name, purpose, instructions, knowledge scope, skill references, tool\nbindings, an inference policy and permission bounds, all under a version number. At every message NexChat sends the\nperson's identity, the Project, the agent version and the intended action to the policy point, which answers with\nthe intersection above; Synapse then resolves the inference policy to one concrete model for that turn and records\nthe choice. The agent itself holds no credential and no model — which is why anyone in the Project can build one\nwithout creating a security question for the organization. The building blocks and their relationships are drawn in\nAgents, Skills, Tools and Flows."],[4706,"The Agent Studio opens on the **Overview** tab."],[6375,"The Agentic Data Scientist — a professional capability as a Flow, not as code"],[6372,"The Agentic Data Scientist — a professional capability composed from agents, skills,\none tool, a sandbox profile and a Flow with goal loops — and why it is not a service; the datasets a run keeps,\nreuse and the merges gate."],[935,"The AgentRun record of a turn with its ToolInvocations — initiator or Project editor"],[4727,"The Agents page of *Weekend trips* lists **Trip planner** with a **Published** pill."],[6015,"The agreement processed. Open it from **Sources → Uploads → Documents**, from a run's **Open document**, or from an\nentity or claim in Studio and Review."],[1368,"The allowed subgraph: the landscape of groups, a group's members, one object and its neighbours, the searchable list."],[6383,"The Analyse a spreadsheet chapter shows a run from the outside: attach a workbook, ask,\nwatch eight stages, publish. This page shows the same thing from the inside — and makes one architectural point.\nNexi has **no data-science service**. The Agentic Data Scientist is a Flow, shipped in a Blueprint, made of the same\nparts every builder has: Agents that apply Skills, one Tool, a Sandbox profile, goal loops with an evaluator, and an\napproval. If you can express a professional capability with those, it ships as content; if you cannot, the platform\nis missing a building block, not a service."],[4047,"The answer arrives in a few seconds as text: &#x2A;Late delivery rate by carrier for 2026 — 27 values. Highest: Summit\nExpress (0.1 %); lowest: Northwind Freight (0.0 %). Computed by the NexBI engine (Shipments 2025–2026 · dsv\\_… ·\n189 rows).* Under it **NEW DRAFTS 2** — a *Chart · v1 · Draft* and a *Table · v1 · Draft* of the same query, each\nwith **Preview** and **Open in Canvas**. The route line reads **Auto → Direct answer · engine:nexbi** — no agent,\nno model call for the number itself. The question also sets the period, the entity filter and the comparison from\nits words: a `filter_derivation` decision, shown in the answer's &#x2A;How was this calculated?* line."],[7134,"The answer is the same each time: &#x2A;*Nexi describes everything it uses in one vocabulary, and machines read that\ndescription.** That vocabulary is the ontology. It has two floors."],[5132,"The answer you would accept, in prose or JSON. Up to 8 000 characters."],[6665,"The applications"],[4857,"The approval's settings: **Approver** *Project owner*; the **Title** the owner will see in NexTasks — *Agentic\nresult for {'{{workflow.name}}'} — review before publishing*, a template filled at run time; **On timeout: Fail\nthe run** after **259200** seconds (three days). The line to remember: &#x2A;The approval is a NexTasks item; the flow\nwaits until it is decided.*"],[6725,"The architecture views are generated from a text model (`architecture/*.c4`) and rendered as interactive\ndiagrams in the page. The model is reviewed like code; there is no drawing tool and no image file to go stale."],[6164,"The area inspector on the right: the same counts, the kinds inside the cell, and **Zoom in**, which opens the cell\nat object level. The *Risk* section states that no risk sources are connected: weather, conflict and advisory\nlayers are a proposal, not a picture."],[6615,"the asker"],[727,"The assertion carries *who you are* — never *what you may do*. Every call is still checked against your\norganization, clearance, Project relations and purpose (how access is decided).\nA valid token with no relation to a Project still gets `403` or `404`."],[7035,"The assistant is a governed **Agent** from the pack; Care Studio's *Assistant* tab is a business-user profile (name,\nlanguages, formality, warmth, brevity, greeting, sign-off, handoff phrase, never-answer topics) that **compiles** into\nan Agent draft a second person reviews before publish — the same rule as every agent. Retrieval reads the Care slice\nof NexGraph with `verified_only` true by default (`GET …/knowledge`, `KNOWLEDGE_SCOPE`); every answer names its\nclaims and versions, and the inspector's *Knowledge* tab shows them. Copilot suggestions to the joined person are\ndecision **features**, never labels."],[572,"the assistant replies only while it holds the conversation; never Joins, never marks identity verified"],[3517,"The atoms every VibeBan list, board card and Inspector row is built from."],[3522,"The atoms every VibeBan list, board card and Inspector row is built from. Priority (`‼ ! · ◦` + the word), stage (`○ ◔ ◑ ◕ ● ⊘`), type (epic · story · task · bug glyphs), blocked (`n` + direction), health (`StatusDot` with the word) — glyph + text, never colour alone. `ActorChip` is a human, an agent or a service with its kind; `DueLabel` says overdue · today · the date. The property fields are the Inspector's editors — bare at rest, framed on hover/focus (`quiet`), Enter commits, Esc