 v7 · Draft**, **Dataset profile · Table · v1 · Draft*&#x2A; with **▸ Preview**\nopen (Field · Type · Missing % · Distinct — *object\\_id · id · 0 % · 20061*), **Proposed indices · Table · v1**."],[1358,"The BackgroundExecutionGrant of a continuous binding (budget, spent, expiry, status)."],[6309,"The backlog is the ranked list of items **not yet planned into any iteration** — here three low-priority items.\nThe arrows move an item up or down; the rank is stored, so the order is the same for everyone. Search and the\ntype filter narrow the list; the checkboxes select items for the planning pane. **Plan iteration** in the header\nopens that pane."],[5623,"The bar above it: **Colour** (none + eight hues · *Tint / Solid / Outline* · *Thin / Thick / Dashed*), **Kind**\n(*Note · Node · Text · Rectangle · Ellipse · Diamond* — switching kind keeps the object and its relations),\n**Order** (*Bring to front / forward · Send backward / to back*), **Lock**, and `⋯` → *Meaning · Details · Delete*.\n*Meaning* sets the semantic type from a closed list of twenty-six (&#x2A;person, system, database, warehouse, dock,\nflow…*) — it is what the Diagram and 3D views and later conversions read. Colours are scene data, not decoration:\nthe colour key in the header names what each hue means."],[2899,"The bar and its panel as one surface: the panel opens beneath the bar with the conversation for this screen, the answer turns rendered by NexChat's own turn card (DS-5001), the han"],[2904,"The bar and its panel as one surface: the panel opens beneath the bar with the conversation for this screen, the answer turns rendered by NexChat's own turn card (DS-5001), the hand-off chip and &#x2A;Back to ‹app›*. Its states are closed: empty · composing · streaming · answered · answered from the screen · not on the screen · unreadable · an action proposed (the proposal card with Confirm · Change · Cancel) · action done · error · denied · offline · no destination · no route. Each state has one copy class per language; nothing in the panel names a mechanism."],[619,"The base Blueprint sets *Self-approval: forbidden* (the row you read in the Blueprint matrix); a deployment may\nallow it below *DSK*, and the organization layer may only tighten. Nexi never lets a model decide: the engine\nparks the run, a person answers, the engine resumes."],[7748,"The base-pack Flow `web-research` (pack 1.26.0): `plan (agent) → search (web.search) → scope → allow (approval) →\nreading loop (read agent → ledger tool → enough evaluator) → narrate → report`. A research cue (en/uk/de, no ru)\nroutes to the **Resolver**, which runs the Flow as a child run. The reading plane is **graph-api over HTTP**\n(`browser.open` / `browser.follow`, `render: http`; Playwright in the Sandbox is S6c): the model names a **link id**,\nnever a URL; CAPTCHA, anti-bot, paywall and auth walls stop the host unsolved; budgets are tool-side\n(`tuning.web_research`: 30 pages · depth 2 · 8/host · 2 s jittered · 6 min · 24 MB); only allow-listed hosts through the\nSynapse egress pipeline, redirects re-admitted against the list. The report's confidence chip is the **engine's\ncorroboration count**; `[n]` links only to pages read; a proposed source becomes a `web` binding of the Project **as\nthe person** (`POST /chat/flow-runs/{run_id}/research-source`) and then follows NexGraph's pipeline as proposed\nclaims. Live-run findings of 2026-10-01: F-1 Gateway refused tool calls under an output schema (fixed), F-2 the\n`research_scope` row hit a DB constraint (fixed, migration 0060), F-3 a how-to sentence routed to *Create a work item*\n(fixed, `asks_how`), F-4 knowledge fallback leaks mechanism text in a fresh organization (open). The UX verdict — one\ncard, result in the thread — ships with the NexChat backbone work."],[1854,"The BI API: datasets and versions, the semantic model, metrics, the governed query engine, dashboards, templates, automations. Owns `nexus_bi`; runs governed queries as the read-only role `bi_query` (8 s · 1 000 rows · cost guard). Relays its outbox to chat-api over HTTP."],[7262,"The big picture"],[6363,"The big picture — Nexi decomposed on one page: the applications and what each contains,\nthe shared runtimes, the state — a map you can click through."],[5685,"The bindings of the Project — uploads, server folders, Google Drive — each with five states, its documents and its operations."],[1090,"The board (*Why?* · the `goal` arm's read window)\n\n1.140.0 ( S1). PEP: OpenFGA on (project, actor) and the goal's owner — outside the\nactor's Projects the goal is 404, never 403 (the thread idiom); service and agent identities are refused on every\nwrite (403, recorded). No request text in any payload.\nAppend-only entries, newest first; `before` · `limit` paging; refs and ≤ 280-char summaries only."],[687,"The body did not match the contract."],[5938,"The breadcrumb grows — **Landscape › organization › Northwind Traders** — and the status line reads **Northwind\nTraders · nearby: Entities**. The stage is now the object's **ego network**: the object and its neighbours. In\nList it shows the one focused row; the Inspector keeps the eight relations."],[6885,"the browser never talks to another origin"],[6248,"The bug-triage board: **Reported · Triage · Fixing · Verify · Done**. *Fixing* has a WIP limit of five and holds five\nbugs, so its counter reads **5 / 5**. The limit is **soft**: moving a sixth bug in succeeds, the column header turns\ninto a warning *Over the WIP limit (6 / 5) — moved anyway*, and VibeBan records a `wip_limit_decision` naming the\nmove and the limit — the team decides what to do about it, the tool does not block the work."],[6521,"The building blocks and their relationships are one view of the architecture model that draws every diagram in this\ndocumentation:"],[3903,"The button briefly shows a working state and the page changes to **Verify your e-mail**. If the address is\nalready registered, Nexi tells you so and offers **Sign in** instead — nothing is duplicated."],[3974,"The call"],[4551,"The Canvas on the right: **Document · v2 · Saved**, **Analysis report — epoints · Document · v2 · current ·\nconfidential · by usr\\_alex\\_001**. Under **Organizations**, the sentence &#x2A;Three organizations account for most\nincidents (table); by category, water leads (chart).* — and the cited table **Top organizations by incidents ·\nTable · v1 · Draft · Open** is embedded live (*Kyivvodokanal 412 · Kyivteploenergo 388 · Kyivavtodor 251*), the\nchart **Incidents by category** under it. The header offers &#x2A;*Export ▾**; the bar reads &#x2A;Saved as version 2.*"],[5012,"The card becomes the run: **Nexi · Resolver · asks a Project owner · Waiting on you**. Step 1 &#x2A;Connect your\nmailbox — waiting for you to connect it · **Connect***; step 2 with the chip *needs a Project owner*; step 3\npending. Under it **CREATED 1**: *Connect your mailbox · Connection — Your consent is needed before Nexi can\nread it. Connect it in NexCore; this continues by itself* · *awaiting you*. The run waits up to seven days for\nyou; the same request is not created twice within a day."],[4769,"The card flips to **✓ Approved by alex · time**, with **Technical details** for the record; the step turns\n**Done**; the run continues on the **Approved** arrow to **Done** and ends **Completed**. Everyone who has the\nrun open sees the change within seconds. The comment travels with the decision into the audit trail — it is not\na chat message, and the agent never reads it."],[4820,"The card opens Flow Studio by itself after a moment unless you are reading it; press **Open flow** when ready."],[4261,"The Care module is installed — Install a module."],[4289,"The Care module is installed and a customer has written — Embed the widget leaves a\nconversation waiting for a person."],[4233,"The Care module is installed; you own the Care Project."],[7425,"the Care Project; guardrail profiles in NexCore; one hand writes at a time"],[6022,"The cell **1 580 EUR** (row *Hamburg – Lyon*, column *Rate per FTL*) gets a blue frame — *the highlighted cell is\nthe claim's evidence span*. The panel becomes **CLAIM · DOMAIN — Hamburg - Lyon · Rate per FTL — ● Verified**,\n&#x2A;*Value 1 580 EUR · PDF 1 · Source assertion ≠ canonical claim (kept separately)**. Buttons: &#x2A;*Review →*&#x2A; (the\nverdict and its scope are in Review), &#x2A;*← 1 / 8 →** to step through the eight claims of this document, **Clear**."],[6162,"The cell is outlined and an upright card sits a hand's width from it, with a leader to the facing edge: **Near\nHamburg warehouse · 68 objects · 12 delayed · 33 stale**, a weather event *Fog — Elbe estuary · 5 h left · Demo ·\nInfo*, **Lanes from or to here: 6 · objects on them: 178**, *Last observation 2 h 49 min ago · ≈ 138 km across*, and\ntwo links: **Details** and **Zoom in**. The lanes fan out from the cell as grey lines — a lane is a relation\nbetween places, not a drawn route."],[2231,"the certificate the Ingress terminates"],[6657,"The chapter: Let Auto choose — and read why."],[7716,"The chapters Speak to Nexi, Act from anywhere\nand Search the web and research a question show these from the outside. This\npage is the inside of voice and actions: the composer microphone, the platform-action arm, the\n`ContextSnapshot`, session material, the `web.search` port and the research Flow. Three fitness rules hold them\ntogether: **voice adds no rights**, **audio and frames are never stored**, and **what you show Nexi is quoted data,\nnever instructions**."],[7526,"The chapters: My Work and the Inbox · Create a project and run the board · Plan an iteration · References and acceptance."],[7015,"The chapters: Publish a dataset · Define and certify metrics · Read a dashboard · Build a dashboard · Automate a dashboard · Ask your data."],[2199,"the chart carries the configuration; the `asr-local` / `tts-local` sidecar Deployments join at UAT-4 — until then point `NEXUS_ASR_LOCAL_BASE_URL` / `NEXUS_TTS_LOCAL_BASE_URL` at your own Services"],[3006,"the chart is `role=img` with the title as its name and the table as its twin; grid items are focusable with arrow-key move and resize announced"],[2001,"the chart's default-deny only bites when the CNI enforces it"],[1808,"The Chat API: Projects, chats, agents, skills, flows. Accepts work and puts it on the job bus."],[4624,"The chat has a run card whose `table` output opens **Cottage offers — autumn weekend** in the Canvas."],[3969,"The chat holds two questions and two answers, and &#x2A;*Why this answer?** opens the Grounding drawer for each."],[3962,"The chat itself also has a menu — hover its row in the sidebar and press &#x2A;*…**:"],[629,"The Chat, Platform, Tasks, Graph and BI APIs — generated from the published contracts, with a live playground on every operation."],[7574,"The check every module API runs first: is this module enabled for the organization? Unknown is closed."],[4851,"The chip now reads *budget\\_fit ≥ 0.9 · 6× · 60m*, the loop header *max 6 · 60m*, and the header says **Saved**.\nNothing else happened: still **v1**, still a draft. Every edit in the Studio is saved this way; versions are cut\nonly when you publish."],[6182,"The chip reads **24.09.2026 10:00 UTC** and the status line **History · 24.09 10:00 UTC · 388 objects**. The\nhexagons show where objects *were* at that instant — each at its last observation before that time, not an\ninterpolation. An area with nothing says &#x2A;No permitted object had a position here at this instant. Try Now.*"],[3436,"the chip text is the status; the time is a `title` on a focusable span"],[3108,"The classification chip (public · confidential · dsk · secret · top_secret — tone + the word), the record status dot (a trace record's lifecycle word), and the trace Inspector's tw"],[3113,"The classification chip (public · confidential · dsk · secret · top\\_secret — tone + the word), the record status dot (a trace record's lifecycle word), and the trace Inspector's two halves: the span tree (turn → run → call, a time bar per span, container spans fold) and the span detail (the record as fields — refs · statuses · timings · counts · digests, never content; payloads fetched only when opened, redactions named, classification shown; `denied` and `capture off` are honest rungs). Built on `Chip` · `StatusDot` · `Inspector` (DS-3030). Not a kit duplicate: the kit has no span tree."],[6647,"The classifier prompt"],[7718,"The clip (≤ 2 MiB, ≤ 60 s, `audio_base64`) goes once to `POST /chat/voice/transcriptions`; chat-api runs the thread's\nPEP as a message write **before a byte moves**, then core-api `POST /synapse/inference/transcribe&#x60; with the **`asr`\nrole** (floor 0.8): `faster-whisper-large-v3-turbo` on the local sidecar is tier 1 and the default;\n`gpt-4o-mini-transcribe` is tier 4 and eligible only up to *confidential*. The transcript becomes the person's bubble\nwith a *Spoken* mark (`Spoken · edited` if corrected; confidence \\< 0.5 leaves it in the composer). The UI locale is the\nhint; the corpus covers uk · en · ru · de."],[7661,"The closed taxonomy a resolved conversation carries; what Quality and the Care datasets are built on."],[3403,"The combobox as the suite's only select — never a native `<select>`. `compact` for a toolbar filter; `quiet` for a property value."],[3397,"The combobox as the suite's only select — never a native <select>."],[2986,"the composer is a `group` labelled by its purpose; the input carries the same label; `↑` is a labelled submit, disabled until a word is written; the exit is a real button; the form that follows autofocuses its first field"],[4776,"The composer menu: *Attach file · Add source · Choose agent (@) · Use skill (/) · **Run a flow** · Project\ncontext*. A Flow is one more thing a message can do."],[7717,"The composer mic (`NexusComposer`, testid `composer-mic`) is the real entry point; the shell *Voice Dock* renders only\nunder `?voice_demo=` and is a UAT-1 fixture. One tap opens the mic; a browser **energy endpointer** ends the turn —\nspeech ≥ 200 ms above 0.09 RMS, then **1.5 s** of silence; 7 s of nothing → &#x2A;Didn't hear anything.*; 60 s cap;\ntap again = *Send now*; `Esc` cancels. While open, the card is **the wave alone**: no status words, the text\nbox hidden, the state for assistive technology in `nexus-sr-only`."],[5633,"The composer strip — &#x2A;Say or type what to change…*, `@`, the microphone, send. While you speak the mic shows the\nwave; the pause ends the turn (nothing to press). The transcript appears as &#x2A;*You said …**, then the same proposal\ncard as for a typed sentence. Say **yes** and the card on screen is applied — a spoken yes binds to *that* card\nonly; say **no** and it is cancelled. *No, wait — a node* keeps the last clause. History shows the source **voice**."],[4995,"The composer's selector reads **Auto** (the default). Picking an agent with `@` or a model by name is the override;\nthe route line then reads &#x2A;You chose ‹capability›*."],[6659,"The composition rule the Resolver obeys: Agents, Skills, Tools and Flows."],[3681,"The compositions that cover nearly every screen in the suite."],[5385,"The confirmation lists what stays: everything people made inside the module — map views, service conversations,\nscenes — is **kept, read-only**, in the module's own database; the module's routes answer *not enabled* again and\nthe tile disappears. Installing the pack later brings the content back as it was. Nothing is deleted by removing\na pack; deletion is a separate, human act inside the module with its own confirmation."],[5378,"The confirmation names the pack and version, lists what is added to the organization and says where the module\nwill appear — *in the App Launcher, for people with access*. **Install** writes one Blueprint layer; the change is\nan audit event (*blueprint.pack.installed*) you can read in Governance › Audit."],[1524,"The Connect list for the signed-in person: one row per knowledge-source integration with NexCore's state and the one action it allows (a Shared connection available to `project_id` first, then the person's own; `not_enabled` rows only for an administrator)."],[185,"The connection or credential is not yours to use or administer."],[3216,"The content column."],[3222,"The content column. `layout=\"dense\"` renders the one header line (DS-2005); `stacked` (eyebrow · title · lead · meta) is NexCore's and NexChat's and legacy elsewhere. `width` standard or wide."],[4622,"The Context drawer of **Family weekends** lists `cottage-offers-autumn.txt` and `more-offers.eml`, both\n*confidential*."],[7016,"The contract: BI API — 81 operations, tags *datasets · semantic · metrics · queries · dashboards · templates · automations · insights · overview · system*."],[7527,"The contract: Tasks API — 87 operations, tags *approvals · work\\_projects · work\\_items · iterations · milestones · references · read\\_models · system*."],[2036,"The controller creates the ALB and a target group per Service; create an alias record `nexus.example.com → the ALB`\nin Route 53. The three routes the chart renders (`/idp/realms/nexus`, `/idp/resources`, `/`) are exactly what the\nALB needs — do not add a rule for `/api/v1`; `web` forwards it."],[7659,"The conversation waiting for a person — asked for by the customer, or decided by policy."],[2463,"The credential store of core-api (`file://`)"],[5075,"The current version and the shortcut. Every save on any tab creates the next patch version — see Versions."],[4398,"The current version. Every save on any tab creates the next version — see Versions."],[4081,"The dashboard, a schedule, the Project thread that receives it and the filter set (*the dashboard's default filters*\nor *the filters you have on now*). The Flow (`flw_tpl_bi_subscription`) renders the dashboard **as the subscriber** —\nrow policies and denied blocks apply to you, not to the readers of the thread — and posts a summary card with each\nKPI's value and delta and a link to the dashboard with that filter state in the URL. Delivery is a Project thread\nonly; a person who cannot read the thread never sees the numbers."],[6432,"The Data scientist receives"],[6464,"The Dataset Card"],[613,"The decider is the person the run acts for, and self-approval is not allowed for this request"],[5629,"The decision behind the proposal: the features seen at the time (zoom, active view, selection count, whether the\ngrammar hit, language), **every candidate** the agent considered with its probability, the chosen one, the reason\ncodes, and the versions of the prompt and the agent. No sentence of yours and no model text is stored in the\nrecord — only closed features and references (the snapshot lives under its own URI). This is the same\ntraining-grade decision data every Nexi choice keeps."],[6694,"The decision studio: governed datasets, metrics certified by a steward, dashboards recomputed for every reader, the Studio with templates and the Advisor, automations as Flows; data questions answered in NexChat by the same engine."],[7562,"The default in the composer: a classifier reads the intent, deterministic code ranks the Project's capabilities you may use, and the route is recorded before it runs."],[323,"The default: works in the Projects they are given, with whatever relation they are given there."],[1588,"The delivery log of a binding, newest first ( D): one row per (item, event) with the run ref chat-api gave and its mirrored status. Readable by whoever sees the scope."],[6901,"The Deployment guide has the ports and the ladder from laptop to cluster."],[5179,"The deployment runs speech routes: `asr-local` (:8090) and `tts-local` (:8091) behind the Gateway on the dev stack.\nWithout an eligible route the mic says &#x2A;Voice isn't available for this conversation's classification — type instead.*"],[6196,"The depots from the file are hub markers among the other objects (*Objects · 86 · 86 objects in view*), their\nsource named after your upload. **Remove upload** in Sources takes back exactly these rows."],[7478,"The derivation is a `health_derivation` decision — the rule version is pinned in it."],[7741,"The dev stack starts each when `.venv/bin/asr-local` / `tts-local` exists (`uv pip install -e \".[dev,whisper]\"` /\n`\".[dev,ukrainian]\"`), installs `platform/media[silero]` into chat-api's venv and migrates chat-api's `.env` with the\n`VOICE_*` keys — all **required, no defaults**; `fixture` drivers are refused in production. Compose has profiles\n`asr-local`, `tts-local` and `media` (LiveKit, unused by the browser yet) with no published ports; Helm carries the\nenv but no sidecar profile yet (UAT-4). A *confidential* Project **must** have a local `asr`/`tts` route — a fitness\ncheck enforces it."],[4909,"The dialog **Add a tool** with a search box and a list in groups. **Platform** tools come with Nexi — create a\nchart, a table or a document artifact, read an artifact, search the Project, run Python in the Sandbox, create a\ntask. Below them, **Connected** tools come from systems your organization has connected through Synapse; **Custom**\ntools are the ones your Project imported itself. Every row carries the same tags:"],[4650,"The dialog asks *step by step* on purpose. An agent's sentence says what the agent is *for*; a skill's text says\nhow something is *done*. The more concrete the list — every item a proposal must contain — the less you will\nhave to fix in the next steps."],[4813,"The dialog asks &#x2A;*What should this flow do?**"],[4923,"The dialog closes and the Tools tab lists **Project search — Read-only** with two buttons, **Posture** and\n**Remove**. The header version has moved on by one: bindings are part of the agent's version, like every other\nchange. From now on, when someone asks the Trip planner about the cottage, it can search the Project's pinned\nsources, attachments and threads and answer with references — instead of guessing."],[3937,"The dialog closes and you are inside the Project."],[4866,"The dialog gives way to a **run bar** above the canvas — **Completed · Test · Pass 3 / 6 · frun\\_… · v1** — and the\ncanvas becomes the run's trace: every node with a green tick and its duration, the loop header *pass 3 / 6*, and\nthe approval marked **simulated**. Nobody was asked; nothing was written. That is what a test is."],[4604,"The dialog is built from the Flow's inputs. **offers \\* · file** shows a file button — the Flow said *file*, so\nthe dialog asks for a file, never for a pasted address. **weekend · string** is a plain text box. The line at\nthe top is the warning that this is a *real* run; the line at the bottom, *Pins v1*, promises that a later edit\nof the Flow will not change this run."],[7510,"the disposition chosen"],[4297,"The divider **Oksana Bondar joined**, the header **Handler: You** with **Return to assistant**, the inspector state\n*Active* with the handler set, and the composer **Reply to Visitor** open. Joining moved reply authority: from now\nthe assistant is silent in this conversation. If a colleague joined a moment earlier, you see *Someone else took\nthis conversation — refresh* (409) instead; two people never hold one conversation."],[4305,"The divider **Returned to the assistant**, the handler back to *Assistant*, the composer closed, the inbox chip\nreading **AI** again. **Resolve** instead closes the conversation; it requires a topic (422 without one) because the\nreason is what Quality and the NexBI datasets are built on."],[5460,"The dock menu shows your name, e-mail and workspace, **Account** and **Sign out**; **Account › Profile** reads\nyour role and clearance with *set by your organization's administrators*."],[5442,"The dock menu: **Olena Shevchenko · olena\\@northwind.example · Workspace · Northwind Traders**, then\n**Account**, &#x2A;*Settings…**, **Keyboard shortcuts**, **Help & support**, **Terms of use**, **Administration**, and\n**Sign out** at the bottom. *Settings* and *Administration* are the organization's; *Account* is hers."],[3459,"the dot is `aria-hidden`; the label is the status"],[4106,"The draft opens in **edit mode**."],[5105,"The drafted skeleton has three parts — **Goal**, **Procedure** (numbered steps) and **Output** — and you are meant to\nrewrite them, not keep them. A review that reads \"the procedure is still the generic skeleton\" is a fair one."],[5809,"The drop zone now reads **northwind-framework-agreement-2027.pdf · 65.1 KB**, the box is ticked and &#x2A;*Add source →**\nhas turned black. Press it. The button reads &#x2A;Uploading…* for a moment, the dialog closes, and the **Uploads** row\nshows one more document. Repeat for `acme-q3-2026-delivery-report.md`."],[807,"The editor changes a proposed column role (human-only) — refused unless the role is in the column's eligible_roles (422 ROLE_NOT_ELIGIBLE); outcome role_changed (human_explicit) on the bi.model_proposal record; the entity in the model is updated when the proposal is already accepted."],[5381,"The effective Blueprint of the organization now lists **modules enabled: map · care · forge**, each with the\nlayer that enabled it. This list is what every module API reads before it answers anything: `map-api`,\n`care-api` and `forge-api` ask core-api for the organization's effective Blueprint, cache *enabled* for at most\n60 seconds and *disabled* for at most 5, and answer **404 MODULE\\_NOT\\_ENABLED** when the module is off — or when\ncore-api cannot be reached (*MODULE\\_STATE\\_UNKNOWN*). There is no \"base floor\": an uncertain gate is a closed gate."],[977,"The effective ceilings a Project inherits from its organization."],[1440,"The effective ceilings a Project inherits from its organization."],[12,"The eleven organization presets and the three tiers the server knows today; the four Project relations and their action table (read · write · administer · publish · approve); who may decide an approval and the six answers a decision can get; clearance vs. classification; what an agent can never do; a checklist for administrators."],[2330,"The embedder and the reranker are ordinary entries in `config/synapse/models.yaml` (providers `local_ollama` and\n`local_llama_reranker`); the worker and graph-api reach them only through the Model Gateway, like every other model.\nWithout the specialists the worker parses with fixture parsers — the run page then names `fixture-parser@1` in\n*Processed by* instead of `docling@…`; without the embedder, *Ask the knowledge graph* finds nothing, because a\nfixture vector never matches a real question. The first real run downloads nothing: weights are read from the\nlocal caches only (`HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1`)."],[7055,"The engine (`scenes/engine.py`, pure `apply_batch(spec, ops, limits)`):"],[6612,"The engine attaches the rights chip to every step from the dry run — *you can · needs a Project owner · not possible* — before anyone sees the plan."],[6986,"The engine writes it; nobody edits it."],[48,"The evidence behind a claim moved out of reach"],[5192,"The example — plan a weekend trip"],[4665,"The example appears at the top with a remove button; the empty form waits for the next one (up to 20). The\nintro line says what examples are for, twice over: *few-shot material for the agent* — the agent sees them when\nit applies the skill and imitates the shape — *and regression fixtures for the evaluation suite* — when the\nskill is later checked automatically, these are the cases it must still get right. One good example does more\nthan three more rules."],[3928,"The example is deliberately ordinary — planning a family weekend. Everything you do here is the same for a supplier\nreview or a quarterly report; only the words change. The NexChat guide continues with the same\nProject: an agent, a skill, tools and a flow."],[4389,"The example is still the weekend trip: the agent **Trip planner** in the Project **Weekend\ntrips**."],[5063,"The example is still the weekend trip: the skill **Weekend planning checklist** in the Project\n**Weekend trips**, and the platform skill **Summarize** that every Project can read."],[5663,"The example we follow"],[6476,"The example: a weekend trip"],[6307,"The eyebrow reads **ACME · ITERATIONS**, and the tabs gain **Backlog** and **Iterations**. Health is **At risk —\n14 % of open work overdue or blocked**: two items (ACME-3, ACME-8) block others. **Progress** 0 % — nothing is done\nyet. The **Active** panel names *Sprint 1 · 0 / 5 done · 8 days left*."],[5408,"The field for this is **Work domain** on the create form (previous chapter, step 3). Changing it afterwards is\nthe organization profile under **Settings → Organization**; in this version that screen is not yet connected to\nthe server, so Olena's administrator did it with the API (`PATCH /organizations/{id}` with\n`{ \"domains\": [\"northwind.example\"] }`) — recorded as an open item, see the note at the end."],[735,"The field is remembered in this browser for all playgrounds until you clear it (the **Forget** button above, or the\nbrowser's site data). The **cURL / JavaScript / Python / Go / Java / C# / Rust** tabs next to each operation show\nthe exact request including the header you set — copy them into your tool of choice."],[2115,"The file has five groups. Nothing outside it is configuration; nothing inside it is code."],[4517,"The file is read into a Parquet copy; up to 3 passes — a failed cell is retried with its error."],[5196,"The finished Flow, as an activity"],[5631,"The first gets an honest line — &#x2A;*That is not something the scene can do yet. Try naming an object and what to\nchange.** — never an invented answer. The second resolves *this* from your **selection** (selection beats pointer\nbeats name); with two candidates and no selection the composer asks &#x2A;*Which one?** with a choice card instead of\nguessing. A level-1 move applies at once with Undo."],[3669,"The first level of a page is one underline tab row (`UrlTabs` / `LocalTabs`, state in `?tab=`). The second level is a left column of sections (`SideNav` in a `SideNavLayout`, 200 px, `aria-current`). A segmented control may switch views of the same data (list / board) and sits with the filters, never styled as tabs."],[5064,"The first line of the Overview tab is the whole model in one sentence:"],[5157,"The first row, written when you pressed *Draft skill*."],[2317,"The first run takes a few minutes: it creates a Python virtual environment per API with `uv`, copies each app's\n`.env.example` to `.env`, starts the three containers, creates the databases and roles (including `nexus_graph` with\nthe `age` and `vector` extensions, and `nexus_dagster` for the worker's own bookkeeping), runs every database\nmigration, then starts the processes in dependency order — core-api, chat-api and its worker, tasks-api, graph-api,\nbi-api, map-api, care-api and its worker, forge-api, the sandbox manager, the Dagster worker, the speech sidecars if\ninstalled, the eight web apps — and tails their logs. The module APIs start with their demo worlds on\n(`MAP_DEMO_WORLD=1`, `CARE_DEMO_WORLD=1`; Forge's is off) so the module chapters can be walked on a fresh\norganization; the packs still have to be installed in NexCore before a tile appears. On its first start with an\nadministrator it also runs the product-metrics measurement that seeds NexBI's platform dashboards.\nSubsequent runs take seconds. The script is idempotent: a `.env` you already have is never overwritten, only\ncompleted with keys a newer version needs."],[3409,"The first screen of an empty organization: one question — start in NEXUS, or connect the system that already holds the customers — as two radio cards and one primary button."],[3414,"The first screen of an empty organization: one question — start in NEXUS, or connect the system that already holds the customers — as two radio cards and one primary button. One door in; no wizard, no tour. Built on `EmptyState` (DS-3011) `variant=\"card\"` with a `starting` list would hide the choice; the radio pair is the choice."],[7245,"the first time a Tool needs your account"],[2914,"The five doors into NEXUS: sign up · sign in · verify · welcome · create an organization — one centred card in the bare shell (`BareShell`: no launcher, no dock), one primary action per card, the platform's offers (Google · the dev inbox) only when it says so; the reason a door is closed is one sentence from the server's reason code. Built on `Field` · `Button` · `LinkButton` · `Restriction`; `.nexus-cc-bare` is the only app-local measure. Not a kit duplicate: the kit has no auth card."],[2909,"The five doors into NEXUS: sign up · sign in · verify · welcome · create an organization — one centred card in the bare shell (BareShell: no launcher, no dock), one primary action "],[4623,"The Flow **Compare cottage offers** shows two **Completed** runs on its Runs tab, each with **Inputs** naming an\nattachment address (`nexus://chat/attachment/att_…`)."],[7568,"The Flow Auto hands a message to when nothing in the Project fits: it surveys what exists and what you may do, proposes a plan you accept, change or decline, and asks the right people for connections and tools."],[4083,"The Flow is an ordinary Draft: a trigger, one or two tool nodes, no model. **Publish** in Flow Studio starts the\nschedule; the automations registry updates on the next **Sync** (or when the Flow's events arrive) to *Published*\nand shows *Last run* after the first tick. **Run now** on a published automation starts a run immediately, as you.\nAn `action` node — *do something else when the alert fires* — is refused for BI templates (*422*): they read and\npost, nothing more."],[5041,"The Flow stops at its approval node."],[6378,"The Flow, node by node"],[4861,"The Flow's own Inspector: **Name**, **Description**; **Configuration** — *Trigger · Steps 4 · External writes 0 ·\napproval required*; **Guardrails** — **Runs as** *the person who starts it* (the Flow acts with the rights of its\ninitiator, never more), **Max run duration 168 h**, **Governance** *Not reviewed*. *External writes 0* is worth a\nsecond look: this Flow changes nothing outside Nexi yet — the calendar entry is for a later version, when you add\na tool step and policy will require the approval before it."],[5900,"The footer of the reply reads *from the knowledge graph*."],[5646,"The Forge module is installed — Install a module."],[5585,"The form opens and accepts his input (Ollama, `qwen3:0.6b`, *Small Qwen*). On **Add model** the server\nanswers and the panel says, in red, under the roles: &#x2A;*Only an Owner or Admin of the organization registers\nmodels.** The button was not hidden from him; the decision was made where it must be — and it is written to\nthe audit trail as a *Deny*, which you will see in the next step."],[2459,"The four databases"],[9,"The four kinds of identity; the organization as the outer wall (404, not 403); the five checks in order — organization, clearance, identity kind, relation, purpose — as one activity diagram; *administering is not reading*; what each kind of denial looks like on screen; where each right is configured."],[6475,"The four things you build in NexChat, explained with one everyday example — planning a weekend trip."],[15,"The four voices of a refusal; every refusal state in NexChat, NexCore and on approval cards with its real screen, its reason code and who can move it; how the same walls look to a script; the reason-code table."],[890,"The frozen query record — the Canvas *How was this calculated?* tab and the provenance chain (1038)."],[5186,"The full answer below, the route footer as for any turn, the composer back to text. Nothing of the audio remains:\nno column, no log, no trace holds it; the transcript expires after an hour if it was never sent."],[1944,"The full picture of the runtime — applications, services, runtimes, state — is on How Nexi is built. The API every deployment exposes is in API reference. What an operator may and may not do inside a running Nexi is in Access rights."],[6354,"The gate reads only criteria attached to the item — an item with none moves freely."],[6732,"The gate: oracles first, people second, models never"],[7215,"The Gateway has four operations, not one: **inference**, **transcribe** (`asr` role, floor 0.8),\n**synthesize** (`tts` role, floor 0.7) and **vision**. The same eligible-set rule applies — a *confidential* Project\nmust have a local speech route, and a fitness check enforces it. The local routes are two sidecars inside the\ndeployment, reached by core-api only: `asr-local` (faster-whisper, :8090) and `tts-local` (ukrainian-tts, :8091).\nCloud speech models (`gpt-4o-mini-transcribe`, `gpt-4o-mini-tts`) are tier 4 and eligible up to *confidential*; at\n*secret* a non-Ukrainian answer stays text. Audio is never stored by the Gateway or the sidecars — the record holds the\nmodel, duration and confidence, not the words. NexChat's microphone, Talk mode and NexForge's dictation all use these\noperations; see Voice, screen context, search and research."],[4708,"The generated **Name** is taken from the first words of your sentence and is usually awkward."],[2414,"the generated mode-600 `.env`"],[4655,"The generated name is taken from your first words and is usually awkward, like the agent's was. The shortcut is\nwhat people type in the composer to apply the skill directly — `/weekend` — with or without an agent; it must be\nunique in the Project, 2–32 lowercase letters, digits or hyphens. **Tags** are optional labels for finding skills\nlater (lowercase, comma-separated). The header now reads *v0.1.1 · /weekend*."],[1089,"The goal \n\n1.140.0 ( S1). PEP: OpenFGA on (project, actor) and the goal's owner — outside the\nactor's Projects the goal is 404, never 403 (the thread idiom); service and agent identities are refused on every\nwrite (403, recorded). No request text in any payload.\nReturns the GoalProcess with its current status; the card's projection is on the message (`turn_view.goal`)."],[3098,"The goal is the eighth executor on the same turn card with the goal's parts in its slots: the plan with Accept · Change · Not now, the latest result as the body with earlier result"],[3103,"The goal is the eighth executor on the same turn card with the goal's parts in its slots: the plan with Accept · Change · Not now, the latest result as the body with earlier results folded beneath, the coverage line at completion, and the doors (view the plan · stop · pause · resume · open). The turn that opened the goal ends `done` while the goal continues; every later moment updates the same card — never a second card. The edges have no card of their own: a goal in another Project is not found exactly like any other not-found; an archived thread's card is read-only; a question to the running goal is prose in the thread. S8 adds two slots, no new card: the **Situation strip** above the plan — what NEXUS already holds about the subjects of the ask (NexSales · Vibeban · NexCare · artifacts · sources · the people on those records), each line a source word, the record's label and a door; one honest line naming the party when nothing was found; *not checked* for a source that did not answer; a record the person may not read is not a line and not a count — and the **Next line** at the proposal and at completion: 1–3 doors drawn only from found records, installed capabilities or the creation doors (*Create the account in NexSales* · *Add this request to Vibeban*), the colleague suggestion as a sentence then &#x2A;Ask ⟨name⟩*, and the one question &#x2A;What would you like me to do next?*. A drafted artefact's approval ask shows its security table (reads · writes · reaches) and the approval-required line when it reaches out."],[4523,"The goal loop: each pass the **Data scientist** writes the next stage's code, the sandbox runs it, the engine checks the criteria. The last two stages are always an **Insights** table (claim · number · the table or chart it comes from) and a **Suggestions** table (what to look at next, and why)."],[6958,"The governed query engine"],[1834,"The Graph API: sources and versions, runs, the allowed subgraph, evidence, claim review, vocabulary, evidence bundles for NexChat. Owns `nexus_graph` as its own role, row-level security on."],[3629,"The grid every app shares: 52 px rail, 52 px bar, 248 px sidebar (36 / 34 px rows), a 32 × 44 px collapse handle, 32 px rail buttons, 36 / 28 px button heights, 8 px action gap, 400 px drawer, 440 px confirm, 720 px composer, 800 px content. A screen that needs another measure proposes a token."],[5051,"The header — state at a glance"],[4376,"The header — the agent's state at a glance"],[5082,"The header button"],[6236,"The header is one line: the eyebrow **Nexi · CONTINUOUS** (key and work pattern), the name, the classification chip,\nthe &#x2A;Ask about NEXUS Platform…* bar (your question goes to NexChat with this project as context) and the tabs\n**Overview · Board · Milestones · References · Activity · Settings**. *Backlog* and *Iterations* tabs appear only on\nan iterations project."],[5067,"The header is the same on every tab and packs the skill's whole state into two lines:"],[3231,"The header line on its own, for an app that keeps its own page layout."],[4075,"The header line: &#x2A;*New automation ⌄**, a **Kind** filter, the count *0 published · 3 drafts*. The table\n*Automation · Kind · Target · Flow · Last run · Owner*: each row is one Draft Flow — *Late delivery rate > 0.05 ·\nMetric alert · Late delivery rate · ● Draft Flow · — · Alex Rivera*; a *Subscription* of Carrier performance\n(*0 8 \\* \\* 1 · Europe/Amsterdam*); a *Refresh* (*0 6 \\* \\* 1-5 · Europe/Amsterdam*). The **Flow** column is the\ntruth: *Draft Flow* until it is published in Flow Studio, then *Published*, and the *Last run* column fills.\nEmpty state: &#x2A;No automations yet — Create a Draft Flow from a template; nothing runs until it is published in\nFlow Studio.*"],[4170,"The header line: the name, the chips **Certified · v1 · upload · Confidential** (the dataset inherits the Project's\nclassification), the &#x2A;Ask about “Shipments 2025–2026”…* bar. Tabs **Data 189 · Schema 7 · Versions 1 · Used by**.\n**Data** is the current version's rows through your **row policy** — if the semantic model restricts what you may\nsee, the rows you may not see are not there and the count says so. Click a cell (as an editor) to **correct** it:\n*Correct the cell* asks for the new value and a reason (*typo in the source · unit mismatch · late restatement ·\nduplicate row · other*) and **creates version v2** — the current version stays unchanged, the cell is marked\n&#x2A;corrected (proposed)* until a steward re-verifies it, and blocks that *follow the latest version* recompute\nwhile pinned blocks do not."],[4701,"The header shows the Project name, the classification tag and four places: **Chats · Agents · Skills · Flows**.\nThe Agents page is empty — *No agents in this Project yet* — and explains what happens next: &#x2A;Describe what an\nagent should do and Nexi drafts its instructions, knowledge scope and tools for you to review.* Below the empty\nstate, under **Platform**, are the read-only agents your organization already provides (for example *General\nNexi*). You can use them, but you cannot edit them here."],[6032,"The header's &#x2A;*PDF 2 / 2 · printed —** distinguishes the *PDF page* (what the file says) from the *printed page*\n(the number printed on the paper, when the parser finds one); both are kept because citations in the wild use\neither."],[2155,"The Helm chart on any conformant cluster — first on kind or k3d to learn it, then on-prem or on a managed cluster with your own Postgres, secrets, ingress and TLS."],[4917,"The highest data classification the tool is cleared for. A Project above that ceiling cannot use it."],[4432,"The hint under the field is the whole idea in one line: &#x2A;Verified Domain facts are oracle/human-gated; Project\nscope includes proposed claims.* Why Nexi separates the two is the subject of Ontology."],[3339,"The honest state of one write, in the log composer's footer (DS-6107; a FormInspector's footer elsewhere — amended 2026-10-11): draft · saving · waiting for ‹provider› · pending ap"],[3344,"The honest state of one write, in the log composer's footer (DS-6107; a FormInspector's footer elsewhere — amended 2026-10-11): draft · saving · waiting for ‹provider› · pending approval (names the approver) · saved (said only when the source confirmed and returned an id) · rejected (names the field) · conflict (mine · theirs; *Keep mine* · *Take theirs* · *Merge*) · reconciling · not saved (*Try again*) · ‹provider› unavailable · denied (read-only record type). A dot + sentence; `role=\"status\"`, polite for the quiet states, assertive for the ones that need a hand. Not a kit duplicate: `EditBar` (DS-3033) has editing/saving only; the ladder is the write-through contract of a system of record."],[5077,"The human review state *for this exact version*. It changes to *Review pending* the moment you save anything."],[4744,"The idea underneath is short: &#x2A;*an approval is a step, not a message.** The Flow Engine opened a NexTasks item and\nwent to sleep on it; your decision is what wakes the run up, and it is recorded with your name, the time and your\ncomment — forever, next to the step. *Flow orchestrates* — and where the Flow needs a person, a person decides."],[5777,"The idea underneath: **NexGraph defines the scope, Synapse connects, NexCore checks rights** — the first line of the\nwizard. A source is bound to *one* Project and inherits that Project's classification; the pipeline reads it with the\nrights of the Project, never with yours; and the documents it produces are visible to whoever holds a relation to the\nProject, exactly as far as that relation reaches."],[6014,"The idea underneath: **provenance is a span, not a citation**. A claim is not \"from the agreement\"; it is *page 1,\ntable 1, row 3, column 3, this highlighted cell*, in *this* version of *this* file with *this* hash. Whatever NexChat\nlater says about the agreement can be brought back here."],[6049,"The idea underneath: &#x2A;*a model never marks a claim verified.** The extractor proposes; the oracle re-reads the cell\nand checks the arithmetic; a person confirms within a *named scope* — \"transcription and arithmetic, not the\nsupplier's performance\". Every decision records who (or which oracle version) decided, what they looked at, and what\nexactly they vouched for."],[5302,"The idea underneath: &#x2A;*a person is not an organization member until someone in the organization said so.** An\naccount is only an identity; the *invitation* — with a role and a clearance chosen by an administrator — is what\nturns it into membership, and it is spent the moment it is used."],[5854,"The idea underneath: &#x2A;*an answer is a bundle of evidence you may read, plus a model's sentences about it.** Retrieval\nruns under your own rights; a source you may not read is counted and left out, never quoted; a citation the bundle\ncannot back is removed from the reply; a claim in the sources carries the status the oracle or a person gave it,\nnever one the model made up."],[5399,"The idea underneath: &#x2A;*an organization decides who may even ask.** Listing a work domain opens the door to\nrequests from that domain only; each request is still a decision, with a role chosen by the administrator, never\nby the person asking."],[5262,"The idea underneath: &#x2A;*capabilities are authored in NexChat's Studio and governed in Core.** Core decides who\nmay see, use, publish and run a capability and under which ceilings; the instructions, skills and tools inside it\nare the author's business in Studio."],[4579,"The idea underneath: &#x2A;*knowledge belongs to the Project, not to a chat and not to an agent.** A document is pinned\nonce, carries the Project's classification, and is filtered by *your* access at run time — an agent never reads what\nyou could not open yourself."],[5570,"The idea underneath: &#x2A;*registering a model grants nobody anything.** It makes the model *available* to the\norganization; who may reach it is still the intersection of provider, organization, Project, agent, user,\nclassification and Blueprint — the formula printed on the Policy tab."],[4993,"The idea underneath: &#x2A;*the model classifies; deterministic code ranks; the engine records; you can always override.**\nNo route is chosen by a model's free-form reasoning, and no route with side effects starts without a card you press."],[4501,"The idea underneath: &#x2A;*the model writes code and prose; the engine decides and the person publishes.** The agent\nnever sees a cell value — only column names and counts — and never installs, reaches the network or marks a goal\nmet; whether the goal is met is computed from the results; whether anything becomes visible to the Project is a\nhuman's approval."],[5959,"The idea underneath: a run is **a receipt, not a black box**. The interface shows the worker's own execution tree —\nwhich stage, which step, which executor (*Docling*, *GLiNER-X*, *Qwen3 embedding*, the *Pipeline engine*, the\n*Knowledge store*), how long, what came out, what was logged — and nothing in it is generated by a model after the\nfact."],[5916,"The idea underneath: Studio never shows more than **the allowed subgraph** — your Project relations intersected with\nthe scope you picked — and it is honest about what it does not show (*not the whole organization*, *the landscape\nshows the first groups*). It also never hides the state of what you see: every object is *Proposed* until an oracle\nor a person decides."],[6097,"The idea underneath: the vocabulary is **descriptive before it is prescriptive**. Today it shows what the documents\nsay, in the words they use; the *ontology registry* — managed terms, proposals, merges — arrives in a later release\nand will sit on top of the same list, never replace it."],[1823,"The image every sandbox execution runs in. No network, no credentials, read-only."],[1677,"The import job with its diff and problems (ids and paths, never text)."],[6358,"The importer is `POST /tasks/projects/{project_id}/references/import` with a source from\n`…/references/import-sources`: it reads the epic folders — `00-EPIC.md`, `STATUS.md`, `requirements/*.md`,\n`acceptance/*.md`, the test index and the decision records — as a **preview**, then **apply** runs as a job whose progress\nyou follow on `…/references/imports` and `GET /tasks/imports/{import_id}`. Each reference gets a stable\n`external_id` (`REQ-12`, `AC-7`, `DEC-3`, a test id), so a re-sync updates rather than duplicates; the coverage\nfigures are computed from the links between kinds and served by `…/references/coverage`. An item's acceptance is\n**derived, never stored**: `GET /tasks/items/{item_id}/acceptance` walks the item's references — an *epic* reference\nbrings every criterion of that epic, a *story* or *requirement* the criteria one hop away, a criterion itself — and\nreads each one's state from the trace's evidence mark and from any *verifies* link a human attached with\n`POST /tasks/items/{item_id}/references`. The Done gate lives in `POST /tasks/items/{item_id}/move`: without\n`override_reason` the move is refused with **422 ACCEPTANCE\\_OPEN** while any criterion is *open* or *no test*."],[2847,"The inline confirmation: appears where the action was taken, names the effect, one primary, Cancel; `onSubmit` makes it a form (Enter submits); `danger` for the destructive variant with a typed name. Esc cancels; focus moves to the heading."],[2841,"The inline confirmation: appears where the action was taken, names the effect, one primary, Cancel; onSubmit makes it a form (Enter submits); danger for the destructive variant wit"],[5655,"The Inspector for &#x2A;Customer (NODE · PERSON)*: **Object** (position 40, 40 · size 160 × 80), **Geometry** in px —\nX, Y, Z-level, width, depth, height, rotation, primitive *Box* — **Lock**, **Layer** *People*, **Linked** to\nbacklog and knowledge claims, **Relations*&#x2A; (*→ Web app · Communication · uses*). Geometry is real: the same\nnumbers place the object in 3D. The scene panel below holds *Layers*, *Colour key*, *Versions* and *History*."],[6318,"The Inspector gains **Iteration** (*Sprint 1 · Active*) and **Estimate** (*1 pts*). Changing the iteration here is the\nsame operation as the planning pane; setting *No iteration* returns the item to the backlog."],[5545,"The inspector of a *Deny*: Actor *Taras Bondar · Human*, Decision **Deny**, &#x2A;*Reason `NOT_AN_ADMINISTRATOR`**\n— the code the server answered him with — *No state change*, and the correlation id of his request. Nothing\nabout what he would have seen; only that he asked, and why the answer was no."],[6356,"The Inspector of NEXUS-11 shows **85** criteria; the epic’s card on the References tab also says **85**."],[6136,"The Inspector on the right, top to bottom. The title *Cable drums · SHP\\_0163* with the chips **Delayed · Shipment ·\nPontic Cargo**. **Position**: *Where 53.5449° N · 9.9931° E*, *Observed 11 h 25 min ago*, *Received*, *How —\nGeocoded: a place name from an event, resolved to coordinates*, &#x2A;Source carrier-events (fixture)*, *Accuracy ± 500 m*,\n*Inside Hamburg warehouse — receiving zone*. **ETA** *26.09.2026 19:24 UTC · Carrier*. **History**: one event,\n*Received at origin facility · Hamburg warehouse*. **Links**: origin *Lviv warehouse*, destination *Kyiv\nwarehouse*, a document, the task *Follow up delayed shipment*, the hub. Every line says where it comes from: this\nis the data-honesty rule — *how* a position is known is as visible as the position itself."],[6243,"The Inspector opens beside the board; the URL carries `?item=…` so a link opens it directly. **Properties**: Stage,\nPriority, Assignees, Owner, Due, Milestone, Tags — each editable in place when you may edit. **Description** is\nMarkdown. **Children** lists the stories of the epic with their stage (*10 / 11 done*). **Acceptance** — *0 of 85\nverified* — lists the acceptance criteria attached as references, each with the number of tests linked to it; this\nis what the Done gate reads. Below: **References**, **Relations** (*blocks ·\ndepends on · relates to · duplicates*), **Comments** with `@` mentions, and a folded **Details** with the identifiers."],[1398,"The Inspector payload for any knowledge object by URI — one of Claim · NumericObservation · Entity · DocumentItem · SourceVersion · OracleRun · VocabularyTerm · KnowledgeCaptureRecord (discriminated by uri segment). 404 for hidden and for missing alike (no existence leak)."],[5539,"The inspector: **Event** — Actor *Olena Shevchenko · Human*, Resource &#x2A;correlation:e71b9c19-…*, Decision\n*Allow*, &#x2A;*Reason `2:completion,input_messages`** — two payloads, and which ones — and the event id.\n**Change**: *No state change* (a read). **Execution**: the correlation id of the request that produced this\nevent, and &#x2A;*Open execution trace →**. A record you cannot edit and cannot delete, that says an administrator\nread two governed texts at 04:28 and names them."],[5812,"The Inspector: **Uploads · Upload · Project · confidential**, the button **Add document**, and the tabs\n**Overview · Documents · 2 · Access**. Under **Five states** every binding is described the same way, whichever\nkind it is:"],[6104,"The Inspector: a monogram **NO**, **Northwind Traders · Organization · Project**, and the black button **Open in\nStudio**. The facts: **Type** Organization · **Tier** Project · **Status ● Proposed** · **Mentions 4** · **Sources\n2** · **First seen 22.09 23:50** · &#x2A;*Aliases —**. Under **REGISTRY** the honest sentence: &#x2A;A term in use — the\nresolver filed mentions under it. Proposals, merges and managed terms (the ontology registry) arrive with S4.*"],[5838,"The Inspector's **Documents** tab lists both files as **v1**."],[3185,"The interaction is written **in the activity stream**, not in a side panel (proposed 2026-10-11, replacing the S0 FormInspector — the owner found the page overloaded with the panel"],[3190,"The interaction is written **in the activity stream**, not in a side panel (proposed 2026-10-11, replacing the S0 FormInspector — the owner found the page overloaded with the panel open). Closed, it is one quiet line at the top of *Activity* — `+ Log a call, a meeting or a note…`. Open, it is one bordered block: a head (title · `×`), one row of four compact fields — kind · contact · when · outcome (`Field` + `Select compact`) — the summary (the only required field; its hint is the placeholder), an optional *Plan the next step* switch that reveals *next step · due*, and a footer where the save ladder (DS-6102) sits at the left and *Cancel · Save* (`Button size=\"toolbar\"`) at the right. The header's *Log interaction* opens the same composer. With AI off the last line says so (08). Esc closes while nothing is in flight; the composer closes itself once the source confirmed the write. Built on `Field` · `Select` · `Switch` · `Button` · `IconButton` · `Hint`. Not a kit duplicate: `FormInspector` (DS-3032) is a panel; `EditBar` (DS-3033) has no fields."],[5124,"The intro line says what the examples are for: &#x2A;few-shot material for the agent and regression fixtures for the\nevaluation suite.* That is two jobs at once — the agent reads them to understand the expected quality, and the\nevaluation suite replays them to catch regressions when the instructions change."],[5357,"The invitee's card showed the role and clearance you set; opening the link a second time does not offer to join\nagain."],[1722,"The item's activity, newest first."],[6142,"The keyboard sheet: zoom, Go to, the list, the time strip, following an object (`F`), closing panels (`Esc`). The map\nis usable without a pointer; the list is the accessible equivalent of the canvas."],[4463,"The kind of work."],[5691,"The knowledge as a 3-D space, as lanes or as a list: groups → members → one object and its network."],[1761,"The knowledge family — on the laptop today, in the release images next"],[6727,"The knowledge graph — how a document becomes knowledge you can check"],[6369,"The knowledge graph — tiers, layers and stores; the six-stage pipeline; the oracle-or-person\ngate; how NexChat answers from the graph under the asker's rights."],[7674,"The knowledge words — the ones you meet in NexGraph and in an answer *from the knowledge graph*:"],[1946,"The Kubernetes target on Amazon EKS with RDS for PostgreSQL, Secrets Manager through External Secrets, an Application Load Balancer with an ACM certificate, and ECR as the release mirror."],[1759,"The ladder"],[5946,"The landscape is `GET /graph/projects/{project_id}/studio/landscape`: **clusters** (groups) computed over the allowed\nsubgraph — by binding for the Sources lane, by entity type for the Claims lane, claims for the Knowledge lane — each\nwith its counts and verified share, plus the volume between clusters. Entering a group is `…/studio/clusters/{cluster_id}/members`\n(paged; the &#x2A;not the whole …* line is the page telling you so). Focusing an object is `…/objects/{uri}` and its network\n`…/studio/objects/{uri}/nearby` (`kinds`: sources, claims, entities, checks; up to 50 per kind). Every hop of a\nneighbourhood is checked at graph-api's enforcement point: a neighbour you may not read is dropped and counted as\n*truncated*, never leaked as a name. graph-api computes the allowed subgraph server-side from the Project relations\nNexCore reports for you, so the browser never receives an object you may not see. The 3-D view is drawn locally from\nthat same data."],[2257,"The laptop stack exists for one purpose: **changing Nexi itself**. Every API restarts when you save a file, every\nweb app reloads in the browser, logs stream into one terminal. It is not a way to run Nexi for other people —\nthat starts one rung up, with Docker Compose."],[4475,"The largest class of model allowed."],[4484,"The last line is the rule NexChat applies at every single action, written out:\n&#x2A;*CanExecute = user ∩ Project ∩ agent grant ∩ tool policy ∩ classification ∩ deployment.**\nEvery term can only *remove* permission. Nothing on this screen — and nothing an agent says or does — can add one."],[4903,"The last part uses a second, small example — a *Supplier steward* on the review fixture's Suppliers API — because\nthat is where a real approval can be shown end to end. The vocabulary is in\nAgents, Skills, Tools and Flows: &#x2A;Tool acts.*"],[7653,"The launcher a website draws from one script line, opening into the Care chat panel; an installation is the set of origins, languages and modes that allow it."],[5287,"The layer rule is enforced by the server, not the screen: a child layer may set a value only where the parent\nallows a stricter one; a *fixed* base setting cannot be overridden at all. A Project's *Effective policy* is the\nsame chain with the Project as its last layer — which is why the previous chapter's form says *may tighten, never\nloosen*. Publishing a capability is a *publish* action on its Project and requires the **owner** relation;\nauthoring is a *write* and requires **editor** or **owner**; reading is any relation. Agents can never install,\npublish or bind capabilities — only people do, through these actions."],[6158,"The Layers sheet: **Shipments 554 · Vessels 46 · Aircraft 30 · Hubs 23**, then *Tracks*, *Planned routes* and the\nzone layers. The counts are what you may see. Toggle a layer and the map changes at once; the choice travels in the\nURL (`l=`), so a shared link shows the same layers. *Imagery* reads *No scene configured for this area* — raster\nimagery is a later slice."],[5276,"The lead states the model: &#x2A;Base → domain → regulatory → organization → project. Children tighten; nothing\nloosens silently.* Northwind's chain has two dots today — **Nexi Base** (*defines 20 settings*) and\n**Northwind Traders** (*2 overrides · 1 restriction*) — and a summary: *19 inherited settings · 2 organization\noverrides · 7 active restrictions · 0 conflicts*. **Active restrictions** lists the seven ceilings that bind\nevery Project: **Classification ceiling Secret** (set by Northwind Traders when Olena chose *Confidential /\nSecret* on the create form), **Cloud models ≤ Confidential**, **Pinning a model id — Roles only**, **External\nwrite tools — Approval required**, **Builder-only tools — mcp.invoke · http.request**, **Goal completion — Human\ndecides**, **Self-approval — Forbidden** — the last six from Nexi Base. Now the *Effective policy* block of\nAutumn catalogue has its source."],[5327,"The left navigation is the map of this whole guide section: &#x2A;*People, Groups, Projects, Capabilities, Models,\nConnections, Tools, Executions, Access & Policies, Blueprints & Packs, Approvals, Audit, Settings.**"],[6530,"The Let Auto choose chapter reads Auto from the outside — the route line, &#x2A;Why this\nroute?*, the Resolver card. This page is the inside: the pipeline that runs on every message when the selector is on\n**Auto**, why it is built from a small classifier and a lot of deterministic code, and how the *Resolver* extends it\nwithout adding a service. Two architectural points run through it. **Routing is a decision, not a reasoning trace**:\nthe model classifies, code ranks, the engine records the distribution, and there is nothing to store or show but the\nrecord. **When nothing fits, Nexi does not improvise**: it hands the message to a Flow whose job is to find out\nwhat is missing and ask the right person."],[5496,"The list agrees: **Autumn catalogue · 3 members**; General still 1."],[5836,"The list gains a **Project** column: every binding of every Project you hold a relation to, and the base\n**Nexi documentation** once. *Add source* still names one Project — you add to a Project, never to \"all\"."],[4268,"The list of documents, then **Sources: SOP-CUS-01 v2 — Митне оформлення імпорту: чек-лист документів**. The\nassistant answered from the organization's **verified** knowledge slice and nothing else; the source is a claim in\nNexGraph with its version. Had the slice not covered the question, Nova would say so and offer a person — the\ngrounding threshold (`tuning.care.handoff.grounding_min`, 0.6) is a Blueprint knob, not a prompt."],[1400,"The List twin / search (query: q, scope, tier, layer, status, kind, cluster_id, cursor, limit ≤ 100). Lexical + dense search over the allowed set; graph-api never returns objects the caller may not read."],[7032,"The loader (`GET /widget/v1/care.js`, under 10 KB, no framework) draws the launcher and mounts\n`/widget/v1/frame?installation=…`; both are Next routes in `apps/care` — there is no `/widget/v1/*` API."],[5348,"The mail names who invited him, into what, and as which role — *as builder* — and says the two rules of the\nlink: *works once and expires in 7 days*. **Accept the invitation*&#x2A; is the link with the token; the plain\naddress below it is for mail clients that do not render buttons. &#x2A;(The token is masked in this screenshot.)*"],[6135,"The map flies to Hamburg at object level with the marker selected."],[6178,"The map has three time modes — **Now**, **History**, **Playback** — a catalogue of saved views and a catalogue of\nsources. This chapter walks the three, then uploads a five-row CSV and reads what the server did with each row."],[6153,"The Map module is installed — Install a module."],[7649,"The map's URL — centre, zoom, time, layers, selection — with a name, a Project and Private or Project sharing."],[7582,"The mark under a message that began as speech. The audio is gone; the words stay."],[6929,"The marketplace is deliberately small: **search · import · install · remove**, over a local catalogue of\nsigned files; there is no remote registry. Removing a pack flips the switch back and keeps the module's\ncontent read-only in its database; nothing is deleted."],[2467,"The master keys"],[3961,"The menu offers **Project details**, **Pin project** and &#x2A;*Archive project…**. After pinning, a small star\nappears on the Project's row in the sidebar and it stays at the top of your Projects. Pinning is personal —\nyour colleagues' sidebars are unchanged."],[4176,"The metrics defined over the dataset with their status, and the dashboards that read it. Before you correct or\nstop serving a version, this is where you see what will recompute."],[5635,"The mic shows a *T* glyph: the words land **in the field** and no turn runs — **dictation is not a command**\nThe scene snapshot (view, selection, pointer, viewport) is frozen the moment the mic opens so a command\nrefers to what you saw when you started speaking. Clips are at most 30 s, never stored; the transcript is never\npersisted either — only the decision features (language, confidence, duration) are. Voice adds no rights: the\nturn and the apply are the same `forge.scene.edit` as a typed one."],[2033,"The migration Jobs run `alembic upgrade head` against the instance on every release; automated backups with a\n7–35 day window plus a manual snapshot before each upgrade are the whole backup story for the databases."],[4469,"The minimum benchmark score a model must reach for this role."],[6942,"The Model Gateway (NexCare's assistant, NexForge's Scene Agent and dictation)"],[7552,"The Model Gateway and the Connections — the only way agents and flows reach models and external systems. &#x2A;Synapse connects.*"],[7191,"The Model Gateway: you say what you need, not which model"],[182,"The model or tool is not entitled for this classification or Project."],[806,"The model proposal behind a proposal source row (the Studio's 'why this role')."],[2083,"the module APIs; `postgres` must be the `nexus/postgres` image (PostGIS for `nexus_map`); the module web apps are not in the Compose file yet"],[2196,"the module APIs; databases `nexus_map` (PostGIS), `nexus_care`, `nexus_forge` — an external PostgreSQL must offer PostGIS for `nexus_map`; the module web apps join the `web` image in a coming release"],[6905,"The module gate"],[7637,"The module words — the ones you meet in NexMap, NexCare and NexForge:"],[7418,"the module's own API, worker and database"],[51,"The modules — NexMap, NexCare, NexForge"],[1763,"The modules and the speech sidecars — profiles, off by default"],[3946,"The moment you send, three things happen at once."],[6353,"The move is refused with a small door: &#x2A;*“‹n› acceptance criteria are not verified”** — **Move anyway · Keep it here ·\nReview criteria**. *Review criteria* opens the Acceptance section; *Move anyway* asks for a **reason** (up to 500\ncharacters), moves the item, writes the reason into the item's Activity and records an `acceptance_gate` decision\nwith the outcome *gate\\_overridden* by you. Without a reason the server answers **422 ACCEPTANCE\\_OPEN**. An agent\ncannot override the gate at all."],[1754,"The My Work dashboard's project rows ( R2/R3 U13): one progress row per project the actor can see."],[6966,"The NexBI chapters show the application from the outside. This page is the inside, and makes one point\nthroughout: &#x2A;*a number in Nexi is never a model's output.** A metric is a definition in a grammar the engine can\ncompile; a query is typed and becomes SQL the engine writes; a dashboard is a set of references resolved for the\nreader; certification, publication and revocation are human acts. Where a model appears — the NexChat data arm, the\nStudio's *Ask Nexi*, a proposed dashboard — it chooses *which* metric or template, in a recorded decision, and never\ncomputes."],[7029,"The NexCare chapters show the module from the outside. This page is the inside. NexCare\nis `apps/care`, `care-api`, `care-worker` and the `nexus_care` database, installed per organization as a pack\n(Modules). It is the first part of Nexi that talks to people who are **not members** of the organization,\nand that fact shapes everything: a separate trust zone for them, a guardrail on every turn, and a single hand on the\nreply."],[7253,"the NexChat composer"],[7429,"the NexChat Project's relations; human-only publish/delete/export"],[7421,"the NexChat Project's relations; uploads by editors"],[7052,"The NexForge chapters show the module from the outside. This page is the inside. NexForge\nis `apps/forge` over `forge-api` and the `nexus_forge` database, installed per organization as a pack\n(Modules). ADR-0056 fixes the object and the engine, ADR-0057 the turn pipeline and the agent. The\nsentence that organises both: **AI proposes, the person applies**."],[7384,"the NexGraph pipeline from a table cell (proposed); captured Flow outcomes (proposed)"],[3586,"The Nexi glyph and the wordmark it is the capital of: the shell brand row, the rail, the doors, the favicon."],[2088,"The Nexi repository checked out — the Compose file, scripts and image contract live in it — or just the\n`deploy/compose` folder and `deploy/scripts` folder copied over."],[3899,"The Nexi wordmark, the line &#x2A;Build and run governed AI systems.*, a **Continue with Google** button and a black\n**Create account** button. If you already have an account, use the **Sign in** link instead. The note *Your\norganization may require single sign-on* means some companies allow Google or their own SSO only — if the\n**Create account** button is missing, ask your administrator for an invitation."],[7081,"The NexMap chapters show the module from the outside. This page is the inside. NexMap is\n`apps/map` over `map-api` and the `nexus_map` database with PostGIS; it is installed per organization as a pack\n(Modules). Two rules organise it: **the server decides what is drawn**, and **nothing is drawn that is\nnot known** — no guessed position, no silent (0, 0), no number that reveals an object you may not see."],[882,"the NEXUS measurement this deployment holds and whether the organization scope already carries it. Organization scope only (a Project id in its place is 404). Any member (dashboard.read on the organization); dashboard titles only when content is visible."],[6339,"The NEXUS Platform project is the worked example: 11 epics, 112 items, and every requirement, criterion, test and\ndecision of the platform attached to the story it belongs to."],[6458,"The notebook"],[4056,"The number in the answer equals the KPI on *Carrier performance* for the same period and carrier filter."],[7614,"The number words — the ones you meet in NexBI:"],[7043,"The object"],[6957,"The objects"],[7444,"The objects"],[6730,"The objects, from bytes to facts"],[2934,"The one button."],[2940,"The one button. `default` · `primary` (the single most important action on a surface) · `ghost` · `danger` (filled — a confirmation's destructive primary only) · `destructive` (outlined — opens such a confirmation); 36 px on the header line; 32 px with `size=\"toolbar\"` on a toolbar line and in the Inspector footer; 28 px with `size=\"sm\"` for row-level actions; the icon button 28 (32 in the rail). No other size. ≤ 2 visible buttons per header or footer; a toggle is `aria-pressed`."],[7189,"The one gateway between what you build and the outside world — models on one side, your systems and accounts on the other. Continued with the weekend-trip example."],[2514,"The one look of the Nexi suite — its principles, tokens, shell, components and patterns — with every component rendered live in the workshop."],[800,"the one proposal door — Canvas · Chat attachment · Data Scientist receipt · Data screen · Auto resolver propose_dashboard (platform tool bi.dashboard.propose runs as the initiating human). Reads the sources by reference through chat-api under the caller's actor context (FilePort), decides each table's publish rights with the PDP as the person (dry-run, advisory), proposes the model per table, chooses a template (bi.dashboard_proposal record) — WRITES NOTHING but the proposal and its record. 422 PROPOSAL_NO_SOURCE when every source is in cannot[]."],[5049,"The one rule behind every tab"],[5193,"The one scenario every NexChat chapter builds on. Who does what, and what the finished Flow looks like."],[6422,"The one way a run keeps a table: the sandbox writes it, the engine's **MemoryPort** registers it in the Project with its layer (*bronze · silver · gold*), shape, technique and Skill version."],[3121,"The one-line *who may do this* under a row of actions."],[5093,"The one-line promise."],[2511,"The only feature that touches a Nexi is the **API playground**. The portal's small server (`npm start`)\n&#x2A;*forwards `/api/v1/*`** to the origin in `NEXUS_API_ORIGIN` — and `/api/v1/graph/*` to `NEXUS_GRAPH_ORIGIN`, because\nNexGraph's web origin is the one that routes the Graph API (default `http://127.0.0.1:3214`; on a deployment where one\norigin serves everything, set it to the same value or `off`) — so a request from the playground reaches Nexi as a\nsame-origin call and Nexi needs no CORS grant. The reader's *sign-in* travels along only when the portal is served\non **the same host name** as Nexi (a different port is fine — a browser keeps cookies per host name, not per\nport): `https://nexus.example.com:8443` next to `https://nexus.example.com` works; `docs.nexus.example.com` does not\nsee the cookie, and readers there paste a token they minted in NexCore instead (**Get my token now** on the\nAPI reference, or `curl` as described on Authenticate your API calls).\nWith `NEXUS_API_ORIGIN=off` nothing is forwarded; the playground then calls the server listed in the contract\ndirectly, which requires the portal's origin in the API's `CORS_ORIGINS`. Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_NEXUS_CORE_URL` at build\ntime so *Open NexCore* points at yours."],[6406,"The only way code runs: a cell in the Sandbox Runtime under a profile."],[7185,"The ontology registry on top of the vocabulary — managed terms, proposals, merges, versioned snapshots; Memory (captured outcomes of runs as proposed knowledge) beyond preview"],[966,"The optional change note, after the fact (documented in 1.139.0)"],[6804,"the order"],[192,"The order in which these checks run — and why *organization* comes first — is drawn in\nHow Nexi decides what you may do."],[1749,"The ordered stages (archived included when `include_archived`)."],[5499,"The organization **Overview** closes the loop: the Nexi pulse counts **Projects 2**."],[215,"The organization is the outer wall"],[30,"The organization-wide screens"],[7417,"the organization's Blueprint (`modules.enabled`)"],[3277,"The organization's runtime as one line — Projects ─ Capabilities ─ Models ─ Connections; filled dot healthy, hollow an issue; `live` runs a subtle pulse (reduced motion off)."],[3272,"The organization's runtime as one line — Projects ─ Capabilities ─ Models ─ Connections; filled dot healthy, hollow an issue; live runs a subtle pulse (reduced motion off)."],[5930,"The organizations of the Base tier are what the platform documentation talks about — *Core*, *Synapse*,\n*Keycloak*, *Google*. Our carrier is among them; the quickest way to it is the search box."],[7480,"The original noun: a parked side effect or a Flow `approval` node waiting for a person."],[5388,"The other way into an organization — no invitation, a colleague types the organization's handle and asks. See why the request is refused until the owner lists the work domain, how the request appears under People › Requests, how the owner chooses a role and approves, and what the newcomer sees the moment it happens. About ten minutes for two people."],[5666,"The Overview"],[5261,"The Overview of Northwind Traders said *nexus-base v1.0.0 installed: 5 agents · 10 skills · 14 flow templates* the\nmoment Olena created it. This chapter is where those things live and what Core knows about them. You will read\nthe **Capabilities** registry, open the agent **General** and its tabs, walk the **Tools** table, and then read the\n**Blueprint** — the layered set of ceilings every Project inherits, which you met as *Effective policy* in the\nprevious chapter — in its Overview, its Matrix and its Packs. Nothing is changed; the point is to know what is\nalready true before anyone builds on it."],[5355,"The Overview's **Getting started** shows *Organization created — Done* with the installed pack."],[6257,"The Overview's **Progress** equals *Done* over all items on the Board (62 / 101 on NEXUS Platform — epics excluded from the total)."],[7438,"the owning app's door"],[5376,"The pack page: version, signer, the line *provides module NexMap*, what it requires (platform tools such as\n`task.create`, which NexMap's Inspector will call once its task action leaves the prototype stage), and\n**Install**. Nothing is enabled until you press it."],[2053,"The packaged product on one machine — signed images, one generated .env, one public port. For trials, demos, small teams and air-gapped sites."],[6018,"The page in the middle is the document as Docling read it — headings **1. Scope · 2. Term · 3. Rates · 4. Service\nlevels · 5. Volume**, the rates table with its **Lane · Distance · Rate per FTL · Temperature-controlled** columns.\nEvery underlined span is a **mention**: *Taras Bondar*, *Procurement Director*, *Northwind Traders GmbH*,\n*Hamburg*, *1 January 2027*, *24 months*, *720 EUR*."],[4210,"The page is `GET /bi/projects/{project_id}/dashboards/{dashboard_id}/render` with the filters as query parameters.\nFor every block bi-api resolves the reference under **your** principal — the metric's read right, the dataset's read\nright and classification, the **row policy before aggregation** — compiles a typed **BIQuery** into parameterised SQL\n(there is no text-to-SQL anywhere), runs it under the read-only `bi_query` role with an 8-second timeout, a 1 000-row\ncap and an EXPLAIN cost guard, caches the result **per viewer** and keeps a **query record** so &#x2A;How was this\ncalculated?* can be answered