** — and the\n**Endpoint** `http://127.0.0.1:11434` (*where the runtime listens inside your network*). **Classification\nceiling** stays *Confidential*; **Roles** keeps *chat* ticked. The footer says the thing to remember:\n&#x2A;Registering a model does not grant anyone access: projects and groups are assigned in the model's policy.*"],[2907,"the panel is a named `dialog`-less region with one polite live region for the answer; Esc and × close and return focus to the bar; the proposal's three decisions are reachable by Tab in order"],[6322,"The panel lists every **unfinished** item and asks for a **disposition**: *Return to backlog* or *Move to next*\n(a named planned iteration). The template's *incomplete behaviour* — *ask* on software-delivery — decides whether a\ndefault is preselected; either way the request is refused until every item has one (*422 DISPOSITION\\_REQUIRED*).\nEach disposition is recorded as an `iteration_carryover_default` decision with both arms and the one you chose. A\ncompleted iteration is immutable for planning; its history stays under **Past**."],[4266,"The panel: the avatar **N**, the name **Nova** and one disclosure line — **AI agent** — then the greeting &#x2A;Hi, I'm\nNova, the SupplyChain Guru assistant. Ask me about a shipment, customs paperwork, a document or a claim.*, the\nmessage box and the foot *Service by Nexi Care*. The disclosure is the only robot mark you will see: bubbles\ncarry no stamp. Behind the scenes the loader minted a **care session** for this origin — a bearer the browser\nholds, hashed on the server, alive 60 minutes sliding and 24 hours at most."],[4975,"The parked call becomes an **approval card** in the thread, for the people who may decide."],[5694,"The parsed page with every mention, entity and claim anchored to its exact span."],[6377,"The parts"],[4274,"The pending notice at the top: &#x2A;*A colleague is on the way — usually within the hour. Keep writing; they'll see\neverything.** The message box stays open. On the desk the conversation now shows *Handoff* and waits for a person\nto **Join** — the next chapter picks it up from there."],[4943,"The permission the *person* must hold for the call to be allowed."],[607,"The person is not in the organization, or the request is above their clearance"],[6998,"The person publishes the Flow in Flow Studio; NexBI reflects its state."],[7636,"The person who certifies metrics and acknowledges revocations (`metric_steward`); owners until one is named."],[6568,"The person…"],[7109,"the person's next zoom (implicit)"],[1636,"The personal work Inbox: assignments · mentions · reviews · approvals (from `GET /tasks/approvals?status=pending`, decided in place) · due · blocked · agent results · shared; ranked with My Work's decision."],[6752,"The physical shape, all inside PostgreSQL."],[7115,"the pick"],[7507,"the pick"],[4612,"The picker lists the published Flows of the Project with their description and how many inputs they take, and\nsays how a Flow behaves in a chat: &#x2A;A flow runs as its own turn; the answer follows the run.* Pick **Compare\ncottage offers**."],[1587,"The picker of the bind panel ( D): the published, unblocked Agents and Flows the CALLER may run for this scope — read through tasks-api's runtime port with the caller's own bearer, never stored, never the service's view. Bind-level access on the scope (`scope_ref`, REQUIRED)."],[2966,"The picker on the composer's surface: field-like trigger, list opening downward, sections, descriptions, disabled options that say why, type-ahead, Esc / Enter / arrows."],[2972,"The picker on the composer's surface: field-like trigger, list opening downward, sections, descriptions, disabled options that say why, type-ahead, Esc / Enter / arrows. `Select` wraps it; the composer pickers use it directly."],[1947,"The picture"],[4726,"The pill changes to **Published**, the version counter increases once more, and **Publish** disappears from the\nheader — only **Test in chat** remains. From now on anyone in *Weekend trips&#x2A; can type &#x2A;*@** in the composer and\npick *Trip planner*. Editing the agent again creates a new draft version; the published one keeps working until\nyou publish the next."],[4674,"The pill reads **Published** and the version jumps to **v0.2.0**: drafts count up the last number (0.1.1,\n0.1.2 …), publishing raises the middle one. The review travels with it — *Reviewed · v0.2.0*, same notes — so\nwhat was approved is exactly what was published. On **Versions** the whole history is listed, newest first.\nFrom now on `/weekend` works in every chat of the Project."],[4872,"The pill turns **Published**; the modify box at the bottom is gone and a note on the left edge explains why:\n&#x2A;Published versions are immutable — use \"Ask Nexi to modify\" to draft the next one.* The trigger is now\n**armed** — from this moment the Flow will start by itself every Thursday at 18:00, as the person who published\nit. Publishing is the moment a Flow becomes real; only a Project owner can do it."],[6805,"the pinned bytes, sanity-checked (size, type)"],[6524,"The pipeline, stage by stage"],[6731,"The pipeline: six stages, one receipt"],[1840,"The pipeline's own UI. Never behind the public origin."],[4105,"The plan is a `dashboard_plan` decision: the template candidates, their scores and the one chosen are recorded, and\nwhat you keep or drop is written back as its outcome."],[6438,"The plan's current stage and criteria"],[1805,"The Platform API: sessions, organizations, access policy, capability catalog, models, connections, audit."],[3588,"The platform is **Nexi**; its mark is `BrandMark` in `@nexus/ui` — a stroked N whose diagonal is a curve, with a dot at its centre, drawn in `currentColor` (the nexiflow\\.ai glyph). The wordmark is **one word whose capital is the glyph**: `BrandWordmark` draws the N at cap height on the baseline and `exi` in the row's bold type (16 px in the shell, 26 px on the doors) — never a mark beside a typed `Nexi`. Expanded shell brand row: the wordmark; NexCore follows it with the app name in tracked uppercase, NexChat ends the row with the Search icon. Collapsed rail: the bare glyph in a 32 px target. The unauthenticated doors (NexCore sign in · sign up · verify · welcome): the wordmark alone as the h1. Every application's favicon: the glyph white on a graphite rounded square (`src/app/icon.svg`). The letter N stays in the DOM, visually hidden, so assistive technology reads \"Nexi\". Applications keep their short names (NexChat · NexCore · NexBI · NexTasks · NexMap · NexCare · NexSales · NexForge · NexGraph); the wordmark is never translated and never written in capitals in copy (`Nexi`, not `NEXI`). Identifiers stay `nexus` (`@nexus/*`, `.nexus-*`, `nexus://`)."],[5109,"The platform skills are good models for this style; here is the real **Summarize** skill:"],[637,"The playground talks to Nexi **through this portal** (same origin, `/api/v1`), and Nexi recognises you by the\nsession cookie NexCore set when you signed in. Cookies belong to a host name, not a port — so the portal keeps\nitself on the host name NexCore uses (open it on `localhost` and it moves you to `127.0.0.1`, or the other way\nround, whichever Nexi runs on), and the **NexCore** link in the helper points at that same host. Sign in there,\ncome back to this tab: the first dot turns green by itself (the helper re-checks when you return, and every few\nseconds until it sees you). **Check my sign-in** forces a check and stamps the time it ran."],[5853,"The point of a knowledge graph is to be asked. In NexChat you do not do anything special: you ask a question in a\nProject chat, **Auto** recognises that it is about the Project's documents or about the platform itself, and answers\n**from the knowledge graph** — with numbered citations, a **Sources** list and a drawer that shows the retrieval step\nby step. This chapter asks one question and reads everything the answer carries."],[6793,"The pointer every object carries back to its item, with a precision: *Exact span · Approximate location · Document-level · Unresolved*."],[7437,"the policy decision point on the exact target, as the person"],[152,"The policy engine or its signed bundle is not available: Nexi fails closed and refuses every protected operation rather than guessing."],[4999,"The popover is the decision record, section by section. **Intent** — what the classifier read and how sure\n(*Data query · 0.95*). **Selected** — the capability. **Tools offered** — for an agent, the tools it was given this\nturn. **Why** — the ranking reasons as ✓ / ! lines: *best match for the request · you may run it · classification\nallowed · this thread already runs with it (sticky) · required tools available*. **Model*&#x2A; — *… selected by\nSynapse*. **Skipped** — every eligible candidate that lost and the one reason each: *needs an input this message\ndoes not have · no model for its role · asks for a side effect you did not mention · not in this Project*.\n&#x2A;*Try another route ▾** lists the alternatives; picking one reroutes the same message and writes your choice back\nas the outcome of the first decision. *Candidates considered: n* and the footer &#x2A;Structured decision record — no\nmodel reasoning is stored or shown.*"],[690,"The portal could not reach Nexi."],[698,"The portal's server forwards `/api/v1/*` to one origin — by default the local NexCore dev stack\n(`http://127.0.0.1:3212`). Point it elsewhere with an environment variable:"],[317,"The preset for people who author agents, skills, tools and flows in the Projects they belong to — their Project relation (editor or owner) is what actually allows it. Intended holder of the builder-only tools (`http.request`, `mcp.invoke`)."],[320,"The preset for people who run and watch flows in the Projects they belong to; their Project relation decides whether they may run."],[3551,"The principle is DS-0006 — Honest copy, two languages, one card;\neach component page lists its copy keys. Conversation surfaces — the composer, the thread, the cards — follow the\nConversation Register as well; this section describes how they look, not what they say."],[2543,"The principle is DS-0008 — Keyboard and screen reader first;\neach component page has an *Accessibility* section with its own contract."],[2166,"the processes; each API pod has a `migrate-wait` initContainer that blocks until its schema is at head"],[2159,"The production switch"],[4240,"The profile business users change: the **name customers see**, languages, **formality** *friendly*, **warmth**\n*very warm*, **brevity** *concise*, greeting, sign-off and handoff phrase, the **Never answers about** topics,\nrefusal style, disclaimers — *Draft v8 · Published v7*, **Save draft** and **Compile**. Compile turns the profile\ninto a governed Agent draft; a second person reviews it before it is published, as with every agent (ADR-0023 §9)."],[7341,"the Project"],[6652,"the Project (agents, Flows) · packs · NexCore catalog"],[4745,"The Project **Family weekends** with the published Flow **Plan the weekend** and one run **Waiting for approval**\n— where the previous chapter ended. Any published Flow with an approval step and a waiting run will do."],[5500,"The Project created in NexChat is in Core's **Projects** list within a refresh, with the organization's\nclassification and pack and **1 member**."],[4073,"The Project has a thread that can receive messages — a Subscription delivers **only** into a Project thread; there is\nno e-mail or webhook delivery in this slice."],[7397,"the Project; a human publishes with the acknowledgement"],[7357,"the Project; approvals in NexTasks"],[1634,"The project's Activity feed, newest first."],[4045,"The Project's Blueprint enables the data arm (`data_arm` is on in the base Blueprint). The thread's mode is **Auto**."],[5703,"The Project's capture policy: whether outcomes of Agent and Flow runs become proposed knowledge."],[1274,"The Project's CapturePolicy."],[7377,"the Project's classification"],[7389,"the Project's classification; row policies; a human publishes and revokes"],[7381,"the Project's classification; the binding's five states"],[341,"The Project's creator and anyone they make co-owner"],[3244,"The Project's door to its artifacts, with no tab of its own: the Project name menu (● ‹name› ▾) carries *View artifacts · ‹n›* after *Project details*; the details line repeats the"],[3249,"The Project's door to its artifacts, with no tab of its own: the Project name menu (● ‹name› ▾) carries &#x2A;View artifacts · ‹n›* after *Project details*; the details line repeats the count with the same door."],[1751,"The project's item types."],[5682,"The Project's knowledge at a glance: pulse (sources → documents → claims → verified), counters, datastores by tier, the pipeline of the last 24 h, what needs attention."],[4429,"The Project's own graph, **including proposed claims** — things a model extracted that no person has confirmed yet. Faster, richer, less certain; the agent must label them as proposed (rule 2)."],[898,"The Project's semantic model (organization-scoped models are read through the organization route later)."],[4437,"The Project's setting."],[801,"The proposal as proposed — the card and the Studio Proposal panel read it; a proposal of a project the actor is not in is 404."],[6616,"The Propose card. Nothing runs, is created or requested before Accept. *Change* re-plans once. A viewer sees the card without buttons."],[4919,"The protocol behind a connected tool; platform tools show none."],[889,"THE query door (1033, /1107): BIQuery → validate against the semantic model → deterministic compiler → parameterised SQL under the read-only role with statement_timeout, row and cost guards → BiQueryRecord (+ ChartSpec when recommend_chart). 422 QUERY_UNRESOLVED ⇒ clarification, never a guess. 429 QUERY_BUDGET · 504 QUERY_TIMEOUT."],[6861,"The question's n-grams are matched to entities — the anchors for a graph hop."],[6084,"The queue is `GET /graph/projects/{project_id}/review` (`state` filter → All / Contested / Proposed / Decided). A\ndecision is `POST /graph/projects/{project_id}/claims/{claim_id}/verify` with the `scope` (the oracle types the person\nvouches for), a required `comment` and the acknowledgement; `…/return` with a `reason` code; `…/reverify` to ask the\noracles to run again. graph-api enforces three things before it writes: the caller is a **human** identity\n(`AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN` otherwise — an agent acting for an owner is still refused), the caller holds the editor/curator\nrelation on the Project, and the claim is not in the Base tier. The decision is recorded twice — as an **OracleRun**\nof type *human\\_review* with a human actor on the claim (that is the *Curator: confirmed* line in History), and as a\n**decision record** whose outcome, with `label_source = human_explicit`, is written back to the extractor's original\n`decision_id` — which is how a curator's corrections become training data for the platform's own models without any\nmodel ever being the judge. The oracles' verdicts carry `label_source = oracle` and the oracle's version\n(`graph-oracle-calc@1.0.0`). A Project's Blueprint may require that a human verdict itself passes an approval: the\ndecision is then parked as a NexTasks approval and the API answers `202` until it is approved."],[6079,"The queue's **Contested 1** row: **On-time deliveries · 92,4 % vs 96,1 % · Contested claim**, with two documents\nin its Context. The Inspector reads **Subject · Contested**; its **Claim** tab shows **WHAT THE SOURCE STATES**\n(the sentence in a supplier's e-mail), the facts — **Metric** On-time deliveries · **Value** 96,1 % · **Period** Q2\n2025 (per supplier mail) · **Method** text mention — and **CONTESTED WITH**: two cards, &#x2A;*96,1 %** from the\nsupplier's e-mail and &#x2A;*92,4 %** from the quarterly report, and the hint &#x2A;Two source assertions, one canonical\nclaim pending. Compare period and denominator before deciding.*"],[4107,"The rail collapses to icons; the header line becomes the Studio's: *Carrier performance · Published · v2 · Edit*,\n**Add block**, the **Coverage** icon (badge: uncovered slots), the **Advisor** icon (badge: open suggestions),\n**Save draft**, **Publish**, close (✕) and ⋯. The filter row gains **Set as default** and **Add filter**. Every block\nshows its kind chip — *Metric · Text · Chart · Table · Section* — and a resize handle; drag to move, `/` on the grid\nto add. The draft autosaves as you go; *Save draft* is the explicit checkpoint."],[6033,"The rail counts **Mentions 80 · Entities 59 · Fragments 8** and the run reads **Completed**."],[50,"The reason codes"],[4758,"The reason. A tool call's card would say what the tool is about to change; an approval node simply asks."],[4532,"The receipt: **✓ Agentic Data Scientist · 8 stages · 7 passes · 8 m 40 s · criteria 6 / 6 · complete**. Every\nstage ticked with its sentence — **Duplicates — 723 candidate groups · 1 512 rows — nothing removed**, **Unit\nnames — 472 spellings → 288 canonical · 17 unmatched**, **Geography — 9 directions · 10 distance bands · no\ncoordinates**, &#x2A;*Charts (≥ 4) — 4 charts · 2 draft(s)**, **Report — 3 pages · cites every artifact**. Then\n**DRAFTS · 9**: the notebook, **Dataset profile**, **Proposed indices**, **Possible duplicates · v2**, the tables,\nthe charts (**Score by direction · Chart · v1**), each with **Draft · Preview · Open in Canvas**."],[6566,"The record is the product: it is what &#x2A;Why this route?* renders and what a future decision model trains on."],[6658,"The record's contract: `GET /chat/routes/{route_id}` in the Chat API."],[7564,"The recorded choice under an answer — *Auto → Analyst · model · runtime* — and the door to &#x2A;Why this route?*, the decision record with every candidate."],[5593,"The registry is core-api's: `GET /synapse/models` returns the deployment's seed models (from `models.yaml`) plus\nthis organization's registrations, each with `endpoint_kind`, `roles`, `tier`, `classification_max`, `status`.\n**Add model** is `POST /synapse/models` with `{ display_name, model, provider: { provider_id | type + base_url | type + api_key },\nroles, classification_max? }`; the server creates a **provider** (`local-<host>-<port>-…`) and a **registration**\n(`GET /synapse/model-registrations` lists what the organization added, `has_credential` says whether a key is\nsealed), probes the provider (`POST /synapse/providers/{id}/health-check`), and writes an audit event. An API key,\nwhen given, is sealed by the Credential Broker and stored as a reference; the response never contains it, and the\nform clears the field. `PATCH /synapse/models/{id}` toggles `status`; `DELETE /synapse/models/{id}` removes the\nregistration and, with the last model on it, the provider and its sealed key. Registering, toggling and deleting\nare **administer** actions on the organization's connections — hence the Builder's *Deny* row reads *Administer ·\nconnection \\_all*. NexChat's `GET /chat/models` is this registry read as the caller's organization and filtered by\navailability, so a new or deleted model changes the Composer's picker on the next read."],[5859,"The reply — here, on the platform's fixture stack, the platform question about Drive binding states — ends with a\nfigure and its caption (*The Sources screen with a Google Drive binding and its Inspector*) drawn from the\ndocumentation itself, then **SOURCES**: a numbered list, one entry per `[n]` in the text. Each entry has a title\nand a **kind** — **1 Google Drive binding states · section**, **2 Binding states · table**, **3 A needs\\_auth\nbinding resumes on its own once the connection is re-authorised · claim · Open claim**, **4 Sources — a Google\nDrive binding · figure**. The footer of the answer: *from the knowledge graph · confidential* and &#x2A;*Why this\nanswer?**; underneath, the usual **copy · thumbs · Branch · Regenerate**."],[6624,"The report: what was done, what was skipped and why, what was created — from the engine's record, not from memory."],[149,"The request asks for something the platform ceiling never allows — or, in NexGraph, a capture policy that would widen a tier."],[611,"The request is already decided, withdrawn or expired"],[5889,"The reranker model scored every candidate against the question."],[5040,"The research cue (*research · investigate · find out about … and tell me*; en/uk/de) routes to the **Resolver**,\nwhose plan card reads *Plan · 1 steps* with the step *Research Kyiv Metro opening and lines · not started*,\n**Accept · Change · Not now**, and &#x2A;Nothing runs, is created or requested before you accept.* Accept starts the base\npack's **web-research Flow** as a child run: plan → search → scope → **allow** → reading loop → narrate → report."],[6526,"The Resolver — a Flow, not a router"],[6593,"The Resolver is the pack Flow `flw_tpl_auto_resolver` from **nexus-base**, published into a Project like any other.\nAuto calls it when the ranking finds nothing; it could equally be run by hand. It is made of the same parts as every\ncapability in Nexi and adds nothing to the platform."],[158,"The resource belongs to another organization. Shown as *Not found*."],[146,"The resource's *state* refuses, not your rights."],[6194,"The result in four chips: **3 placed · 1 without position · 1 rejected · CSV**. The rejected row is listed with its\nreason — *coordinate out of range* — and the note: &#x2A;Nothing is drawn at (0, 0). Objects without coordinates are\nlisted, not placed.* The (0, 0) row became *without position*; the swapped-axes row was placed where it said, in\nthe sea — the server does not guess at intent, it reports. Sixteen reject reasons exist; each is one phrase."],[4137,"The result is a **Draft**: it exists, dashboards cannot resolve it yet, and the Overview lists it under *Needs\nattention* — *no dashboard or plan resolves it until it is validated*."],[249,"The reverse holds too: a Project owner governs their Project fully — members, agents, flows, approvals — and sees\nnothing of the organization's other Projects, nor Executions, nor Audit."],[3139,"The right-hand detail panel: the head owns kind · title · one line of subtitle (13 px secondary, 4 under the title) / avatar · primary · `⋯` · close, 20 px inset, **16 above and below the head rule**; optional tabs; sections; body rows 4 apart; a sticky footer (rule · 12 · action · 12). 360–640 px by a keyboard separator (← → 16 px, Home / End, double-click resets), width persisted as `--inspector-width`; Esc closes and focus returns to the opener. Every vertical measure from DS-1011."],[3133,"The right-hand detail panel: the head owns kind · title · one line of subtitle (13 px secondary, 4 under the title) / avatar · primary · ⋯ · close, 20 px inset, **16 above and belo"],[278,"The roles Core lets you give a person, what each one really unlocks today, the four relations a person can hold in a Project and the action table they map to, who may decide an approval, and why an agent is never a decider."],[7017,"The routing side: Auto — how Nexi picks the capability."],[4967,"The row is gone at once; the agent keeps only **Project search**, and the version counter has moved again. Removing\na tool is not destructive — the tool still exists in the registry; only this agent's binding is gone. Tools the\nTrip planner does not need are tools it cannot misuse, so prune freely."],[4606,"The row now reads **cottage-offers-autumn.txt · 520 B · confidential**. Three things happened the moment you\nchose the file: it was uploaded to the Project as an **attachment**, it was **pinned** as a source of the Project\nwith the Project's classification, and the field was filled with the attachment's address — the only kind of value\na `file` input accepts. The × removes the pin again if you picked the wrong file. Press **Run**."],[3491,"The row of search · filters · primary action above a list — rendered only when `showListControls(total, active)` is true: more than 12 rows, or a control in use."],[3486,"The row of search · filters · primary action above a list — rendered only when showListControls(total, active) is true: more than 12 rows, or a control in use."],[2516,"The rule in one sentence"],[4907,"The rule of the tab in one line — *At run time the agent can only use what you, the Project and policy all allow —\na binding never elevates anyone* — then &#x2A;*No tools bound. The agent can answer from knowledge only.*&#x2A; and a\n**+ Add tool** button. Read the rule twice: a tool you attach here runs with the rights of the *person chatting*,\ninside the *Project's* classification, under *policy*. Attaching it changes what the agent can try, not what\nanyone is allowed."],[4878,"The run bar reads **Waiting · Pass 3 / 6 · … · Waiting for approval: Review results**, with **Cancel run** and\n**Details**. The loop ran its passes as before; then the Flow reached **Review results** and stopped — an amber dot,\n*Waiting for approval*. **Done** has not run. A NexTasks item titled *Agentic result for Plan the weekend — review\nbefore publishing* now exists for the Project owner, with three days to decide — you meet it, as a card on this\nrun, in the next chapter. Approve, and the run completes; reject, and it completes by the *Rejected* arrow; do\nnothing, and after three days the run **fails**, as the approval's *On timeout* says. This is the difference\nbetween a test and a run in one picture."],[5043,"The run completes."],[5995,"The run in our example has nothing to retry. When you do retry, only the failed stage and those after it run\nagain, against the same pinned bytes; a step that would produce the same object recognises it and does not\nduplicate it."],[5997,"The run of the agreement reads **Completed** with **Claims 8 · 8 verified**."],[5998,"The run of the report (`acme-q3-2026-delivery-report.md`) reads **Completed** with **Claims 20** (five rows × four\nnumeric columns); its **Verify** step shows *Verified 15 · falsified 5* — the Review chapter\nexplains why the *On-time rate* column came back falsified."],[6832,"The run page in NexGraph renders the worker's own **RunStep** records — executor kind and version, timings, produced\ncounts, structured log lines — so what you read there is the receipt, not a summary. *Retry failed stages* re-runs\nfrom the failed stage against the same bytes and is idempotent: a step that would produce an object that already\nexists recognises it."],[6450,"the run; owners may download the notebook"],[6449,"The run's Parquet copy, stdout, code"],[4561,"The run's receipt reads **criteria 6 / 6 · complete** and every stage has a computed sentence."],[4774,"The Runs list is your inbox for this Flow: every waiting run says **Needs your decision** to you and nothing to\nothers. **History** is the ledger — *v1 · current · 4 runs · 3 Waiting · 1 Completed* — every run with its time,\nid and outcome, newest first, across versions. Runs never disappear; a Flow you disable keeps its History."],[46,"The same administrator on Sources"],[7271,"The same decomposition as an **architecture view** — one of the views of the single model that also draws\nHow Nexi is built. Double-click an application to open it; NexChat opens into the picture\nfurther down."],[4849,"The same Goal from the other side, complete. Read the sentence under the guardrails: &#x2A;*The engine, not the model,\ndecides when the goal is met and stops at the limits.** This is the rule that makes loops safe to publish: an\nagent can be optimistic, tired or wrong about its own work; the evaluator only compares numbers, and the engine\ncounts passes and minutes. Below it, **No progress**: *No-progress iterations before acting: 3 · Then: ask a\nperson*. If three passes in a row change nothing, the loop stops and hands over instead of spending the budget."],[6140,"The same map as a table: a filter box, **92 rows · 92 without position**, a note *280 objects, aggregated — Zoom\nin* and the columns *Name · Kind · Status · Last observed · How · Source*. The list is the only place the 92 objects\nwithout coordinates appear — they are never placed. It is also the keyboard path to everything on the map: a row is\nan object, Enter opens its Inspector."],[6723,"The same model can replay a scenario step by step. This is what happens between pressing Enter in NexChat and\nreading the reply — and, below it, what happens when the message is spoken and is a command."],[7330,"The same noun often appears in two applications. This table says who *creates*, who *governs* and what *runs* each\none."],[6660,"The same pattern for a data question: NexBI — governed numbers."],[6479,"The same picture in the architecture"],[6738,"The same picture in the architecture"],[7132,"The same picture in the architecture"],[7196,"The same picture in the architecture"],[282,"The same relations in NexBI"],[281,"The same relations in NexGraph"],[284,"The same relations in the modules — NexMap, NexCare, NexForge"],[283,"The same relations in VibeBan"],[4970,"The same row as in step 6, but the *Disabled in this Project* tag is gone and **Add** is active:\n**suppliers.delete — Side effects · REST · Always requires approval · ≤ confidential**. Nothing changed in NexChat;\nthe tool's review state changed in NexCore and the dialog reflects it."],[2416,"the same Secrets, fed by External Secrets from a cloud secret manager"],[4767,"The same steps, the same card — with two differences: the state reads **Waiting for approval · Waiting for a\nProject owner**, and there is no comment box and no button. Authorization is decided on the server for every\ncall; the buttons are hidden because pressing them would be refused, not the other way round. The run list shows\nDana **Waiting for approval**, never *Needs your decision*."],[5269,"The same tab as Kate, an Operator: identical rows. The registry is readable by every member; what differs by\nrole is what one may *do* with a row."],[4554,"The same thread as a **viewer**: the finished run card, then **PUBLISHED · 8** — every published table, chart and\nthe report with **Open in Canvas** — no notebook, no drafts, no file control in the composer."],[2158,"The sandbox boundary, in Kubernetes terms"],[5651,"The scene opens in its default **Diagram** view: &#x2A;Customer \\[Person] → Web app \\[System] → Orders API \\[API] → Orders\nDB \\[Database]*, &#x2A;Events \\[Queue]*, connected by *uses · REST · reads/writes · publishes*. One header line: back, the\ntitle *Untitled scene* in place, **v1 · draft**, the view switch **Board · Diagram · 3D · Present**, zoom, the\nInspector and Objects toggles. The chip **Layered layout** names the renderer (a stand-in until the LikeC4 renderer\nlands in S3); the colour key reads *Green data · Blue customer-facing*. Press the title, type a name, Enter."],[6554,"The scores are reproducible from the record; a Blueprint tunes the weights (`tuning.auto`), no model does."],[66,"The screen is shared; the *write* is not yours to make."],[5664,"The screens"],[3949,"The screenshots come from Nexi's verification environment, where a stand-in responder answers instead of a\nlanguage model so that every screen is reproducible. In your Nexi the answer is a real one; the frame around\nit — the bubble, the grounding line, the actions — is exactly what you see here."],[2383,"The script copies **by digest** from `RELEASE.json`, verifies each signature when `cosign` is installed, and mirrors\nthe chart as an OCI artifact. Afterwards set `NEXUS_IMAGE_REGISTRY` (Compose) or `image.registry` (chart) to your\nregistry; nothing else changes."],[2178,"the sealed credential store of core-api (`file://`) — the reason core-api runs one replica until you move to `vault://`"],[2466,"the sealed files of Tier-2 credentials (absent once you use `vault://`)"],[3955,"The second answer appears under the first, in the same chat, with the same Project context. The first answer\nkeeps its actions except **Regenerate** — only the latest answer can be regenerated. Everything before is the\ncontext of everything after: that is what makes it a conversation."],[7162,"The second floor is about what your agents **know**, and this is where most systems go wrong: they let a model write\nwhatever it extracts straight into \"the knowledge base\". Nexi refuses to."],[639,"The second line of the helper shows the current token and its countdown. **Get my token now** mints one before\nyou send anything — handy when you want the header for curl or Postman (**Copy header**). Every other way to get\nand pass it is on Authenticate your API calls."],[3423,"The second navigation level: a 200 px left column of sections with counts, `aria-current=\"page\"`, ↑ ↓ Home End; state in the URL (`href`) or the parent (`onSelect`). Collapses above the content under 720 px."],[3418,"The second navigation level: a 200 px left column of sections with counts, aria-current=\"page\", ↑ ↓ Home End; state in the URL (href) or the parent (onSelect)."],[3942,"The send arrow turns dark as soon as there is text. **Auto** next to it means Nexi chooses the model for this\nturn; you can change that later (step 8)."],[4598,"The sentence above the fields is the rule this chapter is about: &#x2A;Sources are always filtered by the Project and\nby your access at run time.* Leave the defaults and press **Publish**."],[4587,"The sentence became the agent's purpose word for word; the instructions were drafted from it (see Create an\nAgent for what the drafter does). It needs no tools — the document will be *handed* to it by\nthe Flow, not searched for."],[240,"The server runs the same sequence for every protected operation. The first check that fails is the answer."],[2440,"The session signing key"],[3540,"The shape of a sentence"],[5120,"The shape of the structured result the method teaches the agent to produce — `options[]`, `recommended`, `reason`."],[5117,"The shape of what the applying agent passes to the method — for the weekend skill: `budget`, `people`, `dates`, `home`."],[5317,"The short name people type to ask to join (`northwind-traders`). It follows the name until you edit it; lower-case letters, digits and hyphens."],[4449,"The shortcut after each name (`/flow`, `/summary`) is how a person invokes that skill directly in the composer,\nwith or without an agent."],[3968,"The sidebar shows a pinned Project **Weekend trips** with one chat under it, named after your first question."],[7707,"The sidecars"],[5454,"The sign-in card again, this time with &#x2A;*You have been signed out.** The session row is revoked on the server\nat that moment — not merely forgotten by the browser — so the same cookie cannot be replayed. Her next request\nfor anything protected is a 401 and a redirect here."],[3291,"The six quoting conversations as compositions of DS-5001 (the Flow executor) and DS-5009: a one-line request (working 3 of 5 · the receipt and the Request); a packing list (facts f"],[3296,"The six quoting conversations as compositions of DS-5001 (the Flow executor) and DS-5009: a one-line request (working 3 of 5 · the receipt and the Request); a packing list (facts from cells, one conflict kept, an unreadable photo named); the draft (the approval card with the document beneath its question — *Change a line* → a reason → *Approve*); the gate (stopped · who decides · which documents · under which edition; a person clears with a reason); the reply and its options (a language `tablist`; *Reply is right* → *Reply ready*); the formula sheet in the agent's instructions (change a line · run the golden cases · publish only when all pass); the hand-off (a draft in the known order of steps and a task for the operator — nothing is written)."],[6910,"The six suite applications — Home, NexChat, VibeBan, NexBI, NexGraph, NexCore — every organization has. A\n**module** is an application an organization turns on: today **NexMap**, **NexCare** and\n**NexForge**. Nothing about a module is special at runtime — it is a web app, an API, a worker and a\ndatabase like the others — except one thing: it answers only when the organization's Blueprint says so."],[1837,"The six-stage pipeline as Dagster assets: snapshot, structure (Docling), extraction (GLiNER-X), subject graph, verification (oracles), index (embeddings). Writes under row-level security, no DDL, **no egress** beyond Postgres, NATS and core-api."],[4651,"The Skill Studio opens on the **Overview** tab."],[2112,"The smoke script asks every process for its health, goes through `web` to each API the way a browser would, and\nprints one JSON report with a line of `✓ <check>` on the way. It exits non-zero on the first failure and names the\ncheck. Keep the report: it is the evidence that this installation is sound."],[3116,"the span tree is a `tree` with `aria-level` and arrow keys; the detail is labelled by the span; payload previews are `pre` with the classification announced first"],[2086,"the speech sidecars behind core-api's Gateway — `deploy/docker/{asr,tts}-local.Dockerfile`; no published ports; audio never leaves the network"],[4547,"The stage &#x2A;*Charts (≥ 4)** reads **needs a package: seaborn — not in the sandbox allowlist · Open the run**. The\nsandbox allows six packages; anything else becomes a **package request** the Project owner allows (a request goes\nto NexCore) or declines — nothing installs by itself. Declined, the run exits *stopped — needs you* with a partial\nreport."],[5920,"The stage controls: **Hand** (drag to pan) or **Orbit** (drag to rotate), **Stop motion*&#x2A;, zoom &#x2A;*+ −** and\nfit. The keyboard line at the bottom: &#x2A;Click · Enter — select · Double-click · Shift+Enter — enter · Esc — back ·\ndrag — orbit · Space + drag — move.*"],[3058,"the starting points list is labelled by the title"],[3015,"The state ladder on every read"],[3070,"The state ladder on every read"],[3183,"The state ladder on every read"],[3687,"The state ladder on every read — A screen's content region renders through DataStateView; loading is text, empty is quiet with ≤ 3 starting points, error and offline retry, denied and not found look alike."],[3059,"The state ladder on every read · Empty collection · List with controls · Filter panel"],[3569,"The story must render, pass its interaction, and pass the accessibility check with no serious or critical finding.\nA component without a story, or a story without a row, does not merge."],[6960,"The Studio: a plan and rules, not a model"],[7007,"The Studio's intelligence is deliberately small and inspectable. **Plan**: the decision statement is stemmed and\nmatched against the templates' slot hints; the closest template is chosen and every slot is filled with the best\nvalidated metric or marked *no metric* / *no data* — a `dashboard_plan` decision with all template candidates and\ntheir scores, and the slots you keep or drop written back. **Coverage** compares the draft to the template's slots.\n**Advisor**: nine rules over the draft — *outcome without a driver · no target · no comparison · seasonality risk ·\nconcentration missing · period filter missing · refresh missing · alert missing · subscription missing* — each an\n`advisor_suggestion` decision whose outcome is your Apply or Dismiss, and each editing the **draft only**. *Ask\nNexi* in the Add panel hands a sentence to the NexChat data arm and takes back a draft chart; the Studio never calls a\nmodel itself."],[6664,"The suite"],[6950,"The suite never imports a module: no `svc_map_api` in graph-api, no Care noun in chat-api's Auto, no Forge\n`ArtifactType` in NexChat. Doors go the other way — *Ask in Chat*, *Open in Graph*, *Open in VibeBan*\n— as links and references, never copies."],[3034,"The suite's calendar instead of the browser's `<input type=\"date\">` popup (which cannot take the kit's colours, only its light/dark scheme): the Select trigger (DS-3011) with a calendar glyph, a month grid on the picker surface, the selected day as the primary pair (ink on paper), today a ring, other months muted, `Clear` · `Today` as links; `withTime` adds an hour and a minute Select. Values are the native wire shapes (`YYYY-MM-DD` · `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm`, local time)."],[3029,"The suite's calendar instead of the browser's <input type=\"date\"> popup (which cannot take the kit's colours, only its light/dark scheme): the Select trigger (DS-3011) with a calen"],[5897,"The summary line: &#x2A;Hybrid search, graph and verified claims, reranked: 4 items kept, 412 ms. Outside your access\nand left out: 1. The reranker read only the top candidates within the time budget.* Then **WHY EACH SOURCE IS\nHERE**: for **1 Google Drive binding states · section** the chips **semantic #1 · keyword #2 · top after rerank**\nand its path."],[3844,"The surface is graphite text on warm white (Light) or layered graphite (Graphite); there is one accent (`--nexus-accent`) and it marks only what is selected, running or focused — never navigation chrome, never a chip. Colour is never the only carrier of meaning: a status is a dot *and* a label."],[3584,"The swatches, scales and layers in the workshop read the live tokens of the kit — open Foundations in the workshop."],[5735,"The switcher at the top of the sidebar is how you move between Projects — and out of them."],[5731,"The switcher's first entry: every Project you have a relation to, plus the base tier — in one view."],[3559,"The system has one rule for the person building a screen: &#x2A;*find the row first.** Everything else follows from it."],[4272,"The system line &#x2A;*Verified — I can see your orders now.** and the composer open for the next question. Account\nfields are read from the CRM through Synapse when needed and never stored in Care."],[5700,"The terms in use — every entity the resolver filed a mention under."],[5181,"The text box is replaced by a graphite **wave** that follows your voice; the mic button has become **Send now**;\nnothing else on the screen changes. There are no status words — the wave carries the state (for assistive\ntechnology the line reads *Hearing you*). Speech is detected after 200 ms above the floor; **1.5 s of silence** ends\nthe turn. Seven seconds of nothing gives &#x2A;Didn't hear anything.*; sixty seconds is the cap; `Esc` cancels."],[69,"The thing exists here but is switched off for this Project, this classification or this kind of caller."],[7433,"the thread's classification; `retention=session_only`"],[1803,"the three APIs, Keycloak"],[7684,"The three layers: what was written · what a model proposes it means · what an oracle or a person decided."],[666,"The three modules have their own APIs — **Map API** (`/api/v1/map/…`, :3207), **Care API** (`/api/v1/care/…` and the\npublic edge `/api/v1/care/public/v1/…`, :3208) and **Forge API** (`/api/v1/forge/…`, :3209) — behind the same\nassertion, plus the module gate. Their contracts are JSON Schemas in `packages/contracts/schemas/v1/` (`map-*`,\n`care-*`, `forge-*`, `guardrail-*`); **no OpenAPI file is committed for them yet** (ADR-0051 §4, ADR-0054, ADR-0057\nname the files and defer them), so this reference does not generate pages for them — it would otherwise be\ndescribing an API from memory. Until the files land, each API serves its own FastAPI `/docs` on the dev stack, and the\noperation lists are written out in NexMap, NexCare and\nNexForge. NexChat's voice doors (`/chat/voice/transcriptions`, `/chat/voice/speech`,\n`/chat/voice/files`) and the web-search port (`/synapse/web-search/*`) are in the Chat and Platform contracts and\nappear in those references."],[7686,"The three stores, all in PostgreSQL: raw bytes · fragments, mentions and vectors (pgvector) · entities and verified facts (Apache AGE)."],[7647,"The three time modes: last observed positions · as it was at an instant · replayed with interpolation that says so."],[6107,"The tier filter **Project** leaves a few dozen terms; **Base** leaves thousands."],[6754,"The tier is set once, when a source is bound to a Project, and is **never widened** by anything downstream: not by a\npipeline, not by a Flow that used the document, not by an answer that cited it. The layer is where the gate lives.\nThe store is an implementation detail you meet in Graph Studio's *Datastores* table and nowhere else."],[2996,"the timeline is a `list` of labelled entries; the composer is a `form` with the mode as a radiogroup; the inspector is `complementary` and returns focus on close"],[4710,"The title changes to *Trip planner*, the version counter under it goes from *v1* to *v2*, and **Save** is greyed\nout again. Every save is a new version — you will see all of them on the **Versions** tab and can always read\nwhat changed."],[4754,"The title the approval node's template produced; the same words the owner would see anywhere else this item appears."],[3383,"the toggle is `aria-pressed` with a localized label"],[4250,"The token goes to the Credential Broker and never reaches care-api or a log. The Telegram integration declares a\n*conversation channel* (messaging, polled ingress) and the only egress host `api.telegram.org`; there is no\nTelegram SDK — a thin adapter speaks the Bot API over HTTPS. Back in Studio › Channels the connection is listed with\nits health; care-api polls it every 3 s, a Telegram chat becomes a conversation with the chip **Telegram** on the\nsame desk, under the same assistant, guardrails and Join/Return — the first message from a chat finds or creates\nits session for 24 h."],[188,"The tool is switched off here, or is a raw builder tool that is never exposed to users or agents."],[4974,"The tool-call row says **suppliers.delete · Waiting for approval**, expanded to &#x2A;Waiting for a human approval\nbefore this action runs.* with the **Connection** it would use. Nothing has been deleted. The agent has done its\npart — proposed exactly one call with exactly one argument — and stopped."],[4955,"The tool's own default. Your binding may be stricter (step 4), never looser."],[5459,"The top of the trail, newest first: &#x2A;*Olena Shevchenko · Signed in · session 9b57…** (just now); &#x2A;*Revoked\nsessions · session 7950…** — her own, when she signed out; &#x2A;*Revoked sessions · session a0e2…** — the Safari\none; &#x2A;*Signed in · session a0e2…** — Safari's sign-in; then the organization's creation. Every session has\na beginning and an end in the trail, each with an actor and a reason (`sign_out`, `sign_out_all`) — visible to\nthe administrators, not to the person alone."],[5532,"The trace names its **root** — *AGENT RUN · agt\\_general · Autumn catalogue · Sep 19, 2026 04:28 AM · Complete*\n— with the correlation id under it, and three tabs: **Timeline 5 · Payloads · Summary**. The timeline lists\nevery record that shares the id, in order, each as a bar on one time axis with its URI on the right: **Turn ·\nuser · 44 chars · Complete**, **Turn · assistant · 70 chars · Complete**, **Agent run · agt\\_general ·\nCompleted**, **Model · gpt5 · cloud\\_fixture · Succeeded · 0 ms**, **Audit · write · allow** on the thread. *44\nchars*, not the question; *70 chars*, not the answer. The messages are here as facts about themselves — length,\nrole, status, id — which is what a timeline needs and all that a timeline is allowed to carry. Top right:\n*Laminar not configured* — the place a deployment may plug an external trace viewer; without one the timeline\nis the viewer."],[5184,"The transcript arrives."],[3363,"The transient *Saved* line after a commit — `role=status`, gone after 3 s (`useSavedNote`)."],[3358,"The transient *Saved* line after a commit — role=status, gone after 3 s (useSavedNote)."],[7045,"The turn"],[4764,"The two buttons — present only for people who may decide."],[5960,"The two documents from Add a source uploaded; their runs are the two most recent."],[6098,"The two runs completed. The agreement and the report add the Project's first terms on top of the Base tier's."],[5917,"The two runs from Follow a pipeline run completed. The agreement gives Studio its\npeople, organizations, places and amounts."],[6446,"The uploaded file"],[7074,"The URL is the view"],[3991,"The user guide grows one chapter at a time. Each chapter is verified against the application before it appears here,\nand each one follows the same template as Get started."],[221,"The user interface never decides. It asks, and it shows the answer. A button you can see is not a permission; a\nbutton you cannot see is not a denial — the server would refuse the request either way."],[900,"the values of one dimension the caller may read — the Slice control's list. Computed as an ordinary BIQuery (dimensions=[d], count, limit 200) through the same compiler, PEP and row policy as any block; `period=<BiPeriodPreset | from..to>` counts rows inside that window on the entity's time dimension; `q=` narrows by prefix (case-insensitive). A dimension the model does not name is 404. Never a value the caller could not read as a row."],[1312,"The verification queue; a curator's verdict within a named scope, a return for clarification, re-verification, entity merge proposals. Humans only."],[5697,"The verification queue: contested and proposed claims, the decided ones, the oracle's verdict, a person's decision."],[1320,"The verification queue: proposed and contested claims/observations the caller may read (query: status, layer, cluster_id, cursor)."],[4716,"The version counter increases again and **Save** is disabled. If a colleague saved the same agent while you\nwere typing, Nexi refuses your save with an error instead of overwriting theirs — reload, read their version,\napply yours again."],[7452,"The VibeBan chapters show the application from the outside. This page is the inside. NexTasks began\nas the place a Flow waits for a person — the **approval**. VibeBan grows the same process, `tasks-api` on\nits own database `nexus_tasks`, into work management: what is on your plate, how a team runs a project, and how the\nplatform's own delivery — requirements, criteria, tests, decisions — is tracked against the work. Two rules organise\neverything: **an agent acts within the relation of the human who asked, never beyond it**, and **every place the\napplication ranks or decides for you is a decision record**, not a heuristic."],[4295,"The visitor asked &#x2A;Where is container MSKU7697648?*; the assistant asked to verify first. The handler line reads\n**Assistant**, **Join** is in the header, and the composer is closed — nobody human holds this conversation yet.\nThe visitor can keep writing meanwhile; the assistant keeps answering until someone joins."],[5188,"The voice entries: **Turn voice answers off** (then no speech leaves the server for this tab), **Share screen** and\n**Provide a file for this session** (see Act from anywhere), **Talk hands-free**."],[4786,"The waiting run reads **Needs your decision** to you and **Waiting for approval** to an editor."],[5183,"The wave breathes slowly in accent ink while the clip (≤ 2 MiB, ≤ 60 s) goes to `POST /chat/voice/transcriptions`,\nthrough core-api's Gateway to the `asr` role — the local model first; a hosted one only up to *confidential*. The\nthread's classification is checked before a byte moves. Your UI language is the hint; the model is multilingual."],[7252,"The wave, *Spoken*, *Nexi is speaking*"],[6934,"The web app renders the gate's refusal as one state — *NexMap is not enabled for your organization* / *NexCare isn't\nenabled for this organization* / *NexForge is not enabled here* — with a link to Blueprints & Packs. The App Launcher\ndraws the tile only when the effective Blueprint lists the module; a missing module has no tile at all, never a greyed\none."],[6560,"The web is a source like any other: who answered, from which class, and why is on the card and in two decision records — never the query text."],[7257,"the web-search provider port answered, or no provider is connected"],[7133,"The weekend Flow used one model for drafting and a cheaper one for judging, a weather service, your calendar, a\nchecklist Skill and an approval. Behind that sit at least five technologies from five vendors. Ask yourself how the\nFlow drafter knew a *Weather* Tool existed, how Synapse knew which model qualifies as \"good quality, tier ≤ 2\", how\nNexTasks knew that *creating events* needs a person and *reading a forecast* does not — and how, in a year, you would\nfind out which model saw a given conversation."],[6156,"The whole page is the map at **World** level: a light base map with sage-green hexagons over Europe, the Black Sea\nand the Baltic. Read the status line at the bottom from left to right: the cursor position (*47.5000° N ·\n19.5000° E*), the level and zoom (*World z4.1*), the scale (*1000 km*), **Aggregated · H3 resolution 3**, and the\ncount: *653 objects · aggregated (H3 3) · 92 without position*. The time chip reads **Now**. The 92 objects without\nposition exist — they are in the list (next chapter) — but nothing is drawn for them."],[7530,"The words Nexi uses, in one sentence each."],[3543,"The words on a screen are part of the design system. They follow the same rules in every application, and the rules\nare short."],[1643,"The work context for a ref (chat-api's `context=` chip, the run's `work context` input). Called with the END USER's bearer: the model sees what the person sees. URIs and short labels only."],[7593,"The work words — the ones you meet in VibeBan:"],[2546,"The workbench kit: forty-six exports every suite app composes instead of writing its own. Each row is one component, its contract and the states its stories show."],[6000,"The worker is a **Dagster** code location with six partitioned assets — `snapshot → structure → extraction → subject →\noracle → index` — one partition per source version; a *sync* job scans server folders and Drive folders on a sensor\nand places orders for new or changed files; a daily asset refreshes the platform documentation. The worker runs under\nits own database role with row-level security, so it can only read the Project the order names. Each step writes a\n**RunStep** record — executor kind (*worker · Synapse Model Gateway · PostgreSQL · pgvector · AGE · Dagster*),\nexecutor name and version, timings, produced counts, log lines as structured events — and the run page renders those\nrecords. Models are reached only through the **Synapse Model Gateway**: the embedding model (`qwen3-embedding-0.6b`)\nand, at query time, the reranker; the parser (Docling) and the mention extractor (GLiNER-X) run inside the worker."],[6036,"The workspace reads `GET /graph/projects/{project_id}/source-versions/{version_id}/document` (the parsed document\nwith its pages and items) and `…/sources/{source_id}/versions/{version_id}/pages/{page}` for the page you are on; the\nitems on it are **DocumentItem** records (heading, paragraph, table, table cell, figure, code, formula, list) with\ntheir spans, and the mentions are **EvidenceSpan** records pointing at an item with a precision. `GET\n…/claims/{claim_id}/evidence` returns the claim's spans (the cell) and `GET …/evidence-spans/{span_id}` a single span\nwith its text. The original bytes are served by `…/versions/{version_id}/download` after the same enforcement check\nas the page — the content door is the API, never a public bucket. Figures inside a page come through\n`…/objects/{uri}/figure`, which returns the image only to a caller who may read the page it is on."],[5984,"Then &#x2A;*Search runs…**, an **All states** filter and a legend: *done · running · partial · waiting for a human ·\nfailed · pending*. The table has a dot per stage — **Snap · Struct · Extract · Subject · Verify · Index** — so a\nrun's shape is visible without opening it. The two uploads are **Completed** at 23:50; one older *Nexi\ndocumentation* run reads **Failed** — that is the *1 need attention*."],[2347,"Then `npm run stack` again: migrations recreate the schema, Keycloak re-imports its realm, and `/signup` is waiting."],[3879,"Then continue with the NexChat guide: the same *Weekend trips* Project gets an agent, a skill,\ntools and a flow, one chapter each — and Let Auto choose explains the route\nline you read in chapter 2. When your work is a board rather than a chat, the VibeBan guide\nstarts with *My Work*; when it is a number, the NexBI guide starts with a dataset. You can also\nspeak to Nexi instead of typing, and an Owner can turn on the\nmodules — NexMap, NexCare, NexForge — when the organization needs them."],[2106,"Then open `deploy/compose/.env` once and set:"],[2114,"Then open `http://localhost:3310/chat`. You land on the sign-in page served by Keycloak *through* `web` — the only\npublic origin. Register, verify through the mail your relay delivered, create your organization, and continue with\nGet started."],[4704,"Then press **Draft agent**."],[4649,"Then press **Draft skill**."],[2205,"then smoke-tests through the NodePort. Open `http://localhost:30000/chat`."],[5831,"Then the facts: **Mode** One-time · **Profile** `nexus://graph/scope/prf_default` (the processing profile — which\nparsers, extractors and embedding model the pipeline uses) · **Documents** 2 · **Content lag** 0 s · **Updated**.\nUnder **Operations** a single red-outlined **Revoke**, with the sentence that tells you what it means for this\nkind: &#x2A;An upload binding has nothing to pause. Revoking closes it: later uploads open a new one; documents stay.*"],[2331,"Then upload a document with a table in NexGraph and follow the run: Add a source\n→ Follow a pipeline run."],[5858,"There is no button to press and no source to attach: **Auto** routes the question. While it runs, the live trace\nunder your message reads **Searching the knowledge graph** with counts — *n terms · n candidates · n reranked*. A\nquestion about the platform — &#x2A;How do I connect a Google Drive folder as a source?* — takes the same path and is\nanswered from the Base tier."],[2319,"There is no seeded user and no default password. Open `http://127.0.0.1:3212/signup`, register with any e-mail\naddress, then open **Mailpit** at `http://127.0.0.1:8025` — the verification mail is there. Follow its link, sign\nin, and create your first organization. From here on the laptop behaves exactly like the product:\nYour first Project and conversation applies unchanged."],[293,"These are the presets Core offers when you invite or edit a person. The organization's checks group them into\nthree tiers today; the finer presets are recorded on the person and used by the Blueprint's role-based policies\n(for example *Pinning a model id: roles only*)."],[4560,"These three screens are from the acceptance evidence of the datasets work; that work is paused, so the live stack\nmay still show the earlier run card in places."],[7136,"Thing"],[7331,"Thing"],[7749,"Thing"],[4644,"Think for a minute about what a *good* proposal contains. The skill is only as useful as that list."],[5598,"Think, sketch, model — scenes you shape by hand, by sentence or by voice, projected as a board, a C4 diagram, a 3D model or a presentation; the AI proposes, you apply."],[7314,"Think, sketch, model; the AI proposes, the person applies."],[3952,"This drawer is the reason to use Nexi rather than a plain chatbot: every answer carries where it came from. When\nyou attach knowledge to the Project, the **Sources** list fills with the\ndocuments the answer actually used. Press **Close**."],[4695,"This is the first piece of the weekend-trip example. When you want to know what every tab and\nfield means, read Agent Studio, tab by tab. The next chapters add a Skill, more Tools and the Flow."],[5135,"This is the gate that makes Nexi skills trustworthy. The intro line spells it out: &#x2A;A person must read and approve the\nexact current version; any edit asks for a new review.* The tab shows two facts and offers two actions."],[4870,"This is the most instructive screen of the chapter. The agent worked three times but **never reported a\n`budget_fit` number**, so the evaluator had nothing to compare — three flat passes, and the *No progress* rule\nstopped the loop after three, as configured, and took the *No progress* exit to the review. The engine did exactly\nwhat the Goal said; the sentence the agent works from must ask it, in so many words, to **return `budget_fit` as a\nnumber between 0 and 1**. Edit the Objective in the Goal Inspector to say so, test again, and watch the score move.\n(In the review fixture that draws these screenshots, the agent is a stand-in that reports no metrics, so the loop\nalways ends this way — the honest behaviour of a Goal whose metric is missing.)"],[4668,"This is the one rule of skills that Nexi enforces without exception: a skill that teaches agents must have\nbeen read by a person — this version, not an earlier one. Agents and automated services are refused when they\ntry to review."],[6074,"This is the oracle being honest about the limit of what it can check, and it is exactly the case a person is for:\na curator opens *Kyiv · On-time rate*, sees &#x2A;transcription ✓ · arithmetic ✗*, understands the column is a ratio, and\n**confirms** the claim within the scope *transcription* — recording that the figure is what the document says, not\nthat it is arithmetically derived. Nothing in the history is erased: the oracle's *falsified* stays as the first\nverdict, the curator's *confirmed* follows it."],[6442,"This is why the attachment card can say *2 sheets · 20 061 rows × 57 columns* before anything runs, and why a\nquestion without a file gets a text answer that must not invent counts."],[5683,"this page, below"],[5704,"this page, below"],[2510,"This portal is a **static site** with no runtime dependency on Nexi: build it, put the `out/` directory on any web\nserver or bucket, and it works. It is optional in every deployment profile."],[6362,"This section explains the *why* behind what you see in the applications. Every picture here is a view of one\narchitecture model or a diagram kept next to the text; the words are the ones the applications use."],[4,"This section explains the access model in product language so that an administrator can configure it correctly the\nfirst time — and so that anyone who meets a denied screen knows which wall they hit and who can move it. It is\nwritten from the platform's actual checks and verified against the running application; where the current build\nstill falls short of the rule, the page says so."],[1768,"This section walks up that ladder one rung at a time. Each page is complete on its own; read them in order if you\nare new to the platform, or jump to the target you need."],[5103,"This tab is a single field, **SKILL.md**, and it is the heart of the skill. The hint under it is the design rule:\n&#x2A;The method, step by step. Portable Markdown — no secrets, no credentials.*"],[1211,"Thread visible to the actor (creator or can_view on its Project)"],[1194,"Threads"],[1212,"Threads of a Project (can_view), newest first"],[4844,"Three arrows leave the loop — **Goal met · Limits reached · No progress** — and all three go to the review.\nThat is deliberate: however the loop ends, a person looks before anything acts on the result."],[3473,"Three columns (ownership · governance · usage) of value · label rows on a detail page."],[5923,"Three columns, the three layers of the knowledge model, each with its own count: **SOURCES — Lexical · 79\ndocuments**, **CLAIMS — Subject · 2 000 claims**, **KNOWLEDGE — Domain · 28 verified facts**. Each card is a group\nwith its numbers — *Uploads · documents: 2 · pages: 3 · chunks: 14*; *product · entities: 716 · mentions: 6942*;\n*claims · claims: 28 · verified: 23 · falsified: 5* with a green bar for the verified share. Groups of the Base\ntier carry a padlock and **BASE · READ-ONLY**. The dotted ribbons between the columns are the flow: sources\nproduce mentions and entities, tables produce claims, decisions produce facts."],[5148,"Three consequences worth knowing:"],[4569,"Three cottage offers arrived by e-mail. Hand them to Nexi as a file, let an agent read them into one comparison table you can sort, see the file become a pinned source of the Project, and read what the next answer was grounded on. About twenty minutes."],[7065,"Three doors in order (Modules). `ForgePepAction` (10): `forge.scene.read · create · edit · delete ·\nexport · publish_version · convert · forge.template.manage · forge.present · forge.decision.read`; **human-only**:\ndelete, export, convert, publish. Relations are the Project's: `forge.admin (owner) ⊃ forge.edit (editor) ⊃\nforge.view (viewer, agent_member)`. An Organization Admin without a relation gets `NO_PROJECT_RELATION`; a foreign\nscene 404. RLS is forced on every table. `svc_forge_api` holds `session.verify · blueprint.read · pep.check ·\nmodel.invoke` (the last one added most recently, awaiting acknowledgement)."],[7103,"Three doors in order on every route — session · module gate · PEP (Modules). Reads need any Project\nrelation; an Organization Admin without one gets `NO_PROJECT_RELATION` 403; an object of a Project you do not hold\nanswers 404. View and upload authoring is human-only (`AUTHOR_NOT_HUMAN`); `svc_map_worker` reads tenant-wide,\n`svc_chat_api` reads only, every other service `SERVICE_NOT_ALLOWED`. Every route carries `x-nexus-pep`; audit rows\n`map.module.gate`, `map.view.save`, `map.upload`… go to the audit sink."],[4533,"Three exits exist: **complete** (this one), **budget spent — partial** (the loop hit its limits — 12 passes, 45 min,\n1 000 000 tokens, 2 400 sandbox seconds — and wrote a partial report) and **stopped — needs you** (see step 7)."],[7006,"Three human acts frame a dashboard: **certification** of the metrics it shows (a steward), **publication** with the\nacknowledgement (a person with `dashboard.publish`), and — from NexChat — **acceptance** of a proposed dashboard\n(`dashboard_proposal`, S6b), which creates a draft and nothing more."],[4805,"Three ideas carry the chapter — the vocabulary is in\nAgents, Skills, Tools and Flows: &#x2A;Flow orchestrates. Goal directs.\nEvaluator judges.*"],[4589,"Three lines decide what this agent may read:"],[6313,"Three lists. **Active** — *Sprint 1 · 21 Sept – 5 Oct* with its goal and four figures: **Complete** 0 / 5 items,\n**Points** 0 / 13 (*13 at start* — the snapshot taken when the sprint started), **Days left** 8 of 14, **Scope\nchange** +0 / −0 since start. Its buttons: **Complete sprint**, **Plan iteration**, **Edit**, **Cancel iteration**.\n**Planned** — *Sprint 2 · 5 Oct – 19 Oct · 4 items · 12 pts* with **Start iteration** disabled: &#x2A;Another iteration is\nactive — complete it first.* Only one iteration runs at a time. **Past** — completed iterations with what was\ncarried over."],[3780,"Three looks for three jobs: an *inline* link in running text (text colour, underlined, hover → secondary); a *row* link — the title cell of a table or row list (no underline, under"],[3784,"Three looks for three jobs: an *inline* link in running text (text colour, underlined, hover → secondary); a *row* link — the title cell of a table or row list (no underline, underline on hover, the row is the target); a *meta* link at 12 px secondary (*Open source chat*, &#x2A;Why?*). A `<button>` that looks like a link is the inline look over a button with a 24 px target; a fourth tone, *quiet* (13 px · 500 · secondary, underline on hover), is the look of an action row (DS-7016). One class family `.nexus-link` (`.is-row` · `.is-meta`) and `.nexus-link-btn` (`.is-meta` · `.is-quiet`); nothing app-local."],[1891,"Three more databases — `nexus_map`, `nexus_care`, `nexus_forge` — each with its own role, row-level security\nforced, Alembic migrations run by the `migrate-*` jobs. chat-api needs the voice settings (`VOICE_TRANSCRIBER_DRIVER`,\n`VOICE_SYNTHESIZER_DRIVER`, `VOICE_TRANSPORT_DRIVER=ws`, `VOICE_STREAM_PUBLIC_URL`, `VOICE_VAD_DRIVER`,\n`VOICE_SILERO_MODEL_PATH`, `WEB_SEARCH_DRIVER`) — all required, no defaults; core-api needs\n`NEXUS_ASR_LOCAL_BASE_URL` and `NEXUS_TTS_LOCAL_BASE_URL`. A *confidential* Project must have a local speech route, so a\ndeployment that enables voice should run both sidecars. The chart carries the voice env but **no sidecar profile\nyet*&#x2A;; it joins at UAT-4. Budget roughly **+2.5 GB*&#x2A; of images and weights for the two sidecars and **+1 GB RAM** at\nidle; ASR on a CPU is 8–30 s per clip — a GPU or a cloud `asr` route (≤ confidential) brings it under 2 s."],[2395,"three new Jobs `nexus-migrate-*-r<revision>`; API pods wait in `Init`"],[6556,"Three non-agent answers compete with the agents: **data** (NexBI's governed engine, only when a validated metric matches and its entity has a bound dataset), **knowledge** (NexGraph resolve for a question about documents), **capability** (a product family → &#x2A;General · with ‹product›*, the tools offered this turn, a governed `CapabilityRequest` when a tool needs allowing)."],[5386,"Three optional applications enabled for the organization, visible in every launcher, each guarded by its own\nmodule gate, with their content in their own databases (`nexus_map`, `nexus_care`, `nexus_forge`). The chapters of\nNexMap, NexCare and NexForge continue from here."],[4293,"Three panes. Left, the **inbox**: *7 open · 5 at risk · 1 unassigned*, each row with customer, subject, queue and an\nSLA chip. Middle, the **conversation**: *Andrii Hordiienko · Zernovyk Export*, an ETA question, the assistant's\nanswers marked **AUTOMATED** with their verified SOP source, a divider *Oksana Bondar joined*. Right, the\n**inspector**: *Status* (handler, state, queue, SLA, intent) and the **versions** of the agent, flow and guardrail\nprofile that served the conversation — so a review a month later knows exactly what answered."],[6729,"Three questions every object answers"],[5670,"Three rules run through every chapter:"],[4008,"Three rules run through every chapter. **No text-to-SQL**: a question becomes a typed query over the semantic model,\nand the SQL is generated and parameterised by the engine; you can read it, a model never writes it. **Certification is\nhuman**: a metric becomes *certified*, a dataset version *published*, a dashboard *published* only when a person\nacknowledges it. **Per-viewer rendering**: a dashboard is a set of references — to metrics, artifacts and dataset\nversions — and each block is resolved for the reader; a block you may not see keeps its place and says so."],[5602,"Three rules shape every interaction:"],[1766,"Three rules that never change"],[6428,"Three things about this shape are the platform's rules rather than the template's choices:"],[6115,"Three things make it a Nexi map rather than a map:"],[4357,"Three things that make NexChat the shell's hands and eyes. **Platform actions**: a closed catalogue of commands each\napp declares — *open my inbox*, *open the board Marketing*, &#x2A;create a task…*, &#x2A;run the Flow…* — recognised before any\nmodel and executed through the owning app. **Screen context**: the Ask bar of another app hands over a reference to\nwhat you are looking at, so *this* and *it* mean something. **Session material**: a file or a shared window the\nassistant reads for this session only and never keeps."],[7322,"Three things the picture makes visible:"],[5280,"Three things the server did while this happened, all visible in NexChat's Studio and the audit trail: Taras\ncould **create** the draft (editor may write); Taras could **not publish** it — *403 · permission denied*,\npublishing is the Owner's; Kate, a Viewer, could **not even draft** — the same 403. And a capability made\ninside a Project is *the Project's*: its visibility is **Project**, not Organization."],[440,"Three things the table implies:"],[494,"Three things the table implies:"],[7088,"Three timestamps — `observed_at`, `received_at` required; `valid_until` optional — \"honest time\""],[7269,"Three ways to read this page"],[2407,"Tier"],[2429,"Tier 1 in a vault lets you set `NEXUS_ALLOW_ENV_SECRETS=false` (`coreApi.allowEnvSecrets: \"false\"`): from then on\n**no** process can receive a key through its environment, even by mistake."],[295,"Tier today"],[6728,"Tiers, layers and stores; the six-stage pipeline; the oracle-or-person gate; incremental versions; and how NexChat answers from the graph under the asker's own rights. Continued with the Acme Logistics example."],[6170,"Time, views and sources"],[6121,"Time, views and sources — History and Playback, saved views, zones, uploading a CSV."],[3541,"Title case, numbers, units"],[6281,"Title is the only required field. **Project** defaults to **Personal — Only you see it until you share it**: the\nitem gets a key `MY-<n>` and lives outside every project. Choosing a project instead gives it that project's key\n(`ACME-<n>`) and puts it in the project's backlog stage. **Type** (Task · Story · Bug · Epic), **Priority**\n(No priority · P0 Critical · P1 High · P2 Normal · P3 Low), **Due** and **Description** are optional and editable\nlater in the Inspector."],[810,"Title, decision statement, filters, suggestion mode."],[846,"Title, description, row policy, semantic-model binding, pin."],[2230,"tls type"],[6341,"To import on your own stack the operator sets `IMPORT_SOURCES` on tasks-api to the documentation folders\n(the requirement and decision folders of a repository) and you run `npm run vibeban:import-nexus`, or use the\n**Re-sync** button once the first import exists."],[7248,"to review, reconnect or disconnect your own accounts"],[2146,"To rotate a key: put the new value in `openbao/seed.env`, run `docker compose run --rm openbao-init`, delete the file."],[7187,"To see the vocabulary in use, follow the step-by-step chapters of the NexChat guide — starting with\nCreate an Agent from one sentence. The second floor, at document scale, is\nThe knowledge graph and the NexGraph guide."],[7171,"Today"],[3331,"Today is an instance of the **Overview page** (DS-7006, the NexCore cockpit — amended 2026-10-11 twice: the owner found three columns overloaded, then asked for the NexCore Overvie"],[3335,"Today is an instance of the **Overview page** (DS-7006, the NexCore cockpit — amended 2026-10-11 twice: the owner found three columns overloaded, then asked for the NexCore Overview idiom): a `wide` frame with the health line in the header (`StatusDot` + small age, as NexCore's *operational*); the **Sales pulse** frame (`PulseStrip` — Accounts ─ Opportunities ─ Quotes waiting ─ Follow-ups, each a door; `live` when the provider is connected; the foot line: planned · waiting · overdue · going quiet); three `Stat`s (planned today · open pipeline as money · going quiet, with overdue as the toned delta); then two `nexus-cc-two` rows of `Section`s — *Planned today* (`StatusList`: account · kind · contact · time, row → account with the Log composer open) · *Waiting on me* (the attention list: title · account · assignee · due, dot red when overdue, the task reference as the door to NexTasks) · *Going quiet* (`StatusList`: account · relationship · owner · *n d quiet*, amber ≥30 d, red ≥60 d) · *Recent* (the recent list: who · kind · account · outcome · ago). Only kit classes; no app-local stylesheet. The org-admin sees the pulse figures and the quiet empty state, never the lists."],[3601,"Tokens: `--nexus-accent-mint … --nexus-accent-copper-soft`"],[3603,"Tokens: `--nexus-app-chat-accent … --nexus-app-forge-soft`"],[3597,"Tokens: `--nexus-bg … --nexus-accent-soft`"],[3605,"Tokens: `--nexus-data-1 … --nexus-data-seq-5 (new)`"],[3599,"Tokens: `--nexus-error · --nexus-warning · --nexus-success · --nexus-info`"],[3640,"Tokens: `--nexus-font · --nexus-text-xs … --nexus-text-3xl · --nexus-leading-xs … -3xl · --nexus-composer-font-size · --nexus-composer-placeholder-size`"],[3628,"Tokens: `--nexus-radius-xs · -control · -sm … -xl · -pill · --nexus-radius · --nexus-composer-radius`"],[3622,"Tokens: `--nexus-shell-motion`"],[3630,"Tokens: `--nexus-sidebar-* · --nexus-bar-height · --nexus-btn-height* · --nexus-action-gap · --nexus-drawer-width · --nexus-confirm-width`"],[3635,"Tokens: `--nexus-space-1 … --nexus-space-10 (new) · --nexus-action-gap = space-4 · --nexus-page-pad · --nexus-section-gap · --nexus-inspector-pad`"],[3611,"Tokens: `--nexus-surface* · --nexus-glass-* · --nexus-overlay-* · --nexus-shadow-lg · --nexus-composer-shadow*`"],[3613,"Tokens: `--nexus-z-raised … --nexus-z-skip (new) · --nexus-shadow-sm · --nexus-shadow-md (new) · --nexus-shadow-lg`"],[6514,"Tool"],[7351,"Tool"],[4981,"Tool bindings live on the agent — Bind agent tool and\nUnbind agent tool; what a Project may bind comes from\nGet tool availability. The registry itself is the\nPlatform API › Tools in NexCore, and approvals are\nTasks API › Approvals. Run them from the reference with your own session\n(how to authenticate)."],[2628,"Toolbar · showListControls"],[3485,"Toolbar · showListControls"],[3761,"Toolbar · showListControls · SearchField · Chip · EmptyState"],[3793,"Toolbar · showListControls · SearchField · Select · DataTable · EmptyState"],[1564,"ToolDefinitions visible to the caller's tenancy (platform tools are platform-wide; integration / custom tools are tenant-scoped)."],[982,"Tools"],[1222,"Tools"],[1551,"Tools"],[4381,"Tools"],[1229,"Tools the Project's agents and flows may call = Registry ∩ ProjectPolicy ∩ Enablement ∩ Classification ∩ ConnectionHealth\n\n (S5a). NexChat reads the NexCore Tool Registry (GET /tools) and projects it onto the Project:\n`disabled` (enablement ≠ enabled), `classification` (project classification > tool.classification_max),\n`connection` (no healthy connection for integration/custom tools), `builder_only` (http.request / mcp.invoke\nhidden from business users), `unbound` (agent_id given and no ToolBinding — S5), `governance` (blocked).\nSame contract as model availability: coarse reason + i18n key, never endpoints, credentials or rule text.\nRegistry unreachable ⇒ 503 fail closed. The picker is a hint — every invocation is re-checked."],[6071,"Total checks out → the total *and each of its components* are *verified as components of a verified total*. Total does not check out → the total and its components are *falsified*. No total in the table → the check does not run (`no_total_in_table`)."],[6338,"Trace work to what it is for. In VibeBan a **reference** is a link to something that lives elsewhere — an artifact,\na Flow, an agent, a NexChat Project, a dataset, a document, a URL, a commit — or, for the platform's own delivery, a\n**requirement**, an **acceptance criterion**, a **test** or a **decision** read from the repository's documentation. A\nreference is never a copy: it resolves through the owning application's rights when you open it, and a change to the\nsource shows on the next sync."],[7755,"Transcript"],[733,"Treat the cookie like a password: it *is* your session. Never paste it into a page, a chat, or a ticket."],[4827,"Trigger"],[3037,"trigger `aria-haspopup=dialog` with the Field's label or a visually hidden one; the popover is `role=dialog`; the month is `role=grid` with a roving tabindex — arrows move a day or a week, PageUp/PageDown a month, Home/End the week's ends, Enter picks, Escape closes and returns focus"],[6613,"Trust the planner's opinion of rights."],[630,"Try it in three moves"],[1557,"Try tool"],[984,"Try tool for project"],[1228,"Try tool for project"],[4685,"Turn “Plan weekend trips for my family within a budget” into a working agent, give it a tool, try it in chat and publish it — about ten minutes."],[4320,"Turn &#x2A;\"Plan weekend trips for my family within a budget\"* into a working agent, test it in chat and publish it."],[2744,"Turn card"],[3494,"Turn card"],[5363,"Turn on an optional application for your organization from Blueprints & Packs, see its tile appear in the App Launcher, understand what “enabled” means and how to take it away again. About ten minutes."],[6390,"Turns the dataset profile and your question into 3–10 stages, proposed indices and *criteria the engine can compute*. Applies *Dataset profile* and *Analysis plan*."],[6600,"Turns the message into a `NeedSpec` — goal, constraints (*never send or delete*), cadence, inputs — in a closed schema."],[4925,"Two bound tools. The new one is tagged **Side effects · Always requires approval**. Notice the difference to the\ndialog, where the tool said *Approval by policy*: NexChat binds a side-effect tool to an agent with the stricter\nrule by default, so a fresh agent cannot change anything outside Nexi without a person seeing it first. The tag\non the row is what applies to *this agent*; the next step shows what the tool itself declares."],[4661,"Two boxes. **Input schema** — what the applying agent hands in — is empty, which means *free-form*: the agent\npasses whatever the person said. **Output schema** is pre-filled with a structured result (a *summary*,\n*evidence*, *risks*, *confidence*, *next steps*). Both are JSON Schema objects; Nexi accepts only object\nschemas and refuses anything else."],[702,"Two credentials, one sign-in"],[4531,"Two datasets with different columns get different plans — the stage names above (*Duplicates*, *Unit names*,\n*Geography*) are what the planner chose for that workbook, not a fixed list. The planner picks from four **technique\nfamilies**, each a reviewed Skill — *structure* (column roles · segmentation · clustering · text categories · charts),\n*distributions* (distribution and outliers · correlation · time patterns), *integrity* (duplicates · unit spellings ·\ndata quality) and *synthesis* (insights · suggestions · dataset card) — and writes a *why* for every stage it takes\nand a reason for every one it skips. Every result line is a computed sentence, not a model's summary: *723 candidate\ngroups · 1 512 rows — nothing removed* is what the code counted. Nothing is removed, renamed or merged in your data\nwithout your decision (step 9); duplicates are *candidates*, clusters are *candidate groups*, unit spellings are\n*mappings*, and a suggestion is a suggestion."],[6833,"Two deterministic **oracles** run over every claim:"],[289,"Two different things are called \"a role\" in everyday talk, and Nexi keeps them apart:"],[4403,"Two editable fields and a read-only summary."],[4480,"Two fields, and a formula that explains both. &#x2A;Upper bounds for this agent. The effective permission is the\nintersection of user, Project, agent, tool and classification policy.*"],[4103,"Two fields: the **decision statement** (required — *Name the decision this dashboard supports*) and a title (empty:\nthe template's name). Under **Template**: **Closest to the decision** — *the planner picks by the decision\nstatement* — or one of the templates by name (*Executive overview · Operational control · Performance vs target ·\nRisk & exceptions · Data overview*, and for organization administrators the *Nexi itself* set), or **Start blank**."],[5779,"Two files. Ours:"],[4545,"Two gates can interrupt a run; both are the engine's, not the model's."],[6203,"Two ideas make it different from a generic tracker. **An agent never outranks the person it works for**: an agent\nthat is a member of a project acts only within the relation of the human who asked, and the sensitive decisions —\nstarting or completing an iteration, verifying an acceptance criterion, approving a request, sharing a project — are\nhuman-only by contract. And **every place VibeBan ranks or decides for you is recorded** as a decision with its\nalternatives: how My Work is ordered, when a WIP limit is exceeded and the move goes through anyway, which iteration an\nunfinished item is carried into, how a project's health was derived."],[5523,"Two ideas to carry away: **runs are records by reference** (a trace lists *what* happened, with sizes and ids —\nthe text itself lives behind a second door), and **reading is an action too** — the audit trail records the\nadministrators as faithfully as it records everyone else."],[4238,"Two installations: **Client portal** (*portal.supplychain-guru.example*, its origins, mini + maxi, UK · EN,\nactive) and **Tracking page** (mini, UK · EN, active), with sessions today and *Open the fixture site*. An\ninstallation's inspector holds the **embed snippet** and the **allowed origins** — the list the public edge and the\n`frame-ancestors` header enforce."],[83,"Two lines you may meet in a chat. If your clearance is below the Project's classification, the turn is refused\nbefore it starts: &#x2A;Your access level does not cover this Project's data classification.* If a tool the agent wanted\nis not allowed for you, the answer still arrives, with a note: &#x2A;Some information was not included because your\ncurrent access does not allow it.* — Nexi never silently pretends the tool ran. The upper bounds an agent works\nunder are visible on its **Permissions** tab:"],[5834,"Two links: **acme-q3-2026-delivery-report.md · v1 · 1.3 KB · 1 p** and **northwind-framework-agreement-2027.pdf\n· v1 · 65.1 KB · 2 p**, each with its time. `v1` is the source version; a re-upload of a changed file would add a\n`v2` beside it and mark `v1` superseded — nothing is overwritten. Each link opens the document in the\nEvidence Workspace. The **Access** tab lists who may read this source and why — your own\nProject relation, in plain words."],[7216,"Two more families reach the outside through Synapse: **web search providers** (`web.search` port — Tavily, Brave,\nMojeek, LangSearch as connections; Wikipedia, Wikidata, OpenStreetMap as open data) and **conversation channels**\n(the Telegram bot NexCare answers in — a connection with a `conversation_channel` block, the bot token in the\nCredential Broker, `api.telegram.org` the only egress host)."],[6795,"Two of these deserve a sentence. The **source assertion** is kept separately from the **canonical claim** the Project\nagrees on: when a second document states a different figure for the same metric and period, the two assertions stay\nand the canonical claim becomes *contested* — nothing is silently overwritten. And a **mention** is never promoted:\nentities are Subject-layer objects for good; only *claims* cross into Domain, because only claims can be checked."],[6026,"Two of those facts matter beyond this screen. **Exact span** is the precision of the anchor — the others are\n*Approximate location*, *Document-level* and *Unresolved*, and a claim's evidence tab shows the same word.\n**decision\\_id** is the record of the extractor's choice — the labels it considered, the scores, the one it picked —\nkept so that the platform can learn from later corrections. It is a reference, never the text itself."],[5112,"Two optional JSON Schema fields:"],[3907,"Two options. **Create an organization** — &#x2A;You become its owner. A default project and Blueprint are set up for\nyou.* **Join an existing organization** — &#x2A;Use the invitation you received, or ask an admin for one.* You see\nthis page only while you belong to no organization; next time you sign in you land in your organization\ndirectly."],[6062,"Two oracles ran over every claim, and their rules are short enough to keep in mind:"],[5511,"Two people ask an agent something in NexChat; the Owner follows both runs in Core — Executions, the trace with its timeline, the governed payloads and the summary — then reads the Audit screen, learns that opening payloads is itself an audited act, filters for refusals, and watches a Builder be turned away from both screens. Ten minutes."],[5244,"Two people ask the agent in NexChat; the Owner follows a run through Executions, the trace's timeline, payloads and summary, finds her own *Viewed payloads* line in Audit, filters for a Builder's refusals and reads the Overview pulse."],[4619,"Two pinned sources now, both *confidential*. Then close it and simply ask in the composer: &#x2A;Which of the three\noffers takes the dog and is under 400 euro?* When the answer arrives, press &#x2A;*Why this answer?** under it."],[6001,"Two properties worth knowing. **Incremental**: a chunk whose text hash already has a vector under the same model in an\nearlier version of the same binding reuses it (*Reuse vectors*) — re-uploading a report with one changed paragraph\nembeds one chunk. **Current-only retrieval**: after a successful index, earlier versions of the same source are\n*retired* — their chunks are flagged and their vectors removed from search — so an answer never cites a superseded\npage while the version itself stays readable with its provenance."],[2216,"two random 32-byte values, base64 — seal stored credentials and webhook secrets"],[5544,"Two rows — **Taras Bondar · Administer · connection \\_all · Deny**, one for each screen he opened. The refusal\nis a fact about the organization, recorded with the same weight as an approval."],[5529,"Two rows, newest first — Taras's run on top. Each carries the **Correlation** id (a UUID; the same id NexChat\nput on the request), the **Root record** — *Agent run · agt\\_general* — a **Status** *Completed*, the\n**Project** *Autumn catalogue*, **Wall time** and **Time**. The row does not say who asked or what: the list is\na governance surface, and it stays at the level of *someone ran this agent in this Project, and it finished*."],[5448,"Two rows: **Chrome · macOS · this minute · this device** and **Safari · macOS · this minute**. Each is a\nsession core-api issued when a sign-in completed, described by the client hint it saw — browser and system,\nnothing more — and the time it was last seen. The line under them: &#x2A;Signing out of other devices takes effect\nwithin a minute.* **Revoke other sessions** is enabled now that there is another one."],[251,"Two screens make the rule visible. Kate, an Operator of the organization, opens Core › Projects before anyone has\ngiven her a place in a Project:"],[7190,"Two sides of one gateway"],[5498,"Two things Kate and Taras tried afterwards, both refused by the server with **403 · permission denied**: Kate\ngranting herself *owner*, and Taras — an Editor — adding a member. Managing membership is the Owner's (and the\nOrganization Admin's); editing content is not managing people."],[388,"Two things the table implies that people ask about:"],[2148,"Two things to *not* expose: the API host ports (3300–3304) and the Keycloak admin port (3320). They are bound to the\nloopback for a reason; leave them there and reach them over SSH when you must."],[7020,"Two trust zones"],[2140,"Two variables deserve a sentence each. `NEXUS_BROKER_MASTER_KEY` seals every credential the Credential Broker\nstores for connections; lose it and every stored credential is unrecoverable (back it up with the volume, step 8).\n`SESSION_SIGNING_KEY` signs the five-minute assertions chat-api and tasks-api trust; rotate it by changing\n`SESSION_SIGNING_KID` together with the key."],[3426,"Two-level page"],[3515,"Two-level page"],[3691,"Two-level page — Tabs for the first level, a SideNav column for the second, the content to its right; the active section in the URL."],[3636,"Type"],[3576,"Type — One family, three weights, seven sizes with one line-height each."],[4508,"Type **Analyse this dataset** and send. Leave the model selector on **Auto**."],[5931,"Type **Northwind Traders** into &#x2A;*Search objects…**."],[4922,"Type **search** in the box and press **Add** on **Project search**."],[4542,"Type **Show the score by month for each direction as a stacked bar**."],[4961,"Type **supplier** in the search box, then **http**."],[4362,"Type *create a task Review the developer portal chapters by Friday*."],[4364,"Type *open the conversation Research the Kyiv Metro* (a thread you cannot see)."],[5005,"Type &#x2A;Connect to my Gmail, collect last week's mail and tell me what needs my attention.*"],[5007,"Type &#x2A;Each morning, flag the messages that need me personally, and never send or delete anything.*"],[5003,"Type &#x2A;Run the onboarding process for supplier Acme.*"],[5630,"Type &#x2A;what is on this scene?*; then select *Orders DB* and type *move this below the API*."],[3953,"Type a second line and send it:"],[5856,"Type the question into &#x2A;*Ask Nexi anything…** and send it. Our example, with the two documents in the Project:"],[4815,"Type the sentence and press **Draft flow**:"],[3902,"Type your work e-mail, choose a password of at least 12 characters, then press **Create account**."],[4054,"Type: &#x2A;Make a dashboard for carrier performance.*"],[3367,"type=search with a visually hidden label; shown only when showListControls says the list needs it."],[645,"Typical use"],[4679,"Typing `/` in the Project's composer offers `/weekend`."],[1889,"ukrainian-tts (\\~450 MB) behind `POST /v1/audio/speech`; the Gateway's local `tts` route. Compose profile `tts-local`."],[928,"Unbind agent tool"],[1225,"Unbind agent tool"],[7481,"Unchanged contract; deciders, expiry sweep, outbox event."],[3965,"Under **Chat** one result: the chat, with the matching word highlighted and *Weekend trips* as its Project.\nSearch only ever shows chats in Projects you belong to. Press **Enter** to open it, **Esc** to close."],[4962,"Under **Connected**, the review fixture shows tools of a Suppliers API and of a research agent. Their **Add** buttons\nare grey and each row says why: *Disabled in this Project* (an administrator has not enabled it — it is still\n*Pending review*), *No healthy connection* (the integration exists but nothing is connected). You cannot talk your\nway past these; they change in NexCore, not here."],[4881,"Under **Flows** the row reads *Plan the weekend … v1 · Goal loop · Published*."],[5942,"Under **NEARBY**, pick **Sources** instead of *Entities* and the stage lists the documents the carrier is mentioned\nin; **Open in document** on a document or a claim takes you to the Evidence Workspace with\nthe span highlighted on the page. Everything Studio draws can be traced to a span."],[5165,"Under **Platform** on the Skills page you find the skills your organization provides to every Project — in the\nfixture, *Summarize*, *Create Agent* and *Create Flow*. Opening one shows the same six tabs, all read-only, with\n*Platform skill · read-only* in the header. They are governed in NexCore, not here. If you want a variant, create your\nown skill in the Project and borrow what you like from the platform text."],[7241,"under an assistant message in NexChat"],[4219,"Under both sits the **guardrail port**: every customer turn passes input, retrieval, tool and output checks under a\nprofile (*External · public*, *External · verified customer*, *Internal*); the public profiles fail closed."],[4997,"Under the answer, one line: **Auto → Analyst · gpt-oss-20b · local · ⓘ · Agent Runtime · confidential**. The\narrow is Auto's pick; the model name and *local / cloud* is what Synapse bound for that turn at the Project's\nclassification; the runtime says whether an agent, a Flow or an engine answered. Variants you will see:\n*You chose Writer* (override) · *Auto → General · fallback* (no classifier was available — words alone decided,\nand a fallback never starts a Flow) · *Auto → Direct answer · engine:nexbi* · *Auto → General · with Gmail* (a\ncapability that needs a connected product)."],[4477,"Under the fields, a one-line summary — *Cheapest qualified · Chat · default quality* — is what the Overview shows,\nand a checkbox **Allow fallback to another allowed model**: when the routed model fails, Synapse may try the next\none in the *same eligible set*. It never crosses the classification ceiling or the tier cap, and when no model\nqualifies at all the turn fails with a clear reason rather than quietly using a bigger or an external model."],[5383,"Under the six suite tiles, three more: **Map · Where things are**, **Care · Serve your customers**, **Forge ·\nThink, sketch, model**. They are drawn from the same Blueprint list: a module an organization has not enabled has\nno tile at all. Each opens on its own origin (`/map`, `/care`, `/forge`) with the same session cookie."],[4705,"Under the text box, **Try one of these** offers three example sentences you can adopt with one click — useful to\nsee how much detail a good sentence has: *what* the agent does, *what* it returns, *what it must never do*. The\nlink **Start with an empty form** skips the drafting and gives you the plain form instead."],[4509,"Under your message, the **attachment card**: *sample\\_dataset.xlsx · 44.4 MB · reading the file… · confidential ·\nPreview*. Then the **staged run card** — **Nexi · Agentic Data Scientist · criteria 0 / 6 · 0 / 8** — with eight\npending stages: **Ingest · Plan · Profile · Duplicates · Unit names · Geography · Charts (≥ 4) · Report**; the\ncontrols **Pause · Stop loop · 0 s · View run**; *No drafts yet*. At the bottom, the **route line**: **Auto →\nAgentic Data Scientist · qwen3-8b · local · Why this route? · Flow Runtime**."],[4323,"Understand every tab and field of the agent screen — Overview, Instructions, Knowledge, Skills, Tools, Models, Permissions, Versions."],[4329,"Understand every tab and field of the skill screen — Overview, Instructions, Input / Output, Examples, Evaluations, Versions — and the human review gate."],[1136,"Unpin project"],[1150,"Unpin this Project for *me* (1.16.0 ) — idempotent"],[6035,"Untick **amount** under **MENTIONS BY LABEL** and the underlines under the figures disappear; tick it again."],[6869,"Up to two Gold claims of the anchored entities, with their verdicts."],[924,"Update agent"],[1333,"Update binding schedule"],[782,"Update dashboard"],[833,"Update dataset"],[1594,"Update iteration"],[861,"Update metric"],[1616,"Update milestone"],[1135,"Update project"],[1184,"Update skill"],[2435,"Update the entry in the vault / secret manager; `docker compose run --rm openbao-init` after editing `openbao/seed.env` on the bundled OpenBao"],[1556,"Update tool mapping"],[1383,"Update view"],[1691,"Update wo