5068,"What you see"],[5136,"What you see"],[5195,"What you will have built"],[246,"Whatever the outcome, an **audit record** is written: who, what, on which resource, allowed or denied, and why.\nAdministrators read them in Core › Audit; see Read the audit trail of a run."],[4425,"Whatever the Project's owner configured for all agents."],[7105,"When"],[7239,"When"],[7497,"When"],[604,"When a flow or a tool call pauses for a human, the run's creator resolves at that moment who may decide —\nnormally the Project's owners — and writes those ids on the request. A later change of membership does not\nwiden the list."],[3956,"When a follow-up goes in a different direction — \"actually, what about the seaside instead?\" — press **Branch**\non the answer you want to start from. You get a new chat that begins with the conversation up to that point,\nand the original stays as it was."],[3756,"When a list needs more than three filters, they leave the toolbar for a panel above (a wrapping row of labelled compact selects and chips, 12 px label over each) or beside the list"],[3760,"When a list needs more than three filters, they leave the toolbar for a panel above (a wrapping row of labelled compact selects and chips, 12 px label over each) or beside the list; the toolbar keeps search and the primary action. Active filters show as removable chips with *Clear all*; a filtered-to-empty list says what it filtered. NexBI's `.nexus-bi-fbar` promoted; DS-7010 stays the ≤ 3 case."],[4043,"When a Project has a governed dataset with metrics, a plain question in NexChat — *how many, how much, which is\nhighest* — need not go to an agent at all. **Auto** recognises a *data question*, resolves it to a certified metric and\na bound dataset, and asks NexBI's query engine directly. The answer is a computed number with its provenance, not a\nmodel's estimate; the model is never handed the rows. This chapter asks the Logistics Project about its carriers."],[5286,"When an organization is created, core-api installs the base pack — a signed bundle whose signature is verified\nagainst a known key before anything is written; an unsigned or tampered pack is refused (*Audit* records why). The\npack's agents, skills and flow patterns become the organization's registry in chat-api; its Blueprint becomes\nthe **base layer**. Core's **Capabilities** screen reads `GET /chat/agents`, `GET /chat/skills` and\n`GET /chat/patterns` — organization-wide, published rows — and **Tools** reads the Tool Registry\n(`GET /tools`) together with the Blueprint's tool policy. **Blueprints & Packs** reads `GET /blueprints/effective`\n(the resolved chain: every layer, every setting, the effective value and its source) and `GET /blueprints/packs`\n(installed, available and rejected packs). Every member may read these; import (`POST /blueprints/packs/{name}/install`) and the\norganization layer are administrator actions."],[5155,"When it appears"],[712,"When it fails"],[6562,"When no specialist reaches the minimum and no arm bids, the message goes to the Project's published copy of the Resolver Flow (below)."],[3948,"When the answer is complete a small grey **grounding line** appears under it — who answered, which model,\nthe classification, and &#x2A;*Why this answer?** — followed by the actions copy, thumbs up, thumbs down, **Branch**\nand **Regenerate**."],[5079,"When the current version was saved."],[4790,"When the engine reached the approval node it created an **approval request** in NexTasks — subject *approval\nnode*, title from the template, deciders *Project owner*, expiry from the node — and parked the run, keeping the\nNexTasks item's id on the step. The card in the Studio and the run card in the thread are two views of that one\nrecord: the browser fetches it from NexTasks directly, and NexTasks decides on the server whether you are a decider —\nthat is why an editor sees no buttons and why an owner who tried to approve their own request above a certain\nclassification would be refused. Your decision is written once, immutably, with your identity, the time and the\ncomment; NexTasks then publishes an event that the Flow Engine consumes to resume the run on the chosen branch.\nTimeouts are swept the same way: when the expiry passes the item becomes *expired*, the step fails typed and the run\nfails. Every one of these transitions is an audit event NexCore keeps."],[4828,"When the Flow starts. `0 8 * * 1` is a cron expression — we will fix it in step 7."],[4557,"When the planner finds a kept dataset whose technique already answers a stage, it **reuses*&#x2A; it and says so in the\nplan (&#x2A;↺ reused from …*) — an `analysis_reuse` decision with *reuse* and *recompute* as the two arms. **Recompute**\n(only for the person who started the run) runs the stage again on the current file: &#x2A;Recomputing … — the earlier\nresults stay until this finishes.* Layers follow the platform's memory rule — Bronze is the typed copy of your file,\nSilver a normalised table, Gold a result — and every dataset carries where it came from."],[6053,"When the queue is empty on a Project with no tables at all, the screen says so and offers **Upload a document with\na table**. With **All knowledge** as scope it reads &#x2A;The verification queue is per Project — pick a Project to\nreview its claims.*"],[6321,"When the sprint ends, press **Complete sprint**. (Not done on the documentation stack — the sprint is running.)"],[7207,"When you build the *Trip planner* you do not pick \"model X, version Y\". You describe the job:"],[5166,"When you press *Draft skill*, NexChat asks the platform's authoring drafter for a `SkillManifest` — name, description,\ninstructions skeleton — and stores it as **v0.1.0 · Draft**. Every save is a **patch bump with a snapshot** and resets\nthe human review to *pending*; **review** records the decision against the exact current version; **publish** is\nrefused unless that version is reviewed and the skill is not blocked, then bumps the minor version and emits a\n`skill.published` event that other parts of Nexi (audit, the agent picker, NexCore governance) listen to."],[6349,"When you type a title or a comment that looks like a known reference (*REQ-12*, *AC-7*, *DEC-3*), VibeBan\nsuggests the match; accepting or ignoring the suggestion is written back to the `reference_match` decision."],[259,"Where"],[2259,"Where"],[2362,"Where"],[6628,"Where"],[7172,"Where"],[7184,"Where"],[7238,"Where"],[7663,"Where a business user shapes the assistant, installations, queues, SLA and surveys; the assistant profile compiles into a reviewed Agent."],[4341,"Where a Project keeps its knowledge, an agent's Knowledge tab, a Flow with a *file* input that reads three cottage offers into a Canvas table, the file as a pinned source, and the Grounding drawer."],[3433,"Where a record lives and how fresh the copy is, next to its title: `NEXUS` for a native record; &#x2A;from ‹provider› · ‹age›* for an external one read moments ago; &#x2A;stale · ‹age›&#x2A; when the last read is old; *‹provider› unavailable* when the source does not answer. Built on `Chip` (DS-3003) with the four semantic tones; glyph + text, never colour alone; the tooltip carries the exact verification time. Not a kit duplicate: the kit's Chip has no notion of provenance or age."],[3428,"Where a record lives and how fresh the copy is, next to its title: NEXUS for a native record; *from ‹provider› · ‹age›* for an external one read moments ago; *stale · ‹age›* when t"],[5717,"Where an object sits on the way from words to facts: **Sources** (*Lexical*: documents, pages, fragments), **Claims** (*Subject*: mentions, entities and claims as proposed), **Knowledge** (*Domain*: what was decided)."],[35,"Where every refusal ends up"],[6506,"Where in NexChat"],[5719,"Where it is stored: raw captures in the object store · fragments, mentions and vectors in pgvector · entities and verified facts in Apache AGE. All three live in PostgreSQL."],[6445,"Where it lives"],[70